- text: "Submitting an improved near-tangent construction to push r0 close to 0.1 with minimal safety margin.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tight 5x5 r=0.1-1e-8 + optimal cell filler\"\ntags: \"constructive, grid, lattice, near-tangent\"\nabstract: \"25 circles on a 5x5 grid with r0=0.1-1e-8 to avoid numerical tangency; add one circle at (0.2,0.2) with radius sqrt(0.02)-r0-1e-8. This maximizes 24*r0 + sqrt(0.02)-eps under the 25+1 scheme.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      25 grid circles of radius r0 ~ 0.1, plus one cell-center filler.\n      Grid centers at {0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9}^2.\n      r0 chosen as 0.1 - 1e-8 for a small safety margin.\n      The extra circle sits at (0.2, 0.2) with radius d - r0 - eps, where\n      d = distance to a nearest grid center = sqrt(0.02).\n      \"\"\"\n      r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n      eps = 1e-8\n\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords\
    \ for y in coords]  # 25 grid centers\n      radii = [r0] * 25\n\n      hole_center = np.array([0.2, 0.2], dtype=float)\n      neighbor = np.array([0.1, 0.1], dtype=float)\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - neighbor))  # sqrt(0.02)\n      r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n\n      centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n      radii.append(float(r_hole))\n\n      centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n      radii = np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n      return centers, radii\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
