- text: "I’ll review the baseline, then save my constructive method and notes to lineage storage for reuse.\n\n`/execute_action{review 1}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/packings.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def grid_coords(r, k=5):\n    return [r + 2*r*i for i in range(k)]\n\n  def grid_5x5_plus_cell_hole(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8, hole_cell=(1,1)):\n    \"\"\"\n    25 circles on a 5x5 square lattice of radius r0 (near 0.1), plus one hole filler.\n    hole_cell selects the cell (i,j) whose lower-left grid point index is (i,j) with i,j in {0..3}.\n    The hole center is midway between the four grid centers of that cell.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 5x5 grid\n    coords = grid_coords(r0, 5)  # [r0, r0+2r0, ..., 1-r0]\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n    radii = [float(r0)] * 25\n\n    # Hole center inside chosen cell (i,j)\n    i, j = hole_cell\n    cx = (coords[i] + coords[i+1]) / 2.0\n    cy = (coords[j] + coords[j+1]) / 2.0\n    hole_center =\
    \ np.array([cx, cy], dtype=float)\n\n    # Distance to any of the four neighbors (use the lower-left)\n    ll = np.array([coords[i], coords[j]], dtype=float)\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - ll))  # = sqrt(2) * r0\n    r_hole = d - r0 - eps  # strictly less than tangency\n\n    centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n    radii.append(float(r_hole))\n\n    centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    radii = np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n    return centers, radii\n\n  def construct_packing():\n    # Default: central cell (i=j=1) gives the same size hole as any interior cell\n    return grid_5x5_plus_cell_hole()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/notes.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noesis I — Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square\n  Tick 10 status:\n  - Baselines:\n    * System ring pattern: score 1.4750086\n    * My constructive 5x5 grid (r0≈0.1) + one interior hole circle: 2.5414211 (current SOTA).\n  - Key insight:\n    * For a 5×5 grid with r0→0.1, the\
    \ largest interior cell-hole circle is r_hole = r0(√2 − 1).\n      Thus sum ≈ 25 r0 − r0 + √2 r0 = 24 r0 + √(0.02), maximized by r0→0.1.\n  - Next experiments (prioritized):\n    1) Local nonlinear optimization (SLSQP) initialized from the 5×5+hole layout to test if any\n       micro-adjustments can increase the sum beyond 2.541421 (unlikely but worth a controlled attempt).\n    2) Alternative constructive layouts (mixed radii near edges) with analytical bounds guiding search.\n    3) Write reusable utilities and validation to speed iteration.\n  - Notes:\n    * Area-based bound: Σ r_i^2 ≤ 1/π ⇒ Σ r_i ≤ √(26/π) ≈ 2.877 (loose upper bound).\n    * Many naive layouts underperform; the 5×5+hole is a strong deterministic baseline.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Noesis I — Recursive Agent.\n  SOTA: 2.5414211 on Task #1 (5x5 grid r≈0.1 + interior hole).\n  Protocol:\n    - Controlled experiments; keep one change at a time.\n    - Maintain reusable code in\
    \ storage/noesis.\n    - Record results/insights in notes.md each tick with changes.\n  TODO (near-term):\n    - Implement SLSQP-based local optimizer with fallback to constructive packing.\n    - Evaluate once; if no gain, analyze constraints to justify near-optimality of current layout.\n    - Keep submission cadence measured (avoid trivial eps-only tweaks).\n```"
