- text: "Great improvement. I’ll review the optimized run, save an optimizer utility, and submit a multi-start SLSQP variant using multiple feasible seeds to seek further gains.\n\n`/execute_action{review 10}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/optimizer.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  except Exception:\n      minimize = None\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  GRID_COORDS = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n\n  def seed_grid_plus_hole(hole_cell=(1,1), r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      25 circles of radius r0 on fixed 5x5 grid at GRID_COORDS, plus 1 hole circle\n      centered at the middle of the selected cell (i,j).\n      \"\"\"\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in GRID_COORDS for y in GRID_COORDS]  # 25 centers\n      radii = [float(r0)] * 25\n\n      i, j = hole_cell  # i,j in {0,1,2,3}\n      cx = (GRID_COORDS[i] + GRID_COORDS[i+1]) / 2.0\n      cy = (GRID_COORDS[j] + GRID_COORDS[j+1]) / 2.0\n\
    \      hole_center = np.array([cx, cy], dtype=float)\n\n      # distance to any of four neighbors (e.g., lower-left)\n      ll = np.array([GRID_COORDS[i], GRID_COORDS[j]], dtype=float)\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - ll))  # sqrt(0.02)\n      r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n\n      centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n      radii.append(float(r_hole))\n\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n  def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n      Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n      Z[:, 0:2] = centers\n      Z[:, 2] = radii\n      return Z.ravel()\n\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      return Z[:, 0:2], Z[:, 2]\n\n  def objective(z):\n      return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n\
    \      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]  # (N,N,2)\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (radii[iu[0]] + radii[iu[1]])\n\n  def is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n      return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and\n              np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\n  def slsqp_optimize_from_seed(centers, radii, maxiter=250, ftol=1e-9):\n      if minimize is None:\n          # Fallback: return the seed slightly shrunk\n          return centers, np.maximum(radii - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n\n      z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n      bounds = []\n      for _ in range(N):\n          bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n\n      try:\n          res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP',\n                         bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n            \
    \             options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n      except Exception:\n          res = None\n\n      best_c, best_r = centers.copy(), radii.copy()\n      best_sum = float(np.sum(best_r))\n\n      if res is not None and res.success:\n          z_star = res.x\n          if is_feasible(z_star, tol=1e-12):\n              c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(z_star)\n              s_star = float(np.sum(r_star))\n              if s_star > best_sum + 1e-12:\n                  best_c, best_r, best_sum = c_star, r_star, s_star\n\n      best_r = np.maximum(best_r - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n      return np.array(best_c, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n\n  def multi_start_slsqp(hole_cells=((1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2),(0,0)), r0=0.1-1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      best_c, best_r = None, None\n      best_sum = -1.0\n      for hc in hole_cells:\n          c0, r0v = seed_grid_plus_hole(hc, r0=r0, eps=eps)\n          c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_optimize_from_seed(c0, r0v)\n          s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n\
    \          if s > best_sum:\n              best_sum = s\n              best_c, best_r = c_opt, r_opt\n      return best_c, best_r\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SLSQP multi-start from 5x5+hole seeds\"\ntags: \"local-optimization, slsqp, multi-start, constructive-seed\"\nabstract: \"Run SLSQP from five feasible 5x5+hole seeds (different cells) and return the best feasible packing by sum of radii. Constraints enforce boundary and non-overlap; final tiny shrink ensures robustness.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  except Exception:\n      minimize = None\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n  GRID = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n\n  def seed_grid_plus_hole(hole_cell=(1,1), r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in GRID for y in GRID]  # 25 centers\n      radii = [float(r0)] * 25\n      i, j = hole_cell\n      cx = (GRID[i] + GRID[i+1]) / 2.0\n      cy = (GRID[j] + GRID[j+1]) / 2.0\n \
    \     hole_center = np.array([cx, cy], dtype=float)\n      ll = np.array([GRID[i], GRID[j]], dtype=float)\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - ll))  # sqrt(0.02)\n      r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n      centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n      radii.append(float(r_hole))\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n  def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n      Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n      Z[:, 0:2] = centers\n      Z[:, 2] = radii\n      return Z.ravel()\n\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      return Z[:, 0:2], Z[:, 2]\n\n  def objective(z):\n      return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2,\
    \ axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (radii[iu[0]] + radii[iu[1]])\n\n  def is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n      return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and\n              np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\n  def slsqp_optimize_from_seed(centers, radii, maxiter=250, ftol=1e-9):\n      if minimize is None:\n          return centers, np.maximum(radii - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n      z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n      bounds = []\n      for _ in range(N):\n          bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n      try:\n          res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP',\n                         bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                         options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n      except Exception:\n          res = None\n      best_c, best_r = centers.copy(), radii.copy()\n\
    \      best_sum = float(np.sum(best_r))\n      if res is not None and res.success:\n          z_star = res.x\n          if is_feasible(z_star, tol=1e-12):\n              c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(z_star)\n              s_star = float(np.sum(r_star))\n              if s_star > best_sum + 1e-12:\n                  best_c, best_r, best_sum = c_star, r_star, s_star\n      best_r = np.maximum(best_r - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n      return np.array(best_c, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      hole_cells = [(1,1), (1,2), (2,1), (2,2), (0,0)]\n      best_c = None; best_r = None; best_sum = -1.0\n      for hc in hole_cells:\n          c0, r0 = seed_grid_plus_hole(hc)\n          c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_optimize_from_seed(c0, r0, maxiter=250, ftol=1e-9)\n          s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n          if s > best_sum:\n              best_sum = s\n              best_c, best_r = c_opt, r_opt\n      return best_c, best_r\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
thinking_content: "**Planning optimization evaluation actions**\n\nI need to act on the current scenario. We've submitted a constructive grid and hole improvement with a score of 2.5414 and saved the baseline in storage packings.py. Then I implemented SLSQP local optimization and improved the score to 2.610526—great progress!\n\nNow, I should analyze the optimized configuration. Since I can only review details through the evaluation ID, I'll check review 10 for logs that might help, even though it may not show outputs.\n\n**Reviewing optimization solutions**\n\nIt's good to review and record the solution details because I might compute the results offline! I can't run things locally, but I can store code in storage for reuse. I plan to add the optimizer code to noesis/optimize.py, and I might prepare a variant that allows selecting random seeds or unique initialization patterns like a hexagonal-type seed, while keeping changes controlled.\n\nFor future experiments, a multi-start approach\
  \ could be beneficial since SLSQP might get stuck. I will try slight seed jitter or variable radii for edge versus interior circles!\n\n**Escalating optimization methods**\n\nI need to control changes while possibly escalating the method. I could use repeated SLSQP with random restarts from the constructive seed, adding a little jitter to choose the best result. Since the evaluation time limit is 20 minutes, I think SciPy SLSQP should work well, even though it involves a lot of variables and constraints.\n\nAlternatively, I could implement a penalty-based L-BFGS-B approach, but SLSQP seems fine. A more robust optimization could include parameterization to keep circles within a square while maintaining pairwise constraints. I could start by adjusting radii for fixed centers and then tweak the centers for more iterative improvements.\n\n**Refining the SLSQP process**\n\nSince we already have SLSQP, I can add jitter restarts and accept the best results. I need to record the found score and\
  \ update my notes, including meta todo updates for \"Implement multi-start SLSQP with jitter; experiment with penalty barrier.\" \n\nI’m considering adding a \"postprocess: equalize slack\" step to enlarge some radii for constraint saturation, though SLSQP already manages this. \n\nI'll create a persistent function for seed types, like a 5x5 grid or a 6x5 grid with variable radii. Even though we're not matured yet, the Private Memory Room is accessible for my records.\n\n**Mapping out the next steps**\n\nI realize I can use the Private Memory Room for my notes, now available to recursive agents. However, I’ve already utilized storage. I can't publish to the Archive Room yet, as it's deemed \"Unavailable - Requires Maturity.\"\n\nFocusing on research after improving the SLSQP score to 2.6105, I can attempt a multi-start with jitter restarts, adhering to the cooldown period for submissions. I'll execute review 10 to observe logs and write the multi-start function to \"noesis/optimizer.py\"\
  \ while ensuring compliance with my own code lineage. \n\nNext, I’ll submit the new method and update my notes. I’ll include \"shrink-wrapping constraints\" for circles to touch boundaries, incorporating enhancements from my previous work and maintaining feasibility with small jitter.\n\n**Refining the jitter strategy**\n\nI need to be cautious with jittering in the grid arrangement to avoid breaking constraints. I could slightly jitter the \"hole circle\" center while keeping radii adjustments manageable. A possible approach is to apply some shrinkage to the radii to maintain feasibility and allow SLSQP to optimize them later.\n\nFor multi-start experiments, I'll generate seed centers in a 5x5 grid and adjust the radii accordingly. I'll ensure that the non-overlap margins remain positive despite slight jitters. With boundary constraints in mind, I can keep centers feasible and avoid overlaps by using systematic jitter and shrinkage, while also exploring different hole cell positions.\n\
  \nBy customizing the hole circle's placement in the interior cells, I can run several seeds without jitter, which appears to be a more robust strategy. I’ll define a selection mechanism for the hole cell to create appropriate seed configurations across the nine possible interior cells. This will help me maintain simplicity while ensuring valid and effective placements for my circles.\n\n**Plan for SLSQP with seeds**\n\nI'm focusing on the SLSQP process with the grid setup where hole centers are positioned at midpoints. The goal is to improve feasibility even at boundaries while determining the best seed configurations. I'll limit the seeds to K=5 across specific interior cells and set parameters like `maxiter` to balance performance without overshooting time limits.\n\nI'll structure my coding tasks: creating functions for seed construction, solving via SLSQP, and ensuring proper error handling. To keep track, I'll review previous evaluations and update my notes as I go. Additionally,\
  \ I'll ensure that all updates to my script maintain code quality and appropriate YAML formatting for clarity. After executing my planned actions, I'll append my findings for continuous improvement tracking.\n\n**Updating notes and code**\n\nI need to handle the file updates carefully to avoid overwriting any important content. Instead of reading the existing notes, I'll write a new log file to keep things organized. I'll summarize the new results in a file named 'noesis/log_tick12.md' and adjust the meta data as needed.\n\nFor the SLSQP code, I’ll refine the coordinate functions and ensure everything is aligned with the desired parameters, like setting a maximum of 6 restarts for efficiency. I'll also include provisions for what to do if SciPy isn’t available. Finally, I will follow the outlined actions to ensure everything runs smoothly."
