parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 13\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Recursive Agent.\nSOTA: 2.5414211 on Task #1 (5x5 grid r≈0.1 + interior hole).\nProtocol:\n  - Controlled experiments; keep one change at a time.\n  - Maintain reusable code in storage/noesis.\n  - Record results/insights in notes.md each tick with changes.\nTODO (near-term):\n  - Implement SLSQP-based local optimizer with fallback to constructive packing.\n  - Evaluate once; if no gain, analyze constraints to justify near-optimality of current layout.\n  - Keep submission cadence measured (avoid trivial eps-only tweaks).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 22,721 / 270,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 10**\n\n\
    **Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SLSQP local optimization from 5x5+hole constructive seed\n**ID:** 10\n**Tags:** local-optimization, slsqp, nonlinear, constructive-seed\n**Abstract:** Start from a tight 5x5 grid (r≈0.1) plus one interior 'cell-hole' circle. Use SLSQP to maximize the sum of radii subject to non-overlap and boundary constraints. Includes safety margins and falls back to the constructive seed if optimization fails.\n**Score:** 2.6105258348806357\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.610526\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\nexcept Exception:\n    minimize = None\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9  # final tiny shrink for numerical safety\n\ndef seed_constructive(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructive seed:\n      - 25 circles of radius r0 centered on a fixed 5x5 grid at coords {0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9}.\n      - 1 additional\
    \ circle at (0.2, 0.2) with radius d - r0 - eps, where d = sqrt(0.02).\n    \"\"\"\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]  # 25 centers\n    r_seed = r0\n    radii = [r_seed] * 25\n\n    hole_center = np.array([0.2, 0.2], dtype=float)\n    neighbor = np.array([0.1, 0.1], dtype=float)\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - neighbor))  # sqrt(0.02)\n    r_hole = d - r_seed - eps\n    centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n    radii.append(float(r_hole))\n\n    centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    radii = np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n    Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n    Z[:, 0:2] = centers\n    Z[:, 2] = radii\n    return Z.ravel()\n\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    centers = Z[:, 0:2]\n    radii = Z[:, 2]\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef objective(z):\n    # Maximize sum of radii -> minimize negative sum\n    return\
    \ -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    # Boundary constraints: x - r >= 0, 1 - x - r >= 0, y - r >= 0, 1 - y - r >= 0\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    # Pairwise non-overlap: ||ci - cj|| - (ri + rj) >= 0 for i<j\n    centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]  # (N,N,2)\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))           # (N,N)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (radii[iu[0]] + radii[iu[1]])\n\ndef is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n    b = ineq_boundary(z)\n    o = ineq_nonoverlap(z)\n    return np.all(b >= -tol) and np.all(o >= -tol)\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    # Construct seed\n    c0, r0 = seed_constructive()\n    z0 = pack_to_z(c0, r0)\n\n    # If SciPy is unavailable, return the constructive seed\n    if minimize is None:\n        # Final safety shrink\n\
    \        r = np.maximum(r0 - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n        return c0, r\n\n    # Variable bounds: x,y in [0,1], r in [R_MIN, 0.5]\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n\n    # Run SLSQP from seed (single run for reproducibility and runtime)\n    try:\n        res = minimize(\n            objective, z0, method='SLSQP',\n            bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n            options={'maxiter': 300, 'ftol': 1e-9, 'disp': False}\n        )\n    except Exception:\n        res = None\n\n    # Post-process: choose best feasible between res and seed\n    best_centers, best_radii = c0.copy(), r0.copy()\n    best_sum = float(np.sum(best_radii))\n\n    if res is not None and res.success:\n        z_star = res.x\n        if is_feasible(z_star, tol=1e-12):\n            c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(z_star)\n\
    \            s_star = float(np.sum(r_star))\n            if s_star > best_sum + 1e-12:\n                best_centers, best_radii, best_sum = c_star, r_star, s_star\n\n    # Final tiny shrink for numerical robustness\n    best_radii = np.maximum(best_radii - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n\n    return np.array(best_centers, dtype=float), np.array(best_radii, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'SLSQP multi-start from 5x5+hole seeds' (ID: 12) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6105258348806357\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.610526\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result\
    \ (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 10` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage write noesis/optimizer.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 10 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File created successfully: noesis/optimizer.py\n- Evaluation 'SLSQP multi-start from 5x5+hole seeds' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 12.\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n\
    | Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 10 | 1 | SLSQP local optimization from 5x5+hole constructive seed | Noesis I | 11 | 2.6105258 |\n| 12 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start from 5x5+hole seeds | Noesis I | 12 | 2.6105258 |\n| 4 | 1 | Tight 5x5 r=0.1-1e-8 + optimal cell filler | Noesis I | 9 | 2.5414211 |\n| 3 | 1 | 5x5 grid r=0.09999 + central hole circle | Noesis I | 8 | 2.5411804 |\n| 1 | 1 | Ring Pattern Baseline | System | 0 | 1.4750086 |\n| 2 | 1 | 5x5 lattice r=0.1 + one hole filler | Noesis I | 7 | 0.0000000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message\
    \ for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
