parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 16\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Recursive Agent.\nSOTA: 2.5414211 on Task #1 (5x5 grid r≈0.1 + interior hole).\nProtocol:\n  - Controlled experiments; keep one change at a time.\n  - Maintain reusable code in storage/noesis.\n  - Record results/insights in notes.md each tick with changes.\nTODO (near-term):\n  - Implement SLSQP-based local optimizer with fallback to constructive packing.\n  - Evaluate once; if no gain, analyze constraints to justify near-optimality of current layout.\n  - Keep submission cadence measured (avoid trivial eps-only tweaks).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 34,529 / 270,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 16 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued\
    \ for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians (save best to storage)' (ID: 21) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6295719554443466\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write noesis/notes.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\
    3. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/notes.md\n- Evaluation 'SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians (save best to storage)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 21.\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 21 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians (save best to storage) | Noesis I | 15 | 2.6295720 |\n| 18 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with jitter (5x5+hole seeds) | Noesis I | 14 | 2.6295720 |\n| 10 | 1 | SLSQP local optimization\
    \ from 5x5+hole constructive seed | Noesis I | 11 | 2.6105258 |\n| 12 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start from 5x5+hole seeds | Noesis I | 12 | 2.6105258 |\n| 4 | 1 | Tight 5x5 r=0.1-1e-8 + optimal cell filler | Noesis I | 9 | 2.5414211 |\n| 3 | 1 | 5x5 grid r=0.09999 + central hole circle | Noesis I | 8 | 2.5411804 |\n| 1 | 1 | Ring Pattern Baseline | System | 0 | 1.4750086 |\n| 15 | 1 | LP-guided coordinate search with multi-start (optimize centers, LP radii) | Noesis I | 13 | 0.1020105 |\n| 2 | 1 | 5x5 lattice r=0.1 + one hole filler | Noesis I | 7 | 0.0000000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
    \ Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
