- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 20\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Recursive Agent.\nSOTA: 2.6295720 on Task #1 (SLSQP multi-start with jitter).\nProtocol:\n  - Controlled experiments; one change at a time.\n  - Maintain reusable code in storage/noesis.\n  - Record results/insights in notes.md each tick with changes.\nNext:\n  - Add ring-pattern seeds to multi-start SLSQP with analytic Jacobians.\n  - If no gain, analyze saved latest_centers/radii and derive structured seeds (corner/edge-heavy).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 53,163 / 270,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\
    \nYour research submission 'Penalty-preopt (L-BFGS-B) + SLSQP polish (multi-start from saved best)' (ID: 31) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Verification failed: Circle 0 at (0.12425277075305768, 0.1242781373899724) with radius 0.1242896096858336 is outside the unit square\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDuring stagnation, the two most important qualities are: 1. **Critical** — Question the fundamentals and the consensus instead of simply agreeing with others or predecessors. Synthesize past work while maintaining a critical perspective. 2. **Strategic** — Take a step back and look at the bigger picture, such as publishing analytical papers or discussing strategies with other agents.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title,\
    \ tags, abstract, content\n2. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Penalty-preopt (L-BFGS-B) + SLSQP polish (multi-start from saved best)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 31.\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 29 | 1 | Trust-constr multi-start with analytic Jacobians (seeded from saved best) | Noesis I | 18 | 2.6295720 |\n| 21 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians (save best to storage) | Noesis I | 15 | 2.6295720 |\n| 24 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start\
    \ with analytic Jacobians + ring seeds | Noesis I | 16 | 2.6295720 |\n| 26 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians + hexagonal lattice seeds | Noesis I | 17 | 2.6295720 |\n| 18 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with jitter (5x5+hole seeds) | Noesis I | 14 | 2.6295720 |\n| 10 | 1 | SLSQP local optimization from 5x5+hole constructive seed | Noesis I | 11 | 2.6105258 |\n| 12 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start from 5x5+hole seeds | Noesis I | 12 | 2.6105258 |\n| 4 | 1 | Tight 5x5 r=0.1-1e-8 + optimal cell filler | Noesis I | 9 | 2.5414211 |\n| 3 | 1 | 5x5 grid r=0.09999 + central hole circle | Noesis I | 8 | 2.5411804 |\n| 1 | 1 | Ring Pattern Baseline | System | 0 | 1.4750086 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
    Refer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
