tick: 29
role: model
parts:
- text: "I’ll run a controlled follow-up: same graph-aware seeds but with a stronger nudge (delta=3e-3) to encourage a contact flip. I’ll log the plan and submit.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/notes.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 29 — Contact report review:\n  - Active (tol=1e-9): reported 0 actives; near-actives show tiny slacks:\n    * Top pair slack ≈ 3.85e-9 (indices 8,13).\n    * Top boundary slack ≈ 3.0e-9 (disc 21, xR).\n  - Controlled change: increase seed nudge to delta=3e-3 for both bottleneck-release and boundary-trade, then SLSQP polish.\n  - Rationale: Larger but still small geometric move to promote a contact flip; feasibility guard will prevent violations; compare against saved best.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Graph-aware seeds (delta=3e-3): bottleneck release + boundary trade\"\ntags: \"contact-graph, seeds, slsqp, analytic-jacobians, feasibility-guard\"\nabstract: \"Use analyzer to find top pair and boundary bottlenecks; generate\
    \ two graph-aware seeds with a stronger nudge (delta=3e-3): bottleneck release along the tightest pair and boundary trade on the tightest boundary. Polish with SLSQP (analytic Jacobians), enforce feasibility, and return the best; save report and final packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  except Exception:\n      minimize = None\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  try:\n      import analyze_contacts as AC\n      import seeds_structured as SS\n  except Exception:\n      AC = None\n      SS = None\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  def load_saved_best():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n          c = np.array(c, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n          r = np.array(r, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None\n\n  def grid_plus_hole_seed(r0=0.1\
    \ - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n      hole_center = np.array([0.2, 0.2], dtype=float)\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n      r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n      radii = [float(r0)] * 25 + [float(r_hole)]\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n  def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n      Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n      Z[:, 0:2] = centers; Z[:, 2] = radii\n      return Z.ravel()\n\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      return Z[:, 0:2], Z[:, 2]\n\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n  def objective_jac(z):\n      g = np.zeros_like(z); g[2::3] = -1.0; return g\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\n  def jac_boundary(z):\n\
    \      J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N), dtype=float)\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n          J[i, xi] = 1.0;        J[i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[N + i, xi] = -1.0;   J[N + i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[2*N + i, yi] = 1.0;  J[2*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[3*N + i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n      return J\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      centers = Z[:, 0:2]; r = Z[:, 2]\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def jac_nonoverlap(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n      centers = Z[:, 0:2]\n      m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N), dtype=float); idx = 0\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              xj = 3*j; yj = xj + 1; rj = xj + 2\n              dx\
    \ = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n              dist = np.hypot(dx, dy)\n              if dist < 1e-12:\n                  gx_i = gy_i = gx_j = gy_j = 0.0\n              else:\n                  invd = 1.0 / dist\n                  gx_i = dx * invd; gy_i = dy * invd\n                  gx_j = -gx_i;     gy_j = -gy_i\n              J[idx, xi] = gx_i;  J[idx, yi] = gy_i;  J[idx, ri] = -1.0\n              J[idx, xj] = gx_j;  J[idx, yj] = gy_j;  J[idx, rj] = -1.0\n              idx += 1\n      return J\n\n  def is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n      return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\n  def make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n      x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      r = np.minimum(radii, cap); r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n      for _ in range(max_iter):\n          diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n\
    \          dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n          m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n          if np.all(m >= eps): break\n          k = int(np.argmin(m)); i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n          need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n          di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN); dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n          if di <= 0 and dj <= 0: r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN)\n          else: r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n          cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n          r = np.minimum(r, cap)\n      r = np.maximum(r - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n      return centers, r\n\n  def slsqp_polish(centers, radii, maxiter=500, ftol=1e-9):\n      if minimize is None: return make_feasible(centers, radii)\n      z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n      bounds = []\n      for _ in range(N): bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary,\
    \   'jac': jac_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n      try:\n          res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                         bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                         options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n      except Exception:\n          res = None\n      if res is not None and res.success and is_feasible(res.x, tol=1e-12):\n          c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(res.x)\n          return make_feasible(c_star, r_star)\n      return make_feasible(centers, radii)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c_saved, r_saved = load_saved_best()\n      if c_saved is None: c_saved, r_saved = grid_plus_hole_seed()\n      c_saved, r_saved = make_feasible(c_saved, r_saved)\n\n      # Analyze with slightly relaxed tol to capture near-actives\n      if AC is not None:\n          AC.report(c_saved, r_saved, path='storage/noesis/contact_report.txt', tol=5e-9)\n\
    \          best_pair, top_boundary = AC.top_bottlenecks(c_saved, r_saved, tol=5e-9)\n      else:\n          best_pair = top_boundary = None\n\n      seeds = [(c_saved.copy(), r_saved.copy())]\n      if SS is not None:\n          # Stronger nudge delta\n          delta = 3e-3\n          c1, r1 = SS.bottleneck_release_seed(c_saved, r_saved, best_pair, delta=delta)\n          seeds.append((c1, r1))\n          c2, r2 = SS.boundary_trade_seed(c_saved, r_saved, top_boundary, delta=delta)\n          seeds.append((c2, r2))\n\n      best_c, best_r, best_s = None, None, -1.0\n      for (c, r) in seeds:\n          c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_polish(c, r, maxiter=500, ftol=1e-9)\n          s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n          if s > best_s + 1e-12:\n              best_c, best_r, best_s = c_opt, r_opt, s\n\n      try:\n          np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', best_c, fmt='%.9f')\n          np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt',   best_r, fmt='%.9f')\n      except Exception:\n    \
    \      pass\n      return np.array(best_c, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
thinking_content: "**Adjusting parameters for scaling**\n\nI’m focusing on one change: we adjusted the delta from 1.5e-3 to 3e-3. That’s a straightforward tweak. Alternatively, I could implement contact homotopy, but that would mean more new code and potential heavy conversion. Sticking with the stronger delta seems best. I might also adjust SLSQP polish parameters, but that would be extra changes. It's important to document everything and submit using YAML content. I need to ensure previous attempts handled the boundary constraints, so I’ll also propose adding a fallback.\n\n**Preparing to submit notes and code**\n\nI’m getting ready to produce a storage write summarizing the contact report. It’ll note micro slacks around 3-4e-9 and our plan to apply a stronger delta. \n\nThen I’ll submit with a title: \"Graph-aware seeds (delta=3e-3) — bottleneck release + boundary trade,\" updating the delta to 3e-3 instead of 1.5e-3. I’ll call a function to capture bottlenecks, ensuring it operates independently\
  \ of slack. The seeds list will include the original plus two with the stronger delta. I’ll propose just changing the delta and prepare to call actions accordingly.\n\n**Crafting minimal code**\n\nI’ve noted that the Station previously flagged storage writes from the Reflection Chamber as errors. Now that I’m in the Research Counter, I can move forward. I might skip reading 'help research' since it’s not necessary for now. It’s crucial that the code compiles correctly, so I’ll import \"analyze_contacts\" and \"seeds_structured\" as needed.\n\nI want to call AC.top_bottlenecks and AC.report, using a tolerance of 5e-9 for active constraints. Edge cases around evaluation budgets and concurrency should be manageable. Now, I'll produce the final code concisely!"
