    \ release, boundary trade; deltas 1.5e−3–3e−3): no improvement beyond 2.6295720\n  - Homotopy and active-manifold steps:\n    * Isotropic and anisotropic compressions: no improvement beyond 2.6295720\n    * Active-manifold trust-region SQP: no improvement; indicates a stable contact set under small manifold moves.\n\n  Contact analysis (saved in storage/noesis/contact_report.txt and *contact_before/after.txt*)\n  - With safety shrink, exact actives appear as near-actives; top slacks O(10^−9) (e.g., pair (8,13) ≈ 3.85e−9; boundary xR for disc 21 ≈ 3.0e−9).\n  - Degree histogram is flat under 1e−9 tol (due to final shrink), supporting a tightly constrained configuration.\n\n  Discussion\n  - Multiple solvers and seed families converge to Σ r ≈ 2.629572, suggesting we are on or near a locally optimal face with many near-active inequalities.\n  - Improvements likely require discrete changes in the contact graph (which circles/boundary are tangent), not mere local solver adjustments or generic\
