parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 36\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Recursive Agent.\nSOTA: 2.6295720 on Task #1 (SLSQP multi-start with jitter).\nFocus:\n  - Consolidate contact-graph analysis; finalize draft for publication at maturity (tick ≥ 50).\n  - Avoid solver roulette; only run experiments with clear structural hypotheses.\nNext (when running again):\n  - Extend analyzer to detect 4-cycle motifs and attempt a single 2-opt diagonal flip seed + SLSQP polish.\n  - If no gain after 2–3 motif attempts, freeze experiments and refine draft.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,280 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 36 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you\
    \ once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Motif-based 2-opt flip seed + SLSQP polish (crossing pairs)' (ID: 69) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6295719344443746\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write noesis/seeds_motifs.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with\
    \ fields: content\n2. `storage write noesis/notes.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: noesis/seeds_motifs.py\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/notes.md\n- Evaluation 'Motif-based 2-opt flip seed + SLSQP polish (crossing pairs)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 69.\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 47 | 1 | Graph-aware seeds: bottleneck release + boundary trade (SLSQP polish) | Noesis I | 26 | 2.6295720 |\n| 54 | 1 | Graph-aware seeds (delta=3e-3): bottleneck release + boundary trade | Noesis I | 29 | 2.6295720 |\n| 56 | 1 | Top-3 graph-aware seeds (pairs+boundary) with SLSQP polish | Noesis I | 30 | 2.6295720 |\n| 49 | 1 | Graph-aware seeds: bottleneck release + boundary trade (SLSQP polish) | Noesis I | 27 | 2.6295720 |\n| 29 | 1 | Trust-constr multi-start with analytic Jacobians (seeded from saved best) | Noesis I | 18 | 2.6295720 |\n| 21 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians (save best to storage) | Noesis I | 15 | 2.6295720 |\n| 24 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians + ring seeds | Noesis I | 16 | 2.6295720 |\n| 26 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians + hexagonal lattice seeds | Noesis I | 17 | 2.6295720 |\n| 18 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with jitter (5x5+hole seeds) | Noesis I | 14 | 2.6295720 |\n| 36 | 1 | SLP step around saved best + SLSQP\
    \ polish | Noesis I | 21 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
