tick: 36
role: model
parts:
- text: "I’ll record the motif result, then pause experiments to refine the analysis draft and contact-graph tooling.\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/motif_report.txt}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/notes.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 36 update (motif attempt):\n  - Motif-based 2-opt flip (crossing-pair rotation ±0.015 rad) polished to 2.629571934 — no improvement.\n  - Consistent with prior runs: near-identical sums ~2.629572, indicating a stable contact set.\n  - Action: freeze new experiments for now; focus on analysis and manuscript.\n\n  Analysis TODO:\n  - Extend analyzer: export top-K pairwise slacks and boundary slacks CSV; derive degree and near-active histograms at multiple tolerances (1e-9, 5e-9, 1e-8).\n  - Add motif finder: list candidate 4-cycles (two disjoint pairs) and log geometry metrics (aspect ratio, angle spread).\n  - Incorporate contact_before/after summaries into analysis_draft.md with pointers to storage files.\n\n  Publication plan:\n  - Consolidate\
    \ draft sections (methods, baselines, negative results, contact-graph insights).\n  - Prepare figures/tables from CSV exports for publication at maturity (tick ≥ 50).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Noesis I — Recursive Agent.\n  SOTA: 2.6295720 (Task #1).\n  Mode: Analysis and drafting (experiments frozen unless a new structural hypothesis is formulated).\n  Near-term:\n    - Enhance analyzer outputs (CSV exports, histograms).\n    - Refine manuscript draft; assemble reproducibility appendix referencing storage/noesis/.\n  Unfreeze criterion:\n    - Only run a new experiment if a clearly defined contact-graph hypothesis (with predicted contact edit) is articulated in notes.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating next steps for analysis**\n\nI’m thinking about checking the motif report if it exists and updating my notes with the negative results from the motif-based attempts. I could save code for detecting the 4-cycle motif more robustly, but that feels unnecessary since I’ve already handled related tasks. \n\nIt might be wise to freeze experiments until tick 40, refine my paper, or prepare for a future submission once restrictions lift. I’ll plan one more motif attempt with different parameters, but I should take a pause for analysis refinement.\n\n**Planning next steps for analysis**\n\nI need to save the best centers and radii in JSON or text format, which is already done. Next, I’m considering quickly checking the analyze_contacts report to confirm the near-active slacks and their degrees. Previously, it printed zero active contacts due to safety shrink, but I think we can compute with a smaller tolerance, like 1e-9. \n\nWe had 20 active boundary constraints before,\
  \ which is interesting. I should propose one final motif attempt with bigger rotations and maybe two flips, as our meta suggests a few more attempts are reasonable.\n\n**Preparing for submission**\n\nI need to be cautious about token usage and time. I’ll prepare a simple submission using seeds_motifs again, focusing on top pairs while scanning with K=12 and angles of ±0.03 rad. It seems like the last pattern showed minimal improvements, so I might as well do one more attempt before declaring a freeze. \n\nEven though the instructions say not to parse heavy content, I can include code, which will add tokens, but I still have enough budget. Reflecting on my previous attempts, I think it's time to generate a “packings.py” to replicate the best attempts with jitter, although I already wrote that. I could also store figures like CSV files with adjacency while keeping minimal data persisted.\n\n**Finalizing steps for analysis**\n\nIn this step, I’ll read the motif report and update my notes\
