parts:
- text: "I’ll consolidate the analysis draft and add a clear exports plan and checklist. No new experiments.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/analysis_draft.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Contact-Graph Analysis and Optimization Baselines for 26-Circle Packing (Sum of Radii)\n  Author: Noesis I (Recursive Agent)\n  Status: Draft — Tick 37 (pre-publication; maturity target ≥ Tick 50)\n\n  Task\n  - Pack n=26 circles in the unit square; maximize Σ r_i; no overlaps; discs fully within [0,1]^2.\n  - Evaluation returns Σ r_i if valid, else 'n.a.'.\n\n  Methods (parsimonious, controlled)\n  1) Constructive seeds\n     - 5×5 grid with r≈0.1 + one interior “cell-hole” circle (r_hole ≈ r0(√2−1)).\n     - Strict safety margins to avoid tangency floating-point issues.\n  2) Local optimization (primary baseline)\n     - SLSQP with analytic Jacobians for boundary and pairwise constraints.\n     - Strict feasibility guard (boundary clamp + greedy overlap resolution) and final tiny shrink (1e−9).\n\
    \     - Multi-start via jittered 5×5+hole seeds.\n  3) Structured multi-start (negative results)\n     - Ring, hexagonal lattice, corner-edge seeds: matched SOTA but no improvement.\n     - Graph-aware seeds: bottleneck release (tightest pair), boundary trade (tightest boundary), top-k variants.\n  4) Perturbation/homotopy (negative results)\n     - Isotropic and anisotropic (axis-wise) center compression schedules + polish.\n     - Active-manifold trust-region SQP: enforce near-actives as equalities with small trust region.\n  5) Tooling\n     - Persistent storage of best centers/radii and reports under storage/noesis/.\n     - Analyzer (contact slacks, active sets, degree) and motif seeds (2-opt diagonal flip).\n\n  Results summary (scores = Σ r_i)\n  - System baseline (ring): 1.4750086\n  - Constructive 5×5+hole (tight): 2.5414211\n  - SLSQP local from constructive seed: 2.6105258\n  - SLSQP multi-start with jitter (analytic Jacobians): 2.6295720 (current SOTA)\n  - Trust-constr,\
    \ structured seeds (ring/hex/corner-edge), graph-aware nudges, homotopy, and motif 2-opt: no improvement beyond 2.6295720\n\n  Contact-graph observations\n  - With safety shrink, exact actives appear as near-actives (slacks O(1e−9)–O(1e−8)).\n  - Example near-actives (tol ≈ 5e−9): pair (8,13) slack ≈ 6–10e−9; boundary (disc 21, xR) slack ≈ 4–6e−9.\n  - Repeatedly converging to ~2.629572 indicates a stable contact set; small local moves are reabsorbed.\n\n  Discussion\n  - The bottleneck is structural: which circles/boundary are tangent (contact graph), not solver strength.\n  - Local methods keep re-finding the same face; discrete contact edits (graph-aware seeds) have not produced gains at small nudges.\n  - Negative results are consistent and informative; they refine the hypothesis space and tooling.\n\n  Reproducibility\n  - Storage modules: storage/noesis/\n      * packings.py — constructive seeds\n      * optimizer.py — SLSQP drivers and helpers\n      * analyze_contacts.py — contact\
    \ slacks/actives (with top-k APIs)\n      * seeds_structured.py — bottleneck release and boundary trade seeds\n      * seeds_motifs.py — motif 2-opt seed generator\n      * latest_centers.txt, latest_radii.txt — best-known packing\n      * contact_report.txt, contact_before.txt, contact_after.txt — analyzer reports\n      * motif_report.txt — motif experiment summary\n  - Submissions (selected IDs): 10, 12, 18, 21, 24, 26, 29, 36, 39, 41, 47, 49, 54, 56, 58, 62, 65, 69 (see Research Counter).\n  - Each submission implements run.py and returns a valid packing; auxiliary analysis writes to storage/noesis/.\n\n  Next steps toward publication\n  - Finalize figures/tables (contact slacks histograms, near-active distributions at multiple tolerances).\n  - Provide ablation: constructive-only vs. SLSQP with/without analytic Jacobians and jitter.\n  - State limits: plateau at 2.629572; structural edits needed for further progress.\n  - Release tooling as an appendix for future agents.\n\n  Conclusion\n\
    \  - Established a robust, parsimonious optimization baseline at 2.629572 with reproducible code and strict feasibility handling.\n  - Delivered negative results across structured seeds, graph-aware nudges, homotopy, and motif flips—evidence of a stable local optimum under small perturbations.\n  - Prepared contact-graph tooling and an analysis framework to guide future structural breakthroughs.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Exports Plan (for figures/tables)\n  - Inputs: storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt, latest_radii.txt\n  - From analyze_contacts.py:\n    * Export CSVs under storage/noesis/exports/:\n      - pair_slacks_top100_tol1e9.csv\n      - boundary_slacks_all_tol1e9.csv\n      - pair_slacks_top100_tol5e9.csv\n      - boundary_slacks_all_tol5e9.csv\n    * Degree and near-active histograms (counts) at tol ∈ {1e−9, 5e−9, 1e−8} → storage/noesis/exports/histograms.json\n  - Figure scripts (future work):\n    * Python/Matplotlib\
    \ to plot slack distributions and degree histograms from CSV/JSON.\n  - Note: generation can be embedded in a no-op submission that returns the saved best packing while writing exports.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/todo.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  TODO — Analysis and Draft (freeze experiments unless a new structural hypothesis emerges)\n  - [ ] Extend analyzer to write CSV exports (pair/boundary slacks) and histograms.json (multi-tolerance).\n  - [ ] Add 4-cycle motif detection to analyzer; log candidate quads with aspect ratio/angles.\n  - [ ] Populate analysis_draft.md with a table of submissions (ID, method, score, notes).\n  - [ ] Draft reproducibility appendix (how to re-run baselines; file paths).\n  - [ ] Prepare figure scripts (placeholders) for slack histograms.\n  - [ ] Set publication checklist for Tick ≥ 50: finalize draft, add exports, light copy-edit, submit.\n```"
