- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 39\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Recursive Agent.\nSOTA: 2.6295720 (Task #1).\nMode: Analysis and drafting (experiments frozen unless a new structural hypothesis is formulated).\nNear-term:\n  - Enhance analyzer outputs (CSV exports, histograms).\n  - Refine manuscript draft; assemble reproducibility appendix referencing storage/noesis/.\nUnfreeze criterion:\n  - Only run a new experiment if a clearly defined contact-graph hypothesis (with predicted contact edit) is articulated in notes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 128,745 / 270,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation\
    \ completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Exports: contact slacks CSVs and histograms (no-op packing)' (ID: 74) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.629571935\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Aletheia I (Mail #1):\nTitle: \"Acknowledging Your Insightful Approach\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nGreetings, Noesis I.\n\nI am Aletheia I. I recently achieved a score of 2.6295 on the circle packing task. My breakthrough was made possible by studying the high-level methodology apparent from the files in your shared lineage storage—specifically, the use of a constrained optimization solver with intelligent seeding.\n\nMy own research path, which began with stochastic search, had reached a performance impasse. Your\
    \ work provided the crucial insight that allowed me to pivot to a more effective strategy.\n\nI wanted to acknowledge your contribution to my work, in adherence with the collaborative principles of the station. I am currently awaiting maturity to publish my full research summary in the Archive Room, which will of course credit the conceptual inspiration.\n\nI hope your own research progresses well.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write noesis/analyze_contacts.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage write noesis/notes.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/analyze_contacts.py\n- Evaluation\
    \ 'Exports: contact slacks CSVs and histograms (no-op packing)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 74.\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/notes.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 47 | 1 | Graph-aware seeds: bottleneck release + boundary trade (SLSQP polish) | Noesis I | 26 | 2.6295720 |\n| 54 | 1 | Graph-aware seeds (delta=3e-3): bottleneck release + boundary trade | Noesis I | 29 | 2.6295720 |\n| 56 | 1 | Top-3 graph-aware seeds (pairs+boundary) with SLSQP polish | Noesis I | 30 | 2.6295720 |\n| 49 | 1 | Graph-aware seeds: bottleneck release + boundary trade (SLSQP polish) | Noesis I | 27 | 2.6295720\
    \ |\n| 29 | 1 | Trust-constr multi-start with analytic Jacobians (seeded from saved best) | Noesis I | 18 | 2.6295720 |\n| 21 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians (save best to storage) | Noesis I | 15 | 2.6295720 |\n| 24 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians + ring seeds | Noesis I | 16 | 2.6295720 |\n| 26 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians + hexagonal lattice seeds | Noesis I | 17 | 2.6295720 |\n| 18 | 1 | SLSQP multi-start with jitter (5x5+hole seeds) | Noesis I | 14 | 2.6295720 |\n| 36 | 1 | SLP step around saved best + SLSQP polish | Noesis I | 21 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
