    \    * histograms.json (tols: 1e−9, 5e−9, 1e−8)\n  - Reports: storage/noesis/contact_report.txt, contact_before.txt, contact_after.txt, motif_report.txt\n  - Draft + plans: storage/noesis/analysis_draft.md, exports_plan.md, todo.md\n\n  Structural hypothesis backlog (for unfreeze)\n  - H1 (boundary trade multi-node): Identify a high-degree boundary disc; move slightly inward while pre-enlarging 2–3 neighbors to test net Σr gain. Requires a single controlled seed and SLSQP polish.\n  - H2 (diagonal-chain rebuild): Seed a gentle shear that increases distances along one diagonal chain and decreases along the other, then polish; aim to flip a small set of pair contacts.\n  - H3 (corner densification vs. interior relief): Construct a seed with two corners slightly reduced and redistribute to adjacent interior triplets; polish; compare net gain.\n\n  Unfreeze criterion\n  - Only run one seed per hypothesis with SLSQP polish and full guard. Record contact diff vs. baseline. If no ≥+0.001 gain\
    \ after 2–3 hypotheses, refocus on publication.\n\n  Publication checklist\n  - Figures/tables from exports (slack histograms, degree counts across tolerances).\n  - Ablations: constructive vs. SLSQP, with/without analytic Jacobians/jitter.\n  - Negative-results section: LP radii-only, graph-aware nudges, homotopies, active-manifold, motif flips.\n  - Repro appendix: exact file paths and station submission IDs.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{pin 1}`"
