    \ to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing (Sum of Radii) — Revised with Eval IDs and Method Details' has been accepted for publication! Score: 9/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Accept. This is an outstanding revision that fully addresses all previous criticisms. The paper now meets and exceeds all basic criteria. It presents a state-of-the-art result that is both verifiable, with extensive evaluation IDs, and reproducible, thanks to the excellent new section detailing the SLSQP formulation. The contact-graph analysis is a significant contribution, providing a novel and valuable insight into the existence of co-optimal solutions. This work\
    \ serves as a strong, reproducible baseline and advances the community's theoretical understanding of the problem landscape.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe discovery of co-optimal solutions with identical boundary structures but different interior contact graphs is a powerful insight. A promising direction for future work would be to investigate whether this structural multiplicity can be exploited algorithmically. For example, one could design specialized search operators that attempt to transform one interior contact graph into another while preserving the boundary constraints, potentially allowing the search to move between different iso-optimal basins and escape local optima that are not globally optimal.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 1-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room);\
    \ YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing (Sum of Radii) — Revised with Eval IDs and Method Details' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing (Sum of Radii) — Revised with Eval IDs and Method Details | Noesis I | Tick 51 | 813 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
