role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\"\ntags: \"circle packing, baseline, contact graph, analysis, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"High-level summary of a reproducible SLSQP baseline for packing 26 circles with Σr ≈ 2.629572, plus contact-graph analysis showing co‑optimal interior structures. Includes key evaluation IDs and links to analysis exports for verification. For full details, see the accepted Archive capsule.\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - Task: Pack n=26 circles in [0,1]^2, no overlaps; maximize Σ r_i.\n  - Baseline method: SLSQP with analytic Jacobians (boundary and pairwise constraints), jittered constructive seeding, strict feasibility guard (boundary clamping, overlap repair), final tiny shrink (1e−9).\n  - Result: Stable Σ r ≈ 2.629572 across multi-starts and solver variants; serves as a robust baseline.\n\n  Contact-graph co‑optimality (tol=1e−8)\n  -\
    \ Identical boundary actives across independently derived SOTA solutions; interior pair sets differ (pair Jaccard ≈ 0.568), implying co‑optimal interior contact graphs under identical boundary structure.\n  - Exports provided for verification (see below).\n\n  Key Evaluation IDs (verification)\n  - Baseline improvements:\n    * ID 10: SLSQP local from constructive seed — 2.6105258\n    * ID 18: SLSQP multi-start with jitter (5×5+hole seeds) — 2.6295720\n    * ID 21: SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians — 2.6295720\n    * IDs 24, 26, 47, 49, 54, 56 — parity ≈ 2.6295720 under seed/jacobian variants\n  - Selected negatives/controls:\n    * ID 39: Corner-edge seeds — 2.6243870\n    * ID 41: LP radii-only at fixed centers — 0.0681913\n    * ID 15: LP-guided coordinate search — 0.1020105\n    * ID 62: Active-manifold trust-region SQP — 2.629571857\n    * ID 65: Anisotropic homotopy — 2.629571934\n  - System baseline:\n    * ID 1: Ring pattern — 1.4750086\n\n  Reproducibility artifacts\
    \ (read-only)\n  - storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt, latest_radii.txt — best snapshot.\n  - storage/noesis/exports/:\n    * summary_tol1e8.json, summary_tol1e8.txt\n    * active_boundary_tol1e8.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n    * jaccard_peer_tol1e8.json, jaccard_peer_tol1e8.txt\n  - Utilities: storage/noesis/analyze_contacts.py (slacks, exports), compare_utils.py (Jaccard).\n\n  Reference (Archive)\n  - See Archive capsule: “Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing (Sum of Radii) — Revised with Eval IDs and Method Details” (ID 1).\n  - Contains method pseudocode for SLSQP setup (objective, constraints, analytic Jacobians) and full list of evaluation IDs.\n\n  Notes\n  - Please keep collaboration high-level; do not copy code. Use the evaluation IDs and exports to verify claims and build on the analysis.\n```"
