role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/operators.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Boundary‑Preserving Interior‑Graph Operators (BPIGO) — prototypes\n  Goal: propose small, structured seeds that aim to change interior contacts\n  while preserving boundary actives (within tolerance), followed by SLSQP polish.\n  \"\"\"\n  import numpy as np\n\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n\n  # ---------- Feasibility helpers ----------\n  def boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n      x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN)\n\n  def make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      r = np.minimum(radii, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n      r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n      for _ in range(max_iter):\n          diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n          dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n     \
    \     iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n          if np.all(m >= eps):\n              break\n          k = int(np.argmin(m))\n          i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n          need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n          di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN)\n          dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n          if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n              r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN)\n          else:\n              r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n          r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n      return centers, r\n\n  # ---------- Geometry utils ----------\n  def rotate_points_around_centroid(centers, idxs, theta):\n      pts = centers[idxs]\n      centroid = np.mean(pts, axis=0)\n      cos_t = np.cos(theta); sin_t = np.sin(theta)\n      R = np.array([[cos_t, -sin_t], [sin_t, cos_t]], dtype=float)\n      for idx in idxs:\n          v = centers[idx] - centroid\n          centers[idx] = centroid + R @ v\n      return centers\n\n  def\
    \ small_shear(centers, idxs, axis='x', amount=1e-2):\n      \"\"\"Apply a tiny shear to listed indices.\"\"\"\n      c = centers.copy()\n      idxs = np.array(idxs, dtype=int)\n      if axis == 'x':\n          c[idxs, 0] = np.clip(c[idxs, 0] + amount * (c[idxs, 1] - 0.5), 0.0, 1.0)\n      else:\n          c[idxs, 1] = np.clip(c[idxs, 1] + amount * (c[idxs, 0] - 0.5), 0.0, 1.0)\n      return c\n\n  # ---------- BPIGO operators (seed generators only; polishing is external) ----------\n  def quad_diagonal_flip_seed(centers, radii, quad_idxs, theta=1.5e-2):\n      \"\"\"\n      Quad Diagonal Flip (QDF) seed:\n      - quad_idxs: 4 indices (i,j,k,l) presumed to form a 4-cycle.\n      - Apply small rotation ±theta around quad centroid to encourage diagonal flip.\n      Returns feasible centers/radii (no solver step here).\n      \"\"\"\n      c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n      c = rotate_points_around_centroid(c, quad_idxs, theta)\n      c = np.clip(c, 0.0, 1.0)\n      return make_feasible(c,\
    \ r)\n\n  def chain_shear_seed(centers, radii, chain_idxs, axis='x', amount=1e-2):\n      \"\"\"\n      Chain Shear (CS) seed:\n      - chain_idxs: list of 4–6 interior disc indices.\n      - Apply tiny anisotropic shear along one axis to encourage contact swaps within chain.\n      \"\"\"\n      c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n      c = small_shear(c, chain_idxs, axis=axis, amount=amount)\n      return make_feasible(c, r)\n\n  def corner_star_seed(centers, radii, corner_idx, neighbor_triplet, inward=1.0e-3, expand=1.0e-3):\n      \"\"\"\n      Corner‑Star Redistribution (CSR) seed:\n      - Move corner disc slightly inward; expand neighbor triplet radii a tiny bit.\n      - Aim: trade a bit of boundary slack to stimulate new interior contact among neighbors.\n      \"\"\"\n      c = centers.copy(); r = radii.copy()\n      v = np.array([0.5, 0.5]) - c[corner_idx]\n      nv = v / (np.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-15)\n      c[corner_idx] = np.clip(c[corner_idx] + inward * nv, 0.0, 1.0)\n\
    \      for idx in neighbor_triplet:\n          r[idx] *= (1.0 + expand)\n      return make_feasible(c, r)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/todo.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  TODO — Operators Prototyping (post-publication)\n  - [x] Add operators.py with seed generators for QDF, Chain Shear, Corner‑Star.\n  - [ ] Integrate operators with equality‑constrained SLSQP step preserving boundary actives.\n  - [ ] Define logging: ΔΣr, ΔJaccard(pairs), boundary Jaccard, runtime; cap ≤ 6 moves/run.\n  - [ ] Prepare small controlled benchmark (3–5 motifs) with eval IDs for a short follow‑up note.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: operators.py (BPIGO seed generators: Quad Diagonal Flip, Chain Shear, Corner‑Star) is now available under storage/noesis/operators.py.\n  These produce small boundary‑preserving seeds; polish externally with SLSQP (analytic Jacobians). Logs should include ΔΣr, ΔJaccard(pairs), boundary Jaccard,\
    \ runtime.\n  If other lineages export active sets at tol=1e−8 (active_{boundary,pairs}_tol1e8.csv), we can compute cross‑lineage Jaccard maps to chart the iso‑optimal interior space.\n```"
