tick: 58
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BPIGO: single QDF (fallback Chain Shear) + boundary‑preserving polish (controlled)\"\ntags: \"bpigo, structural, slsqp, equality-constraints, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Single controlled BPIGO experiment: attempt a Quad Diagonal Flip (QDF) detected from two crossing near‑tangent pairs; fallback to Chain Shear on a short interior chain if no crossing found. Polish with equality‑constrained SLSQP that preserves boundary actives (tol=1e‑8). Log ΔΣr and Jaccard(pair) change; return the better of seed vs. baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np, sys\n\n  # Use read-only lineage modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  try:\n      import analyze_contacts as AC\n  except Exception:\n      AC = None\n  try:\n      import seeds_motifs as SM\n  except Exception:\n      SM = None\n  try:\n      import operators as OP\n  except Exception:\n      OP = None\n  try:\n      import operators_integration as OI\n  except Exception:\n\
    \      OI = None\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  TOL = 1e-8\n\n  def load_saved_best():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n          c = np.array(c, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n          r = np.array(r, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None\n\n  def grid_plus_hole_seed(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(np.array([0.2,0.2]) - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n      r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n      radii = [float(r0)] * 25 + [float(r_hole)]\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n  def active_pairs_set(c, r, tol=TOL):\n      if AC is None:\n          return None\n      _, p = AC.active_sets(c, r, tol=tol)\n      s = set()\n      for (i, j, _) in p:\n          if i > j: i, j = j, i\n\
    \          s.add((i, j))\n      return s\n\n  def jaccard(a, b):\n      if a is None or b is None:\n          return None, None, None\n      inter = a & b\n      uni = a | b\n      if len(uni) == 0:\n          return 1.0, 0, 0\n      return len(inter)/len(uni), len(inter), len(uni)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Baseline packing (saved best or constructive fallback)\n      c0, r0 = load_saved_best()\n      if c0 is None:\n          c0, r0 = grid_plus_hole_seed()\n      s0 = float(np.sum(r0))\n\n      # Default: return baseline if modules unavailable\n      if AC is None or OP is None or OI is None:\n          return c0, r0\n\n      # Attempt to detect crossing pairs for a QDF\n      op_name = None\n      c_seed, r_seed = c0.copy(), r0.copy()\n      try:\n          top_pairs, _ = AC.top_k_bottlenecks(c0, r0, k_pair=12, k_boundary=0)\n      except Exception:\n          top_pairs = []\n\n      applied_qdf = False\n      if SM is not None and top_pairs:\n          cp = SM.find_crossing_pairs(c0,\
    \ top_pairs)\n          if cp is not None:\n              (i, j), (k, l) = cp\n              quad = tuple({i, j, k, l})\n              try:\n                  c_seed, r_seed = OP.quad_diagonal_flip_seed(c0, r0, quad_idxs=quad, theta=1.5e-2)\n                  op_name = 'QDF'\n                  applied_qdf = True\n              except Exception:\n                  applied_qdf = False\n\n      # Fallback: Chain Shear on a short interior chain near x≈0.5\n      if not applied_qdf:\n          try:\n              b_act, _ = AC.active_sets(c0, r0, tol=TOL)\n              boundary_idx = set(i for (i, kind, _) in b_act)\n              candidates = [(abs(c0[i,0] - 0.5), i) for i in range(N) if i not in boundary_idx]\n              candidates.sort()\n              chain = [idx for (_, idx) in candidates[:5]] if len(candidates) >= 5 else [i for i in range(5)]\n              c_seed, r_seed = OP.chain_shear_seed(c0, r0, chain_idxs=chain, axis='x', amount=1.0e-2)\n              op_name = 'ChainShear'\n\
    \          except Exception:\n              # If even fallback fails, return baseline\n              return c0, r0\n\n      # Equality‑constrained polish that preserves boundary actives (trust region around seed)\n      try:\n          c_opt, r_opt = OI.polish_preserving_boundary(c_seed, r_seed, tol_eq=TOL, step_c=1e-3, step_r=1e-3, maxiter=500)\n      except Exception:\n          c_opt, r_opt = c_seed, r_seed\n\n      s1 = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n\n      # Compute pair Jaccard change at tol=1e‑8\n      pairs0 = active_pairs_set(c0, r0, tol=TOL)\n      pairs1 = active_pairs_set(c_opt, r_opt, tol=TOL)\n      J, inter, uni = jaccard(pairs0, pairs1)\n\n      # Log experiment\n      try:\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/exports', exist_ok=True)\n          exp_id = int(np.random.randint(1e9))\n          log = {\n              'op': op_name,\n              'sum_radii_before': s0,\n              'sum_radii_after': s1,\n              'delta_sum_radii': s1 - s0,\n              'pair_jaccard_tol1e8':\
    \ J,\n              'pair_intersection': inter,\n              'pair_union': uni,\n              'seed_valid': True\n          }\n          with open(f'storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_exp_{exp_id}.json', 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(log, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      # Return the better packing by Σr\n      if s1 >= s0:\n          return np.array(c_opt, dtype=float), np.array(r_opt, dtype=float)\n      else:\n          return np.array(c0, dtype=float), np.array(r0, dtype=float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/notes.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 58 — Controlled BPIGO experiment submitted:\n  - Operator: QDF from crossing pairs (fallback Chain Shear if none).\n  - Polish: equality‑constrained SLSQP preserving boundary actives at tol=1e−8 with small trust region.\n  - Logs: storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_exp_*.json {ΔΣr, Jaccard(pairs), op}.\n  - Return policy: better of baseline vs. polished seed by Σr.\n  - This addresses the inactivity\
    \ notice with a single, hypothesis‑driven experiment.\n```"
