tick: 60
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{storage read noesis/exports/bpigo_exp_837040580.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/notes.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 60 — BPIGO #1 metrics recorded (see bpigo_exp_837040580.json)\n  - Logged operator, ΔΣr, and pair‑Jaccard change at tol=1e−8.\n  - Proceeding with one complementary, hyperparameter‑tuned BPIGO attempt (single move), then pausing.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BPIGO‑2: complementary operator with tuned trust region (single move, controlled)\"\ntags: \"bpigo, structural, slsqp, equality-constraints, analysis, single-move\"\nabstract: \"Single complementary BPIGO attempt with mild hyperparameter tuning. If the prior BPIGO used QDF, we try Chain Shear along y on an interior chain; otherwise we try QDF with a slightly larger rotation (θ≈0.02). We polish with boundary‑preserving equality‑SLSQP using a slightly larger trust region (step≈2e‑3). We log ΔΣr and pair‑Jaccard changes and return the better of seed vs\
    \ baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np, sys, glob\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  try:\n      import analyze_contacts as AC\n  except Exception:\n      AC = None\n  try:\n      import seeds_motifs as SM\n  except Exception:\n      SM = None\n  try:\n      import operators as OP\n  except Exception:\n      OP = None\n  try:\n      import operators_integration as OI\n  except Exception:\n      OI = None\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n\n  def load_saved_best():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n          return np.array(c, float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r, float).reshape(N,)\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None\n\n  def grid_plus_hole_seed(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(np.array([0.2,0.2]) - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n     \
    \ r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array([r0]*25 + [r_hole], float)\n\n  def last_bpigo_op():\n      try:\n          files = glob.glob('storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_exp_*.json')\n          if not files: return None\n          files.sort(key=lambda p: os.path.getmtime(p))\n          with open(files[-1], 'r') as f:\n              data = json.load(f)\n          return data.get('op', None)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def active_pairs_set(c, r, tol=TOL):\n      if AC is None: return None\n      _, pairs = AC.active_sets(c, r, tol=tol)\n      s = set()\n      for (i, j, _) in pairs:\n          if i > j: i, j = j, i\n          s.add((i, j))\n      return s\n\n  def jaccard(a, b):\n      if a is None or b is None: return None, None, None\n      inter = a & b\n      uni = a | b\n      if len(uni) == 0: return 1.0, 0, 0\n      return len(inter)/len(uni), len(inter), len(uni)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c0, r0 = load_saved_best()\n\
    \      if c0 is None:\n          c0, r0 = grid_plus_hole_seed()\n      s0 = float(np.sum(r0))\n\n      # Default return if modules unavailable\n      if AC is None or OP is None or OI is None:\n          return c0, r0\n\n      prev = last_bpigo_op()\n\n      # Choose complementary operator\n      op_name = None\n      c_seed, r_seed = c0.copy(), r0.copy()\n\n      if prev == 'QDF':\n          # Complement with Chain Shear along y on interior chain\n          try:\n              b_act, _ = AC.active_sets(c0, r0, tol=TOL)\n              boundary_idx = set(i for (i, kind, _) in b_act)\n              # pick ~5 interior discs closest to y=0.5\n              candidates = [(abs(c0[i,1] - 0.5), i) for i in range(N) if i not in boundary_idx]\n              candidates.sort()\n              chain = [idx for (_, idx) in candidates[:5]] if len(candidates) >= 5 else [i for i in range(5)]\n              c_seed, r_seed = OP.chain_shear_seed(c0, r0, chain_idxs=chain, axis='y', amount=1.5e-2)\n      \
    \        op_name = 'ChainShearY'\n          except Exception:\n              return c0, r0\n      else:\n          # Try QDF with slightly larger rotation θ≈0.02 if crossing pairs are available\n          if SM is None:\n              return c0, r0\n          try:\n              top_pairs, _ = AC.top_k_bottlenecks(c0, r0, k_pair=14, k_boundary=0)\n              cp = SM.find_crossing_pairs(c0, top_pairs) if top_pairs else None\n              if cp is None:\n                  return c0, r0\n              (i, j), (k, l) = cp\n              quad = tuple({i, j, k, l})\n              c_seed, r_seed = OP.quad_diagonal_flip_seed(c0, r0, quad_idxs=quad, theta=2.0e-2)\n              op_name = 'QDF_plus'\n          except Exception:\n              return c0, r0\n\n      # Equality‑constrained polish with slightly larger trust region\n      try:\n          c_opt, r_opt = OI.polish_preserving_boundary(c_seed, r_seed, tol_eq=TOL, step_c=2e-3, step_r=2e-3, maxiter=600)\n      except Exception:\n  \
    \        c_opt, r_opt = c_seed, r_seed\n\n      s1 = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n      pairs0 = active_pairs_set(c0, r0, tol=TOL)\n      pairs1 = active_pairs_set(c_opt, r_opt, tol=TOL)\n      J, inter, uni = jaccard(pairs0, pairs1)\n\n      # Log\n      try:\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/exports', exist_ok=True)\n          exp_id = int(np.random.randint(1e9))\n          log = {\n              'op': op_name,\n              'sum_radii_before': s0,\n              'sum_radii_after': s1,\n              'delta_sum_radii': s1 - s0,\n              'pair_jaccard_tol1e8': J,\n              'pair_intersection': inter,\n              'pair_union': uni,\n              'seed_valid': True\n          }\n          with open(f'storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_exp2_{exp_id}.json', 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(log, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      return (c_opt if s1 >= s0 else c0).astype(float), (r_opt if s1 >= s0 else r0).astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write noesis/notes.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 60 — BPIGO #2 submitted (single complementary operator with tuned hyperparameters)\n  - If BPIGO #1 used QDF, this run uses Chain Shear along y (amount≈1.5e−2); else QDF with θ≈0.02.\n  - Polish: equality‑SLSQP with boundary equalities and step≈2e−3.\n  - Logs: storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_exp2_*.json {ΔΣr, Jaccard(pairs), op}.\n  - After this, pause operators unless a clear positive signal appears; otherwise, compile a short follow‑up note with two controlled negatives.\n```"
