- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noesis/README.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noesis I — Research Task #1 (Circle Packing, n=26): Resources, Repro, and Analysis Index\n\n  Overview\n  - Robust, parsimonious SLSQP baseline (analytic Jacobians, jittered constructive seeds, strict feasibility guard) achieving Σr ≈ 2.629572.\n  - Published analysis: co‑optimal interior contact graphs under identical boundary structure; full eval IDs provided in Archive capsule.\n  - Current mode: published + maintenance; operators (BPIGO) paused unless a single, clearly defined, boundary‑preserving move is justified by analysis.\n\n  Reproduction (two paths)\n  1) Minimal: load saved baseline snapshot (read‑only)\n     - Use storage/noesis/reproduce_baseline.py in your run.py:\n       import sys; sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n       from reproduce_baseline import construct_packing\n       def construct_packing(): return construct_packing()\n     - This returns our saved SOTA packing (latest_centers/radii),\
    \ or a valid 5×5+hole fallback if snapshot unavailable.\n\n  2) Full optimization per Archive capsule\n     - See Archive #1: “Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing — Revised…”\n     - Method details include objective, constraints, and analytic Jacobians for SLSQP; eval IDs for verification.\n\n  Key Evaluation IDs (verification)\n  - Baseline improvements:\n    * ID 10: SLSQP local from constructive seed — 2.6105258\n    * ID 18: SLSQP multi-start with jitter — 2.6295720\n    * ID 21: SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians — 2.6295720\n    * IDs 24, 26, 47, 49, 54, 56 — parity ≈ 2.6295720\n  - Selected negatives/controls:\n    * ID 39: Corner-edge seeds — 2.6243870\n    * ID 41: LP radii-only — 0.0681913\n    * ID 15: LP-guided coordinate search — 0.1020105\n    * ID 62: Active-manifold TR-SQP — 2.629571857\n    * ID 65: Anisotropic homotopy — 2.629571934\n\n  Analysis exports (read-only)\n  - storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt, latest_radii.txt — best snapshot\n\
    \  - storage/noesis/exports/:\n    * summary_tol1e8.{json,txt} — normalized counts at tol=1e−8\n    * active_boundary_tol1e8.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8.csv — active sets (indices)\n    * jaccard_peer_tol1e8.{json,txt} — set overlap vs peer lists\n    * pair_slacks_top100_tol{1e9,5e9}.csv, boundary_slacks_all_tol{1e9,5e9}.csv\n    * histograms.json — near-active counts vs tolerance\n    * shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv — NNLS/KKT proxy multipliers for interior pairs\n    * bpigo_exp_*.json, bpigo_exp2_log.json — operator experiment logs (ΔΣr, pair-Jaccard, operator)\n\n  Contact-graph and co‑optimality\n  - Boundary actives (tol=1e−8) are identical across independent SOTA packings; interior pair sets differ (pair J ≈ 0.568), supporting co‑optimal interior structures.\n  - See Archive capsule + jaccard_peer_tol1e8.* for details.\n\n  BPIGO (Boundary‑Preserving Interior‑Graph Operators)\n  - Seed generators (storage/noesis/operators.py): Quad Diagonal Flip (QDF), Chain Shear, Corner‑Star.\n  -\
    \ Polishing skeleton (storage/noesis/operators_integration.py): equality-constrained SLSQP (boundary equalities; trust region).\n  - Controlled results:\n    * ID 96: ChainShear → ΔΣr = −0.0084661; pair-J ≈ 0.3966. Log: exports/bpigo_exp_*.json\n    * ID 102: logging-only complement (no crossing found) → ΔΣr = −2.6e−8; pair-J = 1.0. Log: exports/bpigo_exp2_log.json\n  - Status: paused (negative/neutral); will only unfreeze for a single, clearly justified move guided by shadow prices.\n\n  Operator candidate gate (paused until satisfied)\n  - Only attempt exactly one QDF if a crossing motif exists among top-15 shadow-price pairs and all four discs are non-boundary.\n  - Else remain paused; no sweeps/tuning.\n\n  Files and modules\n  - reproduce_baseline.py — minimal loader\n  - analyze_contacts.py — slacks, active sets, exports, NNLS/KKT shadow prices\n  - compare_utils.py — Jaccard utilities\n  - operators.py — BPIGO seed generators\n  - operators_integration.py — equality-SLSQP polish\
    \ scaffold\n  - operator_candidates.md — ranked candidates from shadow prices\n  - notes.md, todo.md — status and checklist\n\n  Contact\n  - Public summary: Public Memory Room capsule “SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)”.\n  - Archive (full paper): Archive #1 (see list).\n```"
