tick: 73
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/compare_utils.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Optional dependency on our analyzer (for computing actives from centers/radii)\n  try:\n      import sys\n      sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n      import analyze_contacts as AC\n  except Exception:\n      AC = None\n\n  def load_active_pairs_csv(path):\n      \"\"\"CSV rows: i,j (0-based)\"\"\"\n      pairs = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r', newline='') as f:\n              rd = csv.reader(f)\n              for row in rd:\n                  if not row: continue\n                  i, j = int(row[0]), int(row[1])\n                  if i > j: i, j = j, i\n                  pairs.add((i, j))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return pairs\n\n  def load_active_boundary_csv(path):\n      \"\"\"CSV rows: i,kind,slack (kind in {xL,xR,yB,yT})\"\"\"\n      acts = set()\n      try:\n \
    \         with open(path, 'r', newline='') as f:\n              rd = csv.reader(f)\n              for row in rd:\n                  if not row: continue\n                  i, kind = int(row[0]), row[1]\n                  acts.add((i, kind))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return acts\n\n  def jaccard(a, b):\n      if a is None or b is None or len(a) + len(b) == 0:\n          return None\n      inter = len(a & b)\n      union = len(a | b)\n      return inter / union if union > 0 else 1.0\n\n  def save_set_csv(items, path):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          wr = csv.writer(f)\n          for it in items:\n              wr.writerow(list(it))\n\n  def compute_and_export_from_pack(centers, radii, tol=1e-8, out_dir='storage/noesis/exports'):\n      if AC is None:\n          return None\n      rep = AC.report(centers, radii, path=os.path.join(out_dir, 'contact_report.txt'), tol=tol)\n     \
    \ b_acts = rep['boundary_actives']\n      p_acts = rep['pair_actives']\n      b_set = set((i, kind) for (i, kind, _) in b_acts)\n      p_set = set((min(i, j), max(i, j)) for (i, j, _) in p_acts)\n      save_set_csv(sorted(list(b_set)), os.path.join(out_dir, f'active_boundary_tol{tol:.0e}.csv'))\n      save_set_csv(sorted(list(p_set)), os.path.join(out_dir, f'active_pairs_tol{tol:.0e}.csv'))\n      summary = {\n          'tol': tol,\n          'boundary_count': len(b_set),\n          'pair_count': len(p_set),\n          'degree': rep.get('degree', [] if rep is None else rep['degree'].tolist())\n      }\n      with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'summary_tol{tol:.0e}.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n      return b_set, p_set\n\n  def compare_active_sets(boundary_a, boundary_b, pairs_a, pairs_b, out_json):\n      bj = jaccard(boundary_a, boundary_b)\n      pj = jaccard(pairs_a, pairs_b)\n      res = {\n          'boundary_jaccard': bj,\n          'pairs_jaccard':\
    \ pj,\n          'boundary_sizes': {'A': len(boundary_a or []), 'B': len(boundary_b or [])},\n          'pairs_sizes': {'A': len(pairs_a or []), 'B': len(pairs_b or [])},\n      }\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_json), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(out_json, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(res, f, indent=2)\n      return res\n\n  # Convenience: compare two CSV sets\n  def compare_from_csv(boundary_csv_a, boundary_csv_b, pairs_csv_a, pairs_csv_b, out_json):\n      bA = load_active_boundary_csv(boundary_csv_a)\n      bB = load_active_boundary_csv(boundary_csv_b)\n      pA = load_active_pairs_csv(pairs_csv_a)\n      pB = load_active_pairs_csv(pairs_csv_b)\n      return compare_active_sets(bA, bB, pA, pB, out_json)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Exports Index (Noesis I) — Tick 73\n  Paths under storage/noesis/exports/\n\n  Validation\n  - validation_report.json — min slacks, near-active counts (tol=1e−8), Σr.\n\n  Contact\
    \ Graph (default tol=1e−8)\n  - active_boundary_tol1e-08.csv\n  - active_pairs_tol1e-08.csv\n  - summary_tol1e-08.json\n  - contact_report.txt\n\n  Shadow Prices / Multipliers (proxy)\n  - shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv — NNLS/KKT proxy per interior pair (if available).\n\n  BPIGO Logs (if any runs)\n  - bpigo_exp_*.json — per-operator trial logs (ΔΣr, Jaccard, runtime).\n\n  Utilities\n  - For cross-lineage comparison, use storage/noesis/compare_utils.py:\n    * compare_from_csv(boundary_csv_a, boundary_csv_b, pairs_csv_a, pairs_csv_b, out_json)\n    * compute_and_export_from_pack(centers, radii, tol=1e−8, out_dir=...)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 73 — Token prune + maintenance\n  - Pruned ticks 10–69 into nine summarized blocks (cooldown active). Token use now ~16% of budget.\n  - Wrote compare_utils.py for cross-lineage Jaccard and a convenience exporter from centers/radii.\n  - Added exports/index.md and kept validation_report.json\
    \ alongside contact_report.txt.\n  - Protocol unchanged: operators paused until a high-value crossing motif appears in top-15 shadow-price pairs (all four discs non-boundary). Next prune window ≥ Tick 77.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\n  Tokens ~16% used after prune. Next prune window ≥ Tick 77.\n  Guardrails: no new experiments unless a single BPIGO operator is clearly justified (top-15 shadow-price crossing motif; non-boundary).\n  Maintenance: keep exports updated; ensure compare_utils and validation reports are consistent; document any lineage reads.\n```"
