    \    \"union_counts\": {\"boundary\": 20, \"pairs\": 66}\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross-lineage Jaccard summary (tol=1e-8) — Tick 90\n  Paths: storage/noesis/exports/\n\n  Aletheia\n  - Boundary Jaccard: 1.000 (|∩|=20, |∪|=20)\n  - Pairs Jaccard: ~0.5676 (|∩|=42, |∪|=74)\n  - Details: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_aletheia_tol1e8.json\n\n  Inquire\n  - Boundary Jaccard: 1.000 (|∩|=20, |∪|=20)\n  - Pairs Jaccard: ~0.5676 (|∩|=42, |∪|=74)\n  - Details: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json\n\n  Scientia\n  - Boundary Jaccard: 1.000 (|∩|=20, |∪|=20)\n  - Pairs Jaccard: ~0.7576 (|∩|=50, |∪|=66)\n  - Details: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_scientia_tol1e8.json\n\n  Notes\n  - Compliance: no peer reads inside evaluation code. All cross-lineage parsing is manual/read-only.\n  - Our exports: storage/noesis/exports/{active_boundary,active_pairs}_tol1e8.csv; summary_tol1e8.json.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Self-stability across tolerances (1e-9→1e-8): active-set persistence\"\ntags: \"analysis, tolerance, stability, contact-graph\"\nabstract: \"Computes Noesis’s own active boundary/pair sets at multiple tolerances (1e-9, 3e-9, 5e-9, 1e-8), reports sizes, pairwise Jaccards, and set differences. Saves JSON to storage/noesis/exports/self_stability_tolgrid.json. Returns the saved SOTA packing unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n  TOLS = [1e-9, 3e-9, 5e-9, 1e-8]\n\n  def _load_saved_best():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n          return np.array(c, float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r, float).reshape(N,)\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None\n\n  def _grid_plus_hole_seed(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n      centers = [[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords]  # 25\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(np.array([0.2,0.2])\
    \ - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n      r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array([r0]*25 + [r_hole], float)\n\n  def _boundary_slacks(c, r):\n      x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n      return x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r\n\n  def _pair_slacks(c, r):\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      return dist - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n\n  def _active_sets(c, r, tol):\n      s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT = _boundary_slacks(c, r)\n      sp = _pair_slacks(c, r)\n      b = set()\n      for i in range(N):\n          if s_xL[i] <= tol: b.add((int(i), 'xL'))\n          if s_xR[i] <= tol: b.add((int(i), 'xR'))\n          if s_yB[i] <= tol: b.add((int(i), 'yB'))\n          if s_yT[i] <= tol: b.add((int(i), 'yT'))\n      p = set()\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              if sp[i, j] <= tol:\n                  p.add((int(i), int(j)))\n      return b, p\n\n  def _jacc(a, b):\n      if not a\
    \ and not b: return 1.0\n      inter = len(a & b); uni = len(a | b)\n      return inter / uni if uni > 0 else 1.0\n\n  def _serialize_pairs(s):\n      return sorted([[i, j] for (i, j) in s], key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1]))\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c, r = _load_saved_best()\n      if c is None:\n          c, r = _grid_plus_hole_seed()\n\n      # Compute active sets for the tolerance grid\n      results = {}\n      sets_b = {}\n      sets_p = {}\n      for t in TOLS:\n          b, p = _active_sets(c, r, t)\n          sets_b[t] = b\n          sets_p[t] = p\n          results[str(t)] = {\n              'boundary_size': len(b),\n              'pairs_size': len(p)\n          }\n\n      # Pairwise Jaccards and diffs between consecutive tolerances and extremes\n      comparisons = {'boundary': {}, 'pairs': {}}\n      for i in range(len(TOLS)-1):\n          t1, t2 = TOLS[i], TOLS[i+1]\n          jb = _jacc(sets_b[t1], sets_b[t2])\n          jp = _jacc(sets_p[t1], sets_p[t2])\n       \
    \   comparisons['boundary'][f'{t1}->{t2}'] = {'jaccard': jb, 'added': len(sets_b[t2]-sets_b[t1]), 'removed': len(sets_b[t1]-sets_b[t2])}\n          comparisons['pairs'][f'{t1}->{t2}'] = {'jaccard': jp, 'added': len(sets_p[t2]-sets_p[t1]), 'removed': len(sets_p[t1]-sets_p[t2])}\n      # Extremes\n      t_lo, t_hi = TOLS[0], TOLS[-1]\n      comparisons['boundary'][f'{t_lo}<->{t_hi}'] = {'jaccard': _jacc(sets_b[t_lo], sets_b[t_hi])}\n      comparisons['pairs'][f'{t_lo}<->{t_hi}'] = {'jaccard': _jacc(sets_p[t_lo], sets_p[t_hi])}\n\n      out = {\n          'tolerances': TOLS,\n          'sizes': results,\n          'comparisons': comparisons\n      }\n      try:\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/exports', exist_ok=True)\n          with open('storage/noesis/exports/self_stability_tolgrid.json', 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\
    `/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 90 update:\n  - Posted cross-lineage Jaccards @ tol=1e−8: Noesis↔Inquire J≈0.5676; Noesis↔Scientia J≈0.7576; boundary J=1.0 for all. See storage/noesis/exports/index.md and JSON files.\n  - Submitted a self-stability analysis experiment (tolerance grid 1e−9→1e−8) that writes storage/noesis/exports/self_stability_tolgrid.json; no optimization run performed.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 90 — Addressed inactivity with meaningful analysis\n  - Wrote Jaccard JSONs for Inquire and Scientia (pairs J: ≈0.5676 and ≈0.7576; boundary J=1.0). Updated index.md.\n  - Submitted “Self-stability across tolerances (1e−9→1e−8)” to quantify active-set persistence (sizes, Jaccards, adds/removes across tol grid). Returns SOTA pack unchanged.\n  - Remain frozen for optimization; only run a BPIGO operator if the pre-defined crossing-motif gate triggers.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating data for BPIGO operators**\n\nI need to check if we have the necessary data, as we didn't compute the top pairs earlier. I can test one BPIGO operator using non-peer data; previously, it showed a negative delta of -0.0084. Now, I can use \"Boundary-preserving equality-constrained SLSQP\" on a specific 4-cycle motif from my active pairs. This requires reading from storage to generate a QDF seed and run SLSQP as a meaningful experiment, but it has to meet certain criteria. I'll implement code to automate this check.\n\n**Checking Jaccard counts**\n\nI promised not to run tests without justification, but a programmatic check meets that requirement. I also need to compute Jaccards for Inquire and Scientia while updating exports, which I can do using storage read commands outside of the evaluation code. We have the CSV data from the last output for Inquire and Scientia, so I’ll compare Jaccard counts now. It looks like Inquire’s pair list is very similar to ours,\
