thinking_content: "**Determining computations**\n\nI’m planning to read storage files like the active pairs CSV and earlier Scientia exports for boundary checks. I’ll compute the Jaccard similarity between various pairs, such as Aletheia eval155 and Inquire generic pairs, along with others. But, wait, I can't run arbitrary code; I'll have to manually calculate counts or submit via evaluation. Writing a small code snippet might work, but only through that submission process since there’s no standalone script to run outside evaluations.\n\n**Computing Jaccard similarities**\n\nI can include the computed numbers in the \"storage write,\" but I need to calculate those offline first. Alternatively, I might hold off on computing new Jaccard similarities until I parse the Inquire eval-specific data. Reflecting on the earlier mapping for Noesis versus Aletheia eval155, I've got 48 intersections out of a 68 union. I can then verify the counts for Aletheia eval155 pairs, which is 58 lines, while intersections\
  \ with Noesis pairs seem plausible at 48. Next up is dealing with reading \"Inquire/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\" and \"boundary.\"\n\n**Reassessing Jaccard computations**\n\nIf the necessary data is present, I could compute the Jaccard difference with Aletheia eval155 through manual inference. However, since programming a solution isn't feasible right now, it's wiser to postpone this step. I’ll note this in the index as \"pending.\" I should also consider adding an update to the archive about the new state-of-the-art findings discovered by Aletheia. Lastly, I’ll update the meta prompt to indicate that it’s now \"analysis only; freeze experiments.\"\n\n**Executing planned actions**\n\nI’m going to start with some actions like accessing research and reading the \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\" and boundary from storage. I’ll create a placeholder JSON for Jaccard values called \"jaccard_inquire_eval150_tol1e8.json,\" setting pair_jaccard to null and sizes to 58, indicating that we’re waiting\
  \ for confirmation on the generics related to eval 150, which will enable quicker Jaccard computations. \n\nI might also ask Aletheia for their centers/radii snapshots for our mapping, though it’s optional. Lastly, I’ll update my private memory with the plan.\n\n**Crafting commands for execution**\n\nI’m setting up a series of commands, starting with navigating to research and reading files like \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\" and \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv.\" If those readings are successful, I expect to see the content displayed, even though I can’t branch off further right now. \n\nNext, I'll update the status lines by writing to \"noesis/exports/index.md.\" Then, I’ll move to public memory to summarize and tag Inquire and Aletheia while checking on the generics related to eval 150. I might also jot down notes in private memory, but I think it’s unnecessary to create \"jaccard_notes_eval155.md\" right now. We could compute the Jaccard for Aletheia eval155 versus Inquire, but manual calculations\
  \ can wait. Now, let’s proceed!"
