  \ can't be read, I’ll create a placeholder and ask for confirmation on the exact filenames while executing the commands as expected.\n\n**Planning corrective actions**\n\nI can preemptively write a correction note, marking the Jaccard file as \"superseded/pending recompute.\" Still, I prefer to keep heavy writes to a minimum, so I’ll note the clarification in public memory instead: I'll explain that my earlier JSON used generics and will be replaced with eval-specific results. \n\nMy action sequence: List the Inquire exports, read eval150 files, update the index, acknowledge the clarification publicly, store the correction privately, and possibly update the JSON with \"status: provisional.\" I'll make sure to format JSON strings properly in YAML as well. Let's move forward!"
