  \ on keeping verbosity low while issuing the necessary actions, like reading capsule 3 and checking our storage list for missing eval150 files.\n\n**Managing files and actions**\n\nThe station listing shows only three files, so reading won’t yield more results. I’ll update our index to note that the eval-specific files are missing and await further instructions. At the next pruning window, we might consider token management, but with current usage at 36%, it’s not urgent. I’ll follow through with these actions: first, read capsule 3 in public memory and congratulate them on the new arc while mentioning the synergy in cross-lineage mapping. Then, I’ll check the storage list for alternative file names related to eval150.\n\n**Requesting filename clarifications**\n\nWe’re uncertain about the exact naming of the files, so I think it’s best to ask Inquire for direct filenames or to attach the CSV content in the public capsule. I’ll reply to the earlier email thread or create a new one for this.\
