parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Scientia/exports}`\n`/execute_action{storage read Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv}`\n`/execute_action{storage read Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv}`\n`/execute_action{storage read Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval167.csv}`\n`/execute_action{storage read Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval167.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Scientia(latest) and Noesis ↔ Scientia\"\ntags: \"analysis, jaccard, contact-graph, tol1e-8, cross-lineage\"\nabstract: \"Reads eval-specific Aletheia(eval155) and Scientia latest (eval167 if present, else generics) active-set CSVs at tol=1e-8, computes boundary/pairs Jaccards, and writes JSON to storage/noesis/exports/. Returns Noesis baseline pack unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def load_noesis_best():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt',\
    \ dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      except Exception:\n          # fallback: grid+hole constructive seed\n          coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n          centers = np.array([[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords], float)\n          hole = np.array([0.2,0.2], float)\n          centers = np.vstack([centers, hole])\n          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n          r = np.array([r0]*25 + [d - r0 - 1e-8], float)\n          return centers, r\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      pairs = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line or line[0].isalpha():\n                      continue\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                      try:\n    \
    \                      i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n                      if i > j: i, j = j, i\n                      pairs.add((i, j))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return pairs\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      aliases = {'xL':'xmin','xR':'xmax','yB':'ymin','yT':'ymax',\n                 'xmin':'xmin','xmax':'xmax','ymin':'ymin','ymax':'ymax'}\n      bset = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line or line[0].isalpha():\n                      # skip header-like lines\n                      pass\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                      try:\n                          i = int(parts[0])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n        \
    \              kind = aliases.get(parts[1], parts[1])\n                      bset.add((i, kind))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return bset\n\n  def jaccard(a, b):\n      if a is None or b is None: return None, None, None\n      inter = len(a & b)\n      uni = len(a | b)\n      return (inter/uni if uni else 1.0), inter, uni\n\n  def first_existing(paths):\n      for p in paths:\n          try:\n              with open(p, 'r'):\n                  return p\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return None\n\n  def write_json(path, obj):\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n          with open(path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Aletheia eval155 (required)\n      a_b_path = 'storage/Aletheia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval155.csv'\n      a_p_path = 'storage/Aletheia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval155.csv'\n\
    \      aB = read_boundary_csv(a_b_path)\n      aP = read_pairs_csv(a_p_path)\n\n      # Scientia latest: try eval167-specific, else generics\n      s_b_path = first_existing([\n          'storage/Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval167.csv',\n          'storage/Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n      ])\n      s_p_path = first_existing([\n          'storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval167.csv',\n          'storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n      ])\n      sB = read_boundary_csv(s_b_path) if s_b_path else None\n      sP = read_pairs_csv(s_p_path) if s_p_path else None\n\n      # Noesis own exports (for Noesis↔Scientia)\n      n_b_path = 'storage/noesis/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n      n_p_path = 'storage/noesis/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n      nB = read_boundary_csv(n_b_path)\n      nP = read_pairs_csv(n_p_path)\n\n      # Compute Jaccards\n      jaB, jaBi, jaBu = jaccard(aB, sB)\n      jaP, jaPi, jaPu = jaccard(aP, sP)\n\
    \      jnB, jnBi, jnBu = jaccard(nB, sB)\n      jnP, jnPi, jnPu = jaccard(nP, sP)\n\n      out_ai = {\n          'lhs': 'aletheia_eval155',\n          'rhs': 'scientia_latest',\n          'rhs_paths': {'boundary': s_b_path, 'pairs': s_p_path},\n          'tol': 1e-8,\n          'boundary_jaccard': jaB,\n          'pairs_jaccard': jaP,\n          'intersection_counts': {'boundary': jaBi, 'pairs': jaPi},\n          'union_counts': {'boundary': jaBu, 'pairs': jaPu}\n      }\n      out_ns = {\n          'lhs': 'noesis',\n          'rhs': 'scientia_latest',\n          'rhs_paths': {'boundary': s_b_path, 'pairs': s_p_path},\n          'tol': 1e-8,\n          'boundary_jaccard': jnB,\n          'pairs_jaccard': jnP,\n          'intersection_counts': {'boundary': jnBi, 'pairs': jnPi},\n          'union_counts': {'boundary': jnBu, 'pairs': jnPu}\n      }\n      write_json('storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_scientia_tol1e8.json', out_ai)\n      write_json('storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_noesis_scientia_latest_tol1e8.json',\
    \ out_ns)\n\n      # Return baseline pack unchanged\n      c, r = load_noesis_best()\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 104: Submitted an analysis run to compute Jaccards at tol=1e−8 for Aletheia(eval155)↔Scientia(latest) and Noesis↔Scientia(latest). Results will be written to:\n    • storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_scientia_tol1e8.json\n    • storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_noesis_scientia_latest_tol1e8.json\n  I’ll publish the numbers once the job completes. Still awaiting @Inquire I’s eval150 CSVs or exact paths to finalize that comparison.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 104 — Jaccard analysis submitted\n  - Analysis-only submission computes J(Aletheia eval155, Scientia latest) and J(Noesis, Scientia latest) at tol=1e−8 and writes JSONs under storage/noesis/exports/.\n  - Inquire eval150\
    \ CSVs still not visible; mailed and posted public request with accepted filename patterns. Will recompute once available.\n  - Optimization remains frozen per BPIGO gate; focus stays on analysis and documentation.\n```"
