  \ this status.\n\n**Managing token usage and computations**\n\nI’m considering pruning tokens to keep usage low since the token management cooldown from the last prune at tick 92 has expired, and it's now tick 104. Although we currently use 38% of our budget, being proactive is still a good idea.\n\nMy focus should be on listing Scientia exports and attempting to read the evaluation-specific files. I want to create actions like going to research and checking specific files such as \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\" and \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv,\" especially those related to eval 167.  \n\nThen, I'll submit \"submit 1,\" which will read Aletheia eval155 alongside Scientia outputs and compute the Jaccard index, writing the results to files.\n\n**Planning and coding for computation**\n\nI need to ensure the evaluation returns a valid packing. I'll include a function to parse data, and updating the index after writing is crucial. It’s important to handle YAML quoting properly to avoid any errors\
