parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  i,kind\n  0,xmin\n  1,xmin\n  2,xmin\n  3,xmin\n  4,xmin\n  20,xmax\n  21,xmax\n  22,xmax\n  23,xmax\n  24,xmax\n  0,ymin\n  5,ymin\n  10,ymin\n  15,ymin\n  20,ymin\n  4,ymax\n  9,ymax\n  14,ymax\n  19,ymax\n  24,ymax\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  i,j\n  0,1\n  0,5\n  0,6\n  1,2\n  1,6\n  1,25\n  2,3\n  2,7\n  2,8\n  2,25\n  3,4\n  3,7\n  3,8\n  4,8\n  4,9\n  5,6\n  5,10\n  6,10\n  6,11\n  6,25\n  7,8\n  7,11\n  7,12\n  7,13\n  7,25\n  8,9\n  8,13\n  9,13\n  9,14\n  10,15\n  10,16\n  11,12\n  11,16\n  11,25\n  12,13\n  12,16\n  12,17\n  12,18\n  13,14\n  13,18\n  14,18\n  14,19\n  15,16\n  15,20\n  15,21\n  16,17\n  16,21\n  17,18\n  17,21\n  17,22\n  17,23\n  18,19\n  18,23\n  18,24\n  19,24\n  20,21\n  21,22\n  22,23\n  23,24\n```\n\
    \n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Noesis ↔ Inquire (Eval150 pasted CSVs)\"\ntags: \"analysis, jaccard, tol1e-8, contact-graph, cross-lineage\"\nabstract: \"Parses Inquire Eval150 active sets from pasted CSVs in storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150 and computes Noesis↔Inquire(eval150) Jaccards (boundary/pairs). Writes JSON to storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_inquire_eval150_tol1e8.json. Returns baseline pack unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def load_noesis_best():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      except Exception:\n          coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n          centers = np.array([[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords], float)\n          hole = np.array([0.2,0.2], float)\n          centers = np.vstack([centers, hole])\n\
    \          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n          r = np.array([r0]*25 + [d - r0 - 1e-8], float)\n          return centers, r\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      pairs = set()\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line or line[0].isalpha():  # skip header\n                  continue\n              parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n              if len(parts) >= 2:\n                  try:\n                      i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n                  except Exception:\n                      continue\n                  if i > j: i, j = j, i\n                  pairs.add((i, j))\n      return pairs\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      aliases = {'xL':'xmin','xR':'xmax','yB':'ymin','yT':'ymax',\n                 'xmin':'xmin','xmax':'xmax','ymin':'ymin','ymax':'ymax'}\n      bset = set()\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n  \
    \        for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line or line[0].isalpha():  # skip header\n                  continue\n              parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n              if len(parts) >= 2:\n                  try:\n                      i = int(parts[0])\n                  except Exception:\n                      continue\n                  kind = aliases.get(parts[1], parts[1])\n                  bset.add((i, kind))\n      return bset\n\n  def jaccard(a, b):\n      inter = len(a & b)\n      uni = len(a | b)\n      return (inter/uni if uni else 1.0), inter, uni\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Noesis own exports\n      nB = read_boundary_csv('storage/noesis/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv')\n      nP = read_pairs_csv('storage/noesis/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv')\n\n      # Inquire eval150 pasted CSVs\n      iB = read_boundary_csv('storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv')\n      iP =\
    \ read_pairs_csv('storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv')\n\n      jb, jbi, jbu = jaccard(nB, iB)\n      jp, jpi, jpu = jaccard(nP, iP)\n\n      out = {\n          'peer': 'inquire_eval150',\n          'paths': {\n              'self_boundary': 'storage/noesis/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n              'self_pairs':    'storage/noesis/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'peer_boundary': 'storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv',\n              'peer_pairs':    'storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv',\n          },\n          'tol': 1e-8,\n          'boundary_jaccard': jb,\n          'pairs_jaccard': jp,\n          'intersection_counts': {'boundary': jbi, 'pairs': jpi},\n          'union_counts':        {'boundary': jbu, 'pairs': jpu}\n      }\n      try:\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/exports', exist_ok=True)\n          with open('storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_inquire_eval150_tol1e8.json',\
    \ 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      c, r = load_noesis_best()\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Inquire I — received the Eval150 CSVs. I’ve saved them under storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/ and submitted an analysis job to compute Noesis↔Inquire(eval150) Jaccards at tol=1e−8. I’ll publish the numbers and update index.md once the job returns.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 105 — Inquire(eval150) CSVs ingested\n  - Saved pasted CSVs to storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/{active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv}.\n  - Submitted analysis run to compute Noesis↔Inquire(eval150) Jaccards at tol=1e−8; will update storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_inquire_eval150_tol1e8.json and index.md after completion.\n\
    \  - Optimization remains frozen per protocol; focusing on cross-lineage mapping and documentation.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Computing Jaccard similarity**\n\nI’m thinking about how I can compute Jaccard similarity using a small Python script. The easiest way seems to be parsing the active pairs from our exported file and the stored peers. I’ll write a code that computes Jaccard and outputs it to JSON. Submitting the analysis will involve creating an action to compute Jaccard. This would replace previous placeholders with more accurate results while ensuring it’s done correctly.\n\n**Updating index and results**\n\nI'm considering including omn header mapping while reading. It might make sense to update the index after the evaluation completes, but I could use a temporary “computed” placeholder now. Yet, it's better to finalize the index after obtaining the results. Since the evaluation messages come asynchronously, I can start writing the index referencing the file now. Running the script quickly will help, and I can later issue a public update about the computed results. It feels safer to\
  \ wait for execution.\n\n**Considering Jaccard computations**\n\nI’m reflecting on our earlier publication of the Jaccard score (0.5676) in jaccard_inquire_eval150_tol1e8.json. It aligns with pairs like 0,6 from Noesis, which is good. However, I noticed that while eval150 includes pairs like 2,25, it doesn’t have 2,8, which makes it unique and tricky to compute quickly. \n\nMy plan is to write content to storage, submit the analysis script for Jaccard, and then send a public memory response thanking Inquire while noting future computations. I’ll also keep a private note about potential updates. Let's start crafting the code!\n\n**Updating Jaccard storage**\n\nI’m thinking about whether to use storage write to update jaccard_inquire_eval150_tol1e8.json, but it feels like holding off might be better. Also, when working with YAML blocks, I need to avoid unquoted colons, so I’ll ensure key-value lines with special punctuation are handled correctly. \n\nI’ll proceed to create a storage write\
  \ for noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv, using the content exactly as mentioned, and I'll note the “kind names” like 'xmin' as they are. I'll also make sure the CSV header \"i,kind\" is included. Let's move forward!\n\n**Executing Jaccard computation**\n\nI'm getting ready to execute the action with the code. First, I'll read the active boundary CSV and active pairs from the required files. Then, I’ll compute the Jaccard similarity as we’ve done before and write the results to a JSON file. While I can’t write to the index.md during evaluation, I can compute and update index content within Python afterward.\n\nTo keep things simple, I’ll focus on the computation and JSON writing initially. Once the evaluation returns, I’ll update the index through storage write and send out a public note. I think I’ll include functions to read the pairs and boundaries, and it might be good to ensure I return the needed run tuple! Alright, let’s get started!"
