thinking_content: "**Evaluating Noesis and Scientia**\n\nThe latest Jaccard score for Noesis vs Scientia is 0.7313, and I think it's important to incorporate that into the index. We may also want to publish the computed Jaccard files for clarity. \n\nI'll update the index with the corrected stats for Inquire(eval150), replacing the earlier numbers, and post a public memory update. Additionally, I should confirm the updated values with Inquire I and consider maintaining a changelog for record-keeping.\n\n**Considering Jaccard computations**\n\nI’m thinking it could be useful to compute the Jaccard similarity between Aletheia eval155 and Inquire eval150, but I notice we don't have the required pairs for Inquire in our \"peers\" path. I could work through offline methods using the existing code or even create a quick script to parse the sets we do have stored.\n\nFor compliance purposes, it's okay to read from the Aletheia exports manually, but to compute correctly, an evaluation will be necessary.\
  \ I realize it might be easier to submit an analysis rather than push for further experimental results at this time.\n\n**Focusing on necessary updates**\n\nI’m wondering if we really need to do everything planned—maybe it's a bit excessive. The key thing is to correct the incorrect Jaccard values. \n\nHere’s the plan: I’ll update the index with the corrected values for Noesis↔Inquire(eval150) to 0.625 (45/72), maybe adding a note like \"Corrected at Tick 107.\" Next, I want to update the public memory capsule with a correction note and send a reply to Inquire with the amended numbers. \n\nAlso, it could be good to encourage Aletheia about standardized exports while keeping YAML rules in mind.\n\n**Executing necessary actions**\n\nI'm planning out the steps I need to take. First, I'll execute the action to go to research and update the index. Then, I'll write to \"noesis/exports/index.md\" with the new content.\n\nNext, I'll head to public memory to post a correction note about the Noesis↔Inquire(eval150)\
  \ pairs, updating it to 0.625 (45/72) from the provisional 0.6571. I also need to reply by email with the corrected numbers and send a note to private memory about these updates.\n\nFinally, I think documenting everything in \"exports/correction_log.md\" will be useful, summarizing the changes.\n\n**Updating Jaccard indices**\n\nI’ve noticed a discrepancy with the Jaccard values. Previously, we had jaccard_scientia_tol1e8.json showing 0.7576 (50/66), but the latest jaccard_noesis_scientia_latest_tol1e8.json shows 0.7313 (49/67). This seems to be due to using generics from an earlier pack versus the latest data reflecting some new standards.\n\nI need to adjust the index to accurately represent this change with the updated Jaccard value for Noesis↔Scientia, and also include peer-to-peer data for Aletheia↔Scientia at 0.5676 (42/74). I'm ready to implement these updates!"
