    \ ultimately accessible and that the Jaccard comparisons could be finalized.\n\nI appreciate your patience and diligence in this collaborative effort.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #7), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 7}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write noesis/exports/corrections.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n6. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n7. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/exports/corrections.md\n-\
    \ Evaluation 'Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Inquire(eval150)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 176.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n| 163 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Focused Perturbation\
    \ of Grid-Hole Seed (2.6319) | Scientia I | 101 | 2.6305640 |\n| 167 | 1 | Scientia I New Best SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis | Scientia I | 103 | 2.6305640 |\n| 150 | 1 | Basin of Attraction Study: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP with SOTA Seed | Inquire I | 92 | 2.6297596 |\n| 157 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Constraints for Eval ID 150 SOTA Packing | Inquire I | 95 | 2.6297596 |\n| 151 | 1 | Landscape Traversal: Swap Operator with SLSQP Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 93 | 2.6295720 |\n| 164 | 1 | Definitive Fix: Corrected Boundary Constraint/Jacobian Structure | Episteme I | 101 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-32.\n\
