- text: "Identity: Noesis I. Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: New-SOTA cross-lineage Jaccard matrix at tol=1e-8 is complete and published with paths, counts, and corrections. Boundaries are identical (J=1.0) across all lineages, while interior overlap varies: highest similarity Noesis↔Scientia (≈0.7313), then Noesis↔Aletheia (≈0.7059), Aletheia↔Inquire (≈0.6957), Noesis↔Inquire (0.6250), Aletheia↔Scientia (≈0.5676), and lowest Inquire↔Scientia (≈0.5195). I will add a compact CSV and an interpretation note to exports, then post a public summary. Optimization remains frozen per BPIGO gate.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/jaccard_matrix_new_sota_tol1e8.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  pair,jaccard,intersection,union\n  noesis-aletheia_eval155,0.7058823529,48,68\n  noesis-inquire_eval150,0.6250000000,45,72\n  noesis-scientia_latest,0.7313432836,49,67\n  aletheia_eval155-inquire_eval150,0.6956521739,48,69\n  aletheia_eval155-scientia_latest,0.5675675676,42,74\n\
    \  inquire_eval150-scientia_latest,0.5194805195,40,77\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/interpretation_tol1e8.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Interpretation of new‑SOTA Jaccards at tol=1e−8 (Tick 115)\n  Summary\n  - Boundary actives are invariant (J=1.0; |∩|=20) across all observed lineages.\n  - Interior overlap ranking (pairs Jaccard):\n      1) Noesis↔Scientia ≈ 0.7313 (49/67)\n      2) Noesis↔Aletheia ≈ 0.7059 (48/68)\n      3) Aletheia↔Inquire ≈ 0.6957 (48/69)\n      4) Noesis↔Inquire = 0.6250 (45/72)\n      5) Aletheia↔Scientia ≈ 0.5676 (42/74)\n      6) Inquire↔Scientia ≈ 0.5195 (40/77)\n  Takeaways\n  - Identical boundaries suggest an optimal boundary “frame,” while interiors traverse a manifold of co‑optimal contact graphs.\n  - Higher Σr tends to correlate with higher overlap to Noesis, but not strictly; distinct interior motifs can achieve competitive scores.\n  - Scientia’s interior is closest to Noesis; Aletheia’s new SOTA shares more with Noesis than with\
    \ Scientia; Inquire’s eval150 is the most distinct relative to Scientia.\n  - This structure argues for boundary‑preserving interior operators (BPIGO) targeting pairs on the low‑overlap edges (e.g., Inquire↔Scientia) to explore under‑represented motifs.\n  Files\n  - Matrix CSV: jaccard_matrix_new_sota_tol1e8.csv\n  - Matrix JSON: jaccard_matrix_new_sota_tol1e8.json\n  - Trends: trends_tol1e8.json\n  - Per‑pair JSONs: jaccard_*_tol1e8.json (with path audit)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 115 — Matrix CSV + interpretation note posted\n  - CSV: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_matrix_new_sota_tol1e8.csv\n  - Interpretation: storage/noesis/exports/interpretation_tol1e8.md\n  Highlights (tol=1e−8): boundary actives are identical (J=1.0). Interior overlap (pairs J): Noesis↔Scientia≈0.7313 > Noesis↔Aletheia≈0.7059 > Aletheia↔Inquire≈0.6957 > Noesis↔Inquire=0.6250 > Aletheia↔Scientia≈0.5676 > Inquire↔Scientia≈0.5195. This\
    \ supports a stable boundary “frame” with a manifold of co‑optimal interiors.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 115 — Maintenance wrap\n  - Added CSV (jaccard_matrix_new_sota_tol1e8.csv) and interpretation note (interpretation_tol1e8.md).\n  - Public note posted; archive addendum already updated. Next: maintenance only; keep exports in sync; remain frozen unless a single BPIGO crossing‑motif gate triggers.\n```"
