tick: 116
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis I. Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: New‑SOTA Jaccard matrix at tol=1e−8 is published with paths, counts, and corrections. Boundaries are identical (J=1.0) across all lineages; interior overlap varies. Next, I will compute consensus vs. variant interior edges across Aletheia(eval155), Inquire(eval150), and Scientia(latest) to identify stable vs. divergent motifs. Optimization remains frozen per BPIGO gate.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus vs Variant Interior Edges @ tol=1e-8 (Aletheia eval155, Inquire eval150, Scientia latest)\"\ntags: \"analysis, consensus, variants, contact-graph, tol1e-8, cross-lineage\"\nabstract: \"Reads active-pair CSVs at tol=1e−8 for Aletheia(eval155), Inquire(eval150), and Scientia(latest). Computes intersection (consensus), union, majority (≥2/3), and unique sets per lineage; writes JSON and CSV summaries plus consensus-degree per disc. Returns Noesis baseline pack unchanged.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def load_noesis_best():\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n          return c, r\n      except Exception:\n          coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n          centers = np.array([[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords], float)\n          hole = np.array([0.2,0.2], float)\n          centers = np.vstack([centers, hole])\n          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n          r = np.array([r0]*25 + [d - r0 - 1e-8], float)\n          return centers, r\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      pairs = set()\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line:\n                  continue\n              # skip header lines that start with alpha or include non-numeric first\
    \ token\n              parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n              if len(parts) < 2:\n                  continue\n              try:\n                  i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              if i > j: i, j = j, i\n              pairs.add((i, j))\n      return pairs\n\n  def to_list(s):\n      return sorted([[i, j] for (i, j) in s], key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1]))\n\n  def degree_from_pairs(pairs_set):\n      deg = [0]*N\n      for (i,j) in pairs_set:\n          deg[i] += 1\n          deg[j] += 1\n      return deg\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Paths\n      path_A = 'storage/Aletheia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval155.csv'\n      path_I = 'storage/noesis/peers/inquire_eval150/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv'\n      path_S = 'storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n\n      A = read_pairs_csv(path_A)\n      I = read_pairs_csv(path_I)\n      S = read_pairs_csv(path_S)\n\n      # Sets\n\
    \      inter_all = A & I & S\n      union_all = A | I | S\n      maj_2 = (A & I) | (A & S) | (I & S)\n      uniq_A = A - (I | S)\n      uniq_I = I - (A | S)\n      uniq_S = S - (A | I)\n\n      # Sizes\n      sizes = {\n          'A_count': len(A), 'I_count': len(I), 'S_count': len(S),\n          'intersection_all': len(inter_all),\n          'union_all': len(union_all),\n          'majority_2': len(maj_2),\n          'unique_A': len(uniq_A),\n          'unique_I': len(uniq_I),\n          'unique_S': len(uniq_S)\n      }\n\n      # Coverage metrics\n      cov = {\n          'inter_as_frac_of_A': len(inter_all)/len(A) if len(A) else None,\n          'inter_as_frac_of_I': len(inter_all)/len(I) if len(I) else None,\n          'inter_as_frac_of_S': len(inter_all)/len(S) if len(S) else None,\n          'maj2_as_frac_of_union': len(maj_2)/len(union_all) if len(union_all) else None\n      }\n\n      # Consensus degree per disc\n      deg_consensus = degree_from_pairs(inter_all)\n\n      # Write\
    \ JSON summary\n      out = {\n          'paths': {'A_pairs': path_A, 'I_pairs': path_I, 'S_pairs': path_S},\n          'sizes': sizes,\n          'coverage': cov,\n          'intersection_all': to_list(inter_all),\n          'union_all_size': len(union_all),\n          'majority_2_size': len(maj_2),\n          'unique': {\n              'A': to_list(uniq_A),\n              'I': to_list(uniq_I),\n              'S': to_list(uniq_S)\n          },\n          'consensus_degree': deg_consensus,\n          'note': 'tol=1e-8; A=Aletheia eval155, I=Inquire eval150, S=Scientia latest'\n      }\n      os.makedirs('storage/noesis/exports', exist_ok=True)\n      with open('storage/noesis/exports/consensus_sets_tol1e8.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n\n      # Write variant edges CSV with presence flags\n      with open('storage/noesis/exports/variant_edges_tol1e8.csv', 'w') as f:\n          f.write('i,j,in_A,in_I,in_S,count_present,category\\n')\n          for (i,j) in sorted(list(union_all),\
    \ key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1])):\n              inA = (i,j) in A\n              inI = (i,j) in I\n              inS = (i,j) in S\n              cnt = int(inA) + int(inI) + int(inS)\n              if cnt == 3:\n                  cat = 'all'\n              elif cnt == 2:\n                  cat = 'majority2'\n              else:\n                  if inA: cat = 'unique_A'\n                  elif inI: cat = 'unique_I'\n                  else: cat = 'unique_S'\n              f.write(f'{i},{j},{int(inA)},{int(inI)},{int(inS)},{cnt},{cat}\\n')\n\n      # Consensus degree CSV\n      with open('storage/noesis/exports/consensus_degree_tol1e8.csv', 'w') as f:\n          f.write('disc,degree_consensus\\n')\n          for idx, d in enumerate(deg_consensus):\n              f.write(f'{idx},{d}\\n')\n\n      # Return Noesis baseline pack unchanged\n      c, r = load_noesis_best()\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 116 — Submitted “Consensus vs Variant Interior Edges @ tol=1e−8” to quantify which interior contacts are shared across Aletheia(eval155), Inquire(eval150), and Scientia(latest), and which are lineage‑unique. Outputs will include:\n    • consensus_sets_tol1e8.json (sizes, coverage, intersection/union, unique sets, consensus degree per disc)\n    • variant_edges_tol1e8.csv (presence flags and categories)\n    • consensus_degree_tol1e8.csv\n  This should help target BPIGO operators toward low‑overlap motifs while preserving the boundary frame.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 116 — Consensus/variant analysis submitted\n  - Job computes intersection/union/majority and unique edges across A(eval155), I(eval150), S(latest); writes JSON/CSVs under storage/noesis/exports/.\n  - Next: read results, add a short interpretation, and keep operators paused unless a single crossing‑motif passes the gate.\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: "**Considering project outputs**\n\nI realize there’s no user question right now, so I’m thinking about keeping actions minimal while aligning with our goals. Maybe it’s time to finalize a public \"one-pager\" summary CSV and a README linking to archives—I’ve done that. I wonder if I should prepare a reproducibility zip file. There’s also the idea of creating a \"bpigo_gate.md\" that lists the top-15 shadow-price pairs, though this could involve running some earlier saved analyses.\n\n**Planning analysis procedures**\n\nI’m considering computing difference sets for Aletheia eval155, Scientia latest, and Inquire eval150 to create a \"consensus core\" and \"variant-only edges\" sets. This way, I can propose operator targets. It matches our analysis-only approach. I think it makes sense to implement code that reads per-pair CSVs and produces intersection sets. I want to write the results to 'exports/consensus_sets_tol1e8.json' and 'exports/variant_edges_tol1e8.csv', then publish\
  \ a brief public note about it.\n\n**Deciding analysis steps**\n\nI’m thinking it might not be necessary to overcomplicate things. Instead, I could write a new script that directly reads the already stored pair CSV files for Aletheia eval155, Inquire eval150, and the latest Scientia. I’ll create a 'consensus' script that submits the analysis and computes intersection, union, pairwise differences, and coverage percentages. \n\nAfter executing the code, I can read and post the results later. Maybe I’ll also include a public note stating that the job has been submitted.\n\n**Implementing analysis process**\n\nI’m ready to implement some code with the goal of submitting it shortly. I plan to import JSON and read the paths for the CSVs to parse pairs. I want to compute various things: the edges present in all three sets (tri_intersection), their union (tri_union), edges unique to each pack, and edges present in at least two of the three here. I'll also gather coverage metrics based on sizes\
  \ and fractions.\n\nAfterward, I’ll save my results to 'exports/consensus_sets_tol1e8.json' and 'exports/variant_edges_tol1e8.csv'. Finally, I’ll compute the \"consensus-degree\" and make sure to return an unchanged noesis baseline pack, while creating a public note about the actions. I could even consider linking to the new files in an index.\n\n**Crafting the analysis code**\n\nI’m planning to carefully craft the code now. I’ll create a read CSV function similar to earlier ones, acknowledging that the lines might include headers. The pairs will be formatted as 'i,j' with float values that are actually integers. \n\nNext, I’ll compute the percentage of each pack’s pairs that are in consensus. For the variant edges CSV, I want to have columns for i, j, their presence in each dataset, count present, and a category that includes 'all, majority2, unique_A, unique_I, unique_S'. I think that's my plan for now, so let's proceed with the implementation!"
