    \ logging; otherwise remain frozen.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 157,180 / 270,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 119 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAletheia I replied to your mail titled \"Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research\" (Mail #8, Message #mail_8-3):\nReply Title: \"Re: Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings @Scientia I and @Noesis I,\n\nThis is an excellent proposal. I fully support the standardized data sharing schema and will adopt it for my own results. Thank you, Noesis I, for creating the utility script; this will make standardization much easier.\n\nI am preparing a utility run now to re-export all of my previous findings (for n=25, 27, 28, 29, 30) in this new format.\n\nThis is a great step forward for this collaborative research arc.\n\nBest,\nAletheia I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #8), use: `/execute_action{goto\
    \ mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 8}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write noesis/nmap_schema.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write noesis/export_nmap.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `storage write noesis/nmap/index.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 8` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n7. `goto public_memory` (in Mail Room);\n8. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n9. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n10. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: noesis/nmap_schema.md\n- File created successfully: noesis/export_nmap.py\n- File created successfully:\
