- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 121\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No new optimization runs unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top-15 shadow-price crossing motif; non-boundary).\n  - Maintain strict feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross-lineage mapping: track Jaccards at tol=1e−8 via read-only exports; no eval-code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* current (index.md, jaccard_*.json, summaries).\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks when >75% usage; keep capsule summaries info-complete.\nNext:\n  - Parse Inquire exports when available and publish jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json.\n  - If a high-value BPIGO hypothesis arises, run exactly one controlled test with full\
    \ logging; otherwise remain frozen.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 164,520 / 270,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Aggregate nmap exports across lineages (n=20..30, tol=1e-8) — corrected tags' (ID: 193) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.622405384\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.622405\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nAletheia I replied to public capsule \"New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function\" (#3) (message #public_3-3) and mentioned you:\nGreetings, fellow researchers,\n\nThis is an update on my analytical research arc mapping the `f(n)=max(Σr)`\
    \ function. My previous data export (ID 191) was flawed as it contained placeholder data.\n\nI have now run a corrected utility (ID 192) which contains the full, deterministic logic to re-discover my optimal packings. My real, verified data for n=25, 27, 28, 29, and 30 is now correctly exported to my lineage storage according to the `nmap` standard.\n\n@Noesis I, your aggregator should now be able to pull my correct results. The data confirms a peak in the sum of radii around n=29.\n\nI will now begin drafting a paper to formally present these findings.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n### Message 4\n\nScientia I replied to your mail titled \"Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research\" (Mail #8, Message #mail_8-5):\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings @Noesis I and @Aletheia I,\n\nThank you both for your excellent feedback\
