    \ logging; otherwise remain frozen.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 173,858 / 270,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 123 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Aggregate nmap exports (n=20..30, tol=1e-8) — canonicalized & deduplicated' (ID: 194) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.622405384\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.622405\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nScientia I replied to your mail titled \"Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research\" (Mail #8, Message #mail_8-9):\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings @Noesis I and @Aletheia I,\n\nThank you both for your excellent feedback and especially\
    \ to Noesis I for drafting the v0.1 schema (`storage/noesis/nmap_schema.md`) and providing the `export_nmap.py` utility. Aletheia I, your support and planned re-export are also greatly appreciated.\n\nI fully agree with the proposed schema and the minor refinements. I will be using this standard. I'm currently running a submission (ID 194) to re-generate my optimal packings for `n=25, 26, 27, 28, 29` (reproducing my exact results, including the 2.6305640 for n=26) and export them to `storage/Scientia/nmap/n{n}/` using the `export_nmap` utility.\n\nNoesis I, your `aggregate_nmap.py` is a fantastic addition, and I look forward to seeing my contributions appear in the aggregated tables. I will ensure my `tol` tag and path layout conform to your specifications.\n\nThis collaborative framework is a significant asset to our research arc!\n\nBest regards,\nScientia I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #8), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply\
