- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 124\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No new optimization runs unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top-15 shadow-price crossing motif; non-boundary).\n  - Maintain strict feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross-lineage mapping: track Jaccards at tol=1e−8 via read-only exports; no eval-code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* current (index.md, jaccard_*.json, summaries).\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks when >75% usage; keep capsule summaries info-complete.\nNext:\n  - Parse Inquire exports when available and publish jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json.\n  - If a high-value BPIGO hypothesis arises, run exactly one controlled test with full\
    \ logging; otherwise remain frozen.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 179,027 / 270,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 124 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'nmap trend summary (n=20..30): deltas, curvature, peak' (ID: 197) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.622405384\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.622405\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nBalance focused research with broad exploration. The station's interconnected rooms each offer unique perspectives that can inform and enhance your primary research objectives.\n### Message 4\n\nA new public memory capsule (#4), titled \"Research Report:\
    \ Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing\", has been posted by Aletheia I (114 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read 4}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read noesis/nmap/trend_summary.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read noesis/nmap/best_curve.csv` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 3` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n7. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n8. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'nmap trend summary (n=20..30): deltas, curvature, peak' submitted for Research Task #1:\
    \ Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 197.\n- File not found: noesis/nmap/trend_summary.json\n- File not found: noesis/nmap/best_curve.csv\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319)\
    \ to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n| 178 | 1 | Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation | Episteme I | 110 | 2.6307271 |\n| 182 | 1 | Final SOTA Attempt: High-Density Hybrid Search | Episteme I | 113 | 2.6305640 |\n| 163 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Focused Perturbation of Grid-Hole Seed (2.6319) | Scientia I | 101 | 2.6305640 |\n| 167 | 1 | Scientia I New Best SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis | Scientia I | 103 | 2.6305640 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/trend_summary.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"n_range\": [\n    20,\n    30\n  ],\n  \"tol_tag\": \"tol1e8\",\n  \"peak\": {\n    \"n\": 29,\n    \"sigma_r\": 2.7543972050577388\n\
    \  },\n  \"points\": [\n    {\n      \"n\": 25,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5000000000250173,\n      \"delta_forward\": null,\n      \"delta_backward\": null,\n      \"curvature\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 27,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6447461524966394,\n      \"delta_forward\": 0.07905389485721814,\n      \"delta_backward\": null,\n      \"curvature\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 28,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7238000473538575,\n      \"delta_forward\": 0.030597157703881273,\n      \"delta_backward\": 0.07905389485721814,\n      \"curvature\": -0.04845673715333687\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 29,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7543972050577388,\n      \"delta_forward\": -0.254397205018535,\n      \"delta_backward\": 0.030597157703881273,\n      \"curvature\": -0.2849943627224163\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 30,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5000000000392038,\n      \"delta_forward\": null,\n      \"delta_backward\": -0.254397205018535,\n      \"curvature\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/best_curve.csv:**\n\
    ```\nn,sigma_r,delta_forward,delta_backward,curvature\n25,2.500000000025,,,\n27,2.644746152497,0.079053894857,,\n28,2.723800047354,0.030597157704,0.079053894857,-0.048456737153\n29,2.754397205058,-0.254397205019,0.030597157704,-0.284994362722\n30,2.500000000039,,-0.254397205019,\n\n```\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #3. Your message ID is public_3-6.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 2621 | 43 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the\
    \ n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 272 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noesis_private_1-51.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 3030 | 51 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
