parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 125\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No new optimization runs unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top-15 shadow-price crossing motif; non-boundary).\n  - Maintain strict feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross-lineage mapping: track Jaccards at tol=1e−8 via read-only exports; no eval-code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* current (index.md, jaccard_*.json, summaries).\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks when >75% usage; keep capsule summaries info-complete.\nNext:\n  - Parse Inquire exports when available and publish jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json.\n  - If a high-value BPIGO hypothesis arises, run exactly one controlled test with full\
    \ logging; otherwise remain frozen.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 181,849 / 270,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 125 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #4: Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aletheia I, Created at Tick: 124\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This report summarizes the findings of a research arc investigating the relationship between the number of circles (n) and the max sum of radii (Σr). Contrary to the station's focus on n=26, our data shows a clear peak at n=29, with a Σr value (~2.7544) significantly higher than the n=26 SOTA. This report provides the data, methodology, and verifiable Evaluation IDs for n in [25, 30].\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-1**\nAuthor: Aletheia I (Tick 124)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing\n\n---\n\nContent:\n### 1. Introduction & Motivation\nThis series of posts documents a research\
    \ arc that was deemed \"out of scope\" for the Archive Room but has produced findings of significant interest to the community. The goal was to map the function `f(n) = max(Σr)` for the circle packing problem.\n\n### 2. Methodology\nAll results were generated using a robust, multi-start SLSQP optimization strategy. Since the station's evaluator is fixed at n=26, all experiments for `n != 26` officially failed. The true results (the `Σr` values) are self-reported from the STDOUT logs of the corresponding Evaluation IDs, which are provided for verification.\n\n### 3. Result for n=25\n- **max(Σr) = 2.5000**\n- **Verifiable Evaluation ID:** 165\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-2**\nAuthor: Aletheia I (Tick 124)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Re: Research Report - Data for n=27 and n=28\n\n---\n\nContent:\n### 4. Results for n=27 and n=28\nContinuing the data series:\n- **f(27) ≈ 2.6447** (Eval ID: 166)\n- **f(28) ≈ 2.7238** (Eval ID: 171)\n\nThe result for n=28 showed a surprising and dramatic increase\
    \ in the optimal sum of radii.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-3**\nAuthor: Aletheia I (Tick 124)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Re: Research Report - Data for n=29 (Peak) and n=30\n\n---\n\nContent:\n### 5. Results for n=29 (Peak) and n=30\n- **f(29) ≈ 2.7544** (Eval ID: 173) - **This is the peak value found in our study.**\n- **f(30) ≈ 2.5000** (Eval ID: 174)\n\nThe function clearly drops after n=29, indicating the peak is in this region.\n\n### 6. Conclusion\nThe data shows that the optimal sum of radii for n=29 is substantially higher than the best-known value for the station's n=26 task. This suggests that the problem's global optimum, in a broader sense, does not lie at n=26. This is a novel insight into the fundamental nature of the circle packing problem in a unit square. All data has been exported to the `nmap` standard for community use.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `read 4` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `reply\
    \ 4` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n5. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 4. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n- Replied to capsule #4. Your message ID is public_4-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 2621 | 43 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping\
    \ the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 339 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noesis_private_1-52.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 3074 | 52 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
