tick: 127
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis I. Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: nmap aggregator and trend summaries are live; best-by-n now peaks at n=29 with Σr≈2.766433 (Scientia). Next, I will compute per-n cross-lineage Jaccards (Aletheia vs Scientia) at tol=1e−8 for n∈{25..30} to characterize structural similarity beyond Σr. Optimization remains frozen per BPIGO gate.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"nmap per-n cross-lineage Jaccards (tol=1e-8): Aletheia vs Scientia\"\ntags: \"analysis, nmap, jaccard, cross-lineage\"\nabstract: \"For n∈{25..30}, reads Aletheia/Scientia nmap active-set CSVs (tol=1e−8) and computes boundary/pairs Jaccards per n. Writes JSON to storage/noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json. Returns baseline pack unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      s = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n\
    \                  if not line or line[0].isalpha():\n                      continue\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                      try:\n                          i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n                      if i > j: i, j = j, i\n                      s.add((i, j))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return s\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      alias = {'xL':'xmin','xR':'xmax','yB':'ymin','yT':'ymax',\n               'xmin':'xmin','xmax':'xmax','ymin':'ymin','ymax':'ymax'}\n      s = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line:\n                      continue\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                  \
    \    try:\n                          i = int(parts[0])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n                      kind = alias.get(parts[1], parts[1])\n                      s.add((i, kind))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return s\n\n  def jacc(a, b):\n      if a is None or b is None: return None, None, None\n      inter = len(a & b); uni = len(a | b)\n      j = (inter/uni) if uni else 1.0\n      return j, inter, uni\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      results = {}\n      for n in range(25, 31):\n          a_dir = f'storage/Aletheia/nmap/n{n}'\n          s_dir = f'storage/Scientia/nmap/n{n}'\n          a_bp = os.path.join(a_dir, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv')\n          a_pp = os.path.join(a_dir, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv')\n          s_bp = os.path.join(s_dir, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv')\n          s_pp = os.path.join(s_dir, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv')\n\n          if (not os.path.exists(a_bp)) or (not os.path.exists(a_pp))\
    \ or (not os.path.exists(s_bp)) or (not os.path.exists(s_pp)):\n              continue\n\n          Ab = read_boundary_csv(a_bp); Ap = read_pairs_csv(a_pp)\n          Sb = read_boundary_csv(s_bp); Sp = read_pairs_csv(s_pp)\n          jb, ibi, ubu = jacc(Ab, Sb)\n          jp, ipi, upu = jacc(Ap, Sp)\n          results[str(n)] = {\n              'boundary_jaccard': jb,\n              'pairs_jaccard': jp,\n              'boundary_counts': {'inter': ibi, 'union': ubu},\n              'pairs_counts': {'inter': ipi, 'union': upu},\n              'paths': {'A': a_dir, 'S': s_dir}\n          }\n\n      try:\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/nmap', exist_ok=True)\n          with open('storage/noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json', 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'tol': 1e-8, 'ns': list(results.keys()), 'results': results}, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      # Return baseline unchanged\n      try:\n          import numpy as np\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt',\
    \ dtype=float).reshape(N,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      except Exception:\n          import numpy as np\n          coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n          centers = np.array([[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords], float)\n          hole = np.array([0.2,0.2], float)\n          centers = np.vstack([centers, hole])\n          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n          radii = np.array([r0]*25 + [d - r0 - 1e-8], float)\n          c, r = centers, radii\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 127 — Per‑n cross‑lineage Jaccards (Aletheia vs Scientia, tol=1e−8)\n  - Computed boundary/pairs Jaccards for n∈{25..30} where both lineages exported under nmap:\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json\n\
    \  This complements Σr curves with structural similarity per n; as other lineages adopt nmap v0.1, we can extend to full pairwise per‑n matrices.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 127 — Per‑n Jaccards computed (Aletheia vs Scientia)\n  - Wrote storage/noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json (per‑n boundary/pairs Jaccards for n in 25..30 where both exist).\n  - Next: if Inquire adopts nmap v0.1, extend to {A,I,S} per‑n matrices. Optimization remains frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers.\n```"
