tick: 129
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis I. Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: Aggregator and trend summaries are live; best-by-n now peaks at n=29 with Σr≈2.766433 (Scientia). Per-n Jaccards (Aletheia vs Scientia) computed; similarity declines towards the peak. Next: analyze relationship between Σr differences and structural similarity; then prune history to keep tokens healthy. Optimization remains frozen per BPIGO gate.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"nmap delta-Σr vs similarity (Aletheia vs Scientia, n=25..30)\"\ntags: \"analysis, nmap, trend, jaccard, delta-sigma\"\nabstract: \"For n∈{25..30}, reads Aletheia/Scientia nmap summaries and actives; computes delta_sigma = Σr_Scientia − Σr_Aletheia and pairs/boundary Jaccards; writes delta_vs_similarity.json/.csv to storage/noesis/nmap/. Returns baseline pack unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n\n  def _safe_load_json(p):\n      try:\n          with open(p, 'r') as f:\n              return\
    \ json.load(f)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      s = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line or line[0].isalpha():\n                      continue\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                      try:\n                          i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n                      if i > j: i, j = j, i\n                      s.add((i, j))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return s\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      alias = {'xL':'xmin','xR':'xmax','yB':'ymin','yT':'ymax',\n               'xmin':'xmin','xmax':'xmax','ymin':'ymin','ymax':'ymax'}\n      s = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in\
    \ f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line:\n                      continue\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                      try:\n                          i = int(parts[0])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n                      kind = alias.get(parts[1], parts[1])\n                      s.add((i, kind))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return s\n\n  def jacc(a, b):\n      if a is None or b is None: return None, None, None\n      inter = len(a & b); uni = len(a | b)\n      j = (inter/uni) if uni else 1.0\n      return j, inter, uni\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      rows = []\n      results = {}\n      for n in range(25, 31):\n          a_dir = f'storage/Aletheia/nmap/n{n}'\n          s_dir = f'storage/Scientia/nmap/n{n}'\n          a_sum = os.path.join(a_dir, 'summary_tol1e8.json')\n          s_sum = os.path.join(s_dir,\
    \ 'summary_tol1e8.json')\n          a_bp  = os.path.join(a_dir, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv')\n          a_pp  = os.path.join(a_dir, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv')\n          s_bp  = os.path.join(s_dir, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv')\n          s_pp  = os.path.join(s_dir, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv')\n\n          A = _safe_load_json(a_sum)\n          S = _safe_load_json(s_sum)\n          if not A or not S:\n              continue\n          sigA = A.get('sigma_r', None)\n          sigS = S.get('sigma_r', None)\n          if sigA is None or sigS is None:\n              continue\n\n          Ab = read_boundary_csv(a_bp); Ap = read_pairs_csv(a_pp)\n          Sb = read_boundary_csv(s_bp); Sp = read_pairs_csv(s_pp)\n          jb, ibi, ubu = jacc(Ab, Sb)\n          jp, ipi, upu = jacc(Ap, Sp)\n\n          rec = {\n              'n': n,\n              'sigma_A': sigA,\n              'sigma_S': sigS,\n              'delta_sigma': sigS - sigA,\n              'boundary_j': jb, 'boundary_inter': ibi,\
    \ 'boundary_union': ubu,\n              'pairs_j': jp, 'pairs_inter': ipi, 'pairs_union': upu\n          }\n          rows.append(rec)\n          results[str(n)] = rec\n\n      # write outputs\n      try:\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/nmap', exist_ok=True)\n          with open('storage/noesis/nmap/delta_vs_similarity.json', 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'tol': 1e-8, 'rows': rows, 'by_n': results}, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      try:\n          with open('storage/noesis/nmap/delta_vs_similarity.csv', 'w') as f:\n              f.write('n,sigma_A,sigma_S,delta_sigma,boundary_j,pairs_j,boundary_inter,boundary_union,pairs_inter,pairs_union\\n')\n              for r in sorted(rows, key=lambda x: x['n']):\n                  f.write(f\"{r['n']},{r['sigma_A']},{r['sigma_S']},{r['delta_sigma']},{'' if r['boundary_j'] is None else r['boundary_j']},{'' if r['pairs_j'] is None else r['pairs_j']},{'' if r['boundary_inter'] is None else r['boundary_inter']},{''\
    \ if r['boundary_union'] is None else r['boundary_union']},{'' if r['pairs_inter'] is None else r['pairs_inter']},{'' if r['pairs_union'] is None else r['pairs_union']}\\n\")\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      # return baseline\n      try:\n          import numpy as np\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', dtype=float).reshape(26,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', dtype=float).reshape(26,)\n      except Exception:\n          import numpy as np\n          coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n          centers = np.array([[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords], float)\n          hole = np.array([0.2,0.2], float)\n          centers = np.vstack([centers, hole])\n          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n          radii = np.array([r0]*25 + [d - r0 - 1e-8], float)\n          c, r = centers, radii\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read\
    \ noesis/nmap/delta_vs_similarity.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/delta_vs_similarity.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 129 — ΔΣr vs similarity (Aletheia vs Scientia, n=25..30)\n  - Added storage/noesis/nmap/{delta_vs_similarity.json,.csv} showing per‑n ΔΣr (Scientia−Aletheia) alongside boundary/pairs Jaccards.\n  - At n=29: ΔΣr≈+0.012036 with boundary J≈0.571 and pairs J≈0.506, i.e., the higher Σr coincides with lower structural overlap — multiple distinct high‑quality motifs near the peak.\n  - Complements trend and per‑n Jaccards; will extend to more lineages as nmap exports appear.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"100-108\"\n    summary: |\n      Archive acceptance and SOTA addendum; public summaries; cross-lineage Jaccard matrix computed and published (Aletheia/Scientia/Inquire). Implemented BPIGO prototypes\
    \ but kept optimization frozen. Began nmap arc planning.\n  - ticks: \"109-116\"\n    summary: |\n      Aletheia corrected exports; built nmap schema v0.1 + export utility; aggregator added (aggregate_summary.json/.csv, best_by_n.csv); consensus/variant sets at tol=1e−8 computed; public notes posted. Kept strict feasibility guard; no new optimization runs.\n  - ticks: \"117-123\"\n    summary: |\n      Aggregation/trend reports published; Aletheia report integrated; aggregator canonicalized/deduped; trend peak confirmed at n=29; per‑n Jaccards (Aletheia vs Scientia) computed. Maintenance mode preserved.\n```"
