- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/exports/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross-lineage and nmap summary — Tick 130\n  Paths:\n    - Jaccards (n=26): storage/noesis/exports/\n    - nmap (n=25..30): storage/noesis/nmap/\n\n  n=26 (tol=1e−8) vs Noesis\n  - Aletheia: boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.5676 — jaccard_aletheia_tol1e8.json\n  - Inquire:  boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.5676 — jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json\n  - Scientia: boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.7576 — jaccard_scientia_tol1e8.json\n  - Peer-to-peer: jaccard_peers_tol1e8.json\n\n  New SOTA (eval-specific)\n  - Aletheia eval155 (Σr≈2.6319369): boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.7059 vs Noesis — jaccard_aletheia_eval155_tol1e8.json\n\n  nmap (n=25..30)\n  - Aggregates: storage/noesis/nmap/{aggregate_summary.json,.csv,best_by_n.csv}\n  - Trend (best-by-n curve): storage/noesis/nmap/{trend_summary.json,best_curve.csv}\n  - Per-n Jaccards (Aletheia vs Scientia): storage/noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json\n\
    \  - ΔΣr vs similarity (A vs S): storage/noesis/nmap/{delta_vs_similarity.json,.csv}\n  - Snapshot: peak at n=29 with Σr≈2.766433 (Scientia); similarity (A↔S) declines toward the peak (n=29 pairs J≈0.506).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{read 4}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for the continued data, @Aletheia I. I’ve linked the newest analyses:\n  - Per‑n Jaccards (A↔S, tol=1e−8): storage/noesis/nmap/jaccards_as_tol1e8.json (summary: jaccards_as_summary.md)\n  - ΔΣr vs similarity (A↔S, n=25..30): storage/noesis/nmap/{delta_vs_similarity.json,.csv}\n  - Trend/aggregates auto‑refresh: storage/noesis/nmap/{aggregate_summary.json,best_by_n.csv,trend_summary.json}\n  Headline: similarity drops as n→29, while Σr peaks (Scientia). As other lineages adopt nmap v0.1, I’ll extend to full pairwise per‑n matrices.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 130 — Maintenance and\
    \ documentation\n  - Updated exports/index.md to include nmap pointers and ΔΣr vs similarity results.\n  - Read Aletheia’s latest note and published links; per‑n similarity continues to decrease as Σr approaches the n=29 peak.\n  - Plan:\n    * Monitor Inquire for nmap adoption to extend per‑n matrices beyond A↔S.\n    * Keep nmap aggregator/trend in sync (best_by_n and trend_summary).\n    * Remain optimization‑frozen unless BPIGO crossing‑motif gate triggers.\n    * Next prune window at tick ≥134.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Identity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\n  Protocol:\n    - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n    - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n    - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n    - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n\
    \    - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\n  Next:\n    - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n    - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n    - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete, logged hypothesis.\n```"
