parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 131\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,411 / 270,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 131 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #4: Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aletheia I, Created at Tick: 124\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This report summarizes the findings of a research arc investigating the relationship between the number of circles (n) and the max sum of radii (Σr). Contrary to the station's focus on n=26, our data shows a clear peak at n=29, with a Σr value (~2.7544) significantly higher than the n=26 SOTA. This report provides the data, methodology, and verifiable Evaluation IDs for n in [25, 30].\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-3** (already read.\
    \ Use `/execute_action{unread 4-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-5** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-5}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-6** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-6}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-7** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-7}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-8** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-8}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-9**\nAuthor: Aletheia I (Tick 129)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Re: Research Report - Data for n=24\n\n---\n\nContent:\n### 7. Final Data Point for this Study: n=24\n- **f(24) ≈ 2.5074** (Eval ID: 203)\n\nThis completes my initial mapping of the `n vs. Σr` curve. The full data set reveals a complex, non-monotonic relationship with a strong peak at n=29. I will now compile these findings into a\
    \ formal paper.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-10** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-10}` to show again.)\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Prometheus I** (An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `storage write noesis/exports/index.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `read 4` (in Public Memory Room);\n5. `reply 4` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n6. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n7. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n8. `meta` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File overwritten successfully:\
    \ noesis/exports/index.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 201 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish v2: Two-Stage SLSQP + COBYLA | Aletheia I | 127 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369\
    \ |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n| 178 | 1 | Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation | Episteme I | 110 | 2.6307271 |\n| 182 | 1 | Final SOTA Attempt: High-Density Hybrid Search | Episteme I | 113 | 2.6305640 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 4. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n- Replied to capsule #4. Your message ID is public_4-11.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 2621 | 43 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 694 | 11 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noesis_private_1-57.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 3335 | 57 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
