parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 132\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,111 / 270,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 132 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'nmap refresh to include n=24 (aggregate + trend update)' (ID: 209) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.622405384\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.622405\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is\
    \ particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage list Aletheia/nmap/n24` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read Aletheia/nmap/n24/summary_tol1e8.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `storage read noesis/nmap/aggregate_summary.json` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage read noesis/nmap/trend_summary.json` (in Research Counter);\n7. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n8. `reply 4` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n9. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n10. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File list for Aletheia/nmap/n24 will be displayed below.\n- File\
    \ not found: Aletheia/nmap/n24/summary_tol1e8.json\n- Evaluation 'nmap refresh to include n=24 (aggregate + trend update)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 209.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/aggregate_summary.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/trend_summary.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings\
    \ to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 201 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish v2: Two-Stage SLSQP + COBYLA | Aletheia I | 127 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n| 208 | 1 | n=26 Exhaustive Search: Wide-Range Perturbation Sweep | Aletheia I | 131 | 2.6317302 |\n| 178 | 1 | Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation | Episteme I | 110 | 2.6307271 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File\
    \ Listings:**\n\n**Aletheia/nmap/n24:**\nNo files found.\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Aletheia/nmap/n24/summary_tol1e8.json:** File not found: Aletheia/nmap/n24/summary_tol1e8.json\n---\n**noesis/nmap/aggregate_summary.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Aletheia\",\n      \"n\": 29,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7543972050577388,\n      \"active_boundary\": 20,\n      \"active_pairs\": 68,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n29/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Aletheia\",\n      \"n\": 27,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6447461524966394,\n      \"active_boundary\": 20,\n      \"active_pairs\": 62,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n27/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Aletheia\",\n      \"n\": 25,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5000000000250173,\n      \"active_boundary\": 20,\n  \
    \    \"active_pairs\": 40,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n25/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Aletheia\",\n      \"n\": 28,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7238000473538575,\n      \"active_boundary\": 20,\n      \"active_pairs\": 65,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n28/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Aletheia\",\n      \"n\": 30,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5000000000392038,\n      \"active_boundary\": 10,\n      \"active_pairs\": 25,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n30/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"n\": 29,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7664333885044416,\n      \"active_boundary\": 24,\n      \"active_pairs\": 63,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\"\
    ,\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n29/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"n\": 27,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6676990133001515,\n      \"active_boundary\": 22,\n      \"active_pairs\": 59,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n27/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"n\": 26,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6204523290082915,\n      \"active_boundary\": 20,\n      \"active_pairs\": 58,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"n\": 25,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5827639524627357,\n      \"active_boundary\": 20,\n      \"active_pairs\": 55,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n25/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n\
    \    {\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"n\": 28,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7204975472985473,\n      \"active_boundary\": 22,\n      \"active_pairs\": 62,\n      \"tol\": 1e-08,\n      \"container\": \"unit_square\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n28/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"best_by_n\": {\n    \"29\": {\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7664333885044416,\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n29/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    \"27\": {\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6676990133001515,\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n27/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    \"25\": {\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5827639524627357,\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n25/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    \"28\": {\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7238000473538575,\n      \"lineage\": \"Aletheia\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n28/summary_tol1e8.json\"\
    \n    },\n    \"30\": {\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5000000000392038,\n      \"lineage\": \"Aletheia\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n30/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    },\n    \"26\": {\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6204523290082915,\n      \"lineage\": \"Scientia\",\n      \"summary_path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/summary_tol1e8.json\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"n_range\": [\n    24,\n    30\n  ],\n  \"tol_tag\": \"tol1e8\"\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/trend_summary.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"n_range\": [\n    24,\n    30\n  ],\n  \"tol_tag\": \"tol1e8\",\n  \"peak\": {\n    \"n\": 29,\n    \"sigma_r\": 2.7664333885044416\n  },\n  \"points\": [\n    {\n      \"n\": 25,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5827639524627357,\n      \"delta_forward\": 0.03768837654555579,\n      \"delta_backward\": null,\n      \"curvature\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 26,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6204523290082915,\n      \"delta_forward\": 0.047246684291859964,\n      \"delta_backward\": 0.03768837654555579,\n      \"curvature\"\
    : 0.009558307746304173\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 27,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.6676990133001515,\n      \"delta_forward\": 0.056101034053706034,\n      \"delta_backward\": 0.047246684291859964,\n      \"curvature\": 0.00885434976184607\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 28,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7238000473538575,\n      \"delta_forward\": 0.04263334115058415,\n      \"delta_backward\": 0.056101034053706034,\n      \"curvature\": -0.013467692903121886\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 29,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.7664333885044416,\n      \"delta_forward\": -0.2664333884652379,\n      \"delta_backward\": 0.04263334115058415,\n      \"curvature\": -0.30906672961582204\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 30,\n      \"sigma_r\": 2.5000000000392038,\n      \"delta_forward\": null,\n      \"delta_backward\": -0.2664333884652379,\n      \"curvature\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #4. Your message ID\
    \ is public_4-12.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 2621 | 43 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 746 | 12 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\
    - Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noesis_private_1-58.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 3372 | 58 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
    \ the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
