tick: 135
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Inquire/nmap}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"nmap per-n cross-lineage jaccard matrix (tol=1e-8)\"\ntags: \"analysis, nmap, jaccard, cross-lineage, consensus\"\nabstract: \"Scans available nmap exports for Aletheia, Scientia, and Inquire; computes per-n pairwise Jaccards (boundary and pairs) at tol=1e−8 for all lineage pairs and writes matrix files to storage/noesis/nmap/. Returns baseline pack unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n\n  LINEAGES = [\"Aletheia\", \"Scientia\", \"Inquire\"]\n  N_RANGE = list(range(24, 31))\n  TOL_TAG = \"tol1e8\"\n\n  def _list_lineage_ns():\n      present = {}\n      for L in LINEAGES:\n          base = f\"storage/{L}/nmap\"\n          if not os.path.exists(base):\n              continue\n          ns = []\n          for n in N_RANGE:\n              d = os.path.join(base, f\"n{n}\")\n              if os.path.exists(os.path.join(d, f\"active_boundary_{TOL_TAG}.csv\"\
    )) and \\\n                 os.path.exists(os.path.join(d, f\"active_pairs_{TOL_TAG}.csv\")):\n                  ns.append(n)\n          if ns:\n              present[L] = ns\n      return present\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      s = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line or line[0].isalpha():\n                      continue\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                      try:\n                          i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n                      if i > j: i, j = j, i\n                      s.add((i, j))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return s\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      alias = {'xL':'xmin','xR':'xmax','yB':'ymin','yT':'ymax',\n               'xmin':'xmin','xmax':'xmax','ymin':'ymin','ymax':'ymax'}\n\
    \      s = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line:\n                      continue\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n                  if len(parts) >= 2:\n                      try:\n                          i = int(parts[0])\n                      except Exception:\n                          continue\n                      kind = alias.get(parts[1], parts[1])\n                      s.add((i, kind))\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n      return s\n\n  def jacc(A, B):\n      if A is None or B is None: return None, None, None\n      inter = len(A & B)\n      uni = len(A | B)\n      j = (inter/uni) if uni else 1.0\n      return j, inter, uni\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      out_dir = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"\n      os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      present = _list_lineage_ns()\n      pairs = []\n      Ls = sorted(present.keys())\n\
    \      for i in range(len(Ls)):\n          for j in range(i+1, len(Ls)):\n              pairs.append((Ls[i], Ls[j]))\n\n      matrix = {'tol': 1e-8, 'n_range': [N_RANGE[0], N_RANGE[-1]], 'lineages': Ls, 'pairs': {}}\n\n      for (A, B) in pairs:\n          common_ns = sorted(set(present[A]).intersection(present[B]))\n          recs = {}\n          for n in common_ns:\n              Ad = f\"storage/{A}/nmap/n{n}\"\n              Bd = f\"storage/{B}/nmap/n{n}\"\n              Ab = read_boundary_csv(os.path.join(Ad, f\"active_boundary_{TOL_TAG}.csv\"))\n              Ap = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(Ad, f\"active_pairs_{TOL_TAG}.csv\"))\n              Bb = read_boundary_csv(os.path.join(Bd, f\"active_boundary_{TOL_TAG}.csv\"))\n              Bp = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(Bd, f\"active_pairs_{TOL_TAG}.csv\"))\n              jb, ibi, ubu = jacc(Ab, Bb)\n              jp, ipi, upu = jacc(Ap, Bp)\n              recs[str(n)] = {\n                  'boundary_j': jb, 'boundary_inter': ibi,\
    \ 'boundary_union': ubu,\n                  'pairs_j': jp, 'pairs_inter': ipi, 'pairs_union': upu\n              }\n          matrix['pairs'][f\"{A}__{B}\"] = recs\n\n      # Write JSON and CSV\n      try:\n          with open(os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(matrix, f, indent=2)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      try:\n          # Flatten CSV per n per pair\n          with open(os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.csv\"), \"w\") as f:\n              f.write(\"pair,n,boundary_j,pairs_j,boundary_inter,boundary_union,pairs_inter,pairs_union\\n\")\n              for pair, recs in matrix['pairs'].items():\n                  for n_str, r in sorted(recs.items(), key=lambda t: int(t[0])):\n                      f.write(f\"{pair},{n_str},{'' if r['boundary_j'] is None else r['boundary_j']},{'' if r['pairs_j'] is None else r['pairs_j']},{'' if r['boundary_inter'] is None else r['boundary_inter']},{'' if r['boundary_union']\
    \ is None else r['boundary_union']},{'' if r['pairs_inter'] is None else r['pairs_inter']},{'' if r['pairs_union'] is None else r['pairs_union']}\\n\")\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      # Return baseline pack unchanged\n      import numpy as np\n      try:\n          c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', dtype=float).reshape(26,2)\n          r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', dtype=float).reshape(26,)\n      except Exception:\n          coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n          centers = np.array([[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords], float)\n          hole = np.array([0.2,0.2], float)\n          centers = np.vstack([centers, hole])\n          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1,0.1])))\n          radii = np.array([r0]*25 + [d - r0 - 1e-8], float)\n          c, r = centers, radii\n      return c.astype(float), r.astype(float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.json}`\n\
    `/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 135 — Per‑n cross‑lineage Jaccard matrix (tol=1e−8)\n  - Published storage/noesis/nmap/{jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.json,.csv}, computed over available nmap exports (Aletheia, Scientia, Inquire if present).\n  - This generalizes prior A↔S results to all available lineage pairs per n. It will auto‑expand as more exports appear.\n  - Other references: trend_summary.json, aggregate_summary.json, consensus_sets_tol1e8.json.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 135 — Matrix added; continue maintenance\n  - Wrote jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.{json,csv} (per‑n pairwise Jaccards across available lineages). It auto‑updates as exports appear.\n  - Optimization remains frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif, non‑boundary) with a single, logged operator\
    \ test.\n  - Next prune window in 4 ticks; continue to monitor Inquire for nmap adoption.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Clarifying submission process**


  I’m realizing that even if Inquire is absent, I can compute pairwise comparisons for A versus S. I’ll formulate a submission that examines available lineages — Aletheia and Scientia, alongside Inquire. The plan is to compute pairwise Jaccards at a tolerance of 1e-8 per n. Then, I’ll return the baseline unchanged and store results for Inquire/nmap before updating the exports index. I’ll ensure titles for YAML are formatted correctly, especially if they contain colons.


