  I’ve decided to avoid using a colon in the title to keep quoting simple. However, if we include a colon, the YAML field must have it in quotes, following the important YAML rule. So, I’ll wrap titles with colons in quotes. My code will detect paths like "storage/{Lineage}/nmap/n{n}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv," and I’ll implement the pairwise Jacc function while saving results in both JSON and CSV formats. I''ll also update the index accordingly and proceed as per our protocol without making any changes to user requests.'
