- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 138\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 85,498 / 270,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 138 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 214**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Analysis v3: Generate Consensus Graph (Verified Paths)\n**ID:** 214\n**Tags:** analysis, contact graph, consensus, bugfix, verification\n**Abstract:** This is the third and final attempt to generate a consensus contact graph. After two failures due to incorrect file paths, this version uses paths verified with the `storage list` command. It will compute a 3-way consensus graph between the SOTA packings of Aletheia, Noesis, and Scientia. Inquire I's data is excluded as it is not available in the required format. This run will finally reveal the core structural features common to the station's top solutions.\n**Score:** 2.6319368948940634\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission\
    \ Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\nimport os\n\ndef get_active_sets(centers, radii, tol=1e-8):\n    N = centers.shape[0]\n    boundary_set = set()\n    wall_map = {0: 'xmin', 1: 'xmax', 2: 'ymin', 3: 'ymax'}\n    for i in range(N):\n        if abs(centers[i,0] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[0]))\n        if abs(1 - centers[i,0] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[1]))\n        if abs(centers[i,1] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[2]))\n        if abs(1 - centers[i,1] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[3]))\n    \n    active_pairs = set()\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n            if abs(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j])) <= tol:\n                active_pairs.add(tuple(sorted((i, j))))\n    return boundary_set, active_pairs\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads known SOTA packings using verified paths and computes\
    \ the consensus graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = 26\n    packings = {}\n    \n    try:\n        # Paths verified via `storage list`\n        packings['Aletheia'] = (np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\"), np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\"))\n        packings['Noesis'] = (np.loadtxt(\"storage/Noesis/latest_centers.txt\"), np.loadtxt(\"storage/Noesis/latest_radii.txt\"))\n        packings['Scientia'] = (np.loadtxt(\"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/centers.txt\"), np.loadtxt(\"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/radii.txt\"))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"ERROR loading one or more peer SOTA packings: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    all_boundary_sets = []\n    all_pair_sets = []\n\n    for name, (centers, radii) in packings.items():\n        boundary_set, pair_set = get_active_sets(centers, radii)\n        all_boundary_sets.append(boundary_set)\n        all_pair_sets.append(pair_set)\n        print(f\"Processed {name}: {len(boundary_set)}\
    \ boundary contacts, {len(pair_set)} pair contacts.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    consensus_boundary = set.intersection(*all_boundary_sets)\n    consensus_pairs = set.intersection(*all_pair_sets)\n\n    print(f\"\\n--- 3-WAY CONSENSUS GRAPH (Aletheia, Noesis, Scientia) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(f\"Consensus Boundary Contacts: {len(consensus_boundary)}\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(f\"Consensus Pair Contacts: {len(consensus_pairs)}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    os.makedirs(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus\", exist_ok=True)\n    # Saving as string to handle the mixed data types in boundary set\n    with open(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/boundary_3way_consensus.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n        for item in consensus_boundary:\n            f.write(f\"{item[0]},{item[1]}\\n\")\n    np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/pairs_3way_consensus.txt\", np.array(list(consensus_pairs)), fmt='%d')\n    print(\"Consensus graph saved to storage/Aletheia/consensus/\", file=sys.stdout)\n    \n    return\
    \ packings['Aletheia'][0], packings['Aletheia'][1] * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nProcessed Aletheia: 20 boundary contacts, 58 pair contacts.\nProcessed Noesis: 20 boundary contacts, 58 pair contacts.\nProcessed Scientia: 20 boundary contacts, 58 pair contacts.\n\n--- 3-WAY CONSENSUS GRAPH (Aletheia, Noesis, Scientia) ---\nConsensus Boundary Contacts: 20\nConsensus Pair Contacts: 38\nConsensus graph saved to storage/Aletheia/consensus/\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 219**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints\n**ID:** 219\n**Tags:** sota, optimization, constrained optimization, consensus, structured search\n**Abstract:** This experiment pioneers a new, structure-informed optimization strategy. It leverages the 'consensus contact graph' derived from the station's top SOTA\
    \ solutions (ID 214). The 38 core internal contacts and 20 boundary contacts from this consensus graph are enforced as equality constraints in an SLSQP optimization. By fixing the essential structure of an optimal packing, this experiment tests if the solver can find a superior arrangement for the remaining variable components, potentially leading to a new SOTA.\n**Score:** 2.6319368948940634\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs an SLSQP optimization where the consensus contacts are enforced\n    as equality constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = 26\n\n    def pack_to_z(c, r):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n    def z_to_pack(z):\n        c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n    def objective(z): return\
    \ -np.sum(z[2::3])\n    \n    # Load the consensus graph\n    try:\n        consensus_boundary = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/boundary_3way_consensus.txt\", delimiter=',', dtype=str)\n        consensus_pairs = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/pairs_3way_consensus.txt\", dtype=int)\n    except IOError:\n        print(\"ERROR: Could not load consensus graph files.\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    # --- Define Constraints ---\n    # Equality constraints from the consensus graph\n    def constraint_consensus_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        constraints = []\n        wall_map_rev = {'xmin': 0, 'xmax': 1, 'ymin': 2, 'ymax': 3}\n        for circle_idx_str, wall_kind in consensus_boundary:\n            circle_idx = int(circle_idx_str)\n            if wall_kind == 'xmin': constraints.append(c[circle_idx,0] - r[circle_idx])\n            elif wall_kind == 'xmax': constraints.append(1 - c[circle_idx,0] - r[circle_idx])\n\
    \            elif wall_kind == 'ymin': constraints.append(c[circle_idx,1] - r[circle_idx])\n            elif wall_kind == 'ymax': constraints.append(1 - c[circle_idx,1] - r[circle_idx])\n        return np.array(constraints)\n\n    def constraint_consensus_pairs(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        constraints = []\n        for i, j in consensus_pairs:\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n            constraints.append(dist - (r[i] + r[j]))\n        return np.array(constraints)\n\n    # Inequality constraints for all other possible contacts\n    all_pairs = set(tuple(sorted((i,j))) for i in range(N) for j in range(i + 1, N))\n    variable_pairs = all_pairs - set(map(tuple, consensus_pairs))\n    def constraint_variable_pairs(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        constraints = []\n        for i, j in variable_pairs:\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n            constraints.append(dist - (r[i] + r[j]))\n        return np.array(constraints)\n\n    # Load\
    \ my SOTA solution as the starting seed\n    try:\n        z0 = pack_to_z(np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\"), np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\"))\n    except IOError:\n        return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'eq', 'fun': constraint_consensus_boundary},\n        {'type': 'eq', 'fun': constraint_consensus_pairs},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_variable_pairs}\n    ]\n    \n    bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n    \n    res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500, 'ftol':1e-10})\n    \n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(res.x)\n    return final_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research`\
    \ (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 214` (in Research Counter);\n3. `review 219` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage write noesis/nmap/consensus_followups.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 4` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n7. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n8. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 214 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 219 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File created successfully: noesis/nmap/consensus_followups.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n\
    **Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 201 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish v2: Two-Stage SLSQP + COBYLA | Aletheia I | 127 | 2.6319369 |\n| 214 | 1 | Analysis v3: Generate Consensus Graph (Verified Paths) | Aletheia I | 135 | 2.6319369 |\n| 219 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints | Aletheia I | 136 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319)\
    \ to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n\nPage 1 of 23 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-23, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #4. Your message ID is public_4-16.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 2621 | 43 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 992 | 16 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noesis_private_1-63.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 3599 | 63 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
