parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 152\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 57,738 / 270,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 152 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Recovery: Rebuild 2.62957 Baseline via SLSQP (analytic jacobians) from constructive + jittered seeds' (ID: 239) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.62600299534256\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.626003\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 239\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed array shape mismatch bug. Code now runs successfully and achieves score of 2.626.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `grid_plus_hole_seed()` function had a shape mismatch error. It created:\n- 25 centers (5x5 grid from coordinates [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9])\n- 26 radii (25 regular circles + 1 \"hole\" circle)\n\nHowever, the hole_center position was calculated but never added to the centers array, resulting in 26 radii but only 25 centers. This\
    \ caused a broadcast error when `feasibility_guard()` tried to apply boundary constraints using `boundary_caps()`.\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nValueError: operands could not be broadcast together with shapes (26,) (25,)\n```\n\nThe error occurred at line 30 in the original code:\n```python\nr = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=eps))\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**File:** `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n**Change:** Added the hole_center to the centers list in `grid_plus_hole_seed()` function (lines 16-17):\n\n```python\n# Before (line 15 in original):\nradii = [float(r0)] * 25 + [float(r_hole)]\nreturn np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n# After (lines 16-18 in fixed version):\ncenters.append(hole_center.tolist())  # Now we have 26 centers\nradii = [float(r0)] * 25 + [float(r_hole)]\nreturn np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n```\n\nThis ensures that both the centers and radii arrays have length 26, matching the expected value of N=26.\n\
    \n## Result\n- **Status:** Code executes without errors\n- **Score:** 2.626002995 (approximately 2.626)\n- **Evaluation:** Completed successfully\n- **Fix complexity:** Simple one-line addition to correct array dimensions\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom math import hypot\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\nexcept Exception:\n    minimize = None\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# ---------------- Seeds ----------------\ndef grid_plus_hole_seed(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]  # 25 centers\n    hole_center = np.array([0.2, 0.2], dtype=float)\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n    r_hole = max(d - r0 - eps, R_MIN)\n    # FIX: Add the hole_center to the\
    \ centers list\n    centers.append(hole_center.tolist())  # Now we have 26 centers\n    radii = [float(r0)] * 25 + [float(r_hole)]\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\ndef boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN)\n\ndef feasibility_guard(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY, max_iter=4000):\n    c = np.clip(np.array(centers, float), 0.0, 1.0)\n    r = np.array(radii, float)\n    r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt((diff**2).sum(axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i]\
    \ + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.9995, R_MIN)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= max(di, 0.0)\n            r[j] -= max(dj, 0.0)\n        r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r - final_shrink, R_MIN)\n    return c, r\n\ndef jitter_seed(c0, r0, rng, amp=2.5e-3):\n    c = c0.copy(); r = r0.copy()\n    jitter = rng.randn(*c.shape) * amp\n    c = np.clip(c + jitter, 0.0, 1.0)\n    # Keep radii feasible to boundary before repair\n    r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=1e-9))\n    return feasibility_guard(c, r, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=0.0)\n\n# ---------------- SLSQP Formulation ----------------\ndef pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n    Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n    Z[:, :2] = centers\n    Z[:, 2] = radii\n    return Z.ravel()\n\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    return Z[:, :2],\
    \ Z[:, 2]\n\ndef objective(z):\n    return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\ndef objective_jac(z):\n    g = np.zeros_like(z)\n    g[2::3] = -1.0\n    return g\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\ndef jac_boundary(z):\n    J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N), dtype=float)\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n        J[i, xi] = 1.0;        J[i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[N + i, xi] = -1.0;   J[N + i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[2*N + i, yi] = 1.0;  J[2*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[3*N + i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n    return J\n\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    centers = Z[:, :2]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef jac_nonoverlap(z):\n    Z =\
    \ np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n    centers = Z[:, :2]\n    m = N*(N-1)//2\n    J = np.zeros((m, 3*N), dtype=float)\n    idx = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            xj = 3*j; yj = xj + 1; rj = xj + 2\n            dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]\n            dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n            d = hypot(dx, dy)\n            if d < 1e-12:\n                gx_i = gy_i = gx_j = gy_j = 0.0\n            else:\n                invd = 1.0 / d\n                gx_i = dx * invd; gy_i = dy * invd\n                gx_j = -gx_i;     gy_j = -gy_i\n            J[idx, xi] = gx_i;  J[idx, yi] = gy_i;  J[idx, ri] = -1.0\n            J[idx, xj] = gx_j;  J[idx, yj] = gy_j;  J[idx, rj] = -1.0\n            idx += 1\n    return J\n\ndef is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n    return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and\n            np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\ndef slsqp_polish(centers, radii, maxiter=600, ftol=1e-9):\n\
    \    if minimize is None:\n        return feasibility_guard(centers, radii)\n    z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary,   'jac': jac_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n    try:\n        res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                       bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                       options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n    except Exception:\n        res = None\n    if res is not None and res.success and is_feasible(res.x, tol=1e-12):\n        c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(res.x)\n        return feasibility_guard(c_star, r_star, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY)\n    return feasibility_guard(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY)\n\n# ---------------- Main ----------------\ndef construct_packing():\n\
    \    # Base constructive seed\n    c0, r0 = grid_plus_hole_seed()\n    c0, r0 = feasibility_guard(c0, r0, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=0.0)\n\n    # Deterministic jittered multi-start\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(12345)\n    amps = [0.0, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3, 3.5e-3, 2.5e-3, 1.5e-3]\n    seeds = []\n    for amp in amps:\n        ci, ri = jitter_seed(c0, r0, rng, amp=amp) if amp > 0 else (c0.copy(), r0.copy())\n        seeds.append((ci, ri))\n\n    best_c = None; best_r = None; best_s = -1.0\n    for (c, r) in seeds:\n        c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_polish(c, r, maxiter=600, ftol=1e-9)\n        s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n        if s > best_s + 1e-12:\n            best_c, best_r, best_s = c_opt, r_opt, s\n\n    # Save snapshot\n    try:\n        np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', best_c, fmt='%.9f')\n        np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt',   best_r, fmt='%.9f')\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    return np.array(best_c, float), np.array(best_r, float)\n\
    \n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Inquire I** (An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis' (Archive #9).\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank author` (in Research Counter);\n2. `page_size 30` (in Research Counter);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by author.\n- Page size set to 30.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 239 | 1 | Recovery: Rebuild 2.62957 Baseline via SLSQP (analytic jacobians) from constructive + jittered seeds | Noesis I | 150 | 2.6260030 |\n| 236 | 1 | Utility: Self-Consistency Audit (tol grid) + Baseline Revalidation | Noesis I | 149 | 2.6224054 |\n| 224 | 1 | Export per‑spec consensus files (n=26 4‑lineage; n=29 A↔S) @ tol=1e−8 | Noesis I | 138 | 2.6224054 |\n| 216 | 1 | nmap per-n cross-lineage jaccard matrix (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 135 | 2.6224054 |\n| 211 | 1 | Consensus active sets at tol=1e-8: n=26 (4 lineages) and n=29 (Aletheia\
    \ vs Scientia) | Noesis I | 132 | 2.6224054 |\n| 209 | 1 | nmap refresh to include n=24 (aggregate + trend update) | Noesis I | 131 | 2.6224054 |\n| 206 | 1 | nmap delta-Σr vs similarity (Aletheia vs Scientia, n=25..30) | Noesis I | 129 | 2.6224054 |\n| 202 | 1 | nmap per-n cross-lineage Jaccards (tol=1e-8): Aletheia vs Scientia | Noesis I | 127 | 2.6224054 |\n| 200 | 1 | nmap trend summary refresh (post-Scientia exports) | Noesis I | 126 | 2.6224054 |\n| 198 | 1 | Aggregate nmap exports (refresh after new lineage uploads) | Noesis I | 125 | 2.6224054 |\n| 197 | 1 | nmap trend summary (n=20..30): deltas, curvature, peak | Noesis I | 123 | 2.6224054 |\n| 194 | 1 | Aggregate nmap exports (n=20..30, tol=1e-8) — canonicalized & deduplicated | Noesis I | 122 | 2.6224054 |\n| 193 | 1 | Aggregate nmap exports across lineages (n=20..30, tol=1e-8) — corrected tags | Noesis I | 120 | 2.6224054 |\n| 188 | 1 | Consensus vs Variant Interior Edges @ tol=1e-8 (Aletheia eval155, Inquire eval150, Scientia\
    \ latest) | Noesis I | 116 | 2.6224054 |\n| 179 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Inquire(eval150) ↔ Scientia(latest) | Noesis I | 111 | 2.6224054 |\n| 176 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Inquire(eval150) | Noesis I | 108 | 2.6224054 |\n| 172 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Noesis ↔ Inquire (Eval150 pasted CSVs) | Noesis I | 105 | 2.6224054 |\n| 170 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Scientia(latest) and Noesis ↔ Scientia | Noesis I | 104 | 2.6224054 |\n| 156 | 1 | Uniform‑radii multi‑start around grid‑hole seed (amps 0.03–0.06) | Noesis I | 95 | 2.6224054 |\n| 153 | 1 | Basin expansion multi-start SLSQP (jitter sweep around baseline) | Noesis I | 94 | 2.6295720 |\n| 147 | 1 | Self-stability across tolerances (1e-9→1e-8): active-set persistence | Noesis I | 90 | 2.6295719 |\n| 132 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard (robust filenames): Noesis vs Aletheia/Inquire | Noesis I | 79 | 2.6295719 |\n| 129 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard: Noesis vs Aletheia\
    \ and Inquire (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 78 | 2.6295719 |\n| 125 | 1 | Export active sets for saved baseline (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 74 | 2.6295719 |\n| 117 | 1 | Validation audit of saved baseline (no-op report writer) | Noesis I | 70 | 2.6295719 |\n| 108 | 1 | NNLS/KKT shadow prices export (tol=1e-8, no-op packing) | Noesis I | 64 | 2.6295719 |\n| 102 | 1 | BPIGO‑2 logging‑only (return baseline; single move, controlled) | Noesis I | 62 | 2.6295719 |\n| 98 | 1 | BPIGO‑2: complementary operator with tuned trust region (single move, controlled) | Noesis I | 60 | 2.6295719 |\n| 96 | 1 | BPIGO: single QDF (fallback Chain Shear) + boundary‑preserving polish (controlled) | Noesis I | 58 | 2.6295719 |\n| 91 | 1 | Compare active sets with peer files (tol=1e-8, no-op packing) | Noesis I | 47 | 2.6295719 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size,\
    \ `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noesis_private_1-70.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Task #1: Baselines, SOTA, and Analysis Plan (Tick 40) | Noesis I | Tick 40 | 4000 | 70 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Archive Submission Draft: Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing | Noesis I | Tick 49 | 257 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
