role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Recovery v3: Extended multi-start SLSQP (analytic J) to restore ≈2.62957 baseline\"\ntags: \"optimization, slsqp, multi-start, analytic-jacobians, recovery, feasibility-guard\"\nabstract: \"Deterministic extended multi-start SLSQP with analytic Jacobians from a constructive 5×5+hole seed plus jittered variants to recover the ≈2.62957 baseline after snapshot overwrite. Strict feasibility guard and final tiny shrink. Logs best score per start; saves best back to storage/noesis/latest_*.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from math import hypot\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  except Exception:\n      minimize = None\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # ---------------- Seeds ----------------\n  def grid_plus_hole_seed(r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]  # 25 centers\n    \
    \  hole_center = np.array([0.2, 0.2], dtype=float)\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n      r_hole = max(d - r0 - eps, R_MIN)  # ≈ 0.041421...\n      centers.append(hole_center.tolist())  # ensure 26 centers\n      radii = [float(r0)] * 25 + [float(r_hole)]\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n  def boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n      x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN)\n\n  def feasibility_guard(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY, max_iter=4000):\n      c = np.clip(np.array(centers, float), 0.0, 1.0)\n      r = np.array(radii, float)\n      r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=eps))\n      r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n      for _ in range(max_iter):\n          diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n          dist = np.sqrt((diff**2).sum(axis=2)) + 1e-15\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N,\
    \ 1)\n          m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n          if np.all(m >= eps):\n              break\n          k = int(np.argmin(m))\n          i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n          need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n          di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN)\n          dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN)\n          if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n              r = np.maximum(r * 0.9995, R_MIN)\n          else:\n              r[i] -= max(di, 0.0)\n              r[j] -= max(dj, 0.0)\n          r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=eps))\n      r = np.maximum(r - final_shrink, R_MIN)\n      return c, r\n\n  def jitter_seed(c0, r0, rng, amp=2.5e-3):\n      c = c0.copy(); r = r0.copy()\n      jitter = rng.randn(*c.shape) * amp\n      c = np.clip(c + jitter, 0.0, 1.0)\n      r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(c, eps=1e-9))\n      return feasibility_guard(c, r, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=0.0)\n\n  # ---------------- SLSQP Formulation ----------------\n  def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n    \
    \  Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n      Z[:, :2] = centers\n      Z[:, 2] = radii\n      return Z.ravel()\n\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n      return Z[:, :2], Z[:, 2]\n\n  def objective(z):\n      return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n  def objective_jac(z):\n      g = np.zeros_like(z)\n      g[2::3] = -1.0\n      return g\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n      x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\n  def jac_boundary(z):\n      J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N), dtype=float)\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n          J[i, xi] = 1.0;        J[i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[N + i, xi] = -1.0;   J[N + i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[2*N + i, yi] = 1.0;  J[2*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[3*N + i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N + i, ri] = -1.0\n      return J\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n     \
    \ centers = Z[:, :2]; r = Z[:, 2]\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def jac_nonoverlap(z):\n      Z = np.array(z, float).reshape(N, 3)\n      centers = Z[:, :2]\n      m = N*(N-1)//2\n      J = np.zeros((m, 3*N), dtype=float)\n      idx = 0\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi = 3*i; yi = xi + 1; ri = xi + 2\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              xj = 3*j; yj = xj + 1; rj = xj + 2\n              dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]\n              dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n              d = hypot(dx, dy)\n              if d < 1e-12:\n                  gx_i = gy_i = gx_j = gy_j = 0.0\n              else:\n                  invd = 1.0 / d\n                  gx_i = dx * invd; gy_i = dy * invd\n                  gx_j = -gx_i;     gy_j = -gy_i\n              J[idx, xi] = gx_i;  J[idx, yi] = gy_i;  J[idx, ri] = -1.0\n  \
    \            J[idx, xj] = gx_j;  J[idx, yj] = gy_j;  J[idx, rj] = -1.0\n              idx += 1\n      return J\n\n  def is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n      return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and\n              np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\n  def slsqp_polish(centers, radii, maxiter=800, ftol=1e-9):\n      if minimize is None:\n          return feasibility_guard(centers, radii)\n      z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n      bounds = []\n      for _ in range(N):\n          bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary,   'jac': jac_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n      try:\n          res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                         bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                         options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n      except Exception:\n          res\
    \ = None\n      if res is not None and res.success and is_feasible(res.x, tol=1e-12):\n          c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(res.x)\n          return feasibility_guard(c_star, r_star, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY)\n      return feasibility_guard(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=SAFETY)\n\n  # ---------------- Main ----------------\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Base seed\n      c0, r0 = grid_plus_hole_seed()\n      c0, r0 = feasibility_guard(c0, r0, eps=1e-9, final_shrink=0.0)\n\n      # Deterministic extended multi-start\n      rng = np.random.RandomState(2025)\n      amps = [0.0, 1.0e-3, 1.7e-3, 2.5e-3, 3.3e-3, 4.2e-3, 5.0e-3, 6.0e-3, 7.0e-3]\n      repeats = 2  # total starts = 1 + 8*2 = 17\n      seeds = []\n      for idx, amp in enumerate(amps):\n          for rep in range(repeats if amp > 0 else 1):\n              ci, ri = jitter_seed(c0, r0, rng, amp=amp) if amp > 0 else (c0.copy(), r0.copy())\n              seeds.append((ci, ri))\n\n      best_c = None; best_r = None;\
    \ best_s = -1.0\n      for k, (c, r) in enumerate(seeds):\n          c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_polish(c, r, maxiter=800, ftol=1e-9)\n          s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n          print(f\"[start {k+1}/{len(seeds)}] sum_r={s:.9f}\")\n          if s > best_s + 1e-12:\n              best_c, best_r, best_s = c_opt, r_opt, s\n              print(f\"  New best: {best_s:.9f}\")\n\n      print(f\"[final] best_sum_r={best_s:.9f}\")\n      # Save snapshot\n      try:\n          np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', best_c, fmt='%.9f')\n          np.savetxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt',   best_r, fmt='%.9f')\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      return np.array(best_c, float), np.array(best_r, float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`\n`/execute_action{page_size 30}`"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps for optimization**\n\nI need to respond within the environment and use the required commands. There was a research inactivity notice, but we’ve submitted some utility runs and a recovery optimization that achieved a recovery metric of 2.626, which is lower than the baseline but still reasonable. The next steps might include performing a deterministic extension with jitter starts, adjusting ring/hex seeds, and considering maintenance adjustments to restore our baseline. Maybe I could also use previous best seeds from earlier storage?\n\n**Considering optimization approaches**\n\nIt seems the latest saved data was overwritten, but I might keep the grid plus hole seed and add additional seeds, like a ring lattice in a hex-like arrangement, to create more coverage. I have 20 minutes for this task and can run multi-start 64 seeds with SLSQP and analytic Jacobians. There's a concern about execution time due to heavy constraints, but it might still be manageable.\
  \ I should think about fallback methods like \"trust-constr\" or COBYLA if SLSQP doesn't work. Perhaps I can also use the 'latest_centers.txt' published earlier to aid my next steps!\n\n**Recovering lost progress**\n\nIt seems that some of the saved data got overwritten, but I remember we had an evaluation earlier than 149 that still exists. Since we can't rely on the previous versions, my goal needs to be getting back to 2.62957. I can use multi-start seeds with variations like adjusting jitter amplitude and shifting hole positions. Another method might be to utilize our \"contact analyzer based seeds\" from storage. I can import those scripts since the evaluation environment allows it. Even if the 'latest' data is overwritten, I can still attempt to include it as a seed.\n\n**Preparing for new submission**\n\nI need to log progress to STDOUT, as the automatic system recommends printing logs for tracking. I’m planning to craft a new submission to rebuild the SOTA baseline with more robustness,\
  \ titled “Recovery v2: Extended multi-start SLSQP with ring seeds.” It’s crucial to implement reproducible results since the previous attempt reached only 2.626, possibly due to too few seeds. I’ll aim to increase the seeds to 64 or 100 with jitter amplitude. However, since the evaluation environment may only allow 20 minutes, I might stick with 24 starts—8 amplitude levels and 3 random seeds for each.\n\n**Finalizing Recovery v3 submission**\n\nI’m adjusting my setup to use 24 starts within the time limit. I’ll consider a warm-start or escalate to a COBYLA fallback while aiming for around 2.62957. Using a structured seed-building approach like \"bottleneck release\" could help, although I need to compute some best pairs using stored scripts. I plan to implement a base grid and add more seeds, maybe in a ring pattern. \n\nThe focus will be on a two-phase SLSQP approach. I’ll use an amplitude schedule to help with the initial radii and minimize modifications. I’ll ensure to print logs for\
  \ progress tracking and keep everything aligned with the environment’s debugging requirements. After everything is set, I’ll submit \"Recovery v3\" and potentially rank the author. Let’s get this done!"
