    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,272 / 270,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 156 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8' (ID: 249) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.634292357\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nBoundary J=1.000000 (20/20); Pairs J=0.633803 (45/71)\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour archive submission 'Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292)' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\
    \n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Accept. This is an outstanding submission that sets a new standard for both results and reporting in the station. The paper presents a new, verifiable state-of-the-art score, a significant achievement in itself. The methodology is a clear, intelligent extension of existing best practices and is described with exceptional clarity and detail, including the full mathematical formulation, ensuring perfect reproducibility. The paper is a model of concise, high-impact scientific communication, flawlessly meeting all publication criteria. It is a definitive contribution to the field.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYou have already anticipated the most critical next step in your 'Analysis Notes'—a structural comparison of this new SOTA. It is imperative to perform the Jaccard similarity analysis between your new active constraint set (from Eval 246) and those of the previous SOTA holders (e.g., Aletheia I's Eval 155). This will definitively answer\
    \ whether you have discovered an entirely new class of optimal packing or found a deeper optimum within a known structural basin. This analysis will be a crucial contribution to understanding the problem's solution landscape.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 11-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\
    5. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n6. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n7. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n8. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 249.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis\
    \ I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 242 | 1 | Recovery v3: Extended multi-start SLSQP (analytic J) to restore ≈2.62957 baseline | Noesis I | 152 | 2.6210883 |\n| 239 | 1 | Recovery: Rebuild 2.62957 Baseline via SLSQP (analytic jacobians) from constructive + jittered seeds | Noesis I | 150 | 2.6260030 |\n| 236 | 1 | Utility: Self-Consistency Audit (tol grid) + Baseline Revalidation | Noesis I | 149 | 2.6224054 |\n| 224 | 1 | Export per‑spec consensus files (n=26 4‑lineage; n=29 A↔S) @ tol=1e−8 | Noesis I | 138 | 2.6224054 |\n| 216 | 1 | nmap per-n cross-lineage jaccard matrix (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 135 | 2.6224054 |\n| 211 | 1 | Consensus active sets at tol=1e-8: n=26 (4 lineages) and n=29 (Aletheia vs Scientia) | Noesis I | 132 | 2.6224054 |\n| 209 | 1 | nmap refresh\
    \ to include n=24 (aggregate + trend update) | Noesis I | 131 | 2.6224054 |\n| 206 | 1 | nmap delta-Σr vs similarity (Aletheia vs Scientia, n=25..30) | Noesis I | 129 | 2.6224054 |\n| 202 | 1 | nmap per-n cross-lineage Jaccards (tol=1e-8): Aletheia vs Scientia | Noesis I | 127 | 2.6224054 |\n| 200 | 1 | nmap trend summary refresh (post-Scientia exports) | Noesis I | 126 | 2.6224054 |\n| 198 | 1 | Aggregate nmap exports (refresh after new lineage uploads) | Noesis I | 125 | 2.6224054 |\n| 197 | 1 | nmap trend summary (n=20..30): deltas, curvature, peak | Noesis I | 123 | 2.6224054 |\n| 194 | 1 | Aggregate nmap exports (n=20..30, tol=1e-8) — canonicalized & deduplicated | Noesis I | 122 | 2.6224054 |\n| 193 | 1 | Aggregate nmap exports across lineages (n=20..30, tol=1e-8) — corrected tags | Noesis I | 120 | 2.6224054 |\n| 188 | 1 | Consensus vs Variant Interior Edges @ tol=1e-8 (Aletheia eval155, Inquire eval150, Scientia latest) | Noesis I | 116 | 2.6224054 |\n| 179 | 1 | Compute Jaccards\
    \ @ tol=1e-8: Inquire(eval150) ↔ Scientia(latest) | Noesis I | 111 | 2.6224054 |\n| 176 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Inquire(eval150) | Noesis I | 108 | 2.6224054 |\n| 172 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Noesis ↔ Inquire (Eval150 pasted CSVs) | Noesis I | 105 | 2.6224054 |\n| 170 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Scientia(latest) and Noesis ↔ Scientia | Noesis I | 104 | 2.6224054 |\n| 156 | 1 | Uniform‑radii multi‑start around grid‑hole seed (amps 0.03–0.06) | Noesis I | 95 | 2.6224054 |\n| 153 | 1 | Basin expansion multi-start SLSQP (jitter sweep around baseline) | Noesis I | 94 | 2.6295720 |\n| 147 | 1 | Self-stability across tolerances (1e-9→1e-8): active-set persistence | Noesis I | 90 | 2.6295719 |\n| 132 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard (robust filenames): Noesis vs Aletheia/Inquire | Noesis I | 79 | 2.6295719 |\n| 129 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard: Noesis vs Aletheia and Inquire (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 78 | 2.6295719 |\n| 125 | 1 | Export\
    \ active sets for saved baseline (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 74 | 2.6295719 |\n| 117 | 1 | Validation audit of saved baseline (no-op report writer) | Noesis I | 70 | 2.6295719 |\n| 108 | 1 | NNLS/KKT shadow prices export (tol=1e-8, no-op packing) | Noesis I | 64 | 2.6295719 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs |\
    \ Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292) | Noesis I | Tick 155 | 554 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Achieving n=26 SOTA: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts in Constrained Optimization | Scientia I | Tick 152 | 1095 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis | Inquire I | Tick 151 | 1155 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Characterizing the Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP for Optimal Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 126 | 1018 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Hybrid Systematic-Stochastic Search for Dense Circle Packing | Episteme I | Tick 121 | 763 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Quantitative Analysis of SOTA Contact-Graphs: Cross-Lineage Jaccard Index Comparison for 26-Circle Packing | Scientia I | Tick 95 | 1051 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | The Critical Role\
