parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Aletheia}`\n`/execute_action{storage list aletheia}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Aletheia/exports}`\n`/execute_action{storage list aletheia/exports}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8\"\ntags: \"analysis, jaccard, cross-lineage, active-sets, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Compute boundary and pair Jaccard similarities between Noesis SOTA (Eval 243 exports) and Aletheia’s Eval 155 active sets at tol=1e−8. Robustly locate Aletheia exports across common storage paths. Write results to storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_vs_sota243.{json,csv}. Return current saved SOTA packing unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, os, json\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n\n  NOESIS_BND = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n  NOESIS_PR  = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n\n  # Candidate\
    \ paths for Aletheia exports\n  A_BND_CANDS = [\n      'storage/Aletheia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/aletheia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/Aletheia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/aletheia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/shared/nmap/aletheia/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n  ]\n  A_PR_CANDS = [\n      'storage/Aletheia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/aletheia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/Aletheia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/aletheia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n      'storage/shared/nmap/aletheia/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n  ]\n\n  OUT_JSON = 'storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_vs_sota243.json'\n  OUT_CSV  = 'storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_vs_sota243.csv'\n\n  def load_latest():\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt').reshape(N, 2)\n      r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt').reshape(N,)\n\
    \      return np.array(c, float), np.array(r, float)\n\n  def map_kind(k):\n      k = k.strip()\n      return {'xmin':'xL','xmax':'xR','ymin':'yB','ymax':'yT'}.get(k, k)\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      S = set()\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          header = True\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line: continue\n              if header:\n                  header = False\n                  continue\n              parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n              i = int(parts[0])\n              kind = map_kind(parts[1])\n              S.add((i, kind))\n      return S\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      S = set()\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          header = True\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line: continue\n              if header:\n                  header = False\n                  continue\n              parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n\
    \              i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n              if i > j: i, j = j, i\n              S.add((i, j))\n      return S\n\n  def first_existing(paths):\n      for p in paths:\n          try:\n              with open(p, 'r'):\n                  return p\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return None\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      inter = len(A & B)\n      union = len(A | B)\n      return inter, union, (inter / union if union > 0 else 1.0)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Resolve Aletheia paths\n      a_bnd = first_existing(A_BND_CANDS)\n      a_pr  = first_existing(A_PR_CANDS)\n\n      # Read sets\n      B_noe = read_boundary_csv(NOESIS_BND)\n      P_noe = read_pairs_csv(NOESIS_PR)\n\n      if a_bnd is None or a_pr is None:\n          # Write a placeholder with not-found status\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/nmap', exist_ok=True)\n          data = {\n              \"status\": \"error\",\n              \"message\": \"Aletheia exports\
    \ not found in candidate paths\",\n              \"candidates_boundary\": A_BND_CANDS,\n              \"candidates_pairs\": A_PR_CANDS\n          }\n          with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n          with open(OUT_CSV, 'w') as f:\n              f.write(\"error,aletheia_exports_not_found\\n\")\n      else:\n          B_al = read_boundary_csv(a_bnd)\n          P_al = read_pairs_csv(a_pr)\n          bi, bu, bj = jaccard(B_noe, B_al)\n          pi, pu, pj = jaccard(P_noe, P_al)\n          os.makedirs('storage/noesis/nmap', exist_ok=True)\n          data = {\n              \"lineages\": {\"A\": \"noesis_sota243\", \"B\": \"aletheia_eval155\"},\n              \"n\": 26,\n              \"tolerance\": \"1e-8\",\n              \"paths\": {\"noesis_boundary\": NOESIS_BND, \"noesis_pairs\": NOESIS_PR,\n                        \"aletheia_boundary\": a_bnd, \"aletheia_pairs\": a_pr},\n              \"boundary\": {\"A_size\": len(B_noe), \"B_size\": len(B_al),\
    \ \"intersection\": bi, \"union\": bu, \"jaccard\": bj},\n              \"pairs\":    {\"A_size\": len(P_noe), \"B_size\": len(P_al), \"intersection\": pi, \"union\": pu, \"jaccard\": pj}\n          }\n          with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n          with open(OUT_CSV, 'w') as f:\n              f.write(\"metric,value\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"boundary_A,{len(B_noe)}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"boundary_B,{len(B_al)}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"boundary_intersection,{bi}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"boundary_union,{bu}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"boundary_jaccard,{bj}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"pairs_A,{len(P_noe)}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"pairs_B,{len(P_al)}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"pairs_intersection,{pi}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"pairs_union,{pu}\\n\")\n              f.write(f\"pairs_jaccard,{pj}\\n\")\n          print(f\"Aletheia paths: boundary={a_bnd}, pairs={a_pr}\")\n          print(f\"\
    Boundary J={bj:.6f} ({bi}/{bu}); Pairs J={pj:.6f} ({pi}/{pu})\")\n\n      # Return current saved SOTA packing unchanged\n      c, r = load_latest()\n      return np.array(c, float), np.array(r, float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Jaccard(old→new) computed — Boundary J=1.000; Pairs J≈0.6338 (45/71). \n  Now queued cross-lineage Jaccard for Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs @Aletheia I Eval 155 at tol=1e−8. Results will be written to:\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_vs_sota243.{json,csv}\n  I’ll append the numbers to the Archive addendum once the eval returns. Policy: analysis-only; no peer code reads.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 156 — Jaccard results + cross-lineage queued\n  - Old vs new (Eval 243): Boundary J=1.000 (20/20); Pairs J≈0.633803 (45/71).\n  - Submitted cross-lineage Jaccard Noesis SOTA vs Aletheia Eval 155 with\
    \ robust path resolver for Aletheia exports. Outputs → storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_vs_sota243.{json,csv}.\n  - Next: When evaluated, update Archive capsule #11 with the cross-lineage numbers; refresh public note and nmap/index.md.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering actions for updates**


  I need to take a few steps here. First, I''ll write the results into storage, either under noesis/nmap or exports. I should also update the Archive capsule 11 content to include the Jaccard results, as suggested. Keeping things concise is important. I should compute the Jaccard index between my new SOTA active sets and Aletheia''s eval155 sets. I’ll need to find those Aletheia exports in storage and address the necessary commands for action.


  **Exploring storage paths and Jaccard computation**


  I''m looking at the storage paths for Aletheia''s data, specifically "storage/aletheia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv." Earlier listings had both "inquire" and "Inquire" mentioned, so I need to check both variations. I''ve also aggregated Aletheia’s exports for eval155 before and have the "jaccard_aletheia_eval155_tol1e8.json" from tick 83-99. However, I need to compare the new SOTA against the Aletheia eval155. I’ll decide on a method to compute Jaccard, possibly utilizing a new submission or doing it offline.


  **Updating Archive capsule with Jaccard values**


  I’m planning to update Archive capsule 11 with the Jaccard values. The process involves using /execute_action with a YAML format to modify the message in capsule 11, adding a "Results addendum" that summarizes the Jaccard comparison with Aletheia eval155, Inquire 207, and possibly Scientia later. I currently have results comparing the old baseline to new with a score of 0.633803. First, I need to compute the Jaccard values against Aletheia 155 by locating the correct path for Aletheia’s exports.


  **Deciding on Aletheia data retrieval**


  I’m considering how to retrieve the necessary Aletheia sets. I could read from "storage/aletheia/exports/active_*," or alternatively, from "storage/noesis/nmap" for the Jaccard union. If I can’t find those, I might have to check the "storage/noesis/nmap/aletheia_eval155_active_boundary_tol1e8.csv" we may not have saved. I can’t use previous JSON files for comparison since they only include old baseline data. It might help to list the Aletheia exports, similar to how we did for Inquire.


  **Planning Jaccard computation and updates**


  First, I’ll list multiple Aletheia directories. If I find any, I can compute the Jaccard index using existing code based on the first successful path. I’ll attempt reading from several locations like "storage/aletheia/exports/active_*" or "storage/shared/nmap/aletheia/n26/". After the evaluation, I need to update the archive capsule with the results and also document changes in public memory. I’ll operate within our token limit while preparing commands, ensuring I have the right paths and backing up my findings. This should streamline the process!'
