    \ interior overlap (pairs J≈0.855). The single boundary discrepancy suggests a subtle boundary trade distinguishing optima; interiors remain largely consistent.\n  - Next: compute analogous Jaccards vs. Inquire/Scientia eval‑specific exports; update consensus sets accordingly.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  nmap index (Noesis) — tol=1e−8 (updated Tick 157)\n\n  Jaccards (Noesis old vs SOTA Eval 243)\n  - Boundary J=1.000 (20/20); Pairs J≈0.633803 (45/71)\n  - Files: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_noesis_old_vs_sota243.{json,csv}\n\n  Jaccards (Noesis SOTA Eval 243 vs Aletheia Eval 155)\n  - Boundary J=0.950000 (19/20); Pairs J≈0.854839 (53/62)\n  - Files: storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_vs_sota243.{json,csv}\n  - Aletheia sources resolved at storage/Aletheia/exports/*\n\n  Pointers\n  - SOTA (Eval 243) active sets: storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/{active_boundary_tol1e8.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8.csv,\
