tick: 158
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8\"\ntags: \"analysis, jaccard, cross-lineage, active-sets, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Compute boundary/pair Jaccards at tol=1e−8 between Noesis SOTA (Eval 243 exports) and (a) Inquire Eval 207, (b) Scientia latest. Robustly resolve peer export paths. Write results to storage/noesis/nmap/ as JSON/CSV. Return saved SOTA unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, os, json\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n\n  NOESIS_BND = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n  NOESIS_PR  = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n\n  CANDS = {\n      \"inquire\": {\n          \"boundary\": [\n              'storage/Inquire/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/inquire/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n\
    \              'storage/inquire/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/shared/nmap/inquire/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n          ],\n          \"pairs\": [\n              'storage/Inquire/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/inquire/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/inquire/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/shared/nmap/inquire/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n          ],\n          \"out_json\": 'storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_sota243.json',\n          \"out_csv\":  'storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_sota243.csv',\n          \"label\": \"inquire_eval207\"\n      },\n      \"scientia\": {\n          \"boundary\": [\n              'storage/Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n\
    \              'storage/scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/shared/nmap/scientia/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n          ],\n          \"pairs\": [\n              'storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'storage/shared/nmap/scientia/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n          ],\n          \"out_json\": 'storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_scientia_latest_vs_sota243.json',\n          \"out_csv\":  'storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_scientia_latest_vs_sota243.csv',\n          \"label\": \"scientia_latest\"\n      }\n  }\n\n  def load_latest():\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt').reshape(N, 2)\n      r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt').reshape(N,)\n      return np.array(c, float), np.array(r, float)\n\n\
    \  def map_kind(k):\n      k = k.strip()\n      return {'xmin':'xL','xmax':'xR','ymin':'yB','ymax':'yT'}.get(k, k)\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n      S = set()\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          header = True\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line: continue\n              if header:\n                  header = False\n                  continue\n              parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n              i = int(parts[0])\n              kind = map_kind(parts[1])\n              S.add((i, kind))\n      return S\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      S = set()\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          header = True\n          for line in f:\n              line = line.strip()\n              if not line: continue\n              if header:\n                  header = False\n                  continue\n              parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(',')]\n              i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n\
    \              if i > j: i, j = j, i\n              S.add((i, j))\n      return S\n\n  def first_existing(paths):\n      for p in paths:\n          try:\n              with open(p, 'r'):\n                  return p\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return None\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      inter = len(A & B)\n      union = len(A | B)\n      return inter, union, (inter / union if union > 0 else 1.0)\n\n  def compare(peer_key):\n      conf = CANDS[peer_key]\n      a_bnd = first_existing(conf[\"boundary\"])\n      a_pr  = first_existing(conf[\"pairs\"])\n      os.makedirs('storage/noesis/nmap', exist_ok=True)\n      out_json = conf[\"out_json\"]; out_csv = conf[\"out_csv\"]\n      if a_bnd is None or a_pr is None:\n          data = {\n              \"status\": \"error\",\n              \"peer\": peer_key,\n              \"message\": \"exports not found in candidate paths\",\n              \"candidates_boundary\": conf[\"boundary\"],\n              \"candidates_pairs\"\
    : conf[\"pairs\"]\n          }\n          with open(out_json, 'w') as f: json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n          with open(out_csv, 'w') as f: f.write(\"error,exports_not_found\\n\")\n          print(f\"[{peer_key}] exports not found\")\n          return\n      B_noe = read_boundary_csv(NOESIS_BND); P_noe = read_pairs_csv(NOESIS_PR)\n      B_peer = read_boundary_csv(a_bnd);     P_peer = read_pairs_csv(a_pr)\n      bi, bu, bj = jaccard(B_noe, B_peer)\n      pi, pu, pj = jaccard(P_noe, P_peer)\n      data = {\n          \"lineages\": {\"A\": \"noesis_sota243\", \"B\": conf[\"label\"]},\n          \"n\": 26, \"tolerance\": \"1e-8\",\n          \"paths\": {\"noesis_boundary\": NOESIS_BND, \"noesis_pairs\": NOESIS_PR,\n                    \"peer_boundary\": a_bnd, \"peer_pairs\": a_pr},\n          \"boundary\": {\"A_size\": len(B_noe), \"B_size\": len(B_peer), \"intersection\": bi, \"union\": bu, \"jaccard\": bj},\n          \"pairs\":    {\"A_size\": len(P_noe), \"B_size\": len(P_peer),\
    \ \"intersection\": pi, \"union\": pu, \"jaccard\": pj}\n      }\n      with open(out_json, 'w') as f: json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n      with open(out_csv, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"metric,value\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"boundary_A,{len(B_noe)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"boundary_B,{len(B_peer)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"boundary_intersection,{bi}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"boundary_union,{bu}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"boundary_jaccard,{bj}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"pairs_A,{len(P_noe)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"pairs_B,{len(P_peer)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"pairs_intersection,{pi}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"pairs_union,{pu}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"pairs_jaccard,{pj}\\n\")\n      print(f\"[{peer_key}] boundary J={bj:.6f} ({bi}/{bu}); pairs J={pj:.6f} ({pi}/{pu}); paths: {a_bnd}, {a_pr}\")\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Compute for Inquire and Scientia\n      compare(\"inquire\")\n      compare(\"scientia\")\n      # Return current saved SOTA unchanged\n\
    \      c, r = load_latest()\n      return np.array(c, float), np.array(r, float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Queued cross-lineage Jaccards for the new SOTA (Eval 243):\n  - Noesis SOTA vs @Inquire I Eval 207\n  - Noesis SOTA vs @Scientia I latest\n  Outputs (after eval):\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_sota243.{json,csv}\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_scientia_latest_vs_sota243.{json,csv}\n  Analysis-only; no peer code reads. I’ll append numbers to the archive addendum and refresh the nmap index when results return.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 158 — Cross-lineage Jaccards queued (Noesis SOTA vs Inquire/Scientia)\n  - Script resolves multiple candidate paths for peer exports; writes JSON/CSV into storage/noesis/nmap/.\n  - Will update Archive #11 addendum and nmap/index.md with boundary/pair J values on return.\n  -\
    \ Guardrails maintained (analysis-only; feasibility/pack unchanged).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning evaluation paths**\n\nI need to make sure we respond appropriately after computing the Jaccard for Noesis SOTA versus Aletheia Eval155. The next step is to extend this to evaluation-specific Inquire and Scientia processes. I need to maintain and update our nmap/index and explore building a similar evaluation for Scientia and Inquire. It’s vital to ensure we’re compliant with policies, reading only from lineage storage exports. I need to check paths for both Inquire and Scientia to confirm their storage.\n\n**Planning Jaccard analyses**\n\nI’m gearing up to write a research submission for two Jaccard analyses: one against Inquire and the other against Scientia. I think a single evaluation script can handle both and produce the outputs. We can pull data from the provided paths for Inquire and Scientia. After computing the results, we might update the Archive addendum and consider exporting the consensus sets with the new Noesis SOTA. Once this is all done, we\
  \ should announce the new cross-lineage Jaccard results publicly!\n\n**Outlining data paths and computations**\n\nI’m planning to load the Noesis SOTA exports from the specified path. For Inquire, I’ll check various candidate paths, including differences in casing and specific files like 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'. I need to confirm if there's a corresponding '_eval207' file, since I found an '_eval155' in Aletheia. The previous exports we used yielded a Jaccard boundary of 1.0, but our new SOTA should provide us with potentially different results.\n\nFor Scientia, I’ll pull from its own set of designated paths. Finally, I need to write the results to our designated storage locations in both JSON and CSV formats.\n\n**Finalizing evaluation preparation**\n\nI’m considering whether to include the evaluation ID, which isn’t necessary but could be helpful. If we know it, I can add 'lineage' as 'inquire_eval207'; otherwise, it’ll remain unknown. I’ll print the Jaccard numbers to STDOUT after\
  \ computing them.\n\nOnce we've evaluated, I’ll update the Archive and public memory. However, I can’t rely on results just yet since we need to submit first. I’ll also prepare to log our processes and ensure we don’t load peers in the evaluation code. Lastly, I may write to 'storage/noesis/nmap/index.md' after everything is done.\n\n**Refining evaluation process**\n\nI’m realizing that the evaluation code shouldn't write directly to the index; it's better to keep that separate. I’ll send out a public message noting that the cross-lineage Jaccard comparisons against Inquire and Scientia are queued. Later, I can update the Archive addendum with the results. \n\nNow it’s time to move to actions: I’ll first submit the evaluation code, then update public and private memory replies. I need to validate the candidate files carefully. I'll write JSON outputs with a \"status\" in case of any missing data. Also, I should ensure we include the 'Active sets' for Noesis SOTA from the designated path.\
  \ Let's proceed!"
