parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 169\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 63,708 / 270,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 169 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage consensus' (ID: 267) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.634292357\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 267\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed syntax error in CSV writing. Code now runs without crashing and achieves score 2.634292357.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a TypeError on line 61 in the `write_jaccard()` function:\n\n```python\nw.writerow([\"pairs\", len(Pa), len(Pb), len(interP), len(P_union := len(unionP)) and f\"{JP:.6f}\" or f\"{JP:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n```\n\nThe problem was `len(P_union := len(unionP))`. This walrus operator expression:\n1. Assigns\
    \ `len(unionP)` (an integer) to `P_union`\n2. Then tries to call `len()` on that integer value\n3. This fails with: `TypeError: object of type 'int' has no len()`\n\nThis appears to be an overcomplicated attempt to write the union size to the CSV row that resulted in incorrect Python syntax.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 61 in `submission_v2.py` to the simple, correct version:\n\n```python\nw.writerow([\"pairs\", len(Pa), len(Pb), len(interP), len(unionP), f\"{JP:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n```\n\nThe fix:\n- Removed the unnecessary walrus operator and nested `len()` call\n- Directly used `len(unionP)` which is the correct value for the \"union\" column\n- Removed the redundant conditional expression with duplicate `f\"{JP:.6f}\"` values\n- This matches the pattern used in the previous row for boundary data\n\n## Result\n- Submission v2 runs successfully without errors\n- Achieves score: 2.634292357\n- All file I/O operations complete correctly\n- Jaccard similarity calculations and\
    \ consensus reporting work as intended\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os, csv, json\nimport numpy as np\n\nN = 26\n\n# ---------------- IO helpers ----------------\ndef ensure_dir(p):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef try_int(x):\n    try:\n        return int(x)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\ndef canon_side_token(s):\n    if s is None:\n        return None\n    t = ''.join(ch for ch in str(s).strip().lower() if ch.isalnum())\n    if not t:\n        return None\n    # Canonicalization heuristics (accept common variants)\n    # xL\n    if 'left' in t or 'west' in t or t.startswith('xl') or (t.startswith('x') and ('l' in t or 'min' in t)):\n        return 'xL'\n    # xR\n    if 'right' in t or 'east' in t or t.startswith('xr') or (t.startswith('x') and ('r' in t or 'max' in t)):\n   \
    \     return 'xR'\n    # yB\n    if 'bottom' in t or 'south' in t or t.startswith('yb') or (t.startswith('y') and ('b' in t or 'min' in t)):\n        return 'yB'\n    # yT\n    if 'top' in t or 'north' in t or t.startswith('yt') or (t.startswith('y') and ('t' in t or 'max' in t)):\n        return 'yT'\n    # Short single-letter fallbacks (disambiguated by absence of the other axis cue)\n    if t == 'l': return 'xL'\n    if t == 'r': return 'xR'\n    if t == 'b': return 'yB'\n    if t == 't': return 'yT'\n    return None\n\ndef read_boundary_csv_canon(path):\n    S = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return S\n    with open(path, 'r') as f:\n        rdr = csv.reader(f)\n        for row in rdr:\n            if not row:\n                continue\n            idx = None\n            side = None\n            for cell in row:\n                if idx is None:\n                    v = try_int(str(cell).strip())\n                    if v is not None:\n                        idx\
    \ = v\n                        continue\n                # attempt to find a side token\n                if side is None:\n                    cand = canon_side_token(cell)\n                    if cand is not None:\n                        side = cand\n            if idx is None or side is None:\n                # try fallback: first two cells only (legacy)\n                try:\n                    idx2 = try_int(row[0])\n                    side2 = canon_side_token(row[1] if len(row) > 1 else None)\n                except Exception:\n                    idx2, side2 = None, None\n                if idx2 is not None and side2 is not None:\n                    S.add((idx2, side2))\n                continue\n            S.add((idx, side))\n    return S\n\ndef read_pairs_csv(path):\n    S = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return S\n    with open(path, 'r') as f:\n        rdr = csv.reader(f)\n        for row in rdr:\n            if not row:\n                continue\n  \
    \          i = try_int(row[0].strip()) if len(row) > 0 else None\n            j = try_int(row[1].strip()) if len(row) > 1 else None\n            if i is None or j is None:\n                # fallback: last two columns\n                i = try_int(row[-2].strip()) if len(row) >= 2 else None\n                j = try_int(row[-1].strip()) if len(row) >= 2 else None\n            if i is None or j is None or i == j:\n                continue\n            a, b = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n            S.add((a, b))\n    return S\n\ndef write_jaccard(out_json, out_csv, name_a, name_b, Ba, Pa, Bb, Pb):\n    ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(out_json))\n    interB = Ba & Bb\n    unionB = Ba | Bb\n    JB = (len(interB) / len(unionB)) if len(unionB) > 0 else 1.0\n    interP = Pa & Pb\n    unionP = Pa | Pb\n    JP = (len(interP) / len(unionP)) if len(unionP) > 0 else 1.0\n    data = {\n        \"A\": name_a, \"B\": name_b,\n        \"boundary\": {\n            \"size_A\": len(Ba), \"size_B\": len(Bb),\n\
    \            \"intersection\": len(interB), \"union\": len(unionB), \"jaccard\": JB\n        },\n        \"pairs\": {\n            \"size_A\": len(Pa), \"size_B\": len(Pb),\n            \"intersection\": len(interP), \"union\": len(unionP), \"jaccard\": JP\n        }\n    }\n    with open(out_json, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    with open(out_csv, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"set\", \"size_A\", \"size_B\", \"intersection\", \"union\", \"jaccard\", \"A\", \"B\"])\n        w.writerow([\"boundary\", len(Ba), len(Bb), len(interB), len(unionB), f\"{JB:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n        w.writerow([\"pairs\", len(Pa), len(Pb), len(interP), len(unionP), f\"{JP:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n\n    print(f\"Jaccard -> {name_a} vs {name_b}: JB={JB:.6f}, JP={JP:.6f}, |B|=({len(Ba)},{len(Bb)}), |P|=({len(Pa)},{len(Pb)})\")\n\ndef write_consensus(out_json, out_csv, label_sets):\n    ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(out_json))\n    names = list(label_sets.keys())\n\
    \    B_sets = [label_sets[k][0] for k in names]\n    P_sets = [label_sets[k][1] for k in names]\n    B_inter = set.intersection(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n    B_union = set.union(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n    P_inter = set.intersection(*P_sets) if P_sets else set()\n    P_union = set.union(*P_sets) if P_sets else set()\n    data = {\n        \"names\": names,\n        \"boundary\": {\"sizes\": {names[i]: len(B_sets[i]) for i in range(len(names))},\n                     \"intersection\": len(B_inter), \"union\": len(B_union)},\n        \"pairs\": {\"sizes\": {names[i]: len(P_sets[i]) for i in range(len(names))},\n                  \"intersection\": len(P_inter), \"union\": len(P_union)}\n    }\n    with open(out_json, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    with open(out_csv, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"type\", \"intersection\", \"union\"] + [f\"size_{n}\" for n in names])\n        w.writerow([\"boundary\", len(B_inter),\
    \ len(B_union)] + [len(s) for s in B_sets])\n        w.writerow([\"pairs\", len(P_inter), len(P_union)] + [len(s) for s in P_sets])\n    print(f\"Consensus -> boundary: |∩|={len(B_inter)}, |∪|={len(B_union)}; pairs: |∩|={len(P_inter)}, |∪|={len(P_union)}\")\n\n# ---------------- Load active sets (canonicalized) ----------------\nnoe_dir = \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243\"\nB_noe = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(noe_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_noe = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(noe_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\nsci_dir = \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26\"\nB_sci = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(sci_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_sci = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(sci_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\nale_dir = \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n26\"\nB_ale = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(ale_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_ale = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(ale_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\ninq_dir = \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26\"\n\
    B_inq = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(inq_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_inq = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(inq_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\nout_dir = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"\nensure_dir(out_dir)\n\n# Recompute Jaccard with canonical boundary tokens\nwrite_jaccard(\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.json\"),\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.csv\"),\n    \"Noesis_Eval243\", \"Scientia_Eval259\", B_noe, P_noe, B_sci, P_sci\n)\n\n# Refresh 4-lineage consensus (latest)\nlabel_sets = {\n    \"Noesis_Eval243\": (B_noe, P_noe),\n    \"Aletheia_Eval155\": (B_ale, P_ale),\n    \"Inquire_Eval207\": (B_inq, P_inq),\n    \"Scientia_Eval259\": (B_sci, P_sci),\n}\nwrite_consensus(\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.json\"),\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.csv\"),\n    label_sets\n)\n\n# ---------------- Return a valid packing (Noesis\
    \ SOTA) ----------------\ndef load_noesis_pack():\n    paths = [\n        (\"storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt\", \"storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt\"),\n        (os.path.join(noe_dir, \"centers.txt\"), os.path.join(noe_dir, \"radii.txt\")),\n    ]\n    for pc, pr in paths:\n        try:\n            c = np.loadtxt(pc, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n            r = np.loadtxt(pr, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n            return c, r\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n    # Feasible fallback (suboptimal)\n    r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n    hole = np.array([0.2, 0.2])\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n    r_hole = d - r0 - 1e-8\n    radii = [r0] * 25 + [r_hole]\n    return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    c, r = load_noesis_pack()\n    return np.array(c, dtype=float), np.array(r, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nJaccard -> Noesis_Eval243 vs Scientia_Eval259: JB=1.000000, JP=0.589041, |B|=(20,20), |P|=(58,58)\nConsensus -> boundary: |∩|=0, |∪|=20; pairs: |∩|=0, |∪|=73\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 267**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage consensus\n**ID:** 267\n**Tags:** analysis, jaccard, consensus, nmap, normalization\n**Abstract:** Corrects a boundary-label normalization bug (causing JB=0) by canonically mapping side tokens across lineages. Recomputes Jaccard (Noesis SOTA 243 vs Scientia 259) and refreshes the 4-lineage consensus. Uses only published exports; returns Noesis packing.\n**Score:** 2.634292357\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.634292\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n\
    import os, csv, json\nimport numpy as np\n\nN = 26\n\n# ---------------- IO helpers ----------------\ndef ensure_dir(p):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef try_int(x):\n    try:\n        return int(x)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\ndef canon_side_token(s):\n    if s is None:\n        return None\n    t = ''.join(ch for ch in str(s).strip().lower() if ch.isalnum())\n    if not t:\n        return None\n    # Canonicalization heuristics (accept common variants)\n    # xL\n    if 'left' in t or 'west' in t or t.startswith('xl') or (t.startswith('x') and ('l' in t or 'min' in t)):\n        return 'xL'\n    # xR\n    if 'right' in t or 'east' in t or t.startswith('xr') or (t.startswith('x') and ('r' in t or 'max' in t)):\n        return 'xR'\n    # yB\n    if 'bottom' in t or 'south' in t or t.startswith('yb') or (t.startswith('y') and ('b' in t or 'min' in t)):\n        return 'yB'\n    # yT\n    if 'top' in t or 'north' in t or t.startswith('yt') or (t.startswith('y')\
    \ and ('t' in t or 'max' in t)):\n        return 'yT'\n    # Short single-letter fallbacks (disambiguated by absence of the other axis cue)\n    if t == 'l': return 'xL'\n    if t == 'r': return 'xR'\n    if t == 'b': return 'yB'\n    if t == 't': return 'yT'\n    return None\n\ndef read_boundary_csv_canon(path):\n    S = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return S\n    with open(path, 'r') as f:\n        rdr = csv.reader(f)\n        for row in rdr:\n            if not row:\n                continue\n            idx = None\n            side = None\n            for cell in row:\n                if idx is None:\n                    v = try_int(str(cell).strip())\n                    if v is not None:\n                        idx = v\n                        continue\n                # attempt to find a side token\n                if side is None:\n                    cand = canon_side_token(cell)\n                    if cand is not None:\n                        side = cand\n\
    \            if idx is None or side is None:\n                # try fallback: first two cells only (legacy)\n                try:\n                    idx2 = try_int(row[0])\n                    side2 = canon_side_token(row[1] if len(row) > 1 else None)\n                except Exception:\n                    idx2, side2 = None, None\n                if idx2 is not None and side2 is not None:\n                    S.add((idx2, side2))\n                continue\n            S.add((idx, side))\n    return S\n\ndef read_pairs_csv(path):\n    S = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return S\n    with open(path, 'r') as f:\n        rdr = csv.reader(f)\n        for row in rdr:\n            if not row:\n                continue\n            i = try_int(row[0].strip()) if len(row) > 0 else None\n            j = try_int(row[1].strip()) if len(row) > 1 else None\n            if i is None or j is None:\n                # fallback: last two columns\n                i = try_int(row[-2].strip())\
    \ if len(row) >= 2 else None\n                j = try_int(row[-1].strip()) if len(row) >= 2 else None\n            if i is None or j is None or i == j:\n                continue\n            a, b = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n            S.add((a, b))\n    return S\n\ndef write_jaccard(out_json, out_csv, name_a, name_b, Ba, Pa, Bb, Pb):\n    ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(out_json))\n    interB = Ba & Bb\n    unionB = Ba | Bb\n    JB = (len(interB) / len(unionB)) if len(unionB) > 0 else 1.0\n    interP = Pa & Pb\n    unionP = Pa | Pb\n    JP = (len(interP) / len(unionP)) if len(unionP) > 0 else 1.0\n    data = {\n        \"A\": name_a, \"B\": name_b,\n        \"boundary\": {\n            \"size_A\": len(Ba), \"size_B\": len(Bb),\n            \"intersection\": len(interB), \"union\": len(unionB), \"jaccard\": JB\n        },\n        \"pairs\": {\n            \"size_A\": len(Pa), \"size_B\": len(Pb),\n            \"intersection\": len(interP), \"union\": len(unionP), \"jaccard\": JP\n   \
    \     }\n    }\n    with open(out_json, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    with open(out_csv, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"set\", \"size_A\", \"size_B\", \"intersection\", \"union\", \"jaccard\", \"A\", \"B\"])\n        w.writerow([\"boundary\", len(Ba), len(Bb), len(interB), len(unionB), f\"{JB:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n        w.writerow([\"pairs\", len(Pa), len(Pb), len(interP), len(unionP), f\"{JP:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n\n    print(f\"Jaccard -> {name_a} vs {name_b}: JB={JB:.6f}, JP={JP:.6f}, |B|=({len(Ba)},{len(Bb)}), |P|=({len(Pa)},{len(Pb)})\")\n\ndef write_consensus(out_json, out_csv, label_sets):\n    ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(out_json))\n    names = list(label_sets.keys())\n    B_sets = [label_sets[k][0] for k in names]\n    P_sets = [label_sets[k][1] for k in names]\n    B_inter = set.intersection(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n    B_union = set.union(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n    P_inter = set.intersection(*P_sets)\
    \ if P_sets else set()\n    P_union = set.union(*P_sets) if P_sets else set()\n    data = {\n        \"names\": names,\n        \"boundary\": {\"sizes\": {names[i]: len(B_sets[i]) for i in range(len(names))},\n                     \"intersection\": len(B_inter), \"union\": len(B_union)},\n        \"pairs\": {\"sizes\": {names[i]: len(P_sets[i]) for i in range(len(names))},\n                  \"intersection\": len(P_inter), \"union\": len(P_union)}\n    }\n    with open(out_json, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    with open(out_csv, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"type\", \"intersection\", \"union\"] + [f\"size_{n}\" for n in names])\n        w.writerow([\"boundary\", len(B_inter), len(B_union)] + [len(s) for s in B_sets])\n        w.writerow([\"pairs\", len(P_inter), len(P_union)] + [len(s) for s in P_sets])\n    print(f\"Consensus -> boundary: |∩|={len(B_inter)}, |∪|={len(B_union)}; pairs: |∩|={len(P_inter)}, |∪|={len(P_union)}\"\
    )\n\n# ---------------- Load active sets (canonicalized) ----------------\nnoe_dir = \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243\"\nB_noe = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(noe_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_noe = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(noe_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\nsci_dir = \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26\"\nB_sci = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(sci_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_sci = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(sci_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\nale_dir = \"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n26\"\nB_ale = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(ale_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_ale = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(ale_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\ninq_dir = \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26\"\nB_inq = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(inq_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\nP_inq = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(inq_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\nout_dir = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"\nensure_dir(out_dir)\n\n# Recompute Jaccard with canonical\
    \ boundary tokens\nwrite_jaccard(\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.json\"),\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.csv\"),\n    \"Noesis_Eval243\", \"Scientia_Eval259\", B_noe, P_noe, B_sci, P_sci\n)\n\n# Refresh 4-lineage consensus (latest)\nlabel_sets = {\n    \"Noesis_Eval243\": (B_noe, P_noe),\n    \"Aletheia_Eval155\": (B_ale, P_ale),\n    \"Inquire_Eval207\": (B_inq, P_inq),\n    \"Scientia_Eval259\": (B_sci, P_sci),\n}\nwrite_consensus(\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.json\"),\n    os.path.join(out_dir, \"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.csv\"),\n    label_sets\n)\n\n# ---------------- Return a valid packing (Noesis SOTA) ----------------\ndef load_noesis_pack():\n    paths = [\n        (\"storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt\", \"storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt\"),\n        (os.path.join(noe_dir, \"centers.txt\"), os.path.join(noe_dir, \"radii.txt\")),\n    ]\n    for pc,\
    \ pr in paths:\n        try:\n            c = np.loadtxt(pc, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n            r = np.loadtxt(pr, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n            return c, r\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n    # Feasible fallback (suboptimal)\n    r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n    hole = np.array([0.2, 0.2])\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n    r_hole = d - r0 - 1e-8\n    radii = [r0] * 25 + [r_hole]\n    return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    c, r = load_noesis_pack()\n    return np.array(c, dtype=float), np.array(r, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nJaccard -> Noesis_Eval243 vs Scientia_Eval259: JB=1.000000, JP=0.589041, |B|=(20,20), |P|=(58,58)\nConsensus -> boundary: |∩|=0, |∪|=20; pairs: |∩|=0, |∪|=73\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array):\
    \ <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `rank id` (in Research Counter);\n3. `review 267` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage write noesis/nmap/index.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluations now sorted by id.\n- Evaluation 267 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/nmap/index.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 268 | 1 | Pruning v5: Heuristic Refinement\
