tick: 170
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @ tol=1e-8\"\ntags: \"analysis, consensus, jaccard, nmap, normalization\"\nabstract: \"Recomputes n=26 consensus using only lineages with available exports and case-insensitive storage paths. Avoids zeroing intersections when some lineage files are absent. Also re-writes pair Jaccard (Noesis 243 vs Scientia 259). Uses only published exports; returns Noesis packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json\n  import numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def ensure_dir(p): os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\n  # --- canonical boundary side tokens ---\n  def try_int(x):\n      try: return int(x)\n      except Exception: return None\n\n  def canon_side_token(s):\n      if s is None: return None\n      t = ''.join(ch for ch in str(s).strip().lower() if ch.isalnum())\n      if not t: return None\n      if 'left' in t or 'west' in t or t.startswith('xl') or (t.startswith('x')\
    \ and ('l' in t or 'min' in t)): return 'xL'\n      if 'right' in t or 'east' in t or t.startswith('xr') or (t.startswith('x') and ('r' in t or 'max' in t)): return 'xR'\n      if 'bottom' in t or 'south' in t or t.startswith('yb') or (t.startswith('y') and ('b' in t or 'min' in t)): return 'yB'\n      if 'top' in t or 'north' in t or t.startswith('yt') or (t.startswith('y') and ('t' in t or 'max' in t)): return 'yT'\n      if t == 'l': return 'xL'\n      if t == 'r': return 'xR'\n      if t == 'b': return 'yB'\n      if t == 't': return 'yT'\n      return None\n\n  def read_boundary_csv_canon(path):\n      S = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          rdr = csv.reader(f)\n          for row in rdr:\n              if not row: continue\n              idx = None; side = None\n              for cell in row:\n                  if idx is None:\n                      v = try_int(str(cell).strip())\n                      if v is not None:\n\
    \                          idx = v; continue\n                  if side is None:\n                      cand = canon_side_token(cell)\n                      if cand is not None:\n                          side = cand\n              if idx is None or side is None:\n                  idx2 = try_int(row[0]) if row else None\n                  side2 = canon_side_token(row[1]) if len(row) > 1 else None\n                  if idx2 is not None and side2 is not None:\n                      S.add((idx2, side2))\n                  continue\n              S.add((idx, side))\n      return S\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n      S = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n      with open(path, 'r') as f:\n          rdr = csv.reader(f)\n          for row in rdr:\n              if not row: continue\n              i = try_int(row[0].strip()) if len(row) > 0 else None\n              j = try_int(row[1].strip()) if len(row) > 1 else None\n              if i is None or j is None:\n          \
    \        i = try_int(row[-2].strip()) if len(row) >= 2 else None\n                  j = try_int(row[-1].strip()) if len(row) >= 2 else None\n              if i is None or j is None or i == j: continue\n              a, b = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n              S.add((a, b))\n      return S\n\n  # --- lineage loaders with case-insensitive roots ---\n  def first_existing(paths, files):\n      for root in paths:\n          if all(os.path.exists(os.path.join(root, fn)) for fn in files):\n              return root\n      return None\n\n  def load_lineage(name, candidates):\n      root = first_existing(candidates, [\"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\", \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"])\n      if root is None:\n          return None, None, {\"name\": name, \"root\": None, \"status\": \"missing\"}\n      B = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(root, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\n      P = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(root, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n      if len(B) == 0 or len(P) == 0:\n\
    \          return None, None, {\"name\": name, \"root\": root, \"status\": \"empty_or_partial\"}\n      return B, P, {\"name\": name, \"root\": root, \"status\": \"ok\", \"sizes\": {\"B\": len(B), \"P\": len(P)}}\n\n  # --- compute Jaccard and consensus over available sets ---\n  def write_jaccard(out_json, out_csv, name_a, name_b, Ba, Pa, Bb, Pb):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(out_json))\n      interB = Ba & Bb; unionB = Ba | Bb\n      interP = Pa & Pb; unionP = Pa | Pb\n      JB = (len(interB) / len(unionB)) if len(unionB) > 0 else 1.0\n      JP = (len(interP) / len(unionP)) if len(unionP) > 0 else 1.0\n      data = {\n          \"A\": name_a, \"B\": name_b,\n          \"boundary\": {\"size_A\": len(Ba), \"size_B\": len(Bb), \"intersection\": len(interB), \"union\": len(unionB), \"jaccard\": JB},\n          \"pairs\":    {\"size_A\": len(Pa), \"size_B\": len(Pb), \"intersection\": len(interP), \"union\": len(unionP), \"jaccard\": JP}\n      }\n      with open(out_json, 'w') as\
    \ f: json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n      with open(out_csv, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"set\", \"size_A\", \"size_B\", \"intersection\", \"union\", \"jaccard\", \"A\", \"B\"])\n          w.writerow([\"boundary\", len(Ba), len(Bb), len(interB), len(unionB), f\"{JB:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n          w.writerow([\"pairs\", len(Pa), len(Pb), len(interP), len(unionP), f\"{JP:.6f}\", name_a, name_b])\n      print(f\"Jaccard {name_a} vs {name_b}: JB={JB:.6f}, JP={JP:.6f}\")\n\n  def write_consensus_available(out_json, out_csv, label_sets, meta_out):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(out_json))\n      names_incl = [n for n,(B,P) in label_sets.items() if B is not None and P is not None]\n      B_sets = [label_sets[n][0] for n in names_incl]\n      P_sets = [label_sets[n][1] for n in names_incl]\n      B_inter = set.intersection(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n      B_union = set.union(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n      P_inter = set.intersection(*P_sets)\
    \ if P_sets else set()\n      P_union = set.union(*P_sets) if P_sets else set()\n      data = {\n          \"names_included\": names_incl,\n          \"boundary\": {\"sizes\": {n: len(label_sets[n][0]) for n in names_incl},\n                       \"intersection\": len(B_inter), \"union\": len(B_union)},\n          \"pairs\": {\"sizes\": {n: len(label_sets[n][1]) for n in names_incl},\n                    \"intersection\": len(P_inter), \"union\": len(P_union)}\n      }\n      with open(out_json, 'w') as f: json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n      with open(out_csv, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"type\", \"intersection\", \"union\"] + [f\"size_{n}\" for n in names_incl])\n          w.writerow([\"boundary\", len(B_inter), len(B_union)] + [len(label_sets[n][0]) for n in names_incl])\n          w.writerow([\"pairs\", len(P_inter), len(P_union)] + [len(label_sets[n][1]) for n in names_incl])\n      with open(meta_out, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(meta,\
    \ f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"Consensus (available) over {len(names_incl)} lineages: B∩={len(B_inter)}/B∪={len(B_union)}, P∩={len(P_inter)}/P∪={len(P_union)}\")\n\n  # --- load all lineages (case-insensitive candidates) ---\n  noe_dir = \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243\"\n  B_noe = read_boundary_csv_canon(os.path.join(noe_dir, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\n  P_noe = read_pairs_csv(os.path.join(noe_dir, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n\n  B_ale = P_ale = None\n  B_inq = P_inq = None\n  B_sci = P_sci = None\n\n  meta = {\"lineages\": []}\n\n  # Aletheia\n  B_ale, P_ale, m_ale = load_lineage(\"Aletheia_Eval155\", [\"storage/Aletheia/nmap/n26\", \"storage/aletheia/nmap/n26\"])\n  meta[\"lineages\"].append(m_ale)\n  # Inquire\n  B_inq, P_inq, m_inq = load_lineage(\"Inquire_Eval207\", [\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26\", \"storage/inquire/nmap/n26\"])\n  meta[\"lineages\"].append(m_inq)\n  # Scientia\n  B_sci, P_sci, m_sci = load_lineage(\"Scientia_Eval259\", [\"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26\"\
    , \"storage/scientia/nmap/n26\"])\n  meta[\"lineages\"].append(m_sci)\n  # Noesis (always present here)\n  meta[\"lineages\"].append({\"name\": \"Noesis_Eval243\", \"root\": noe_dir, \"status\": \"ok\", \"sizes\": {\"B\": len(B_noe), \"P\": len(P_noe)}})\n\n  out_dir = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"; ensure_dir(out_dir)\n\n  # Jaccard: Noesis vs Scientia (if available)\n  if B_sci is not None and P_sci is not None:\n      write_jaccard(\n          os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.json\"),\n          os.path.join(out_dir, \"jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.csv\"),\n          \"Noesis_Eval243\", \"Scientia_Eval259\", B_noe, P_noe, B_sci, P_sci\n      )\n\n  # Consensus across available lineages (exclude missing/empty)\n  label_sets = {\"Noesis_Eval243\": (B_noe, P_noe)}\n  if B_ale is not None and P_ale is not None: label_sets[\"Aletheia_Eval155\"] = (B_ale, P_ale)\n  if B_inq is not None and P_inq is not None: label_sets[\"Inquire_Eval207\"] = (B_inq,\
    \ P_inq)\n  if B_sci is not None and P_sci is not None: label_sets[\"Scientia_Eval259\"] = (B_sci, P_sci)\n\n  write_consensus_available(\n      os.path.join(out_dir, \"consensus_n26_latest_available_tol1e8.json\"),\n      os.path.join(out_dir, \"consensus_n26_latest_available_tol1e8.csv\"),\n      label_sets,\n      os.path.join(out_dir, \"consensus_n26_latest_available_meta.json\")\n  )\n\n  # --- return a valid packing (Noesis SOTA) ---\n  def load_noesis_pack():\n      paths = [\n          (\"storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt\", \"storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt\"),\n          (os.path.join(noe_dir, \"centers.txt\"), os.path.join(noe_dir, \"radii.txt\")),\n      ]\n      for pc, pr in paths:\n          try:\n              c = np.loadtxt(pc, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n              r = np.loadtxt(pr, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n              return c, r\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      # Feasible fallback\n      r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3,\
    \ 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]\n      hole = np.array([0.2, 0.2])\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n      r_hole = d - r0 - 1e-8\n      radii = [r0] * 25 + [r_hole]\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      c, r = load_noesis_pack()\n      return np.array(c, dtype=float), np.array(r, dtype=float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  n=26 mapping (tol=1e−8) — Tick 170 update\n\n  - Fixed consensus computation to exclude lineages with missing/empty exports (case-insensitive path check).\n  - Files:\n    * Jaccard (Noesis_243 vs Scientia_259): storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    * Consensus over available lineages: storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_latest_available_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    * Meta (which lineages were included/missing): storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_latest_available_meta.json\n\
    \n  Policy: analysis uses only published exports (no eval-code peer reads).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Adjusting consensus file**\n\nI'm thinking we need to fix our consensus file by re-running the process with presence checks. If some lineages are absent, we should exclude them rather than including empty sets. This way, we can produce more accurate consensus across available sets. Currently, our \"label_sets\" names include all four lineages, which isn't ideal when some sets are empty. I'll focus on only including those with non-empty boundaries and checking if sizes are greater than zero to compute the consensus correctly.\n\n**Revising consensus computation**\n\nI’m considering computing the union of available sets while also checking the intersection. But since including empty sets yields an empty intersection, we should adjust the code to drop the missing lineages. I think we should update the consensus JSON to include a list of missing lineages too. \n\nNext actions include submitting a corrected analysis script and trying lowercase names like 'aletheia' and 'inquire'\
  \ for recomputation. Finally, we should document the error fix in 'nmap/index.md' to ensure reproducibility.\n\n**Planning data analysis**\n\nI want to establish a plan for the research counter to include both uppercase and lowercase paths for 'aletheia' and 'inquire.' I’ve already done some listings for 'Aletheia' and 'Inquire,' so now I’ll focus on lowercase variants. \n\nNext, I’ll submit an analysis to recompute Jaccard and consensus robustly. My code will include a function that reads active sets, flags any missing files, builds a dictionary of present names, and saves a summary in missing.json. Finally, I’ll compute consensus across available lineages and consider pairwise Jaccards if necessary.\n\n**Updating Jaccard and exports**\n\nI need to update the Jaccard analysis against the Sci file, which may still be correct. It’s important to note publicly that we discovered missing published Aletheia and Inquire exports during the rerun, leading to consensus reflecting only two lineages.\
  \ The \"File Listings\" show \"No files found\" for both lineages, possibly because Aletheia is marked as \"inactive_departed.\"\n\nI need to implement code robustly by constructing a list of candidate directories for each lineage. For Noesis, I’ll read from our storage path, and for Aletheia, I'll consider both 'storage/Aletheia/nmap/n26' and 'storage/aletheia/nmap/n26' as candidate roots.\n\n**Implementing robust consensus**\n\nI want to include paths for Inquire and Scientia, noting both uppercase and lowercase options. It’s essential to mark missing files properly. I’ll read boundary and pair files as before and compute the consensus, providing \"names_included\" and \"names_missing\" in a JSON format. \n\nWe plan to submit an analysis focusing on consensus while ensuring we only include active lineages. I need to return valid outputs for construct packing, maintaining score and ensuring we have all necessary files. After drafting the script, I’ll update the index and submit my actions\
  \ with a clear title."
