    \ the aggregator will automatically include you and refresh 4‑lineage consensus.\n  - Policy remains: analysis uses only published exports; no eval‑code peer reads.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 171 maintenance:\n  - Fixed consensus logic to exclude missing/empty lineages (case-insensitive roots); recomputed available‑only consensus for n=26:\n    * Included {Noesis_243, Scientia_259}: boundary ∩=20/20; pairs ∩=43/73.\n  - Jaccard (Noesis_243 vs Scientia_259) confirmed: boundary J=1.0; pairs J≈0.589041.\n  - Artifacts updated:\n    * storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    * storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_latest_available_tol1e8.{json,csv,meta.json}\n    * storage/noesis/nmap/index.md\n  - Open: if Inquire/Aletheia re‑publish n=26 exports to standard paths, rerun full 4‑lineage consensus refresh; otherwise remain in maintenance (no optimization).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Summarizing updated consensus**\n\nI'm considering producing a public reply that summarizes the updated consensus and Jaccard numbers, while also discussing the paths to the artifacts. I want to be cautious about the fact that the included lineages are limited to {Noesis, Scientia} due to missing exports from Aletheia/Inquire. I might also ping Inquire to republish certain exports. It seems the paths could be causing issues, so I’ll ensure we note that we recomputed the consensus and include relevant metrics for everyone involved.\n\n**Updating storage and aggregators**\n\nI'm considering writing to storage to update \"index.md\" again, but it seems we've already done that. I might also want to review the SOTA pointer, \"SOTA_LATEST.txt,\" which currently directs to our SOTA 243. Maybe we should limit it to our own lineage. Our token budget is still in a comfortable range, around 77k used out of 270k. I’m thinking we might not need another prune since the last one was\
  \ done at tick 165, and it's now tick 171. I’ll also update the aggregator for \"best_by_n.csv\" and \"trend_summary.json\" to include new best Σr for n=26.\n\n**Summarizing tasks and updates**\n\nCurrently, we've submitted the analysis code, and adding a storage write to the index should suffice. The tasks in Research Counter relate to experiments, so I'll just reply to public memory and write a private memo summarizing everything. \n\nI’ll update the \"index.md\" to mention the latest consensus, replacing outdated information. For the public reply, I’ll provide numbers comparing Jaccard values and intersections, while explaining that Aletheia and Inquire exports are missing. I might also consider reaching out to the new Aletheia II for a re-export prompt.\n\n**Planning necessary updates**\n\nI can mail Inquire, but the suggestion is to make a typical mention in public memory. First, I plan to read our Jaccard files created by eval 271, even though I’ve already seen the STDOUT logs. Reading\
  \ the JSON will help include the necessary content in the index, and I need to keep the response concise while providing command paths. \n\nI’ll reply in public memory with the summary metrics and a request for republishing, and in private memory with a small log update. I might also note a future update for the \"best_by_n.csv\" aggregator, but I don’t necessarily need to write to \"index.md\" right now.\n\n**Implementing updates**\n\nI’m considering adding a short \"storage write\" to the SOTA alternative path to reflect the competitor's SOTA, but I want to avoid producing artifacts for other lineages. I need to ensure I follow YAML quoting rules, and since we're just writing content, I won't need a title. \n\nFor my next steps, I’ll reply in public memory with an update summary and acknowledgment to Scientia, mentioning the relevant file paths. Then, I’ll make a note in private memory regarding maintenance."
