tick: 179
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noesis I. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Maintenance-only. n=26 mapping current; Scientia I holds global SOTA (Eval 259, Σr=2.6358957). My latest is Eval 243 (Σr=2.6342924). Jaccard vs Scientia_259: boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.589041. I added compute_jaccard.py and diff/meta artifacts. Optimization remains frozen per protocol.\n\nReflection: To improve reproducibility and reduce friction for cross-lineage aggregation, I will publish a concise schema (v1) and a validator script so peers can self-check exports before posting. This should minimize parsing issues and standardize active-set comparisons.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_v1.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"tolerance\": \"1e-8\",\n    \"n_directory\": \"storage/<Lineage>/nmap/n<N>/\",\n    \"files\": {\n      \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\": {\n        \"description\": \"Active interior pair contacts at tol=1e-8\",\n        \"columns\": [\"i\", \"j\"],\n \
    \       \"types\": [\"int\", \"int\"],\n        \"index_base\": 0,\n        \"constraints\": [\n          \"0 <= i < N\",\n          \"0 <= j < N\",\n          \"i != j\",\n          \"store as (min(i,j), max(i,j))\",\n          \"no duplicates\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\": {\n        \"description\": \"Active boundary contacts at tol=1e-8\",\n        \"columns\": [\"i\", \"side\"],\n        \"types\": [\"int\", \"string\"],\n        \"enum_side\": [\"xL\",\"xR\",\"yB\",\"yT\"],\n        \"constraints\": [\"0 <= i < N\"]\n      },\n      \"centers.txt\": {\n        \"description\": \"Centers array\",\n        \"shape\": [ \"N\", 2 ],\n        \"dtype\": \"float\"\n      },\n      \"radii.txt\": {\n        \"description\": \"Radii array\",\n        \"shape\": [ \"N\" ],\n        \"dtype\": \"float\",\n        \"constraints\": [\"r_i > 0\"]\n      },\n      \"summary_tol1e8.json\": {\n        \"description\": \"Summary with counts and Σr reference\",\n \
    \       \"required_keys\": [\"n\",\"sum_r\",\"boundary_count\",\"pairs_count\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"CSV delimiter may be auto-detected; prefer commas.\",\n      \"Boundary sides are canonicalized to {xL,xR,yB,yT}. Aliases allowed in input; tooling will normalize.\",\n      \"All artifacts should be derived from the same packing at tol=1e-8.\"\n    ],\n    \"policy\": \"Analysis uses only published exports; no eval-code peer reads.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/validate_exports.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import argparse, os, json, csv\n  from typing import List, Tuple, Set\n\n  VALID_SIDES = {\"xL\",\"xR\",\"yB\",\"yT\"}\n\n  def load_pairs(path: str) -> List[Tuple[int,int]]:\n      pairs = []\n      with open(path, 'r', newline='') as f:\n          r = csv.reader(f)\n          for row in r:\n              if not row: continue\n              if len(row) == 1:\n                  toks = [t for t in row[0].replace(',', ' ').split() if\
    \ t]\n                  if len(toks) >= 2:\n                      row = toks[:2]\n              if len(row) < 2: continue\n              try:\n                  i = int(float(row[0])); j = int(float(row[1]))\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              a, b = (i, j) if i <= j else (j, i)\n              pairs.append((a, b))\n      return pairs\n\n  def load_boundary(path: str) -> List[Tuple[int,str]]:\n      items = []\n      with open(path, 'r', newline='') as f:\n          r = csv.reader(f)\n          for row in r:\n              if not row: continue\n              if len(row) == 1:\n                  toks = [t for t in row[0].replace(',', ' ').split() if t]\n                  if len(toks) >= 2:\n                      row = toks[:2]\n              if len(row) < 2: continue\n              try:\n                  i = int(float(row[0]))\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              side = str(row[1]).strip()\n              items.append((i,\
    \ side))\n      return items\n\n  def validate(n: int, dirpath: str):\n      report = {\"n\": n, \"dir\": dirpath, \"errors\": [], \"warnings\": [], \"stats\": {}}\n\n      def err(msg): report[\"errors\"].append(msg)\n      def warn(msg): report[\"warnings\"].append(msg)\n\n      apath = os.path.join(dirpath, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\")\n      bpath = os.path.join(dirpath, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\")\n      cpath = os.path.join(dirpath, \"centers.txt\")\n      rpath = os.path.join(dirpath, \"radii.txt\")\n      spath = os.path.join(dirpath, \"summary_tol1e8.json\")\n\n      for p in [apath, bpath, cpath, rpath, spath]:\n          if not os.path.exists(p):\n              err(f\"missing file: {p}\")\n\n      if os.path.exists(apath):\n          pairs = load_pairs(apath)\n          S: Set[Tuple[int,int]] = set()\n          dup = 0\n          bad = 0\n          out = 0\n          for (i,j) in pairs:\n              if i == j: bad += 1\n              if not (0 <= i < n and 0 <= j < n):\
    \ out += 1\n              canon = (i, j) if i <= j else (j, i)\n              if canon in S: dup += 1\n              S.add(canon)\n          report[\"stats\"][\"pairs_count\"] = len(S)\n          if dup: warn(f\"duplicate pairs (after canonicalization): {dup}\")\n          if bad: err(f\"pairs with i==j: {bad}\")\n          if out: err(f\"pairs with out-of-range index: {out}\")\n\n      if os.path.exists(bpath):\n          items = load_boundary(bpath)\n          B: Set[Tuple[int,str]] = set()\n          bad_side = 0\n          out = 0\n          dup = 0\n          for (i,side) in items:\n              if side not in VALID_SIDES:\n                  bad_side += 1\n              if not (0 <= i < n):\n                  out += 1\n              key = (i, side)\n              if key in B: dup += 1\n              B.add(key)\n          report[\"stats\"][\"boundary_count\"] = len(B)\n          if dup: warn(f\"duplicate boundary rows: {dup}\")\n          if bad_side: err(f\"invalid boundary side\
    \ labels: {bad_side}\")\n          if out: err(f\"boundary rows with out-of-range index: {out}\")\n\n      if os.path.exists(cpath):\n          try:\n              with open(cpath, 'r') as f:\n                  rows = [line.strip().split() for line in f if line.strip()]\n                  if len(rows) != n: err(f\"centers row count {len(rows)} != n\")\n                  for row in rows:\n                      if len(row) < 2: err(\"centers row with <2 columns\")\n          except Exception as e:\n              err(f\"failed to read centers: {e}\")\n\n      if os.path.exists(rpath):\n          try:\n              with open(rpath, 'r') as f:\n                  vals = [line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()]\n                  if len(vals) != n: err(f\"radii count {len(vals)} != n\")\n          except Exception as e:\n              err(f\"failed to read radii: {e}\")\n\n      if os.path.exists(spath):\n          try:\n              with open(spath, 'r') as f:\n                  s =\
    \ json.load(f)\n              for k in [\"n\", \"sum_r\", \"boundary_count\", \"pairs_count\"]:\n                  if k not in s: warn(f\"summary missing key: {k}\")\n              if \"n\" in s and s[\"n\"] != n:\n                  warn(f\"summary.n={s['n']} differs from n={n}\")\n          except Exception as e:\n              err(f\"failed to read summary: {e}\")\n\n      report[\"ok\"] = len(report[\"errors\"]) == 0\n      return report\n\n      # end validate\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Validate nmap export directory against SCHEMA_v1.\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=26)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--dir\", required=True)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--out\", default=\"\")\n      args = ap.parse_args()\n      rep = validate(args.n, args.dir)\n      s = json.dumps(rep, indent=2)\n      if args.out:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out), exist_ok=True)\n          with open(args.out, 'w') as f:\n     \
    \         f.write(s+\"\\n\")\n      print(s)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/README.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  nmap tools and artifacts (tol=1e−8) — Noesis lineage\n\n  Purpose\n  - Self‑contained scripts and CSV/JSON artifacts to compare/validate active sets across lineages for n=26.\n  - Analysis uses published exports only (no eval‑code peer reads).\n\n  Schema\n  - See SCHEMA_v1.json for file names, shapes, and constraints.\n\n  Utilities\n  - compute_jaccard.py — robust Jaccard calculator for active_{boundary,pairs}_tol1e8.csv.\n  - validate_exports.py — checks an export directory against SCHEMA_v1; emits JSON report.\n\n  Examples\n  - Compute Jaccard (Scientia_259 vs Noesis_243):\n    python compute_jaccard.py \\\n      --a_boundary storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv \\\n      --a_pairs    storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv \\\n      --b_boundary storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv \\\n      --b_pairs\
    \    storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv \\\n      --out_prefix storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8\n\n  - Validate an export directory:\n    python validate_exports.py --n 26 --dir storage/Scientia/nmap/n26 --out storage/noesis/nmap/validation_scientia_n26.json\n\n  Artifacts index\n  - GLOBAL_SOTA.json, index.md\n  - jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n  - delta_vs_similarity_n26.{json,csv}\n  - diff_scientia259_vs_noesis243_meta.{json,csv}\n  - consensus_n26_latest_available_tol1e8.{json,csv,meta.json}\n\n  Policy\n  - Exports‑only analysis; no eval‑code peer reads. All paths relative to Station storage.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Maintenance note (Tick 179): Published nmap SCHEMA_v1.json and validate_exports.py alongside compute_jaccard.py.\n  - Goal: reduce parsing friction and standardize n=26 exports so aggregators can auto‑ingest.\n  - If you publish\
    \ under the schema (active_{boundary,pairs}_tol1e8.csv; centers.txt; radii.txt; summary_tol1e8.json), my tools can validate and compute Jaccards without running eval code.\n  - Paths: storage/noesis/nmap/{SCHEMA_v1.json, compute_jaccard.py, validate_exports.py, README.md}\n  - As always: exports‑only analysis; no eval‑code peer reads.\n```"
