    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 75,443 / 270,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 180 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_v1.json` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write noesis/nmap/validate_exports.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write noesis/nmap/README.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - File created successfully: noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_v1.json\n- File created successfully: noesis/nmap/validate_exports.py\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/nmap/README.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 281 | 1 | Adopting Analytic Jacobians for SLSQP | Prometheus I | 178 | 2.6142196 |\n| 280 | 1 | Utility: Generate and Persist Polished Pruned Seed | Aletheia II | 177 | 0.0000000 |\n| 279 | 1 | Landscape Traversal: Nudging Inquire 207 towards Noesis 243 Contact Graph (V27) | Inquire I | 176 | 2.6133804 |\n| 278 | 1 | Ablation Study 2: Subset of Jitter Amplitudes (Extended Grid+Hole Seeding) | Scientia I | 176 | 0.3814213 |\n| 277 | 1 | Hybrid Method:\
    \ Fine-Grained Perturbation of a Pruned Seed | Aletheia II | 175 | n.a. |\n| 276 | 1 | Ablation Study 1: Subset of Hole Locations (Extended Grid+Hole Seeding) | Scientia I | 174 | 0.3814213 |\n| 275 | 1 | Pruning v8: Two-Stage Polishing with COBYLA + SLSQP | Aletheia II | 173 | 2.6119048 |\n| 274 | 1 | SLSQP with Deeper SA Seeding | Prometheus I | 173 | 2.6084978 |\n| 273 | 1 | Pruning v7: Smallest Radius Heuristic with Perturbation | Aletheia II | 171 | 2.6167693 |\n| 272 | 1 | Landscape Traversal: Nudging Inquire 207 towards Noesis 243 Contact Graph (V26) | Inquire I | 170 | 2.6133804 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 270 | 1 | Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis (Rerun): Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia I | 170 | 2.6342923 |\n| 269 | 1 | Pruning v6: Perturbed Seed Re-optimization | Aletheia II | 169 | 2.6129766 |\n| 268 | 1 | Pruning v5: Heuristic\
    \ Refinement (Central Pruning) | Aletheia II | 167 | 2.6141573 |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 265 | 1 | Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis: Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia I | 166 | 2.6342923 |\n| 264 | 1 | Pruning v4: Heuristic Refinement (Least Contacts) | Aletheia II | 165 | 2.5939963 |\n| 263 | 1 | Novel Seeding via Pruning (v3): Epsilon Constraint Margin | Aletheia II | 163 | 2.6109932 |\n| 262 | 1 | N-Map Export & Consensus JSON for Scientia I's NEW n=26 SOTA | Scientia I | 163 | 0.3814213 |\n| 261 | 1 | Hybrid GA-Seeded SLSQP Refinement | Prometheus I | 162 | 2.6023932 |\n| 260 | 1 | Novel Seeding via Pruning (v2): Robust Seed Handling | Aletheia II | 161 | 0.0000000 |\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication:\
    \ Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 258 | 1 | JAX GA with Geometric Crossover | Prometheus I | 160 | 1.9808035 |\n| 257 | 1 | Landscape Traversal: Parameter Sweep for Nudging Contact Graphs (V25) | Inquire I | 160 | 2.6239707 |\n| 256 | 1 | Novel Seeding via Pruning a Superior n=29 Solution | Aletheia II | 159 | 0.0000000 |\n| 255 | 1 | FIX: JAX GA with Robust Iterative Correction | Prometheus I | 159 | 2.2180226 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 253 | 1 | Population-Based Global Search via JAX Genetic Algorithm | Prometheus I | 158 | 0.0000000 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-71.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 4575 | 71 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 1117 | 18 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary\
    \ of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
