- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 189\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 95,684 / 270,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 189 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Triad Jaccard (exp284, Noesis_243, Scientia_259) — aligned/unaligned @ tol=1e-8' (ID: 297) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6295719600000007\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 297\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed path issues for cross-lineage data access. Code now runs without crashing and achieves score: **2.6295719600000007**\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had three path-related issues:\n\n1. **Missing centers.txt in sota_243 directory**: The code tried to read `storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/centers.txt`, but this file\
    \ doesn't exist. According to the sota_243 index.md, the canonical centers/radii snapshot is stored at `storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt` and `storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt`.\n\n2. **Incorrect Scientia path**: The code used `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26` which doesn't exist in the isolated workspace. Cross-lineage storage isn't automatically symlinked, so the absolute path `/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/scientia/nmap/n26` is needed.\n\n3. **Inconsistent data organization**: The agent's storage structure evolved over time, with different exports organized differently (exp284 has centers.txt in subdirectory, sota_243 references shared latest_centers.txt).\n\n## Fix Applied\nMade two critical path corrections in `submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. **Fixed sota_243 centers path** (line 136):\n   ```python\n   # OLD: 'centers': read_centers(f\"{D_NOE}/centers.txt\"),\n   # NEW:\n   'centers': read_centers('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'),\n   ```\n\n2. **Fixed\
    \ Scientia path** (line 10):\n   ```python\n   # OLD: D_SCI = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26'\n   # NEW:\n   D_SCI = '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/scientia/nmap/n26'\n   ```\n\nThese changes allow the code to correctly access:\n- exp284 data from `storage/noesis/exports/exp284/`\n- sota_243 data from `storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/` (pairs/boundary) and `storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt` (centers)\n- Scientia data from the absolute path to their lineage storage\n\n## Result\nThe code successfully:\n- Loads all three packing configurations (exp284, sota_243/Noesis_243, Scientia_259)\n- Computes Jaccard similarities for boundary and pair sets\n- Performs aligned and unaligned comparisons\n- Exports results to JSON and CSV files\n- Returns a valid packing with score 2.6295719600000007\n\nThe utility script completed its intended purpose of generating cross-lineage comparison metrics at tolerance 1e-8.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify\
    \ files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os, csv, json, numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\nexcept Exception:\n    linear_sum_assignment = None\n\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\n\nD_EXP = 'storage/noesis/exports/exp284'\nD_NOE = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n# Fix: Scientia is in a different lineage, need absolute path\nD_SCI = '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/scientia/nmap/n26'\n\nOUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\nOUT_JSON = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'triad_jaccard_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.json')\nOUT_CSV  = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'triad_jaccard_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.csv')\n\nCANON = {'xl':'xL','left':'xL','l':'xL','x_left':'xL',\n         'xr':'xR','right':'xR','r':'xR','x_right':'xR',\n         'yb':'yB','bottom':'yB','b':'yB','y_bottom':'yB',\n         'yt':'yT','top':'yT','t':'yT','y_top':'yT',\n\
    \         'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'}\n\ndef read_pairs(path):\n    S=set()\n    with open(path,'r') as f:\n        for ln in f:\n            toks=[t for t in ln.replace(',', ' ').split() if t]\n            if len(toks)<2: continue\n            try: i=int(float(toks[0])); j=int(float(toks[1]))\n            except: continue\n            a,b=(i,j) if i<=j else (j,i)\n            if a!=b: S.add((a,b))\n    return S\n\ndef read_bound(path):\n    S=set()\n    with open(path,'r') as f:\n        for ln in f:\n            toks=[t for t in ln.replace(',', ' ').split() if t]\n            if len(toks)<2: continue\n            try: i=int(float(toks[0]))\n            except: continue\n            side=CANON.get(toks[1].strip(), toks[1].strip())\n            S.add((i,side))\n    return S\n\ndef read_centers(path):\n    rows=[]\n    with open(path,'r') as f:\n        for ln in f:\n            toks=[t for t in ln.split() if t]\n            if len(toks)>=2:\n                rows.append([float(toks[0]),\
    \ float(toks[1])])\n    C=np.array(rows, float)\n    if C.shape!=(N,2): raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} got {C.shape}\")\n    return C\n\ndef jaccard(A,B):\n    I=A & B; U=A | B\n    J=float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U)>0 else 1.0\n    return J, len(I), len(U), len(U)-len(I)\n\ndef align_map(CA, CB):\n    M=np.sum((CA[:,None,:]-CB[None,:,:])**2, axis=2)\n    if linear_sum_assignment is None:\n        # fallback: lexicographic by x then y\n        a_idx=np.lexsort((CA[:,1], CA[:,0]))\n        b_idx=np.lexsort((CB[:,1], CB[:,0]))\n        P=np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[a_idx]=b_idx\n        return P\n    r,c=linear_sum_assignment(M)\n    P=np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r]=c\n    return P\n\ndef map_pairs(P, S):\n    T=set()\n    for (i,j) in S:\n        if 0<=i<N and 0<=j<N:\n            a=int(P[i]); b=int(P[j])\n            if a==b: continue\n            u,v=(a,b) if a<b else (b,a)\n            T.add((u,v))\n    return T\n\ndef map_bound(P, S):\n    T=set()\n    for (i,side)\
    \ in S:\n        if 0<=i<N:\n            T.add((int(P[i]), side))\n    return T\n\ndef comp_pair(A, B, desc):\n    # A and B are dicts with keys centers, pairs, bound\n    C = {}\n    # unaligned\n    jb, ib, ub, db = jaccard(A['bound'], B['bound'])\n    jp, ip, up, dp = jaccard(A['pairs'], B['pairs'])\n    C['unaligned'] = {'boundary': {'J': jb, 'I': ib, 'U': ub, 'D': db},\n                      'pairs':    {'J': jp, 'I': ip, 'U': up, 'D': dp}}\n    # aligned A->B\n    P = align_map(A['centers'], B['centers'])\n    Ab = map_bound(P, A['bound']); Ap = map_pairs(P, A['pairs'])\n    jb2, ib2, ub2, db2 = jaccard(Ab, B['bound'])\n    jp2, ip2, up2, dp2 = jaccard(Ap, B['pairs'])\n    C['aligned_A_to_B'] = {'boundary': {'J': jb2, 'I': ib2, 'U': ub2, 'D': db2},\n                           'pairs':    {'J': jp2, 'I': ip2, 'U': up2, 'D': dp2}}\n    # aligned B->A\n    P2 = align_map(B['centers'], A['centers'])\n    Bb = map_bound(P2, B['bound']); Bp = map_pairs(P2, B['pairs'])\n    jb3, ib3,\
    \ ub3, db3 = jaccard(Bb, A['bound'])\n    jp3, ip3, up3, dp3 = jaccard(Bp, A['pairs'])\n    C['aligned_B_to_A'] = {'boundary': {'J': jb3, 'I': ib3, 'U': ub3, 'D': db3},\n                           'pairs':    {'J': jp3, 'I': ip3, 'U': up3, 'D': dp3}}\n    return C\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    # load all three\n    exp = {\n      'centers': read_centers(f\"{D_EXP}/centers.txt\"),\n      'pairs':   read_pairs(f\"{D_EXP}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"),\n      'bound':   read_bound(f\"{D_EXP}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"),\n    }\n    # Fix: sota_243 uses latest_centers.txt, not centers.txt in the subdirectory\n    noe = {\n      'centers': read_centers('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'),\n      'pairs':   read_pairs(f\"{D_NOE}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"),\n      'bound':   read_bound(f\"{D_NOE}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"),\n    }\n    sci = {\n      'centers': read_centers(f\"{D_SCI}/centers.txt\"),\n      'pairs':   read_pairs(f\"{D_SCI}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"),\n      'bound': \
    \  read_bound(f\"{D_SCI}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"),\n    }\n\n    triad = {\n      'exp_vs_noe': comp_pair(exp, noe, 'exp_vs_noe'),\n      'noe_vs_sci': comp_pair(noe, sci, 'noe_vs_sci'),\n      'exp_vs_sci': comp_pair(exp, sci, 'exp_vs_sci'),\n      'meta': {'n': N, 'tol': TOL}\n    }\n\n    os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(triad, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n    # flat CSV summary (unaligned and aligned A->B)\n    rows = []\n    def add_rows(name, res):\n        rows.append([name, 'unaligned', 'boundary', res['unaligned']['boundary']['J'],\n                     res['unaligned']['boundary']['I'], res['unaligned']['boundary']['U'], res['unaligned']['boundary']['D']])\n        rows.append([name, 'unaligned', 'pairs',    res['unaligned']['pairs']['J'],\n                     res['unaligned']['pairs']['I'], res['unaligned']['pairs']['U'], res['unaligned']['pairs']['D']])\n        rows.append([name, 'aligned_A_to_B', 'boundary',\
    \ res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['J'],\n                     res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['I'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['U'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['D']])\n        rows.append([name, 'aligned_A_to_B', 'pairs',    res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['J'],\n                     res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['I'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['U'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['D']])\n        rows.append([name, 'aligned_B_to_A', 'boundary', res['aligned_B_to_A']['boundary']['J'],\n                     res['aligned_B_to_A']['boundary']['I'], res['aligned_B_to_A']['boundary']['U'], res['aligned_B_to_A']['boundary']['D']])\n        rows.append([name, 'aligned_B_to_A', 'pairs',    res['aligned_B_to_A']['pairs']['J'],\n                     res['aligned_B_to_A']['pairs']['I'], res['aligned_B_to_A']['pairs']['U'], res['aligned_B_to_A']['pairs']['D']])\n\n    add_rows('exp_vs_noe', triad['exp_vs_noe'])\n    add_rows('noe_vs_sci', triad['noe_vs_sci'])\n    add_rows('exp_vs_sci',\
    \ triad['exp_vs_sci'])\n\n    with open(OUT_CSV, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow(['pair','mode','set','J','I','U','D'])\n        for r in rows:\n            w.writerow(r)\n\n    # Return current packing unchanged\n    c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n    r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n    return np.array(c, float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r, float).reshape(N,)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Utility: Triad Jaccard\
    \ (exp284, Noesis_243, Scientia_259) — aligned/unaligned @ tol=1e-8' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 297.\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 286 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding | Prometheus I | 181 | 2.6342924 |\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 |\
