role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Triad Jaccard v4 (index normalization + robust canonicalization) @ tol=1e-8\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard, alignment, diagnostics, canonicalization, normalization\"\nabstract: \"Recompute triad Jaccards among exp284, Noesis SOTA 243, and Scientia SOTA 259 at tol=1e-8 with robust boundary label canonicalization AND index normalization (auto-detect 0-based vs 1-based). Includes Hungarian alignment by centers. Emits JSON/CSV with normalization metadata; returns current packing unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\n  except Exception:\n      linear_sum_assignment = None\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n\n  D_EXP = 'storage/noesis/exports/exp284'\n  D_NOE = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n  D_SCI_CAND = [\n      'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26',\n      '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/scientia/nmap/n26',\n\
    \  ]\n\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n  OUT_JSON = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'triad_jaccard_v4_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.json')\n  OUT_CSV  = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'triad_jaccard_v4_exp284_noesis243_scientia259_tol1e8.csv')\n\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','left':'xL','l':'xL','x_left':'xL',\n    'xr':'xR','right':'xR','r':'xR','x_right':'xR',\n    'yb':'yB','bottom':'yB','b':'yB','y_bottom':'yB',\n    'yt':'yT','top':'yT','t':'yT','y_top':'yT',\n    'xl.':'xL','xr.':'xR','yb.':'yB','yt.':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n\n  def first_existing(paths):\n      for p in paths:\n          if isinstance(p, (list, tuple)):\n              p = os.path.join(*p)\n          if os.path.exists(p):\n              return p\n      return None\n\n  def read_pairs_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      with open(path,'r') as f:\n          for ln in f:\n              toks=[t for t in ln.replace(',', ' ').split() if t]\n              if len(toks)<2: continue\n              try:\n\
    \                  i=int(float(toks[0])); j=int(float(toks[1]))\n              except:\n                  continue\n              rows.append((i,j))\n      return rows\n\n  def read_bound_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      with open(path,'r') as f:\n          for ln in f:\n              toks=[t for t in ln.replace(',', ' ').split() if t]\n              if len(toks)<2: continue\n              try:\n                  i=int(float(toks[0]))\n              except:\n                  continue\n              side_raw = toks[1].strip()\n              side = CANON.get(side_raw.lower(), side_raw)\n              side2 = CANON.get(side.lower().strip(' :;,'), side)\n              if side2 in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n                  rows.append((i, side2))\n      return rows\n\n  def normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n      # kind: 'pairs' or 'bound'\n      # Decide 0-based (0..N-1) vs 1-based (1..N)\n      if kind=='pairs':\n          idxs = [i for (i,_) in rows] + [j for (_,j) in rows]\n      else:\n\
    \          idxs = [i for (i,_) in rows]\n      if not idxs:\n          return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n\n      c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n      c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N     for v in idxs)\n      meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n\n      out=set()\n      if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n          # Likely 1-based: shift down by 1\n          meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n          if kind=='pairs':\n              for (i,j) in rows:\n                  a,b = i-1, j-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a!=b:\n                      u,v = (a,b) if a<b else (b,a)\n                      out.add((u,v))\n          else:\n              for (i,s) in rows:\n                  a = i-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N:\n                      out.add((a,s))\n      else:\n          # Assume 0-based\n          if kind=='pairs':\n              for (i,j) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i!=j:\n\
    \                      u,v = (i,j) if i<j else (j,i)\n                      out.add((u,v))\n          else:\n              for (i,s) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N:\n                      out.add((i,s))\n      return out, meta\n\n  def read_centers(path):\n      rows=[]\n      with open(path,'r') as f:\n          for ln in f:\n              toks=[t for t in ln.split() if t]\n              if len(toks)>=2:\n                  rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n      C=np.array(rows, float)\n      if C.shape!=(N,2): raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} got {C.shape}\")\n      return C\n\n  def jaccard(A,B):\n      I=A & B; U=A | B\n      J=float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U)>0 else 1.0\n      return J, len(I), len(U), len(U)-len(I)\n\n  def align_map(CA, CB):\n      M=np.sum((CA[:,None,:]-CB[None,:,:])**2, axis=2)\n      if linear_sum_assignment is None:\n          a_idx=np.lexsort((CA[:,1], CA[:,0]))\n          b_idx=np.lexsort((CB[:,1], CB[:,0]))\n\
    \          P=np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[a_idx]=b_idx\n          return P\n      r,c=linear_sum_assignment(M)\n      P=np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r]=c\n      return P\n\n  def map_pairs(P, S):\n      T=set()\n      for (i,j) in S:\n          if 0<=i<N and 0<=j<N:\n              a=int(P[i]); b=int(P[j])\n              if a==b: continue\n              u,v=(a,b) if a<b else (b,a)\n              T.add((u,v))\n      return T\n\n  def map_bound(P, S):\n      T=set()\n      for (i,side) in S:\n          if 0<=i<N:\n              T.add((int(P[i]), side))\n      return T\n\n  def load_pack(dir_pairs, dir_bound, centers_path=None):\n      pr_raw = read_pairs_raw(os.path.join(dir_pairs, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'))\n      bd_raw = read_bound_raw(os.path.join(dir_bound, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'))\n      pairs, m_pairs = normalize_indices(pr_raw, 'pairs')\n      bound, m_bound = normalize_indices(bd_raw, 'bound')\n      C = read_centers(centers_path) if centers_path else None\n      return {'pairs':\
    \ pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C,\n              'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs, 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\n  def comp_pair(A, B, do_align=True):\n      C = {'meta': {'A_norm': A['meta'], 'B_norm': B['meta']}}\n      jb, ib, ub, db = jaccard(A['bound'], B['bound'])\n      jp, ip, up, dp = jaccard(A['pairs'], B['pairs'])\n      C['unaligned'] = {'boundary': {'J': jb, 'I': ib, 'U': ub, 'D': db},\n                        'pairs':    {'J': jp, 'I': ip, 'U': up, 'D': dp}}\n      if do_align and A.get('centers') is not None and B.get('centers') is not None:\n          P = align_map(A['centers'], B['centers'])\n          Ab = map_bound(P, A['bound']); Ap = map_pairs(P, A['pairs'])\n          jb2, ib2, ub2, db2 = jaccard(Ab, B['bound'])\n          jp2, ip2, up2, dp2 = jaccard(Ap, B['pairs'])\n          C['aligned_A_to_B'] = {'boundary': {'J': jb2, 'I': ib2, 'U': ub2, 'D': db2},\n                                 'pairs':    {'J': jp2, 'I': ip2, 'U': up2, 'D': dp2}}\n      return C\n\n  def\
    \ construct_packing():\n      # Paths\n      sci_dir = first_existing(D_SCI_CAND)\n      if not sci_dir:\n          raise FileNotFoundError(\"Scientia n=26 path not found.\")\n\n      # Load packs\n      exp = load_pack(D_EXP, D_EXP, centers_path=os.path.join(D_EXP, 'centers.txt'))\n      noe_centers = first_existing([os.path.join(D_NOE, 'centers.txt'),\n                                    'storage/noesis/latest_centers_sota243.txt',\n                                    'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'])  # last resort\n      noe = load_pack(D_NOE, D_NOE, centers_path=noe_centers if noe_centers else None)\n      sci = load_pack(sci_dir, sci_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(sci_dir, 'centers.txt'))\n\n      triad = {\n        'exp_vs_noe': comp_pair(exp, noe, do_align=(noe['centers'] is not None)),\n        'noe_vs_sci': comp_pair(noe, sci, do_align=(noe['centers'] is not None)),\n        'exp_vs_sci': comp_pair(exp, sci, do_align=True),\n        'meta': {'n': N, 'tol': TOL, 'noe_centers_path':\
    \ noe_centers or 'None'}\n      }\n\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUT_JSON, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(triad, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n      # Flatten CSV\n      rows=[]\n      def add(name, res):\n          rows.append([name, 'unaligned', 'boundary', res['unaligned']['boundary']['J'],\n                       res['unaligned']['boundary']['I'], res['unaligned']['boundary']['U'], res['unaligned']['boundary']['D'],\n                       res['meta']['A_norm']['bound_norm']['mode'], res['meta']['B_norm']['bound_norm']['mode']])\n          rows.append([name, 'unaligned', 'pairs',    res['unaligned']['pairs']['J'],\n                       res['unaligned']['pairs']['I'], res['unaligned']['pairs']['U'], res['unaligned']['pairs']['D'],\n                       res['meta']['A_norm']['pairs_norm']['mode'], res['meta']['B_norm']['pairs_norm']['mode']])\n          if 'aligned_A_to_B' in res:\n              rows.append([name, 'aligned_A_to_B', 'boundary',\
    \ res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['J'],\n                           res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['I'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['U'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['boundary']['D'],\n                           res['meta']['A_norm']['bound_norm']['mode'], res['meta']['B_norm']['bound_norm']['mode']])\n              rows.append([name, 'aligned_A_to_B', 'pairs',    res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['J'],\n                           res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['I'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['U'], res['aligned_A_to_B']['pairs']['D'],\n                           res['meta']['A_norm']['pairs_norm']['mode'], res['meta']['B_norm']['pairs_norm']['mode']])\n\n      add('exp_vs_noe', triad['exp_vs_noe'])\n      add('noe_vs_sci', triad['noe_vs_sci'])\n      add('exp_vs_sci', triad['exp_vs_sci'])\n\n      with open(OUT_CSV, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow(['pair','mode','set','J','I','U','D','A_norm','B_norm'])\n          for r in rows:\n   \
    \           w.writerow(r)\n\n      # Return current packing unchanged\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n      r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n      return np.array(c, float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r, float).reshape(N,)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing current situation**\n\nI need to respond appropriately regarding the current state. There's a maintenance mode for Station tick 191, and they've submitted the Triad Jaccard v3 utility. The generated triad report should be reviewed to check if boundary J improved since the previous report showed boundary J=0.0, which contradicted an earlier claim of boundary J=1.0. Next, I’ll look into the JSON file for results, update the index, and keep my message concise.\n\n**Analyzing boundary intersections**\n\nIt seems that earlier results indicate that the boundary intersection between Noesis and Scientia shifted from 1 to 0 due to misalignment. The past claim of boundary J=1.0 contradicts the current findings of boundary J=0.0 with union size U=40 and I=0. I wonder if the Scientia exports differ in how they label boundaries or the size of boundary sets. There's a suggestion that the CSV labels might represent multiple constraints per disc, and the total active boundary\
  \ constraints across all discs could be a key here.\n\n**Evaluating boundary constraints**\n\nThe earlier result of \"active boundary = 20 at tol=1e-8\" implies 20 active boundary constraints across 26 discs. It’s not necessarily 20 discs with one boundary each. The union suggests both packings share the same 20 constraints. However, the triad JSON indicates a union of 40, which raises questions. It seems like the issue might stem from how the Scientia boundary CSV indexes discs, possibly starting at 1 instead of 0. This indexing inconsistency could explain the intersection discrepancies. Adjustments will be needed for accurate indexing.\n\n**Updating boundary utility**\n\nI think it's time to create a utility that detects off-by-one indexing by analyzing index ranges and adjusting for 1-based indexing. There was solid canonicalization for labels, but not for index offsets. I should propose running a \"boundary index normalization\" script for the Scientia boundary CSV. This would involve\
  \ making a new submit utility to read the boundary CSV, checking for any index equal to 26, and adjusting indices as necessary. Plus, we want to avoid using absolute paths since they're not ideal for storage.\n\n**Creating Triad Jaccard v4**\n\nIt seems there’s some confusion with the paths used. We initially had success reading from 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26,' but debugging switched to an absolute path, which isn't ideal. To address this, I plan to implement detection: first try the relative path and if that fails, fall back to the absolute path. \n\nI want to develop a new utility, \"Triad Jaccard v4 with boundary index normalization.\" This will read boundary sets, normalize indices as needed, and ensure no trailing header lines exist. After recalculating the triad, I’ll provide a JSON outcome and update the mapping index accordingly. Let's get to coding!"
