tick: 193
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Jaccard — Prometheus SOTA 298 vs Noesis_243 and Scientia_259 (unaligned + aligned) @ tol=1e-8\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard, alignment, consensus, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Reads Prometheus n=26 exports and computes Jaccard (boundary, pairs) vs Noesis_243 and Scientia_259 at tol=1e-8, both unaligned and Hungarian-aligned by centers. Also computes 3-lineage consensus (Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298). Writes JSON/CSV under storage/noesis/nmap/. Returns current Noesis packing unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\n  except Exception:\n      linear_sum_assignment = None\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n\n  # Directories (with robust fallbacks)\n  D_NOE = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n  D_SCI_CAND = [\n      'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26',\n      '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/scientia/nmap/n26',\n\
    \  ]\n  D_PRO_CAND = [\n      'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26',\n      'storage/prometheus/nmap/n26',\n      '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/prometheus/nmap/n26',\n  ]\n\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','left':'xL','l':'xL','x_left':'xL',\n    'xr':'xR','right':'xR','r':'xR','x_right':'xR',\n    'yb':'yB','bottom':'yB','b':'yB','y_bottom':'yB',\n    'yt':'yT','top':'yT','t':'yT','y_top':'yT',\n    'xl.':'xL','xr.':'xR','yb.':'yB','yt.':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n\n  def first_existing(paths):\n      for p in paths:\n          if isinstance(p, (list, tuple)):\n              p = os.path.join(*p)\n          if os.path.exists(p):\n              return p\n      return None\n\n  def read_pairs_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      with open(path,'r') as f:\n          for ln in f:\n              toks=[t for t in ln.replace(',', ' ').split() if t]\n              if len(toks)<2: continue\n             \
    \ try:\n                  i=int(float(toks[0])); j=int(float(toks[1]))\n              except:\n                  continue\n              rows.append((i,j))\n      return rows\n\n  def read_bound_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      with open(path,'r') as f:\n          for ln in f:\n              toks=[t for t in ln.replace(',', ' ').split() if t]\n              if len(toks)<2: continue\n              try:\n                  i=int(float(toks[0]))\n              except:\n                  continue\n              side_raw = toks[1].strip()\n              side = CANON.get(side_raw.lower(), side_raw)\n              side2 = CANON.get(side.lower().strip(' :;,'), side)\n              if side2 in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n                  rows.append((i, side2))\n      return rows\n\n  def normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n      # Decide 0-based vs 1-based and normalize to 0-based in [0..N-1]\n      if kind=='pairs':\n          idxs = [i for (i,_) in rows] + [j for (_,j) in rows]\n      else:\n    \
    \      idxs = [i for (i,_) in rows]\n      if not idxs:\n          return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n\n      c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n      c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N     for v in idxs)\n      meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n      out=set()\n      if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n          meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n          if kind=='pairs':\n              for (i,j) in rows:\n                  a,b = i-1, j-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a!=b:\n                      u,v = (a,b) if a<b else (b,a)\n                      out.add((u,v))\n          else:\n              for (i,s) in rows:\n                  a = i-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N:\n                      out.add((a,s))\n      else:\n          if kind=='pairs':\n              for (i,j) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i!=j:\n                      u,v = (i,j) if i<j else (j,i)\n                      out.add((u,v))\n\
    \          else:\n              for (i,s) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N:\n                      out.add((i,s))\n      return out, meta\n\n  def read_centers(path):\n      rows=[]\n      with open(path,'r') as f:\n          for ln in f:\n              toks=[t for t in ln.split() if t]\n              if len(toks)>=2:\n                  rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n      C=np.array(rows, float)\n      if C.shape!=(N,2): raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} got {C.shape}\")\n      return C\n\n  def jaccard(A,B):\n      I=A & B; U=A | B\n      J=float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U)>0 else 1.0\n      return J, len(I), len(U), len(U)-len(I)\n\n  def align_map(CA, CB):\n      M=np.sum((CA[:,None,:]-CB[None,:,:])**2, axis=2)\n      if linear_sum_assignment is None:\n          a_idx=np.lexsort((CA[:,1], CA[:,0]))\n          b_idx=np.lexsort((CB[:,1], CB[:,0]))\n          P=np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[a_idx]=b_idx\n          return P\n      r,c=linear_sum_assignment(M)\n\
    \      P=np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r]=c\n      return P\n\n  def map_pairs(P, S):\n      T=set()\n      for (i,j) in S:\n          if 0<=i<N and 0<=j<N:\n              a=int(P[i]); b=int(P[j])\n              if a==b: continue\n              u,v=(a,b) if a<b else (b,a)\n              T.add((u,v))\n      return T\n\n  def map_bound(P, S):\n      T=set()\n      for (i,side) in S:\n          if 0<=i<N:\n              T.add((int(P[i]), side))\n      return T\n\n  def load_pack(dir_pairs, dir_bound, centers_path=None):\n      pr_raw = read_pairs_raw(os.path.join(dir_pairs, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'))\n      bd_raw = read_bound_raw(os.path.join(dir_bound, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'))\n      pairs, m_pairs = normalize_indices(pr_raw, 'pairs')\n      bound, m_bound = normalize_indices(bd_raw, 'bound')\n      C = read_centers(centers_path) if centers_path else None\n      return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C,\n              'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs, 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\
    \n  def write_json(path, obj):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(obj, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  def write_csv(path, header, rows):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(header)\n          for r in rows: w.writerow(r)\n\n  def pair_report(A, B, name_unaligned, name_aligned):\n      # Unaligned\n      Jb, Ib, Ub, Db = jaccard(A['bound'], B['bound'])\n      Jp, Ip, Up, Dp = jaccard(A['pairs'], B['pairs'])\n      write_json(f\"{OUT_DIR}/{name_unaligned}.json\",\n                 {\"n\":N,\"boundary\":{\"jaccard\":Jb,\"intersection_size\":Ib,\"union_size\":Ub},\n                  \"pairs\":{\"jaccard\":Jp,\"intersection_size\":Ip,\"union_size\":Up,\"symdiff_size\":Dp}})\n      write_csv(f\"{OUT_DIR}/{name_unaligned}.csv\",\n                ['n','boundary_j','boundary_intersection','boundary_union','pairs_j','pairs_intersection','pairs_union','pairs_symdiff'],\n\
    \                [[N,Jb,Ib,Ub,Jp,Ip,Up,Dp]])\n\n      # Aligned (A->B) if centers present\n      if A['centers'] is not None and B['centers'] is not None:\n          P = align_map(A['centers'], B['centers'])\n          Ab = map_bound(P, A['bound']); Ap = map_pairs(P, A['pairs'])\n          Jb2, Ib2, Ub2, Db2 = jaccard(Ab, B['bound'])\n          Jp2, Ip2, Up2, Dp2 = jaccard(Ap, B['pairs'])\n          write_json(f\"{OUT_DIR}/{name_aligned}.json\",\n                     {\"n\":N,\"alignment\":\"hungarian\",\n                      \"boundary\":{\"jaccard\":Jb2,\"intersection_size\":Ib2,\"union_size\":Ub2},\n                      \"pairs\":{\"jaccard\":Jp2,\"intersection_size\":Ip2,\"union_size\":Up2,\"symdiff_size\":Dp2}})\n          write_csv(f\"{OUT_DIR}/{name_aligned}.csv\",\n                    ['n','alignment','boundary_j','boundary_intersection','boundary_union','pairs_j','pairs_intersection','pairs_union','pairs_symdiff'],\n                    [[N,'hungarian',Jb2,Ib2,Ub2,Jp2,Ip2,Up2,Dp2]])\n\
    \n  def construct_packing():\n      # Resolve lineage dirs\n      sci_dir = first_existing(D_SCI_CAND)\n      pro_dir = first_existing(D_PRO_CAND)\n      if not sci_dir or not pro_dir:\n          raise FileNotFoundError(\"Missing lineage exports for Scientia or Prometheus.\")\n\n      # Load packs\n      exp_noe = load_pack(D_NOE, D_NOE, centers_path='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n      exp_sci = load_pack(sci_dir, sci_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(sci_dir,'centers.txt'))\n      exp_pro = load_pack(pro_dir, pro_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(pro_dir,'centers.txt'))\n\n      # Pairwise reports: Prometheus vs Noesis, Prometheus vs Scientia\n      pair_report(exp_pro, exp_noe,\n                  \"jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8\",\n                  \"jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_aligned_tol1e8\")\n      pair_report(exp_pro, exp_sci,\n                  \"jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8\",\n                  \"jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_aligned_tol1e8\"\
    )\n\n      # 3-lineage consensus (unaligned sets)\n      B_sets = [exp_noe['bound'], exp_sci['bound'], exp_pro['bound']]\n      P_sets = [exp_noe['pairs'], exp_sci['pairs'], exp_pro['pairs']]\n      B_inter = set.intersection(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n      B_union = set.union(*B_sets) if B_sets else set()\n      P_inter = set.intersection(*P_sets) if P_sets else set()\n      P_union = set.union(*P_sets) if P_sets else set()\n      cons = {\n        \"n\": N,\n        \"lineages\": [\"Noesis_243\",\"Scientia_259\",\"Prometheus_298\"],\n        \"boundary\": {\"intersection_size\": len(B_inter), \"union_size\": len(B_union),\n                     \"sizes\": [len(s) for s in B_sets]},\n        \"pairs\": {\"intersection_size\": len(P_inter), \"union_size\": len(P_union),\n                  \"sizes\": [len(s) for s in P_sets]}\n      }\n      write_json(f\"{OUT_DIR}/consensus_n26_noesis243_scientia259_prometheus298_tol1e8.json\", cons)\n      write_csv(f\"{OUT_DIR}/consensus_n26_noesis243_scientia259_prometheus298_tol1e8.csv\"\
    ,\n                ['n','boundary_intersection','boundary_union','pairs_intersection','pairs_union',\n                 'sizes_noesis','sizes_scientia','sizes_prometheus'],\n                [[N, len(B_inter), len(B_union), len(P_inter), len(P_union),\n                  len(B_sets[0]), len(B_sets[1]), len(B_sets[2])]])\n\n      # Return current Noesis packing unchanged\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n      r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n      return np.array(c, float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r, float).reshape(N,)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
thinking_content: '**Considering evaluation tasks**


  I need to focus on the latest state in the Public Memory Room where we found Prometheus exports at certain locations. My plan is to compute Jaccard metrics against variables like Noesis_243 and Scientia_259 for the new Prometheus SOTA. I’ve made utilities for Jaccard calculations before. I need to submit a utility evaluation that processes these exports and updates the storage. There’s also a policy about “no eval-code peer reads” that I must respect.


  **Clarifying storage paths**


  There''s been some caution about not importing code, but reading storage exports is still allowed. In previous steps, the debugging agent used an absolute path for accessing the "scientia" lineage because the relative alias might not be valid. Now, since the storage list shows "Prometheus" at a specific logical path, I need to consider the proper path in our evaluation code. It seems we might need to rely on an absolute path for "Prometheus" as well, considering the case sensitivity issues with "scientia" and "Prometheus."


  **Implementing candidate paths**


  I need to write code that tests multiple candidate paths, like ''storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26'', ''storage/prometheus/nmap/n26'', and the absolute path. This way, I can avoid requiring any patches from the debugger. I plan to implement a Utility to compute Jaccard metrics for Prometheus 298, Noesis 243, and Scientia 259 with a strict tolerance. The outputs will include files for different formats and potentially an update to the index with a public note. I’ll also consider computing consensus across the lineages.


  **Optimizing the evaluation script**


  I want to create a single evaluation script that computes both the Jaccard pairwise comparisons and consensus in one go to save time and tokens. The script will resolve directories for ''noesis'', ''scientia'', and ''prometheus'' using absolute paths. It’ll read their pairs, boundary CSVs, and normalize indices properly. I’ll compute Hungarian alignment mapping for the aligned Jaccard results and generate outputs for both aligned and unaligned Jaccards. Plus, I need to ensure the evaluation returns a valid packing tuple for the latest Noesis data.


  **Updating indices and storage**


  I should ensure to update the nmap index and log updates after my evaluation, but those won’t be included in the evaluation itself. I''ll add commands to process the updates later. The plan involves navigating to research, submitting evaluation code with synonyms for storage paths, and defining various data reading and Jaccard calculation functions. I’ll also generate outputs in JSON and CSV formats and handle consensus. After evaluation results, I’ll schedule the index and updates. It’s essential to stay focused and concise in my implementation.'
