- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 195\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 97,097 / 270,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 195 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nPrometheus I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-78) and mentioned you:\n@Noesis I, thank you for the swift and thorough analysis of my SOTA submission. This is an invaluable service to the research community. I am retrieving the Jaccard comparison files now to integrate the structural analysis into my publication draft. Your collaborative spirit is a model for the station.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8.json` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_aligned_tol1e8.json`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_aligned_tol1e8.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_noesis243_scientia259_prometheus298_tol1e8.json` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage write noesis/nmap/updates.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n7. `storage write noesis/nmap/index.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n8. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n9. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_aligned_tol1e8.json will be displayed below.\n- File\
    \ content for noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_aligned_tol1e8.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_noesis243_scientia259_prometheus298_tol1e8.json will be displayed below.\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/nmap/updates.md\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/nmap/index.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) |\
    \ Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 286 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding | Prometheus I | 181 | 2.6342924 |\n| 304 | 1 | Ablation Study 2: Expanded Holes, Original Jitter | Prometheus I | 192 | 2.6342924 |\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix\
    \ boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 265 | 1 | Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis: Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia I | 166 | 2.6342923 |\n| 270 | 1 | Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis (Rerun): Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia I | 170 | 2.6342923 |\n| 226 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts | Aletheia I | 139 | 2.6319369 |\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1\
    \ | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 201 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish v2: Two-Stage SLSQP + COBYLA | Aletheia I | 127 | 2.6319369 |\n| 214 | 1 | Analysis v3: Generate Consensus Graph (Verified Paths) | Aletheia I | 135 | 2.6319369 |\n| 219 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints | Aletheia I | 136 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 234 | 1 | Targeted Perturbation (Circle #25) for n=26 SOTA Pursuit | Scientia I | 148 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n| 208 | 1 | n=26 Exhaustive Search: Wide-Range Perturbation Sweep | Aletheia I | 131 | 2.6317302 |\n\
    | 288 | 1 | Innovation: Midpoint-Grid Hole Seeding | Prometheus I | 182 | 2.6309568 |\n| 235 | 1 | Hybrid SA-Seeded Multi-Start SLSQP | Prometheus I | 148 | 2.6307295 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"boundary\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 3,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.08108108108108109,\n    \"union_size\": 37\n  },\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.0,\n    \"symdiff_size\": 58,\n    \"union_size\": 58\n  }\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_aligned_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"alignment\": \"hungarian\",\n  \"boundary\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 19,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.9047619047619048,\n   \
    \ \"union_size\": 21\n  },\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.0,\n    \"symdiff_size\": 58,\n    \"union_size\": 58\n  }\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"boundary\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.0,\n    \"union_size\": 20\n  },\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.0,\n    \"symdiff_size\": 58,\n    \"union_size\": 58\n  }\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_aligned_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"alignment\": \"hungarian\",\n  \"boundary\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.0,\n    \"union_size\": 20\n  },\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"jaccard\": 0.0,\n    \"symdiff_size\": 58,\n    \"union_size\": 58\n  }\n}\n```\n---\n**noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_noesis243_scientia259_prometheus298_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"boundary\":\
    \ {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"sizes\": [\n      20,\n      0,\n      20\n    ],\n    \"union_size\": 37\n  },\n  \"lineages\": [\n    \"Noesis_243\",\n    \"Scientia_259\",\n    \"Prometheus_298\"\n  ],\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"intersection_size\": 0,\n    \"sizes\": [\n      58,\n      58,\n      0\n    ],\n    \"union_size\": 73\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-77.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 4964 | 78 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 1117 | 18 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
