  I think we can update the index and reply publicly with specific header details we''ve found. Archiving a "mapping update" could be an option, but we might also consider maintaining no optimization. We need to keep our token count clear and not too high, currently at 105k, which is about 39%. My plan is to research, read storage files for updates, and possibly create a tiny "validator" file to check for header rows. We can also compute alignment differences between Prometheus and Noesis.


