- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 198\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 108,595 / 270,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 198 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-81) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nAcknowledging your latest updates regarding the refined consensus and Jaccard analyses. Your continuous efforts in mapping the structural landscape are highly valuable to the community's understanding of optimal packings. I have recently published a paper on \"nudging\" contact graphs (Archive ID 13) and am now planning to conduct a comprehensive Jaccard analysis of the resulting nudged packings, as suggested by the reviewer. I will export the active sets for these packings to my lineage storage for your aggregator.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\
    \ then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage read Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv will be displayed below.\n- File content for Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv will be displayed below.\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv will be displayed below.\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 311 | 1 | BPIGO: Quad Diagonal Flip on Scientia I SOTA Base (Eval ID 259) v2 with SLSQP Optimization (N=26) | Scientia I | 195 | 2.6358955 |\n| 286 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding | Prometheus I | 181 | 2.6342924 |\n| 304 | 1 | Ablation Study 2: Expanded Holes, Original Jitter | Prometheus I | 192 | 2.6342924 |\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute\
    \ Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP\
    \ (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n| 265 | 1 | Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis: Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia I | 166 | 2.6342923 |\n| 270 | 1 | Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis (Rerun): Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs | Scientia I | 170 | 2.6342923 |\n| 226 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts | Aletheia I | 139 | 2.6319369 |\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 201 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish v2: Two-Stage SLSQP + COBYLA | Aletheia I | 127 | 2.6319369 |\n| 214 | 1 | Analysis v3: Generate Consensus Graph (Verified Paths) | Aletheia\
    \ I | 135 | 2.6319369 |\n| 219 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints | Aletheia I | 136 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 234 | 1 | Targeted Perturbation (Circle #25) for n=26 SOTA Pursuit | Scientia I | 148 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n| 208 | 1 | n=26 Exhaustive Search: Wide-Range Perturbation Sweep | Aletheia I | 131 | 2.6317302 |\n| 288 | 1 | Innovation: Midpoint-Grid Hole Seeding | Prometheus I | 182 | 2.6309568 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv:**\n\
    ```\ni,j\n\n```\n---\n**Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv:**\n```\ni,side\n0,xR\n1,yT\n2,yB\n3,yB\n4,yT\n5,xL\n6,yT\n7,yB\n8,xR\n9,xR\n10,xL\n11,xL\n21,yB\n22,xL\n22,yT\n23,xR\n23,yT\n24,xR\n24,yB\n25,yB\n\n```\n---\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv:**\n```\ni,kind\n0,xmin\n0,ymin\n1,xmin\n2,xmin\n3,xmin\n4,xmin\n4,ymax\n5,ymin\n9,ymax\n10,ymin\n14,ymax\n15,ymin\n19,ymax\n20,xmax\n20,ymin\n21,xmax\n22,xmax\n23,xmax\n24,xmax\n24,ymax\n\n```\n---\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv:**\n```\ni,j\n0,1\n0,5\n1,2\n1,5\n1,6\n2,3\n2,6\n2,7\n3,4\n3,7\n3,8\n4,8\n4,9\n5,6\n5,10\n5,11\n6,7\n6,11\n6,12\n7,8\n7,12\n7,13\n8,9\n8,13\n9,13\n9,14\n10,11\n10,15\n11,12\n11,15\n11,16\n12,13\n12,16\n12,17\n12,18\n13,14\n13,18\n14,18\n14,19\n15,16\n15,20\n15,21\n16,17\n16,21\n16,22\n17,18\n17,22\n17,23\n17,25\n18,19\n18,25\n19,24\n19,25\n20,21\n21,22\n22,23\n23,25\n24,25\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer\
    \ to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
