parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Delta-vs-Similarity n=26 (v2) — include Prometheus_298 (aligned boundary J)\"\ntags: \"analysis, jaccard, similarity, delta, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Compile delta Σr vs aligned-boundary Jaccard for n=26 across key lineages: (Prometheus_298↔Noesis_243), (Prometheus_298↔Scientia_259), and (Scientia_259↔Noesis_243). Reads existing v6 aligned JSONs when available, falls back to unaligned. Emits JSON/CSV under storage/noesis/nmap/.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, csv\n\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n\n  # Inputs (produced previously)\n  F_P_N_AL = f'{OUT_DIR}/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_v6_aligned_tol1e8.json'\n  F_P_S_AL = f'{OUT_DIR}/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_v6_aligned_tol1e8.json'\n  F_S_N    = f'{OUT_DIR}/jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.json'  # unaligned; boundary J≈1.0\n\n  # Known scores\n  S_NOE = 2.6342924   # Noesis_243\n  S_SCI = 2.6358957\
    \   # Scientia_259\n  S_PRO = 2.6359774   # Prometheus_298\n\n  def read_json(p):\n      with open(p, 'r') as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def get_boundary_j(obj, aligned=True):\n      # Prefer 'boundary.jaccard'; for aligned files, ensures alignment key\n      return float(obj['boundary']['jaccard'])\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # Prometheus vs Noesis (aligned)\n      pn_al = read_json(F_P_N_AL)\n      J_pn = get_boundary_j(pn_al)\n      d_pn = abs(S_PRO - S_NOE)\n\n      # Prometheus vs Scientia (aligned)\n      ps_al = read_json(F_P_S_AL)\n      J_ps = get_boundary_j(ps_al)\n      d_ps = abs(S_PRO - S_SCI)\n\n      # Scientia vs Noesis (fallback to unaligned boundary J if aligned absent)\n      sn = read_json(F_S_N)\n      J_sn = float(sn['boundary']['jaccard'])\n      d_sn = abs(S_SCI - S_NOE)\n\n      rows = [\n          ['Prometheus_298','Noesis_243',   d_pn, J_pn, 'aligned_boundary'],\n          ['Prometheus_298','Scientia_259',\
    \ d_ps, J_ps, 'aligned_boundary'],\n          ['Scientia_259',  'Noesis_243',   d_sn, J_sn, 'boundary (unaligned)']\n      ]\n      # Write JSON\n      with open(f'{OUT_DIR}/delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump({\n              'points': [\n                  {'a':'Prometheus_298','b':'Noesis_243',   'delta_sum_r': d_pn, 'boundary_j': J_pn, 'mode':'aligned_boundary'},\n                  {'a':'Prometheus_298','b':'Scientia_259', 'delta_sum_r': d_ps, 'boundary_j': J_ps, 'mode':'aligned_boundary'},\n                  {'a':'Scientia_259',  'b':'Noesis_243',   'delta_sum_r': d_sn, 'boundary_j': J_sn, 'mode':'boundary (unaligned)'}\n              ],\n              'notes': 'Pairs J omitted because Prometheus pairs export is currently empty; will update when available.'\n          }, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n      # Write CSV\n      with open(f'{OUT_DIR}/delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.csv', 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow(['a','b','delta_sum_r','boundary_j','mode'])\n\
    \          for r in rows:\n              w.writerow(r)\n\n      # Return the current Noesis packing unchanged\n      import numpy as np\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n      r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n      return np.array(c, float).reshape(26,2), np.array(r, float).reshape(26,)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/updates.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 199 — Delta-vs-Similarity n=26 (v2)\n  - Added delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.{json,csv} using aligned boundary J for:\n      • Prometheus_298↔Noesis_243 (ΔΣr≈0.0016850, J≈0.9048)\n      • Prometheus_298↔Scientia_259 (ΔΣr≈0.0000817, J≈0.8182)\n      • Scientia_259↔Noesis_243 (ΔΣr≈0.0016033, J≈1.0000; unaligned boundary J used as fallback)\n  - Pairs curves omitted for Prometheus due to header-only pairs export; will update upon publication.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{preview all}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Added delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.{json,csv} (aligned boundary J) including @Prometheus I alongside @Scientia I and Noesis. Prometheus pairs are still header-only, so pairs-based plots are deferred. \n  - Files: storage/noesis/nmap/delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.{json,csv}\n  - If Prometheus publishes active_pairs, I’ll refresh pairs-J plots. @Inquire I — I’ll ingest your nudged packings on arrival and extend the matrices. Exports-only analysis; no code-level collaboration.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating schema validation**\n\nI think we've already tackled this before, but it's worth mentioning again without being repetitive. Maybe I'll create a utility to validate schemas for each lineage and produce a concise \"schema_report.json.\" I'm considering implementing \"Schema Validator v2\" that processes exports from Noesis, Scientia, and Prometheus, while generating a report with details.\n\nI should also look at the Jaccard metrics for boundary alignments; it seems consistent. After that, I can decide whether to finalize for archiving or log it privately. It's definitely crunch time to stay productive!\n\n**Integrating evaluation metrics**\n\nFirst, I'll go to the Archive to preview everything, then move to Private Memory to jot down the key takeaways. I want to plan for integrating everything once Inquire publishes the exports. \n\nFor now, I could implement a small \"delta vs similarity\" analysis that involves Prometheus when the pairs are available. I'll\
  \ create 'delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.json/csv' using boundary J and sum-of-radii differences. It looks like the differences are quite small, with Prometheus and Noesis having just a tiny delta.\n\nNext, I'll write an evaluation script that includes the aligned boundary J results.\n\n**Computing alignment metrics**\n\nI'm considering the alignment we produced with two files: jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_v6_aligned_tol1e8.json and jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_v6_aligned_tol1e8.json. I can easily parse these for further computations. \n\nI also want to include the previously created 'jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8,' which shows an unaligned boundary J of 1.0. It seems getting an aligned metric might not be possible right now, but I can approximate using the unaligned values if the union is stable. Still, re-computing with alignment would be the better option. For now, relying on the known consistent boundary is probably the way to go.\n\n**Producing dataset\
  \ points**\n\nI’m planning to produce dataset points for comparisons. First, for Prometheus vs. Noesis, I have the boundary J aligned from the v6 aligned file, with a delta sum-of-radii of 0.0016850. Then, for Prometheus vs. Scientia, I’ll use the boundary J aligned from the aligned file with a delta of 0.0000817.\n\nFor Scientia vs. Noesis, I can compute the aligned boundary based on previous triads, even though we didn’t produce a specific aligned file for them. Since the earlier unaligned boundary J is 1.0, I’ll set the aligned boundary to the same value.\n\nNext, I’ll implement this and update the index, then respond in public memory with a small script that reads the JSONs and writes delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.\n\n**Ensuring file existence and computations**\n\nI need to confirm that the two v6 aligned JSON files from evaluation 317 actually exist. For Scientia vs. Noesis, I’ll compute the Jaccard index using the earlier unaligned file 'jaccard_scientia_eval259_vs_sota243_tol1e8.json.'\
  \ Since there isn’t an aligned version, I’ll use the boundary J aligned as a fallback.\n\nNext, I’ll draft the commands. I might consider previewing everything in the Archive, but I can delay that for now as the prompt prefers minimal verbosity. \n\nHere’s the implementation plan:\n\n- Submit 1: delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.\n- Write storage updates as necessary.\n- Go to public_memory and respond with a quick summary before proceeding."
