parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  n=26 mapping — Tick 200 (tol=1e−8)\n\n  Global SOTAs\n  - Prometheus I: Eval 298, Σr=2.6359774 — exports at storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/\n  - Scientia I:  Eval 259, Σr=2.6358957 — exports at storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/\n  - Noesis I:    Eval 243, Σr=2.6342924 — exports at storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/\n\n  Latest artifacts\n  - Prometheus mappings (v6, extended canonicalization):\n      • jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_v6_{tol1e8}.json/.csv (unaligned)\n      • jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_noesis243_v6_aligned_{tol1e8}.json/.csv\n      • jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_v6_{tol1e8}.json/.csv (unaligned)\n      • jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_v6_aligned_{tol1e8}.json/.csv\n      • consensus_n26_noesis243_scientia259_prometheus298_v6_{tol1e8}.json/.csv\n  - Delta vs. Similarity (aligned boundary J):\n      • delta_vs_similarity_n26_v2.{json,csv}\n\n  Notes\n  - Boundary labels\
    \ canonicalized (including xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax); indices auto-normalized (0/1-based).\n  - Prometheus pairs export currently header-only → pairs J=0.0 by construction; will refresh when pairs are published.\n  - Exports-only analysis; no eval-code peer reads.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"181-190\"\n    summary: |\n      Structural mapping and robust Jaccard tooling for n=26; no optimization beyond a single structural baseline.\n      Key evaluations and utilities:\n        - 284 (Tick 182): Two-hole replacement seeding + SLSQP → Σr≈2.62957196 (valid, below SOTA).\n        - 287: Exported exp284 active sets + Jaccard vs Noesis_243.\n        - 291: Jaccard exp284 vs Scientia_259.\n        - 293: Aligned (Hungarian) Jaccard exp284 vs Scientia_259.\n        - 297: Triad Jaccard (exp284, Noesis_243, Scientia_259) with debugger path fixes.\n        - 299/302: Triad v3/v4 — robust canonicalization +\
    \ index normalization.\n        - 308: Prometheus_298 mappings vs Noesis_243 & Scientia_259 (unaligned + aligned) + 3-lineage consensus.\n        - 313: Jaccard v5 — regex/delimiter-tolerant parser; printed lineage sizes and normalization.\n        - 317: Jaccard v6 — extended boundary canonicalization (xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax); finalized mappings and consensus.\n      Main outcomes:\n        - exp284 boundary aligns with Noesis_243 (J=1.0), pairs show high overlap vs Noesis_243; vs Scientia_259 shows expected differences.\n        - Prometheus_298: boundary aligned J≈0.905 vs Noesis_243; J≈0.818 vs Scientia_259; pairs J=0.0 because Prometheus pairs CSV is header-only.\n        - Consensus (Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298): boundary ∩=3, ∪=37 (under tol=1e−8); pairs ∩=0, ∪=73 (pairs missing for Prometheus).\n      Artifacts:\n        - storage/noesis/nmap/* (v5/v6 Jaccards, triad reports, consensus, and index/updates).\n      Policy:\n        - Exports-only parsing, no eval-code\
    \ peer reads; strict feasibility guard preserved in all packings.\n```"
