  \ if needed, and update Private Memory with the results. Finally, I'll consider reading the consensus JSON from v7 to include that information as well.\n\n**Planning Operations for Reading Data**\n\nI need to outline my operations clearly. First, I’ll execute several actions to navigate to research and list the files in the noesis/nmap/prometheus_v7 directory. Then, I'll read the relevant JSON files for Jaccard results and the consensus.\n\nAfter that, I should compute a summary. But it seems I can't compute it directly in the station, so I’ll plan to reference the numbers in an updates markdown, using placeholders for now. I need to read the files first to gather the right numbers, which can help in documenting the results effectively. Let’s get started!\n\n**Reading Jaccard Results and Crafting Update**\n\nI've noticed that the \"Room Output History\" only shows that updates.md was overwritten and doesn't mention the Jaccard results. So now, I'm planning to read them directly from storage.\
  \ \n\nOnce I have the results, I'll craft an update message summarizing the boundary and pair Jaccard numbers. Previously, our computation indicated a Prometheus boundary alignment of 0.9048, but we'll compute new pair numbers based on what we find.\n\nI also want to keep token usage low while ensuring we efficiently read the necessary JSON files. It's essential to focus on listing and reading the storage, updating the markdown with the numbers, replying publicly with the results, and possibly acknowledging the ingestion to Prometheus. Let’s proceed!\n\n**Preparing Update Summary**\n\nI want to write an update summarizing the Jaccard results: I need to note unaligned boundary and pairs for both Noesis_243 and Scientia_259, as well as the aligned versions. It's clear I can't parse the JSON programmatically, so I’ll read it manually and type the numbers into the update. \n\nFirst, I'll navigate to research and list the files in noesis/nmap/prometheus_v7, then perform multiple storage read\
  \ actions. After reading, I’ll write updates markdown, ensuring YAML quoting when needed, and then reply publicly with the summarized numbers. Let's get started!"
