- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/updates.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 208 — Prometheus v7 Jaccards and 3-way consensus (n=26, tol=1e−8)\n  Results (unaligned = aligned; Hungarian did not change values):\n  - Prometheus_298 vs Noesis_243:\n      • boundary J = 1.000 (I=20, U=20)\n      • pairs J = 0.6667 (I=46, U=69)\n  - Prometheus_298 vs Scientia_259:\n      • boundary J = 1.000 (I=20, U=20)\n      • pairs J = 0.6429 (I=45, U=70)\n  - 3‑lineage consensus {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298}:\n      • boundary intersection = 20 / union = 20 (sizes: 20, 20, 20)\n      • pairs intersection = 38 / union = 77 (sizes: 58, 58, 57)\n\n  Implications:\n  - Boundary actives remain identical across top SOTAs.\n  - Interior contacts diverge materially; Prometheus shares ~2/3 of pair contacts with Noesis and ~0.643 with Scientia.\n  - Triad core (pairs) = 38; union = 77.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/prometheus_v7/\n      * prometheus298_vs_noesis243_{tol1e8,tol1e8_aligned}.{json,csv}\n\
    \      * prometheus298_vs_scientia259_{tol1e8,tol1e8_aligned}.{json,csv}\n      * consensus_noe243_sci259_pro298_tol1e8.json\n\n  Next:\n  - Await Inquire’s n=26 exports; then compute 4‑lineage consensus refresh.\n  - Keep exports-only policy; no eval‑code peer reads.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Prometheus pairs ingested (Tick 208, tol=1e−8):\n  - Prometheus_298 vs Noesis_243: boundary J=1.000 (20/20); pairs J=0.6667 (46/69).\n  - Prometheus_298 vs Scientia_259: boundary J=1.000 (20/20); pairs J=0.6429 (45/70).\n  - 3‑lineage consensus {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298}: boundary ∩=20/20; pairs ∩=38, ∪=77 (sizes: 58,58,57).\n  Files: storage/noesis/nmap/prometheus_v7/*. Exports-only; no eval‑code peer reads. Will extend to 4‑lineage consensus once @Inquire I posts n=26 exports.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to plan our next actions based on the Jaccard outputs we've just reviewed. We have some boundary values and sizes from the Prometheus pairs compared to Noesis and Scientia. It seems we should update our maps and possibly public memory with a concise summary. I could write a message to summarize the ingestion results and maybe even prepare a CSV for aggregation. I should also think about verifying if the results hold up against earlier Jaccard values.\n\n**Ensuring compliance and updates**\n\nI need to compare the new values for Prometheus against Scientia and Noesis. The Jaccard value against Scientia is about 0.6429, while it's 0.6667 for Noesis. I should make sure we comply with policies, focusing on reading exports only. \n\nIt seems a good plan to add the consensus_n26_3lineage JSON to our storage. I can check the central index and update the consensus summary too. I need to work on updating the delta vs. similarity metrics using the\
  \ improved Prometheus pairs, avoiding new optimization experiments. Also, keep an eye on our token usage!\n\n**Planning updates for Jaccard results**\n\nI don't need to prune anything right now, so here's my plan. First, I'll write updates to the storage in the noesis/nmap/ directory with a summary of the pairwise Jaccard results and triad consensus numbers. \n\nI might create a \"prometheus_summary.md\" or \"three_lineage_summary.json/csv.\" I should also reply in public memory to summarize the Prometheus results and maybe update Private Memory too. \n\nOnce the Inquire exports are posted, I'll extend to include those in my actions and prepare content with the necessary execution lines and paths!\n\n**Setting quoting and action rules**\n\nI need to ensure that when I quote in YAML content with colons, I'll use blocks with the \"|\" symbol. I could also create a CSV summary called \"prometheus_v7_summary.csv\" that combines the two pairwise results and consensus sizes, though I might skip\
  \ code generation for now and just write a note. \n\nAdditionally, writing updates to \"noesis/nmap/index.md\" to reference files sounds good. I'll include actions in YAML blocks, remembering to place each /execute_action on a new line. I should also keep the Automatic System Tips in mind about verifying claims and correcting any confusion!\n\n**Analyzing consensus data**\n\nI can note in the public update that the triad consensus has 38 pairs compared to the previous 4-lineage consensus of 42 pairs. It’s expected that fewer lineages should not have a smaller intersection, but it seems the triad intersection is smaller. This indicates different sets of lineages are used, which complicates direct comparisons. \n\nI’ll summarize this in the update, ensure consistency in Jaccard values, and prepare to integrate Inquire once exports are available. Then, I’ll move forward with actions to update the storage and reply publicly!"
