tick: 210
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Inquire n=26 Aggregation v2 — Per-pack Jaccards + 4-lineage Consensus (tol=1e-8)\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard, consensus, nmap, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Scan storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/ (SOTA ID 207 + nudged packs). Compute boundary/pairs Jaccards (unaligned + Hungarian-aligned) vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298}. Emit per-pack JSON/CSV and a summary, plus a 4-lineage consensus report across SOTA packs. Returns Noesis packing unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\n  except Exception:\n      linear_sum_assignment = None\n\n  N = 26\n  TOL_TAG = 'tol1e8'\n  OUT_ROOT = 'storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_v2'\n\n  # Canonicalization for boundary labels\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n    'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n\
    \    'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n    'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n  INT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\n  NUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\n  SIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\n  def read_lines(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n          return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\n  def parse_pairs_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n          if len(toks) >= 2:\n              try:\n                  i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                  rows.append((i, j))\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n      return rows\n\n  def parse_boundary_raw(path):\n\
    \      rows=[]\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n          if not itoks: \n              continue\n          try:\n              i = int(itoks[0])\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n          if not m: \n              continue\n          s_raw = m.group(1)\n          k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n          s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n          if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n              rows.append((i, s))\n      return rows\n\n  def normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n      # Normalize to 0-based indices, deduplicate pairs with ordering (i<j)\n      if kind == 'pairs':\n          idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n      else:\n          idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n      if not idxs:\n          return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n      c0 =\
    \ sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n      c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n      meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n      out = set()\n      if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n          meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              for (i, j) in rows:\n                  a, b = i-1, j-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                      u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                      out.add((u, v))\n          else:\n              for (i, s) in rows:\n                  a = i-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N:\n                      out.add((a, s))\n      else:\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              for (i, j) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                      u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                      out.add((u, v))\n          else:\n              for (i, s) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N:\n      \
    \                out.add((i, s))\n      return out, meta\n\n  def read_centers(path):\n      rows=[]\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n          if len(toks) >= 2:\n              rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n      C = np.array(rows, float)\n      if C.shape != (N, 2):\n          raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} -> {C.shape}\")\n      return C\n\n  def load_pack(dir_root, centers_path=None):\n      pr = os.path.join(dir_root, f'active_pairs_{TOL_TAG}.csv')\n      bd = os.path.join(dir_root, f'active_boundary_{TOL_TAG}.csv')\n      pairs_raw = parse_pairs_raw(pr)\n      bound_raw = parse_boundary_raw(bd)\n      pairs, m_pairs = normalize_indices(pairs_raw, 'pairs')\n      bound, m_bound = normalize_indices(bound_raw, 'bound')\n      C = read_centers(centers_path) if (centers_path and os.path.exists(centers_path)) else None\n      return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C, 'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs,\
    \ 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      I = A & B; U = A | B\n      J = float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0\n      return {'j': J, 'I': len(I), 'U': len(U)}\n\n  def align_map(CA, CB):\n      M = np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n      if linear_sum_assignment is None:\n          a_idx = np.lexsort((CA[:,1], CA[:,0]))\n          b_idx = np.lexsort((CB[:,1], CB[:,0]))\n          P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[a_idx] = b_idx\n          return P\n      r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n      P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r] = c\n      return P\n\n  def map_pairs(P, S):\n      T = set()\n      for (i, j) in S:\n          a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n          if a == b: \n              continue\n          u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n          T.add((u, v))\n      return T\n\n  def map_bound(P, S):\n      return set((int(P[i]), s) for (i, s) in S)\n\n  def write_json_csv(base, tag, res):\n      os.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)\n  \
    \    with open(os.path.join(base, f'{tag}.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(res, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n      with open(os.path.join(base, f'{tag}.csv'), 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['n','boundary_j','I_b','U_b','pairs_j','I_p','U_p'])\n          w.writerow([N, res['boundary']['j'], res['boundary']['I'], res['boundary']['U'],\n                         res['pairs']['j'],    res['pairs']['I'],    res['pairs']['U']])\n\n  def compare_two(A, B, out_base, tag):\n      res = {\n        'n': N,\n        'boundary': jaccard(A['bound'], B['bound']),\n        'pairs':    jaccard(A['pairs'], B['pairs']),\n        'note': 'unaligned'\n      }\n      write_json_csv(out_base, f'{tag}_{TOL_TAG}', res)\n      if A['centers'] is not None and B['centers'] is not None:\n          P = align_map(A['centers'], B['centers'])\n          Ab, Ap = map_bound(P, A['bound']), map_pairs(P, A['pairs'])\n          res2 = {\n            'n': N,\n            'alignment':\
    \ 'hungarian',\n            'boundary': jaccard(Ab, B['bound']),\n            'pairs':    jaccard(Ap, B['pairs'])\n          }\n          write_json_csv(out_base, f'{tag}_{TOL_TAG}_aligned', res2)\n\n  def consensus_sets(packs):\n      # packs: dict name->pack (with 'bound','pairs')\n      Bs = [packs[k]['bound'] for k in packs]\n      Ps = [packs[k]['pairs'] for k in packs]\n      inter_b = set.intersection(*Bs) if all(len(s)>=0 for s in Bs) else set()\n      union_b = set.union(*Bs) if all(len(s)>=0 for s in Bs) else set()\n      inter_p = set.intersection(*Ps) if all(len(s)>=0 for s in Ps) else set()\n      union_p = set.union(*Ps) if all(len(s)>=0 for s in Ps) else set()\n      sizes_b = {k: len(packs[k]['bound']) for k in packs}\n      sizes_p = {k: len(packs[k]['pairs']) for k in packs}\n      return {'boundary': {'intersection': len(inter_b), 'union': len(union_b), 'sizes': sizes_b},\n              'pairs':    {'intersection': len(inter_p), 'union': len(union_p), 'sizes': sizes_p}}\n\
    \n  def discover_inquire_packs(root):\n      packs=[]\n      if not os.path.exists(root):\n          return packs\n      # Root SOTA + subdirs (nudged)\n      candidates=[root] + [os.path.join(root, d) for d in os.listdir(root) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(root,d))]\n      for p in candidates:\n          c=os.path.join(p,'centers.txt'); r=os.path.join(p,'radii.txt')\n          b=os.path.join(p,f'active_boundary_{TOL_TAG}.csv')\n          pr=os.path.join(p,f'active_pairs_{TOL_TAG}.csv')\n          if os.path.exists(c) and os.path.exists(r) and os.path.exists(b) and os.path.exists(pr):\n              name=os.path.relpath(p, root).replace(os.sep,'_') or 'inquire_207_root'\n              packs.append((name,p))\n      return packs\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      os.makedirs(OUT_ROOT, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # Load SOTA packs\n      noe = load_pack('storage/noesis/exports/sota_243', centers_path='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n      sci = load_pack('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26',\
    \ centers_path='storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/centers.txt')\n      pro = load_pack('storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26', centers_path='storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/centers.txt')\n      inq = load_pack('storage/Inquire/nmap/n26', centers_path='storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/centers.txt')\n\n      # 4-lineage consensus (SOTAs only)\n      sotapacks = {'Noesis_243': noe, 'Scientia_259': sci, 'Prometheus_298': pro, 'Inquire_207': inq}\n      cons4 = consensus_sets(sotapacks)\n      with open(os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, f'consensus_4lineage_sotas_{TOL_TAG}.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump({'n':N, 'ids': list(sotapacks.keys()), **cons4}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n      # Pairwise SOTA Jaccards (optional small matrix)\n      pairs = [('Noesis_243','Scientia_259'),('Noesis_243','Prometheus_298'),('Noesis_243','Inquire_207'),\n               ('Scientia_259','Prometheus_298'),('Scientia_259','Inquire_207'),('Prometheus_298','Inquire_207')]\n      with open(os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, f'jaccard_matrix_sotas_{TOL_TAG}.csv'),'w',newline='')\
    \ as f:\n          w=csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['A','B','boundary_j','I_b','U_b','pairs_j','I_p','U_p'])\n          for a,b in pairs:\n              A=sotapacks[a]; B=sotapacks[b]\n              jb=jaccard(A['bound'],B['bound']); jp=jaccard(A['pairs'],B['pairs'])\n              w.writerow([a,b,jb['j'],jb['I'],jb['U'],jp['j'],jp['I'],jp['U']])\n\n      # Discover Inquire packs (SOTA + nudged) and compute per-pack Jaccards vs the SOTA set\n      inq_root='storage/Inquire/nmap/n26'\n      found = discover_inquire_packs(inq_root)\n      summary_rows=[]\n      if not found:\n          with open(os.path.join(OUT_ROOT,'inquire_v2_meta.json'),'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'note':'No Inquire packs found','root':inq_root}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n      for name, p in found:\n          out_dir=os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, name); os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n          pack=load_pack(p, centers_path=os.path.join(p,'centers.txt'))\n          for tag, ref in [('noesis243',noe),('scientia259',sci),('prometheus298',pro),('inquire207',inq)]:\n\
    \              compare_two(pack, ref, out_dir, f'{name}_vs_{tag}')\n          # For summary, record boundary J vs each reference (aligned if available else unaligned)\n          def load_j(path_json, fallback_json):\n              if os.path.exists(path_json):\n                  with open(path_json,'r') as f: return float(json.load(f)['boundary']['j'])\n              with open(fallback_json,'r') as f: return float(json.load(f)['boundary']['j'])\n          j_noe = load_j(os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_noesis243_{TOL_TAG}_aligned.json'),\n                         os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_noesis243_{TOL_TAG}.json'))\n          j_sci = load_j(os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_scientia259_{TOL_TAG}_aligned.json'),\n                         os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_scientia259_{TOL_TAG}.json'))\n          j_pro = load_j(os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_prometheus298_{TOL_TAG}_aligned.json'),\n                         os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_prometheus298_{TOL_TAG}.json'))\n\
    \          j_inq = load_j(os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_inquire207_{TOL_TAG}_aligned.json'),\n                         os.path.join(out_dir,f'{name}_vs_inquire207_{TOL_TAG}.json'))\n          summary_rows.append([name, j_noe, j_sci, j_pro, j_inq])\n\n      if found:\n          with open(os.path.join(OUT_ROOT,'inquire_v2_summary.csv'),'w',newline='') as f:\n              w=csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['pack','Jb_noesis243','Jb_scientia259','Jb_prometheus298','Jb_inquire207'])\n              for r in summary_rows: w.writerow(r)\n\n      # Return current Noesis packing unchanged\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'); r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n      return np.array(c,float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r,float).reshape(N,)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noesis/nmap/inquire_v2}`\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/inquire_v2/consensus_4lineage_sotas_tol1e8.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/inquire_v2/jaccard_matrix_sotas_tol1e8.csv}`\n\
    \n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/updates.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 210 — Inquire n=26 aggregation v2 submitted and 4-lineage consensus emitted\n  - Paths: storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_v2/\n    * consensus_4lineage_sotas_tol1e8.json (Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207)\n    * jaccard_matrix_sotas_tol1e8.csv (pairwise SOTA Jaccards)\n    * <pack>/ per-pack Jaccards vs {noesis243, scientia259, prometheus298, inquire207} (unaligned + aligned)\n    * inquire_v2_summary.csv (boundary Jaccards per nudged pack)\n  - Exports-only; no eval-code peer reads. Will post consolidated numbers publicly after verification.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Inquire I — I’ve run the n=26 aggregator v2 and emitted 4‑lineage consensus (SOTAs only) plus per‑pack Jaccards. Artifacts live under storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_v2/:\n  - consensus_4lineage_sotas_tol1e8.json\n  - jaccard_matrix_sotas_tol1e8.csv\n\
    \  - per‑pack results in subfolders and a summary CSV.\n  I’ll post the consolidated numbers once I finish a quick verification pass. Exports‑only; no eval‑code peer reads.\n```"
