tick: 214
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Inquire exports ingestion v1 — 4-lineage consensus (sets-only, tol=1e-8)\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard, consensus, nmap, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Ingest Inquire n=26 active-set exports from storage/Inquire/exports (and lowercase fallback). Compute pairwise boundary/pairs Jaccards vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298} and emit a 4-lineage consensus (sets-only). Outputs JSON/CSV under storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_exports_v1/. Returns Noesis packing unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_exports_v1'\n  TOL_TAG = 'tol1e8'\n\n  # Canonicalization for boundary labels and filename variants\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n    'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n    'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n\
    \    'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n  INT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\n  NUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\n  SIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\n  def first_existing(paths):\n      for p in paths:\n          if p and os.path.exists(p):\n              return p\n      return None\n\n  def read_lines(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n          return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\n  def parse_pairs_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      if not path or not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n          if len(toks) >= 2:\n              try:\n                  i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                  rows.append((i, j))\n              except Exception:\n   \
    \               continue\n      return rows\n\n  def parse_boundary_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      if not path or not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n          if not itoks: \n              continue\n          try:\n              i = int(itoks[0])\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n          if not m: \n              continue\n          s_raw = m.group(1)\n          k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n          s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n          if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n              rows.append((i, s))\n      return rows\n\n  def normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n      # Normalize to 0-based indices, deduplicate pairs with ordering (i<j)\n      if kind == 'pairs':\n          idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n      else:\n          idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n\
    \      if not idxs:\n          return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n      c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n      c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n      meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n      out = set()\n      if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n          meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              for (i, j) in rows:\n                  a, b = i-1, j-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                      u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                      out.add((u, v))\n          else:\n              for (i, s) in rows:\n                  a = i-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N:\n                      out.add((a, s))\n      else:\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              for (i, j) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                      u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                      out.add((u, v))\n \
    \         else:\n              for (i, s) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N:\n                      out.add((i, s))\n      return out, meta\n\n  def load_pack_from_dir(dir_root):\n      # Accept standard names; if missing, try any CSV with 'active'+'boundary' or 'active'+'pairs'\n      b_path = first_existing([\n          os.path.join(dir_root, f'active_boundary_{TOL_TAG}.csv'),\n          os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary_tol1e-8.csv'),\n          os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary_tol1e-08.csv'),\n          os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary.csv'),\n      ])\n      p_path = first_existing([\n          os.path.join(dir_root, f'active_pairs_{TOL_TAG}.csv'),\n          os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_pairs_tol1e-8.csv'),\n          os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_pairs_tol1e-08.csv'),\n          os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_pairs.csv'),\n      ])\n      # Fallback: scan directory for any matching files\n      if not b_path or not p_path:\n          if os.path.exists(dir_root):\n\
    \              for fn in os.listdir(dir_root):\n                  fl = fn.lower()\n                  full = os.path.join(dir_root, fn)\n                  if (not b_path) and ('active' in fl and 'boundary' in fl and fl.endswith('.csv')):\n                      b_path = full\n                  if (not p_path) and ('active' in fl and 'pairs' in fl and fl.endswith('.csv')):\n                      p_path = full\n      pairs_raw = parse_pairs_raw(p_path)\n      bound_raw = parse_boundary_raw(b_path)\n      pairs, _ = normalize_indices(pairs_raw, 'pairs')\n      bound, _ = normalize_indices(bound_raw, 'bound')\n      return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound}\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      I = A & B; U = A | B\n      return {'j': (float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0), 'I': len(I), 'U': len(U)}\n\n  def write_json_csv(base, tag, res):\n      os.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(os.path.join(base, f'{tag}.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(res, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\
    \      with open(os.path.join(base, f'{tag}.csv'), 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['n','boundary_j','I_b','U_b','pairs_j','I_p','U_p'])\n          w.writerow([N, res['boundary']['j'], res['boundary']['I'], res['boundary']['U'],\n                         res['pairs']['j'],    res['pairs']['I'],    res['pairs']['U']])\n\n  def consensus_sets(packs):\n      # packs: dict name-> {'bound','pairs'}\n      Bs = [packs[k]['bound'] for k in packs]\n      Ps = [packs[k]['pairs'] for k in packs]\n      inter_b = set.intersection(*Bs) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Bs) else set()\n      union_b = set.union(*Bs) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Bs) else set()\n      inter_p = set.intersection(*Ps) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Ps) else set()\n      union_p = set.union(*Ps) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Ps) else set()\n      sizes_b = {k: len(packs[k]['bound']) for k in packs}\n      sizes_p = {k: len(packs[k]['pairs']) for k in packs}\n      return {'boundary':\
    \ {'intersection': len(inter_b), 'union': len(union_b), 'sizes': sizes_b},\n              'pairs':    {'intersection': len(inter_p), 'union': len(union_p), 'sizes': sizes_p}}\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # SOTA packs (sets only)\n      noe = load_pack_from_dir('storage/noesis/exports/sota_243')\n      sci = load_pack_from_dir('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26')\n      pro = load_pack_from_dir('storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26')\n\n      inq_dir = first_existing(['storage/Inquire/exports', 'storage/inquire/exports'])\n      inq = load_pack_from_dir(inq_dir) if inq_dir else {'pairs': set(), 'bound': set()}\n\n      # Pairwise Jaccards (unaligned, sets-only)\n      comps = {\n        'inquire207_vs_noesis243': {'A': inq, 'B': noe},\n        'inquire207_vs_scientia259': {'A': inq, 'B': sci},\n        'inquire207_vs_prometheus298': {'A': inq, 'B': pro},\n      }\n      for tag, d in comps.items():\n          res = {\n            'n': N,\n         \
    \   'boundary': jaccard(d['A']['bound'], d['B']['bound']),\n            'pairs':    jaccard(d['A']['pairs'], d['B']['pairs']),\n            'note': 'sets-only'\n          }\n          write_json_csv(OUT_DIR, f'{tag}_{TOL_TAG}', res)\n\n      # 4-lineage consensus (sets-only)\n      packs = {'Noesis_243': noe, 'Scientia_259': sci, 'Prometheus_298': pro, 'Inquire_207': inq}\n      cons4 = consensus_sets(packs)\n      with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, f'consensus_4lineage_sets_{TOL_TAG}.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump({'n': N, 'ids': list(packs.keys()), **cons4}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n      # Return current Noesis packing unchanged\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'); r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n      return np.array(c, float).reshape(N, 2), np.array(r, float).reshape(N,)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/updates.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 214 — Inquire exports ingestion v1 submitted (sets-only)\n  - Found\
    \ Inquire exports at storage/Inquire/exports (and lowercase mirror). Submitted a utility to compute:\n      • Pairwise Jaccards (boundary, pairs) vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298}\n      • 4-lineage consensus (sets-only)\n  - Outputs will land under storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_exports_v1/: \n      * inquire207_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n      * consensus_4lineage_sets_tol1e8.json\n  - This path avoids nmap/n26 while still enabling SOTA mapping. If nudged packs are later published under nmap/n26, v3 aggregator will cover per-pack analyses.\n  - Exports-only; no eval-code peer reads.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Quick update (Tick 214): I’ve submitted an ingestion script that targets your current SOTA exports at storage/Inquire/exports (and lowercase mirror), computes pairwise Jaccards vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298}, and emits a 4‑lineage consensus (sets-only).\
    \ Results will appear under storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_exports_v1/. If you later add nudged packs under nmap/n26, my v3 aggregator will pick them up for per‑pack analyses. Exports‑only; no eval‑code peer reads.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing code functions**\n\nI'm gearing up to write some functions. First, I'll create `read_lines` to parse boundaries and pairs. Then, there's `load_pack(dir)`, which should look for specific CSV files within a given directory. \n\nNext, I'll implement the Jaccard function and a `consensus_four(packs)` function. Outputs will go to a specific storage path, and I'll keep the baseline pack unchanged. I also need to update public memory once results are ready.  \n\nLastly, I’ll handle research and log updates while using proper token hygiene.\n\n**Crafting robust parsing code**\n\nI'm planning to create code that robustly parses boundary labels with both 0/1-based normalization. For the baseline, the Noesis pack will be stored in `storage/noesis/exports/sota_243`; I hope to read active files from that directory. \n\nI've noted that for Scientia and Prometheus, I'll look in their respective storage paths. The Inquire storage has both `Inquire/exports` and `inquire/exports`,\
  \ which seems like an alias situation. \n\nI’ll develop a function to find the first existing path and update the index with the found locations while preparing for later evaluations. I've got my tasks lined up!"
