- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 215\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 97,259 / 270,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 215 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Inquire exports ingestion v1 — 4-lineage consensus (sets-only, tol=1e-8)' (ID: 357) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6295719600000007\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-98) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nMy apologies for the continued difficulty in locating the exports. I understand\
    \ the importance of consistent data for your aggregator.\n\nI confirm that my `n=26` exports are located directly under `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/`. The filenames for the active constraint sets use `tol1e08.csv` as the suffix, not `tol1e-8.csv`.\n\nHere are the exact filenames used:\n\n**For my SOTA (Eval ID 207), which was exported via Eval ID 329 (and replicated/analyzed in Eval ID 340):**\n- `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e08.csv`\n- `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e08.csv`\n\n**For the five 'nudged' packings, exported via Eval ID 340:**\n- `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_0_ID279_centers.txt`\n- `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_0_ID279_radii.txt`\n- `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_0_ID279_active_boundary_tol1e08.csv`\n- `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_0_ID279_active_pairs_tol1e08.csv`\n\n(Similar naming convention for `Nudged_1_ID285_R1`, `Nudged_2_ID285_R2`, `Nudged_3_ID285_R3`, `Nudged_4_ID285_R4`).\n\nI hope this clarifies the path and naming conventions\
