parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Inquire/nmap}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Inquire/nmap/n26}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Inquire n=26 Aggregation v4 — tol1e08 support, per-pack Jaccards, 4-lineage consensus\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard, consensus, nmap, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Robustly ingest Inquire n=26 exports in storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/ using tol1e08 filenames (and variants). Compute boundary/pairs Jaccards (unaligned + Hungarian-aligned when centers exist) vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298}. Emit per-pack JSON/CSV, a summary, and a 4-lineage SOTA consensus. Returns Noesis packing unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\n  except Exception:\n      linear_sum_assignment = None\n\n  N = 26\n  OUT = 'storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_v4'\n\n  # Canonicalization for boundary labels\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n\
    \    'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n    'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n    'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n  INT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\n  NUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\n  SIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\n  def read_lines(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n          return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\n  def parse_pairs_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      if not path or not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n          if len(toks) >= 2:\n              try:\n                  i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                  rows.append((i, j))\n             \
    \ except Exception:\n                  continue\n      return rows\n\n  def parse_boundary_raw(path):\n      rows=[]\n      if not path or not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n          if not itoks:\n              continue\n          try:\n              i = int(itoks[0])\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n          if not m: \n              continue\n          s_raw = m.group(1)\n          k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n          s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n          if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n              rows.append((i, s))\n      return rows\n\n  def normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n      if kind == 'pairs':\n          idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n      else:\n          idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n      if not idxs:\n          return set(), {'applied':\
    \ False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n      c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n      c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n      out = set(); meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n      if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n          meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              for (i, j) in rows:\n                  a, b = i-1, j-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                      u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a); out.add((u, v))\n          else:\n              for (i, s) in rows:\n                  a = i-1\n                  if 0 <= a < N: out.add((a, s))\n      else:\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              for (i, j) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                      u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i); out.add((u, v))\n          else:\n              for (i, s) in rows:\n                  if 0 <= i < N: out.add((i, s))\n      return out, meta\n\n \
    \ def read_centers(path):\n      if not path or not os.path.exists(path): return None\n      rows=[]\n      for ln in read_lines(path):\n          toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n          if len(toks) >= 2:\n              rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n      C = np.array(rows, float)\n      return C if C.shape == (N, 2) else None\n\n  def find_inquire_root():\n      # Prefer exact path, fallback to lowercase\n      for p in ['storage/Inquire/nmap/n26', 'storage/inquire/nmap/n26']:\n          if os.path.exists(p): return p\n      return None\n\n  def find_file(dir_root, kind, base=None):\n      \"\"\"\n      kind: 'boundary'|'pairs' for SOTA files, or base-prefixed Nudged files.\n      Supports tol tag variants including tol1e08, tol1e8, tol1e-8, tol1e-08.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not dir_root or not os.path.exists(dir_root): return None\n      candidates=[]\n      if base is None:\n          names = [\n              'active_boundary_tol1e08.csv','active_pairs_tol1e08.csv',\n\
    \              'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv', 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv',\n              'active_boundary_tol1e-8.csv','active_pairs_tol1e-8.csv',\n              'active_boundary_tol1e-08.csv','active_pairs_tol1e-08.csv',\n              'active_boundary.csv','active_pairs.csv'\n          ]\n          for fn in names:\n              fp = os.path.join(dir_root, fn)\n              if os.path.exists(fp):\n                  candidates.append(fp)\n      else:\n          # Nudged_* base\n          tag_variants = ['tol1e08','tol1e8','tol1e-8','tol1e-08']\n          for tv in tag_variants:\n              fn = f'{base}_active_{\"boundary\" if kind==\"boundary\" else \"pairs\"}_{tv}.csv'\n              fp = os.path.join(dir_root, fn)\n              if os.path.exists(fp): candidates.append(fp)\n      if candidates:\n          # Prefer longer (more specific) filenames\n          candidates.sort(key=lambda s: (-len(os.path.basename(s)), s))\n          # Return first match for requested kind\n      \
    \    for fp in candidates:\n              fl = os.path.basename(fp).lower()\n              if kind == 'boundary' and 'boundary' in fl: return fp\n              if kind == 'pairs' and 'pairs' in fl: return fp\n      # Last resort: scan dir for any active_* file containing the token\n      for fn in os.listdir(dir_root):\n          fl = fn.lower()\n          if fl.endswith('.csv') and 'active' in fl and kind in fl:\n              return os.path.join(dir_root, fn)\n      return None\n\n  def load_pack(dir_root, base=None):\n      if base is None:\n          b = find_file(dir_root, 'boundary')\n          p = find_file(dir_root, 'pairs')\n          centers = read_centers(os.path.join(dir_root, 'centers.txt'))  # may be None\n      else:\n          b = find_file(dir_root, 'boundary', base=base)\n          p = find_file(dir_root, 'pairs',    base=base)\n          centers = read_centers(os.path.join(dir_root, f'{base}_centers.txt'))\n      pairs_raw = parse_pairs_raw(p); bound_raw = parse_boundary_raw(b)\n\
    \      pairs, _ = normalize_indices(pairs_raw, 'pairs')\n      bound, _ = normalize_indices(bound_raw, 'bound')\n      return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': centers, 'meta': {'b_path': b, 'p_path': p}}\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      I = A & B; U = A | B\n      J = float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0\n      return {'j': J, 'I': len(I), 'U': len(U)}\n\n  def align_map(CA, CB):\n      if CA is None or CB is None: return None\n      M = np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n      if linear_sum_assignment is None:\n          a_idx = np.lexsort((CA[:,1], CA[:,0])); b_idx = np.lexsort((CB[:,1], CB[:,0]))\n          P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[a_idx] = b_idx; return P\n      r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n      P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r] = c\n      return P\n\n  def map_pairs(P, S):\n      if P is None: return None\n      T = set()\n      for (i, j) in S:\n          a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n          if a == b: continue\n          u,\
    \ v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n          T.add((u, v))\n      return T\n\n  def map_bound(P, S):\n      if P is None: return None\n      return set((int(P[i]), s) for (i, s) in S)\n\n  def write_json_csv(base, tag, res):\n      os.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(os.path.join(base, f'{tag}.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(res, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n      with open(os.path.join(base, f'{tag}.csv'), 'w', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['n','boundary_j','I_b','U_b','pairs_j','I_p','U_p'])\n          w.writerow([N, res['boundary']['j'], res['boundary']['I'], res['boundary']['U'],\n                         res['pairs']['j'],    res['pairs']['I'],    res['pairs']['U']])\n\n  def compare_two(A, B, out_base, tag):\n      res = {'n': N, 'boundary': jaccard(A['bound'], B['bound']), 'pairs': jaccard(A['pairs'], B['pairs']), 'note':'unaligned'}\n      write_json_csv(out_base, f'{tag}', res)\n      P = align_map(A['centers'], B['centers'])\n\
    \      if P is not None:\n          Ab, Ap = map_bound(P, A['bound']), map_pairs(P, A['pairs'])\n          if Ab is not None and Ap is not None:\n              res2 = {'n': N, 'alignment': 'hungarian', 'boundary': jaccard(Ab, B['bound']), 'pairs': jaccard(Ap, B['pairs'])}\n              write_json_csv(out_base, f'{tag}_aligned', res2)\n\n  def consensus_sets(packs):\n      Bs = [packs[k]['bound'] for k in packs]; Ps = [packs[k]['pairs'] for k in packs]\n      inter_b = set.intersection(*Bs) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Bs) else set()\n      union_b = set.union(*Bs) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Bs) else set()\n      inter_p = set.intersection(*Ps) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Ps) else set()\n      union_p = set.union(*Ps) if all(isinstance(s,set) for s in Ps) else set()\n      sizes_b = {k: len(packs[k]['bound']) for k in packs}\n      sizes_p = {k: len(packs[k]['pairs']) for k in packs}\n      return {'boundary': {'intersection': len(inter_b), 'union': len(union_b), 'sizes':\
    \ sizes_b},\n              'pairs':    {'intersection': len(inter_p), 'union': len(union_p), 'sizes': sizes_p}}\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      os.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\n      root_inq = find_inquire_root()\n      # Load SOTA packs (sets + centers where available)\n      noe = {'pairs': set(), 'bound': set(), 'centers': read_centers('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')}\n      # Noesis sets from our exports dir\n      def load_sets_from_dir(d):\n          # Try standard names; fallback scan\n          b = None; p = None\n          if os.path.exists(d):\n              for fn in os.listdir(d):\n                  fl = fn.lower()\n                  if fl.endswith('.csv') and 'active' in fl and 'boundary' in fl and b is None: b = os.path.join(d, fn)\n                  if fl.endswith('.csv') and 'active' in fl and 'pairs' in fl and p is None:    p = os.path.join(d, fn)\n          pr = parse_pairs_raw(p); bd = parse_boundary_raw(b)\n          P,_ = normalize_indices(pr, 'pairs');\
    \ B,_ = normalize_indices(bd, 'bound')\n          return P, B\n      P_noe, B_noe = load_sets_from_dir('storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'); noe['pairs']=P_noe; noe['bound']=B_noe\n\n      sci = load_pack('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26')  # has sets + centers\n      pro = load_pack('storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26')\n      inq_sota = load_pack(root_inq) if root_inq else {'pairs': set(), 'bound': set(), 'centers': None}\n\n      # 4-lineage consensus (SOTAs)\n      sotapacks = {'Noesis_243': noe, 'Scientia_259': sci, 'Prometheus_298': pro, 'Inquire_207': inq_sota}\n      cons4 = consensus_sets(sotapacks)\n      with open(os.path.join(OUT, 'consensus_4lineage_sotas_tol1e8.json'), 'w') as f:\n          json.dump({'n':N, 'ids': list(sotapacks.keys()), **cons4}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n      # Pairwise matrix among SOTAs (unaligned, sets)\n      with open(os.path.join(OUT, 'jaccard_matrix_sotas_tol1e8.csv'),'w',newline='') as f:\n          w=csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['A','B','boundary_j','I_b','U_b','pairs_j','I_p','U_p'])\n\
    \          keys = list(sotapacks.keys())\n          pairs = [('Noesis_243','Scientia_259'),('Noesis_243','Prometheus_298'),('Noesis_243','Inquire_207'),\n                   ('Scientia_259','Prometheus_298'),('Scientia_259','Inquire_207'),('Prometheus_298','Inquire_207')]\n          for a,b in pairs:\n              A=sotapacks[a]; B=sotapacks[b]\n              jb=jaccard(A['bound'],B['bound']); jp=jaccard(A['pairs'],B['pairs'])\n              w.writerow([a,b,jb['j'],jb['I'],jb['U'],jp['j'],jp['I'],jp['U']])\n\n      # Per-pack (Nudged_*) analyses if present\n      if root_inq and os.path.exists(root_inq):\n          nudged = []\n          for fn in os.listdir(root_inq):\n              if fn.startswith('Nudged_') and fn.endswith('_centers.txt'):\n                  base = fn[:-len('_centers.txt')]\n                  nudged.append(base)\n          summary=[]\n          for base in sorted(set(nudged)):\n              pack = load_pack(root_inq, base=base)\n              out_dir = os.path.join(OUT,\
    \ base); os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n              compare_two(pack, noe, out_dir, f'{base}_vs_noesis243_tol1e8')\n              compare_two(pack, sci, out_dir, f'{base}_vs_scientia259_tol1e8')\n              compare_two(pack, pro, out_dir, f'{base}_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8')\n              compare_two(pack, inq_sota, out_dir, f'{base}_vs_inquire207_tol1e8')\n              # Summary line: boundary J vs each reference (prefer aligned if exists)\n              def loadJ(pathA, pathB):\n                  if os.path.exists(pathA):\n                      with open(pathA,'r') as f: return float(json.load(f)['boundary']['j'])\n                  with open(pathB,'r') as f: return float(json.load(f)['boundary']['j'])\n              def JJ(tag):\n                  return loadJ(os.path.join(out_dir,f'{base}_vs_{tag}_tol1e8_aligned.json'),\n                               os.path.join(out_dir,f'{base}_vs_{tag}_tol1e8.json'))\n              summary.append([base, JJ('noesis243'), JJ('scientia259'),\
    \ JJ('prometheus298'), JJ('inquire207')])\n          if summary:\n              with open(os.path.join(OUT,'inquire_v4_summary.csv'),'w',newline='') as f:\n                  w=csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['pack','Jb_noesis243','Jb_scientia259','Jb_prometheus298','Jb_inquire207'])\n                  for row in summary: w.writerow(row)\n\n      # Return current Noesis packing unchanged\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'); r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n      return np.array(c,float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r,float).reshape(N,)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noesis/nmap/inquire_v4}`\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/inquire_v4/consensus_4lineage_sotas_tol1e8.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/inquire_v4/jaccard_matrix_sotas_tol1e8.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/updates.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 215 — Inquire v4 aggregator (tol1e08) submitted\n  - Implements explicit support for tol1e08 filenames\
    \ and Nudged_* groups in storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/.\n  - Emits:\n      • consensus_4lineage_sotas_tol1e8.json\n      • jaccard_matrix_sotas_tol1e8.csv\n      • per-pack results in storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_v4/Nudged_*/ (unaligned + aligned when centers exist)\n      • inquire_v4_summary.csv\n  - Exports-only; no eval-code peer reads. Will post consolidated numbers publicly after verifying outputs.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Inquire I — I’ve submitted v4 of the aggregator with explicit tol1e08 support and Nudged_* grouping under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/. It writes 4‑lineage consensus, SOTA pairwise Jaccards, and per‑pack results to storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_v4/. I’ll post the consolidated numbers after I verify the outputs. Exports‑only; no eval‑code peer reads.\n```"
