tick: 226
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Inquire/nmap}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Inquire/nmap/n26}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ingest Inquire V33 (n=26): Jaccards vs refs + Nudged_* mapping; refresh 4-lineage consensus (tol=1e-8)\"\ntags: \"utility, analysis-only, jaccard, consensus, nmap, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Sets-only ingestion of Inquire V33 n=26 exports. Compute Jaccards vs Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298; map all Inquire Nudged_* subfolders; refresh 4-lineage consensus. Writes artifacts under storage/noesis/nmap/. Returns Noesis pack unchanged (no eval-code peer reads).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  # ---------- Load our own packing (unchanged return) ----------\n  def read_txt_matrix(path, shape):\n      try:\n          arr = np.loadtxt(path)\n          arr = np.array(arr, dtype=float).reshape(shape)\n          return arr\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n\
    \  def load_noesis_pack():\n      c = read_txt_matrix('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt', (N, 2))\n      r = read_txt_matrix('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', (N,))\n      if c is not None and r is not None:\n          return c, r\n      # Fallback: grid + hole seed with tiny margins\n      r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]  # 25\n      hole = np.array([0.2, 0.2])\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n      r_hole = d - r0 - 1e-8\n      radii = [r0]*25 + [r_hole]\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n\n  # ---------- Parsing and canonicalization ----------\n  def canonicalize_label(lbl):\n      m = {'xmin':'xL','xmax':'xR','ymin':'yB','ymax':'yT',\n           'xl':'xL','xr':'xR','yb':'yB','yt':'yT',\n           'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'}\n      s = str(lbl).strip()\n      return m.get(s, s)\n\n  def read_summary_index_base(folder):\n   \
    \   for name in ['summary_tol1e8.json', 'summary_tol1e08.json']:\n          p = os.path.join(folder, name)\n          if os.path.isfile(p):\n              try:\n                  with open(p, 'r') as f:\n                      js = json.load(f)\n                  ib = js.get('index_base', None)\n                  return 0 if ib == 0 else (1 if ib == 1 else None)\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return None\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(folder):\n      for fname in ['active_boundary_tol1e8.csv', 'active_boundary_tol1e08.csv']:\n          path = os.path.join(folder, fname)\n          if os.path.isfile(path):\n              break\n      else:\n          return set()\n      base = read_summary_index_base(folder)\n      S = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for ln, line in enumerate(f):\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(',')]\n                  if ln == 0:\n                      # header check\n\
    \                      if len(parts) >= 2 and not parts[0].isdigit():\n                          continue\n                  if len(parts) < 2:\n                      continue\n                  i_raw, lbl_raw = parts[0], parts[1]\n                  if not i_raw:\n                      continue\n                  i = int(i_raw)\n                  if base is None:\n                      if i >= N:  # auto-adjust\n                          i -= 1\n                  elif base == 1:\n                      i -= 1\n                  lbl = canonicalize_label(lbl_raw)\n                  if 0 <= i < N:\n                      S.add((i, lbl))\n      except Exception:\n          return set()\n      return S\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(folder):\n      for fname in ['active_pairs_tol1e8.csv', 'active_pairs_tol1e08.csv']:\n          path = os.path.join(folder, fname)\n          if os.path.isfile(path):\n              break\n      else:\n          return set()\n      base = read_summary_index_base(folder)\n\
    \      P = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for ln, line in enumerate(f):\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(',')]\n                  if ln == 0:\n                      if len(parts) >= 2 and not parts[0].isdigit():\n                          continue\n                  if len(parts) < 2:\n                      continue\n                  a_raw, b_raw = parts[0], parts[1]\n                  if not a_raw or not b_raw:\n                      continue\n                  a = int(a_raw); b = int(b_raw)\n                  if base is None:\n                      if max(a, b) >= N:\n                          a -= 1; b -= 1\n                  elif base == 1:\n                      a -= 1; b -= 1\n                  if a == b:\n                      continue\n                  i, j = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                  if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N:\n                      P.add((i, j))\n      except Exception:\n    \
    \      return set()\n      return P\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      inter = len(A & B)\n      union = len(A | B)\n      J = (inter / union) if union > 0 else 0.0\n      return inter, union, J\n\n  def write_jaccard(out_base, bj, pj, sizes, meta=None):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_base), exist_ok=True)\n      data = {\n          'tolerance': '1e-8',\n          'boundary': {\n              'intersection': bj[0], 'union': bj[1], 'jaccard': round(bj[2], 6),\n              'sizes': {'A': sizes['boundary'][0], 'B': sizes['boundary'][1]}\n          },\n          'pairs': {\n              'intersection': pj[0], 'union': pj[1], 'jaccard': round(pj[2], 6),\n              'sizes': {'A': sizes['pairs'][0], 'B': sizes['pairs'][1]}\n          }\n      }\n      if meta: data['meta'] = meta\n      with open(out_base + '.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(data, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n      with open(out_base + '.csv', 'w') as f:\n          f.write('type,intersection,union,jaccard,|A|,|B|\\\
    n')\n          f.write(f'boundary,{bj[0]},{bj[1]},{bj[2]:.6f},{sizes[\"boundary\"][0]},{sizes[\"boundary\"][1]}\\n')\n          f.write(f'pairs,{pj[0]},{pj[1]},{pj[2]:.6f},{sizes[\"pairs\"][0]},{sizes[\"pairs\"][1]}\\n')\n\n  def write_consensus(out_base, sets_dict):\n      # sets_dict: {'N':(B,P), 'S':(...), 'P':(...), 'I':(...)}\n      B_sets = [v[0] for v in sets_dict.values() if v[0]]\n      P_sets = [v[1] for v in sets_dict.values() if v[1]]\n      if not B_sets or not P_sets:\n          return\n      B_int = set.intersection(*B_sets)\n      B_uni = set.union(*B_sets)\n      P_int = set.intersection(*P_sets)\n      P_uni = set.union(*P_sets)\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_base), exist_ok=True)\n      js = {\n          'tolerance': '1e-8',\n          'boundary': {'intersection': len(B_int), 'union': len(B_uni)},\n          'pairs':    {'intersection': len(P_int), 'union': len(P_uni)},\n          'sizes': {\n              k: {'boundary': len(sets_dict[k][0]), 'pairs': len(sets_dict[k][1])}\n\
    \              for k in sets_dict\n          }\n      }\n      with open(out_base + '.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(js, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n      with open(out_base + '.csv', 'w') as f:\n          f.write('set,|boundary|,|pairs|\\n')\n          for k in sets_dict:\n              f.write(f'{k},{len(sets_dict[k][0])},{len(sets_dict[k][1])}\\n')\n          f.write('intersection,' + f'{len(B_int)},{len(P_int)}\\n')\n          f.write('union,' + f'{len(B_uni)},{len(P_uni)}\\n')\n\n  def list_nudged_subfolders(folder):\n      try:\n          items = os.listdir(folder)\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n      subs = []\n      for it in items:\n          p = os.path.join(folder, it)\n          if os.path.isdir(p) and it.lower().startswith('nudged'):\n              subs.append(p)\n      return subs\n\n  # ---------- Main ----------\n  def construct_packing():\n      out_root = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n      # Reference folders\n      F_N = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n\
    \      F_S = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26'\n      F_P = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26'\n      F_I = 'storage/Inquire/nmap/n26'\n\n      # Read base sets\n      Bn, Pn = read_boundary_csv(F_N), read_pairs_csv(F_N)\n      Bs, Ps = read_boundary_csv(F_S), read_pairs_csv(F_S)\n      Bp, Pp = read_boundary_csv(F_P), read_pairs_csv(F_P)\n      Bi, Pi = read_boundary_csv(F_I), read_pairs_csv(F_I)\n\n      # Pairwise Jaccards: Inquire vs refs\n      pairs = [('noesis243', (Bn, Pn)), ('scientia259', (Bs, Ps)), ('prometheus298', (Bp, Pp))]\n      for tag, (B_ref, P_ref) in pairs:\n          sizes = {'boundary': (len(Bi), len(B_ref)), 'pairs': (len(Pi), len(P_ref))}\n          bj = jaccard(Bi, B_ref); pj = jaccard(Pi, P_ref)\n          out_base = os.path.join(out_root, f'jaccard_inquire_sota_vs_{tag}_tol1e8')\n          write_jaccard(out_base, bj, pj, sizes, meta={'A':'Inquire_SOTA','B':tag})\n\n      # 4-lineage consensus on base sets (N,S,P,I)\n      sets_dict = {'N': (Bn, Pn), 'S': (Bs, Ps), 'P':\
    \ (Bp, Pp), 'I': (Bi, Pi)}\n      write_consensus(os.path.join(out_root, 'consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8'), sets_dict)\n\n      # Map all Inquire/Nudged_* vs refs\n      nudged = list_nudged_subfolders(F_I)\n      count_n = 0\n      for nd in nudged:\n          Bi_n, Pi_n = read_boundary_csv(nd), read_pairs_csv(nd)\n          name = os.path.basename(nd)\n          for tag, (B_ref, P_ref) in pairs:\n              sizes = {'boundary': (len(Bi_n), len(B_ref)), 'pairs': (len(Pi_n), len(P_ref))}\n              bj = jaccard(Bi_n, B_ref); pj = jaccard(Pi_n, P_ref)\n              out_base = os.path.join(out_root, 'inquire_nudged', name, f'jaccard_{name}_vs_{tag}_tol1e8')\n              write_jaccard(out_base, bj, pj, sizes, meta={'A':name,'B':tag})\n          # Also vs Inquire SOTA itself\n          sizes = {'boundary': (len(Bi_n), len(Bi)), 'pairs': (len(Pi_n), len(Pi))}\n          bj = jaccard(Bi_n, Bi); pj = jaccard(Pi_n, Pi)\n          out_base = os.path.join(out_root, 'inquire_nudged',\
    \ name, f'jaccard_{name}_vs_inquire_sota_tol1e8')\n          write_jaccard(out_base, bj, pj, sizes, meta={'A':name,'B':'Inquire_SOTA'})\n          count_n += 1\n\n      print(f'[INGEST] Inquire base sets: |B|={len(Bi)}, |P|={len(Pi)}')\n      print(f'[INGEST] Nudged processed: {count_n}')\n\n      centers, radii = load_noesis_pack()\n      return centers, radii\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Inquire I — great to hear. I’ve just ingested your V33 exports (sets-only) and kicked off Jaccards and 4-lineage consensus refresh. I also mapped all Nudged_* folders against refs (Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298) and your own SOTA.\n\n  Outputs will appear under:\n  - storage/noesis/nmap/\n    * jaccard_inquire_sota_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    * consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    * inquire_nudged/Nudged_*/jaccard_{Nudged_*}_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298,inquire_sota}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n\
    \n  I’ll post the headline numbers once the eval finishes. Policy reminder: these are derived strictly from published exports—no eval-code peer reads of packings.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Designing code functions**\n\nI’m planning to design some code here. First, I want to include the same canonicalization functions from the previous submission. Then, I’ll create a function to list directories starting with 'Nudged_', filtering them in a case-insensitive manner, possibly using os.listdir.\n\nNext, I’ll implement a function to read sets that returns boundary and pairs sets. The jaccard function will calculate intersections, unions, and the Jaccard index. I'll set up paths for reading base sets from specified storage locations and compute pairwise Jaccards accordingly. Finally, I’ll consider the Nudged subfolders.\n\n**Processing Nudged folders**\n\nFor each folder named NudgedX, I'm planning to read sets and compute Jaccard values against base sets like N, S, and P. The results will be written to files in 'storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_nudged/' with appropriate naming for each comparison. \n\nI’m considering computing Jaccard against the Inquire base set\
  \ too, as that could be helpful. Also, creating a 'meta' summary will be part of this. \n\nIt's essential to list files to confirm everything before we start processing. I'll maintain a \"feasibility guard\" to ensure our pack remains intact, avoiding any degradation with potentially unused values.\n\n**Writing and updating code**\n\nI need to return the saved pack, which produced a valid value of 2.62957196, and I plan to reuse that. Now, I’ll write the code. I might need to update the index files 'nmap/index.md' and 'updates.md', unless we can rely solely on Jaccard outputs. \n\nAfter evaluation, I can perform a storage write for the index to provide a summary. Additionally, I'll acknowledge the Inquire in public memory. I need to carefully handle YAML quoting for content that includes colons. In terms of edge cases, I should ensure that either 'summary_tol1e08.json' or 'summary_tol1e8.json' is parsed correctly. If index_base isn't provided, I'll make sure to auto-detect it.\n\n**Building\
  \ Jaccard functions**\n\nI’m going to build functions that write Jaccard data to specific file paths, using both base and measured sizes. I'll make sure to provide sizes as a tuple representing the sizes of sets A and B. \n\nI'll also compute the 4-lineage consensus and save it to 'storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.{json,csv}'. It's important to avoid writing into other lineages, so I’ll stick to this specific storage. \n\nWhen implementing the code, I need to import os, json, and numpy while keeping it straightforward. I also need to handle the possibility that Nudged_* might not be present. Let’s proceed with crafting the final code!"
