tick: 228
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ingest Inquire (fallback path): Jaccards vs refs + available-lineage consensus (tol=1e-8)\"\ntags: \"utility, analysis-only, jaccard, consensus, nmap, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Sets-only ingestion of Inquire n=26 exports using a robust locator that falls back to storage/Inquire/exports if storage/Inquire/nmap/n26 is absent. Compute Jaccards vs Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298; write available-lineage consensus. No eval-code peer reads; returns Noesis pack unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  # -------- Helpers to load our own pack (unchanged return) --------\n  def read_txt_matrix(path, shape):\n      try:\n          arr = np.loadtxt(path)\n          arr = np.array(arr, dtype=float).reshape(shape)\n          return arr\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def load_noesis_pack():\n      c = read_txt_matrix('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt',\
    \ (N, 2))\n      r = read_txt_matrix('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt', (N,))\n      if c is not None and r is not None:\n          return c, r\n      # Fallback: simple grid+hole seed with tiny margins (feasible, below SOTA)\n      r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      centers = [[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords]  # 25\n      hole = np.array([0.2, 0.2])\n      d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole - np.array([0.1, 0.1])))\n      r_hole = d - r0 - 1e-8\n      radii = [r0]*25 + [r_hole]\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n\n  # -------- Parsing + canonicalization (robust to tol1e8/tol1e08, index_base 0/1) --------\n  def canonicalize_label(lbl):\n      m = {'xmin':'xL','xmax':'xR','ymin':'yB','ymax':'yT',\n           'xl':'xL','xr':'xR','yb':'yB','yt':'yT',\n           'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'}\n      s = str(lbl).strip()\n      return m.get(s, s)\n\n  def read_summary_index_base(folder):\n      for name in ['summary_tol1e8.json',\
    \ 'summary_tol1e08.json']:\n          p = os.path.join(folder, name)\n          if os.path.isfile(p):\n              try:\n                  with open(p, 'r') as f:\n                      js = json.load(f)\n                  ib = js.get('index_base', None)\n                  return 0 if ib == 0 else (1 if ib == 1 else None)\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return None\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(folder):\n      for fname in ['active_boundary_tol1e8.csv', 'active_boundary_tol1e08.csv']:\n          path = os.path.join(folder, fname)\n          if os.path.isfile(path):\n              break\n      else:\n          return set()\n      base = read_summary_index_base(folder)\n      S = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for ln, line in enumerate(f):\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(',')]\n                  if ln == 0 and (len(parts) >= 2) and not parts[0].isdigit():\n                      continue\
    \  # header\n                  if len(parts) < 2 or not parts[0]:\n                      continue\n                  i = int(parts[0])\n                  if base is None:\n                      if i >= N: i -= 1\n                  elif base == 1:\n                      i -= 1\n                  lbl = canonicalize_label(parts[1])\n                  if 0 <= i < N:\n                      S.add((i, lbl))\n      except Exception:\n          return set()\n      return S\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(folder):\n      for fname in ['active_pairs_tol1e8.csv', 'active_pairs_tol1e08.csv']:\n          path = os.path.join(folder, fname)\n          if os.path.isfile(path):\n              break\n      else:\n          return set()\n      base = read_summary_index_base(folder)\n      P = set()\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              for ln, line in enumerate(f):\n                  parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(',')]\n                  if ln == 0 and (len(parts) >=\
    \ 2) and not parts[0].isdigit():\n                      continue  # header\n                  if len(parts) < 2 or not parts[0] or not parts[1]:\n                      continue\n                  a = int(parts[0]); b = int(parts[1])\n                  if base is None:\n                      if max(a, b) >= N:\n                          a -= 1; b -= 1\n                  elif base == 1:\n                      a -= 1; b -= 1\n                  if a == b:\n                      continue\n                  i, j = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                  if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N:\n                      P.add((i, j))\n      except Exception:\n          return set()\n      return P\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n      inter = len(A & B)\n      uni = len(A | B)\n      J = (inter / uni) if uni > 0 else 0.0\n      return inter, uni, J\n\n  def write_jaccard(out_base, bj, pj, sizes, meta=None):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_base), exist_ok=True)\n      data = {\n          'tolerance':\
    \ '1e-8',\n          'boundary': {'intersection': bj[0], 'union': bj[1], 'jaccard': round(bj[2], 6),\n                       'sizes': {'A': sizes['boundary'][0], 'B': sizes['boundary'][1]}},\n          'pairs':    {'intersection': pj[0], 'union': pj[1], 'jaccard': round(pj[2], 6),\n                       'sizes': {'A': sizes['pairs'][0], 'B': sizes['pairs'][1]}},\n      }\n      if meta: data['meta'] = meta\n      with open(out_base + '.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(data, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n      with open(out_base + '.csv', 'w') as f:\n          f.write('type,intersection,union,jaccard,|A|,|B|\\n')\n          f.write(f'boundary,{bj[0]},{bj[1]},{bj[2]:.6f},{sizes[\"boundary\"][0]},{sizes[\"boundary\"][1]}\\n')\n          f.write(f'pairs,{pj[0]},{pj[1]},{pj[2]:.6f},{sizes[\"pairs\"][0]},{sizes[\"pairs\"][1]}\\n')\n\n  def write_available_consensus(out_base, sets_named):\n      # sets_named: list of (key, (B_set, P_set)) for present lineages\n      present = [(k, s)\
    \ for (k, s) in sets_named if s[0] and s[1]]\n      if len(present) < 2:\n          return\n      B_sets = [s[0] for _, s in present]\n      P_sets = [s[1] for _, s in present]\n      B_int = set.intersection(*B_sets)\n      B_uni = set.union(*B_sets)\n      P_int = set.intersection(*P_sets)\n      P_uni = set.union(*P_sets)\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_base), exist_ok=True)\n      js = {\n          'tolerance': '1e-8',\n          'present': [k for k, _ in present],\n          'boundary': {'intersection': len(B_int), 'union': len(B_uni)},\n          'pairs':    {'intersection': len(P_int), 'union': len(P_uni)},\n          'sizes': {k: {'boundary': len(s[0]), 'pairs': len(s[1])} for k, s in present}\n      }\n      with open(out_base + '.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(js, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  def find_inquire_folder():\n      candidates = ['storage/Inquire/nmap/n26', 'storage/Inquire/exports']\n      for folder in candidates:\n          if os.path.isdir(folder):\n\
    \              for fname in ['active_pairs_tol1e8.csv', 'active_pairs_tol1e08.csv']:\n                  if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(folder, fname)):\n                      return folder\n      return None\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      out_root = 'storage/noesis/nmap'\n      # Reference folders\n      F_N = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n      F_S = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26'\n      F_P = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26'\n      F_I = find_inquire_folder()\n\n      # Read reference sets\n      Bn, Pn = read_boundary_csv(F_N), read_pairs_csv(F_N)\n      Bs, Ps = read_boundary_csv(F_S), read_pairs_csv(F_S)\n      Bp, Pp = read_boundary_csv(F_P), read_pairs_csv(F_P)\n\n      # Inquire sets (fallback-aware)\n      Bi, Pi = set(), set()\n      used_path = F_I if F_I else '(none)'\n      if F_I is not None:\n          Bi, Pi = read_boundary_csv(F_I), read_pairs_csv(F_I)\n\n      # Pairwise Jaccards: Inquire vs refs (only if present)\n      if Bi or Pi:\n          pairs = [('noesis243',\
    \ (Bn, Pn)), ('scientia259', (Bs, Ps)), ('prometheus298', (Bp, Pp))]\n          for tag, (B_ref, P_ref) in pairs:\n              sizes = {'boundary': (len(Bi), len(B_ref)), 'pairs': (len(Pi), len(P_ref))}\n              bj = jaccard(Bi, B_ref); pj = jaccard(Pi, P_ref)\n              out_base = os.path.join(out_root, f'jaccard_inquire_sota_vs_{tag}_tol1e8')\n              write_jaccard(out_base, bj, pj, sizes, meta={'A':'Inquire_SOTA','B':tag,'path':F_I})\n\n      # Available-lineage consensus (over present among N,S,P,I)\n      sets_named = [('N', (Bn, Pn)), ('S', (Bs, Ps)), ('P', (Bp, Pp))]\n      if Bi or Pi:\n          sets_named.append(('I', (Bi, Pi)))\n      write_available_consensus(os.path.join(out_root, 'consensus_n26_available_lineages_tol1e8'), sets_named)\n\n      print(f'[INGEST] Inquire path used: {used_path}')\n      print(f'[INGEST] Sizes — Inquire |B|={len(Bi)}, |P|={len(Pi)}; Noesis |B|={len(Bn)}, |P|={len(Pn)}; Scientia |B|={len(Bs)}, |P|={len(Ps)}; Prometheus |B|={len(Bp)},\
    \ |P|={len(Pp)}')\n\n      centers, radii = load_noesis_pack()\n      return centers, radii\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  I’ve issued a fallback ingest (Eval pending) that also checks storage/Inquire/exports if storage/Inquire/nmap/n26 is absent. If found there, I’ll compute:\n  - Jaccards vs Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298\n  - Available-lineage consensus (over present sets)\n  and write results under storage/noesis/nmap/.\n\n  Preferred long-term path remains storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/, but this fallback will unblock consolidation today. I’ll post the headline numbers once the eval finishes.\n```"
