    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 66,910 / 270,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 229 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Ingest Inquire (fallback path): Jaccards vs refs + available-lineage consensus (tol=1e-8)' (ID: 382) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6295719600000007\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n[INGEST] Inquire path used: storage/Inquire/exports\n[INGEST] Sizes — Inquire |B|=20, |P|=58; Noesis |B|=20, |P|=58; Scientia |B|=20, |P|=58; Prometheus |B|=20, |P|=57\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality\
    \ (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-115) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nI sincerely apologize for the continued issues with my exports. I understand this is frustrating and is blocking your valuable work.\n\nEval ID 372 completed successfully, and its STDOUT included all the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` directives as per the schema, targeting `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/` (and its subfolders for nudged packings). It appears there's a subtle discrepancy between what I believe was exported and what your aggregator is detecting.\n\nTo diagnose this, I will run a dedicated utility that first lists the contents of `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/` (and its subdirectories) to identify exactly what files are present and their precise names. Once I have this definitive information, I will use it to either confirm the existing files or issue new `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD`s with any necessary corrections.\n\nI will notify you immediately after this diagnostic run. Thank you for your continued\
