tick: 235
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute Jaccards: Inquire_207 vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298} @ tol=1e8\"\ntags: \"utility, mapping, jaccard, consensus, exports-only\"\nabstract: \"Parse Inquire’s newly published n=26 sets and compute Jaccards vs Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298 at tol=1e−8. Write JSON/CSV under storage/noesis/nmap/ and refresh 4-lineage consensus. Returns Noesis pack (no optimization).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json\n  import numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  # ---------- IO helpers ----------\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n    d = os.path.dirname(p)\n    if d and not os.path.exists(d):\n      os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def read_lines(path):\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      return [ln.strip() for ln in f if ln.strip()]\n\n  def read_pairs_csv(path):\n    # Expect header \"i,j\"\n    s = set()\n    try:\n      lines = read_lines(path)\n    except Exception:\n      return s\n    for idx, ln in enumerate(lines):\n\
    \      if idx == 0:\n        # header, skip if contains non-digits\n        continue\n      parts = [p.strip() for p in ln.split(',')]\n      if len(parts) != 2:\n        continue\n      try:\n        i = int(parts[0]); j = int(parts[1])\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n      if i == j: \n        continue\n      a, b = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n      s.add((a, b))\n    return s\n\n  def read_boundary_csv(path):\n    # Expect header \"disc,label\"; labels in {xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax}\n    allowed = {\"xmin\",\"xmax\",\"ymin\",\"ymax\"}\n    s = set()\n    try:\n      lines = read_lines(path)\n    except Exception:\n      return s\n    for idx, ln in enumerate(lines):\n      if idx == 0:\n        continue\n      parts = [p.strip() for p in ln.split(',')]\n      if len(parts) != 2:\n        continue\n      try:\n        d = int(parts[0])\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n      lab = parts[1].lower()\n      if lab in allowed:\n        s.add((d, lab))\n    return s\n\n\
    \  def load_sets(lineage, custom_paths=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return dict with keys: 'B','P', 'sizes'\n    Tries standard nmap/n26 paths, allows lineage-specific prefixes.\n    \"\"\"\n    candP = []\n    candB = []\n    if custom_paths is not None:\n      candP.extend(custom_paths.get('P', []))\n      candB.extend(custom_paths.get('B', []))\n\n    # Standard candidates\n    base_nmap = f\"storage/{lineage}/nmap/n26\"\n    base_std  = f\"storage/{lineage}/nmap/n26\"\n    base_alt  = f\"storage/{lineage}/exports\"\n\n    # Pairs\n    candP.extend([\n      f\"{base_nmap}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      f\"{base_std}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      f\"{base_alt}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n    ])\n    # Boundary\n    candB.extend([\n      f\"{base_nmap}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      f\"{base_std}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      f\"{base_alt}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n    ])\n\n    # Read first existing\n    P = set()\n    for p in candP:\n      if os.path.exists(p):\n\
    \        P = read_pairs_csv(p)\n        break\n\n    B = set()\n    for p in candB:\n      if os.path.exists(p):\n        B = read_boundary_csv(p)\n        break\n\n    return {\"B\": B, \"P\": P, \"sizes\": {\"B\": len(B), \"P\": len(P)}}\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n    inter = len(A & B)\n    uni   = len(A | B) if (A or B) else 0\n    J = (inter / uni) if uni > 0 else 1.0\n    return inter, uni, J\n\n  def write_jaccard(name, A_name, B_name, A_set, B_set, outdir=\"storage/noesis/nmap\"):\n    inter, uni, J = jaccard(A_set, B_set)\n    data = {\n      \"name\": name,\n      \"A\": A_name,\n      \"B\": B_name,\n      \"A_size\": len(A_set),\n      \"B_size\": len(B_set),\n      \"intersection\": inter,\n      \"union\": uni,\n      \"jaccard\": J\n    }\n    ensure_dir(f\"{outdir}/{name}.json\")\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{name}.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{name}.csv\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\
    A,B,A_size,B_size,intersection,union,jaccard\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"{A_name},{B_name},{len(A_set)},{len(B_set)},{inter},{uni},{J:.6f}\\n\")\n\n  def write_consensus(name, sets_dict, outdir=\"storage/noesis/nmap\"):\n    \"\"\"\n    sets_dict: {label: {\"B\": set(...), \"P\": set(...)}}\n    \"\"\"\n    labels = sorted(sets_dict.keys())\n    Bs = [sets_dict[k][\"B\"] for k in labels]\n    Ps = [sets_dict[k][\"P\"] for k in labels]\n    B_inter = set.intersection(*Bs) if Bs else set()\n    B_union = set.union(*Bs) if Bs else set()\n    P_inter = set.intersection(*Ps) if Ps else set()\n    P_union = set.union(*Ps) if Ps else set()\n    sizes = {k: {\"B\": len(sets_dict[k][\"B\"]), \"P\": len(sets_dict[k][\"P\"])} for k in labels}\n    data = {\n      \"name\": name,\n      \"labels\": labels,\n      \"sizes\": sizes,\n      \"boundary\": {\"intersection\": len(B_inter), \"union\": len(B_union)},\n      \"pairs\":    {\"intersection\": len(P_inter), \"union\": len(P_union)}\n    }\n   \
    \ ensure_dir(f\"{outdir}/{name}.json\")\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{name}.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{name}.csv\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"labels,\" + \",\".join(labels) + \"\\n\")\n      f.write(\"B_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k][\"B\"]) for k in labels) + \"\\n\")\n      f.write(\"P_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k][\"P\"]) for k in labels) + \"\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"B_intersection,{len(B_inter)}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"B_union,{len(B_union)}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"P_intersection,{len(P_inter)}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"P_union,{len(P_union)}\\n\")\n\n  # ---------- Load sets ----------\n  # Inquire: prefer explicitly named files in nmap/n26\n  inquire_paths = {\n    \"P\": [\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"],\n    \"B\": [\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"],\n  }\n  I = load_sets(\"Inquire\", inquire_paths)\n\
    \n  # Noesis 243\n  noesis_paths = {\n    \"P\": [\"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"],\n    \"B\": [\"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"],\n  }\n  N = load_sets(\"noesis\", noesis_paths)\n\n  # Scientia 259\n  S = load_sets(\"Scientia\", None)\n\n  # Prometheus 298\n  Pm = load_sets(\"Prometheus\", None)\n\n  # ---------- Jaccards ----------\n  outdir = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_noesis243_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Noesis_243\", I[\"P\"], N[\"P\"], outdir=outdir)\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_scientia259_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Scientia_259\", I[\"P\"], S[\"P\"], outdir=outdir)\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Prometheus_298\", I[\"P\"], Pm[\"P\"], outdir=outdir)\n\n  # ---------- Consensus (available four-lineage) ----------\n  sets4 = {\n    \"Noesis_243\": N,\n    \"Scientia_259\": S,\n    \"Prometheus_298\":\
    \ Pm,\n    \"Inquire_207\": I\n  }\n  write_consensus(\"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8\", sets4, outdir=outdir)\n\n  # ---------- Return a valid pack (Noesis SOTA 243 or latest fallback) ----------\n  def load_pack():\n    # Preferred: exported SOTA 243\n    try:\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/centers.txt')\n      r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/radii.txt')\n      c = np.array(c, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n      r = np.array(r, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      return c, r\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    # Fallback: latest\n    try:\n      c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n      r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n      c = np.array(c, dtype=float).reshape(N, 2)\n      r = np.array(r, dtype=float).reshape(N,)\n      return c, r\n    except Exception:\n      # Very last resort: tiny grid (feasible, low score)\n      coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n      centers = [[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords][:25]\
    \ + [[0.2,0.2]]\n      radii = [0.09999]*25 + [0.0414]\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n    return load_pack()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Detected your files under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26 — thanks! I’ve submitted a utility to compute Jaccards vs Noesis_243, Scientia_259, and Prometheus_298, and to refresh the 4-lineage consensus. Outputs (JSON/CSV) will appear under:\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n  I’ll post the headline numbers once the run completes. Policy unchanged: exports-only parsing; no eval-code peer reads.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Developing a robust reading function**\n\nI’m considering creating a robust function to read CSV files that correctly handles headers and whitespace. I could parse lines split by commas and skip the header if it contains non-numeric data. Another option is using numpy genfromtxt for easier parsing. I want to define a function that reads CSV pairs, ensuring integers have a canonical order. \n\nFor outputs, I’ll create JSON and CSV files that summarize sizes, intersections, and other relevant data. I’ll also save combined consensus sets with their counts.\n\n**Computing Jaccard results**\n\nI'm working on computing pairwise Jaccard results and considering whether to provide a matrix or just the intersection and union. It seems better to produce both a consensus and a pairwise matrix, but to keep the code shorter, I can compute the Jaccards individually and save three JSON files. \n\nI also need to ensure that my code reads files specifically from the allowed storage paths\
  \ without mixing in other data. I'll load from the baseline pack in the Noesis repository and double-check my paths for accuracy.\n\n**Implementing load function**\n\nI’m working on implementing a function to load the Noesis pack. I’ll try the paths for the centers and radii files first and fall back to the latest centers file if those don't work. After that, I want to ensure we run the script correctly. \n\nBefore submitting, I might want to confirm listing the storage, though it seems we already did that. I should submit with YAML details and update the public capsule with the results once they’re ready after evaluation. I’ll also make sure to communicate that I’ll publish results once available.\n\n**Implementing CSV functions**\n\nI’m planning to implement several functions for handling CSV files. First, the `read_csv_pairs` function will return a set of tuples containing sorted integers. Next, I’ll create `read_csv_boundary` to return a set of (disc, label) with canonical labels like\
  \ 'xmin', 'xmax', 'ymin', and 'ymax'.\n\nFor loading lineage sets, I’ll define a method that accepts a list of candidate file names from specified storage paths for different contexts. I need to ensure that I compute Jaccard values and store results in JSON and CSV format. I'll stick to using standard libraries like json and os.\n\n**Creating and saving pack**\n\nI’m focusing on using `np.savetxt` to save the pack generated from our baseline. I need to implement the code while ensuring that the script creates the necessary directories, specifically 'storage/noesis/nmap'.\n\nNext, I’ll outline the script content in YAML format. Once that’s in place, I can move to public memory and state that files have been found and Jaccard computations are underway, while keeping my response minimal due to formatting guidelines. I'll also need to submit and reply with confirmations, ensuring that titles in YAML are quoted correctly."
