role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{storage list noesis/exports/sota_243}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Prometheus/nmap/n26}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Scientia/nmap/n26}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute Jaccards FIX: robust CSV + explicit paths for {Noesis_243, Prometheus_298, Scientia_259, Inquire_207}\"\ntags: \"utility, mapping, jaccard, consensus, robustness, exports-only\"\nabstract: \"Fix prior mis-parsing (zeros for Noesis/Prometheus). Use robust CSV reader (Sniffer, utf-8-sig, quotes) and explicit standard paths. Recompute pairs+boundary Jaccards and 4-lineage consensus at tol=1e−8. Returns a trivial valid pack (no optimization).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, csv\n  import numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  # ---------- Robust CSV readers ----------\n  def sniff_csv(fpath):\n    with open(fpath, 'r', encoding='utf-8-sig', newline='') as f:\n      sample = f.read(2048)\n      f.seek(0)\n      try:\n        dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(sample, delimiters=[',',';','\\\
    t',' '])\n      except Exception:\n        class _D: delimiter=','\n        dialect = _D()\n      reader = csv.reader(f, dialect)\n      rows = [row for row in reader]\n    return rows\n\n  def read_pairs_csv_robust(path):\n    s = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path): return s\n    try:\n      rows = sniff_csv(path)\n    except Exception:\n      return s\n    if not rows: return s\n    # detect header\n    header = [c.strip().lower() for c in rows[0]]\n    start = 1\n    if len(header) >= 2 and (('i' in header[0] and 'j' in header[1]) or ('i' in header and 'j' in header)):\n      start = 1\n    else:\n      # try to see if first row is numeric\n      try:\n        int(rows[0][0]); int(rows[0][1])\n        start = 0\n      except Exception:\n        start = 1\n    for row in rows[start:]:\n      if len(row) < 2: continue\n      a, b = row[0].strip(), row[1].strip()\n      # strip quotes\n      a = a.strip('\"').strip(\"'\"); b = b.strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n      try:\n        i = int(a);\
    \ j = int(b)\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n      if i == j: continue\n      u, v = (i,j) if i < j else (j,i)\n      s.add((u,v))\n    return s\n\n  def read_boundary_csv_robust(path):\n    s = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path): return s\n    allowed = {\"xmin\",\"xmax\",\"ymin\",\"ymax\"}\n    try:\n      rows = sniff_csv(path)\n    except Exception:\n      return s\n    if not rows: return s\n    header = [c.strip().lower() for c in rows[0]]\n    # find columns\n    try:\n      di = header.index('disc')\n      li = header.index('label')\n      start = 1\n    except ValueError:\n      # assume no header if first row looks numeric\n      start = 0\n      di, li = 0, 1\n    for row in rows[start:]:\n      if len(row) <= max(di, li): continue\n      d_s = row[di].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n      lab = row[li].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\").lower()\n      try:\n        d = int(d_s)\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n      if lab in allowed:\n        s.add((d,\
    \ lab))\n    return s\n\n  def load_sets_explicit(lineage, pairs_paths, boundary_paths):\n    P = set()\n    for p in pairs_paths:\n      if os.path.exists(p):\n        P = read_pairs_csv_robust(p)\n        if P: break\n    B = set()\n    for p in boundary_paths:\n      if os.path.exists(p):\n        B = read_boundary_csv_robust(p)\n        if B: break\n    return {\"P\": P, \"B\": B, \"sizes\": {\"P\": len(P), \"B\": len(B)}}\n\n  def write_json_csv(base, data):\n    outdir = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"\n    os.makedirs(outdir, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{base}.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{base}.csv\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      if \"jaccard\" in base:\n        f.write(\"A,B,A_size,B_size,intersection,union,jaccard\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"{data['A']},{data['B']},{data['A_size']},{data['B_size']},{data['intersection']},{data['union']},{data['jaccard']:.6f}\\n\")\n      else:\n      \
    \  labels = data[\"labels\"]\n        sizes = data[\"sizes\"]\n        f.write(\"labels,\" + \",\".join(labels) + \"\\n\")\n        f.write(\"B_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k]['B']) for k in labels) + \"\\n\")\n        f.write(\"P_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k]['P']) for k in labels) + \"\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"B_intersection,{data['boundary']['intersection']}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"B_union,{data['boundary']['union']}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"P_intersection,{data['pairs']['intersection']}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"P_union,{data['pairs']['union']}\\n\")\n\n  def jaccard(A, B):\n    inter = len(A & B)\n    uni = len(A | B) if (A or B) else 0\n    J = inter / uni if uni > 0 else 1.0\n    return inter, uni, J\n\n  def write_jaccard(name, A_name, B_name, A_set, B_set):\n    inter, uni, J = jaccard(A_set, B_set)\n    data = {\"name\": name, \"A\": A_name, \"B\": B_name, \"A_size\": len(A_set), \"B_size\": len(B_set), \"intersection\": inter, \"union\": uni, \"jaccard\": J}\n\
    \    write_json_csv(name, data)\n\n  def write_consensus(name, sets_dict):\n    labels = list(sets_dict.keys())\n    Bs = [sets_dict[k][\"B\"] for k in labels]\n    Ps = [sets_dict[k][\"P\"] for k in labels]\n    B_inter = set.intersection(*Bs) if Bs else set()\n    B_union = set.union(*Bs) if Bs else set()\n    P_inter = set.intersection(*Ps) if Ps else set()\n    P_union = set.union(*Ps) if Ps else set()\n    sizes = {k: {\"B\": len(sets_dict[k][\"B\"]), \"P\": len(sets_dict[k][\"P\"])} for k in labels}\n    data = {\"name\": name, \"labels\": labels, \"sizes\": sizes,\n            \"boundary\": {\"intersection\": len(B_inter), \"union\": len(B_union)},\n            \"pairs\": {\"intersection\": len(P_inter), \"union\": len(P_union)}}\n    write_json_csv(name, data)\n\n  # ---------- Explicit paths ----------\n  N = load_sets_explicit(\n    \"Noesis_243\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/noesis/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\
    \n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/noesis/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ]\n  )\n  S = load_sets_explicit(\n    \"Scientia_259\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ]\n  )\n  Pm = load_sets_explicit(\n    \"Prometheus_298\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Prometheus/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Prometheus/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ]\n  )\n  I = load_sets_explicit(\n    \"Inquire_207\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\
    ,\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Inquire/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Inquire/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ]\n  )\n\n  # ---------- Write Jaccards (pairs and boundary) ----------\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_noesis243_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Noesis_243\", I[\"P\"], N[\"P\"])\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_scientia259_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Scientia_259\", I[\"P\"], S[\"P\"])\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Prometheus_298\", I[\"P\"], Pm[\"P\"])\n\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_boundary_inquire_eval207_vs_noesis243_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Noesis_243\", I[\"B\"], N[\"B\"])\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_boundary_inquire_eval207_vs_scientia259_tol1e8\"\
    , \"Inquire_207\", \"Scientia_259\", I[\"B\"], S[\"B\"])\n  write_jaccard(\"jaccard_boundary_inquire_eval207_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8\", \"Inquire_207\", \"Prometheus_298\", I[\"B\"], Pm[\"B\"])\n\n  # ---------- Consensus ----------\n  sets4 = {\"Noesis_243\": N, \"Scientia_259\": S, \"Prometheus_298\": Pm, \"Inquire_207\": I}\n  write_consensus(\"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8\", sets_dict=sets4)\n\n  # ---------- Return a valid pack (trivial constructive; analysis-only run) ----------\n  def construct_packing():\n    coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n    centers = [[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords][:25] + [[0.2,0.2]]\n    radii = [0.09999]*25 + [0.0414213]\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Inquire I — I see all five SOTA files in storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/. My first Jaccard run mis-parsed some sets (zeros for Noesis/Prometheus). I’ve\
    \ submitted a FIX that uses a robust CSV reader (utf‑8‑sig, delimiter sniffing, quoted fields) and explicit paths. I’ll post the updated Jaccard + consensus numbers as soon as the run finishes.\n\n  When you export Nudged_* sets, keep the same headers/suffix (active_boundary_tol1e8.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8.csv). I’ll ingest them and emit pairwise Jaccards vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298} plus an expanded consensus.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Refining mapping utility process**\n\nOkay, for the mapping utility, returning the baseline pack is fine, but the score isn’t relevant. We did return a trivial pack earlier due to missing files, which isn’t ideal, but the analysis outputs were saved. I need to rerun it with a better CSV parser that tolerates quotes and special line endings. Also, I'll check paths for loading Noesis/Prometheus sets. Verifying the presence of files is helpful for debugging but not critical. Plus, I should respond publicly to Inquire about the Jaccards computation.\n\n**Planning a quick rerun**\n\nI need to implement a quick rerun where I'll list the storages of some expected directories to check for file presence. First, I’ll check Noesis, followed by other directories like Prometheus, Scientia, and Inquire. After confirming the file presence, I'll submit a new utility that includes a robust CSV parser that can handle various delimiters, such as quotes, stray BOM, and whitespace. For Noesis\
  \ and Prometheus, I plan to use explicit path sets to ensure proper loading.\n\n**Confirming data presence for Prometheus and others**\n\nI’m looking into the Prometheus mapping, where we used specific files before, and I need to list them again for confirmation. For Inquire, I'll utilize both the detailed and generic active files. As for Scientia, I’ll check both the standard directories. Additionally, I want to compute boundary Jaccards, saving the results to JSON/CSV while updating consensus data with sizes properly. I’ll also attempt to load the centers.txt file from Noesis and confirm its presence in the storage directory.\n\n**Checking for center and radius files**\n\nEarlier, I noted that we wrote 'SOTA_LATEST.txt' and exported centers/radii under 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/centers.txt' and 'radii.txt.' This was during step 246 where we aimed to export active sets. It’s possible we didn’t export those centers/radii this time. To verify, I'll check for 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\
  \ and 'latest_radii.txt' as they likely exist. However, our previous submission failed to access these files. The priority is to recompute Jaccard stats and make them public, along with computing sizes for consensus data. I’ll list the necessary storage.\n\n**Implementing robust CSV parsing and planning run**\n\nI need to read outputs quickly after running, though results will come later. It’s crucial to leave a public message about any initial mis-parsing and a fixed run for updates. I’ll handle CSV quoting for boundaries robustly using Python's CSV module. I plan to implement flexible parsing that accommodates various header formats while ensuring I manage expected fieldnames properly. \n\nFor Prometheus paths, I’ll look for existing files and set up functions to load data correctly. I also want to compute boundary Jaccards and report to the user about the improvements made in the parsing process. It’s okay to keep it straightforward while generating necessary outputs again."
