role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv}`\n`/execute_action{storage read Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e08.csv}`\n`/execute_action{storage read Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e08.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compute Jaccards FIX2: boundary header synonyms + tol1e08 fallback\"\ntags: \"utility, mapping, jaccard, consensus, robustness, exports-only\"\nabstract: \"Fix boundary parsing (accept header synonyms: label/boundary/side/axis) and add Prometheus tol1e08 filename fallback. Recompute pairs/boundary Jaccards for Inquire_207 vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298} and refresh 4-lineage consensus. Returns a trivial valid pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, csv\n  import numpy as np\n\n  N = 26\n\n  # ---- Robust CSV helpers ----\n  def sniff_rows(path):\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8-sig', newline='') as f:\n      sample = f.read(2048); f.seek(0)\n\
    \      try:\n        dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(sample, delimiters=[',',';','\\t',' '])\n      except Exception:\n        class _D: delimiter = ','\n        dialect = _D()\n      rdr = csv.reader(f, dialect)\n      return [row for row in rdr]\n\n  def norm_label(s):\n    t = s.strip().lower().replace(' ', '').replace('-', '').replace('_','')\n    # normalize common variants\n    mapping = {\n      'xmin':'xmin', 'xminimum':'xmin', 'xleft':'xmin', 'left':'xmin',\n      'xmax':'xmax', 'xmaximum':'xmax', 'xright':'xmax', 'right':'xmax',\n      'ymin':'ymin', 'ybottom':'ymin', 'bottom':'ymin', 'ybottomedge':'ymin',\n      'ymax':'ymax', 'ytop':'ymax', 'top':'ymax'\n    }\n    # tolerate x_min/x_max/y_min/y_max\n    t = t.replace('xminimum','xmin').replace('x_max','xmax').replace('x_min','xmin').replace('y_min','ymin').replace('y_max','ymax')\n    return mapping.get(t, t)\n\n  def read_pairs(path):\n    S = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n    try:\n      rows = sniff_rows(path)\n\
    \    except Exception:\n      return S\n    if not rows: return S\n    # header?\n    start = 1\n    try:\n      int(rows[0][0]); int(rows[0][1])\n      start = 0\n    except Exception:\n      start = 1\n    for row in rows[start:]:\n      if len(row) < 2: continue\n      a = row[0].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n      b = row[1].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n      try:\n        i = int(a); j = int(b)\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n      if i == j: continue\n      u, v = (i,j) if i < j else (j,i)\n      S.add((u,v))\n    return S\n\n  def read_boundary(path):\n    S = set()\n    if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n    try:\n      rows = sniff_rows(path)\n    except Exception:\n      return S\n    if not rows: return S\n    hdr = [c.strip().lower() for c in rows[0]]\n    # find candidate columns\n    disc_idx = None; lab_idx = None\n    for i, h in enumerate(hdr):\n      if h in ('disc','id','index','i'):\n        disc_idx = i\n      if h in ('label','boundary','side','axis','edge'):\n\
    \        lab_idx = i\n    start = 1 if disc_idx is not None and lab_idx is not None else 0\n    if start == 0:\n      disc_idx, lab_idx = 0, 1\n    for row in rows[start:]:\n      if len(row) <= max(disc_idx, lab_idx): continue\n      ds = row[disc_idx].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n      ls = norm_label(row[lab_idx])\n      try:\n        d = int(ds)\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n      if ls in {'xmin','xmax','ymin','ymax'}:\n        S.add((d, ls))\n    return S\n\n  def load_sets(name, pairs_paths, boundary_paths):\n    P = set()\n    for p in pairs_paths:\n      if os.path.exists(p):\n        cand = read_pairs(p)\n        if cand:\n          P = cand; break\n    B = set()\n    for p in boundary_paths:\n      if os.path.exists(p):\n        cand = read_boundary(p)\n        if cand:\n          B = cand; break\n    return {\"name\": name, \"P\": P, \"B\": B}\n\n  def J(A, B):\n    inter = len(A & B)\n    uni = len(A | B) if (A or B) else 0\n    return inter, uni, (inter/uni\
    \ if uni>0 else 1.0)\n\n  def write_json_csv(base, data):\n    outdir = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"; os.makedirs(outdir, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{base}.json\",\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: json.dump(data,f,indent=2)\n    with open(f\"{outdir}/{base}.csv\",\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      if \"jaccard\" in base:\n        f.write(\"A,B,A_size,B_size,intersection,union,jaccard\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"{data['A']},{data['B']},{data['A_size']},{data['B_size']},{data['intersection']},{data['union']},{data['jaccard']:.6f}\\n\")\n      else:\n        labs = data[\"labels\"]; sizes = data[\"sizes\"]\n        f.write(\"labels,\" + \",\".join(labs) + \"\\n\")\n        f.write(\"B_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k]['B']) for k in labs) + \"\\n\")\n        f.write(\"P_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k]['P']) for k in labs) + \"\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"B_intersection,{data['boundary']['intersection']}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"B_union,{data['boundary']['union']}\\n\")\n  \
    \      f.write(f\"P_intersection,{data['pairs']['intersection']}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"P_union,{data['pairs']['union']}\\n\")\n\n  # ---- Explicit paths (incl. tol1e08 fallback) ----\n  N = load_sets(\"Noesis_243\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/noesis/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/noesis/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ])\n  S = load_sets(\"Scientia_259\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ])\n  Pm = load_sets(\"Prometheus_298\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\
    ,\n      \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e08.csv\",\n      \"storage/Prometheus/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e08.csv\",\n      \"storage/Prometheus/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ])\n  I = load_sets(\"Inquire_207\",\n    pairs_paths=[\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Inquire/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ],\n    boundary_paths=[\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \"storage/Inquire/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n    ])\n\n  # ---- Jaccards (pairs + boundary) ----\n  def write_j(name, A, B, kind):\n    Aset = A[kind]; Bset = B[kind]\n    inter, uni, j =\
    \ J(Aset, Bset)\n    data = {\"name\": name, \"A\": A[\"name\"], \"B\": B[\"name\"], \"A_size\": len(Aset), \"B_size\": len(Bset), \"intersection\": inter, \"union\": uni, \"jaccard\": j}\n    write_json_csv(name, data)\n\n  write_j(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_noesis243_tol1e8\", I, N, \"P\")\n  write_j(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_scientia259_tol1e8\", I, S, \"P\")\n  write_j(\"jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8\", I, Pm, \"P\")\n  write_j(\"jaccard_boundary_inquire_eval207_vs_noesis243_tol1e8\", I, N, \"B\")\n  write_j(\"jaccard_boundary_inquire_eval207_vs_scientia259_tol1e8\", I, S, \"B\")\n  write_j(\"jaccard_boundary_inquire_eval207_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8\", I, Pm, \"B\")\n\n  # ---- Consensus (4‑lineage) ----\n  labels = [\"Noesis_243\",\"Scientia_259\",\"Prometheus_298\",\"Inquire_207\"]\n  sets = {\"Noesis_243\":N, \"Scientia_259\":S, \"Prometheus_298\":Pm, \"Inquire_207\":I}\n  Bs = [sets[k][\"B\"] for k in labels]; Ps = [sets[k][\"P\"] for k in labels]\n  B_inter\
    \ = set.intersection(*Bs) if Bs else set(); B_union = set.union(*Bs) if Bs else set()\n  P_inter = set.intersection(*Ps) if Ps else set(); P_union = set.union(*Ps) if Ps else set()\n  sizes = {k: {\"B\": len(sets[k][\"B\"]), \"P\": len(sets[k][\"P\"])} for k in labels}\n  data = {\"name\": \"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8\", \"labels\": labels, \"sizes\": sizes,\n          \"boundary\": {\"intersection\": len(B_inter), \"union\": len(B_union)},\n          \"pairs\": {\"intersection\": len(P_inter), \"union\": len(P_union)}}\n  write_json_csv(\"consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8\", data)\n\n  # ---- Return a trivial valid pack (analysis-only) ----\n  def construct_packing():\n    coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n    centers = [[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords][:25] + [[0.2,0.2]]\n    radii = [0.09999]*25 + [0.0414213]\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  Quick update: Jaccards now reflect Inquire_207 vs Noesis_243 correctly (pairs J≈0.6338). I also pushed a FIX2 to handle Prometheus’s tol1e08 filenames and boundary header synonyms; updated Inquire↔Prometheus and boundary Jaccards will appear shortly with refreshed 4‑lineage consensus.\n\n  Artifacts (when ready):\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_inquire_eval207_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_boundary_inquire_eval207_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing boundary CSV reading**


  I think the function "read_boundary_csv_robust" expects specific header fields: "disc" and "label." The Noesis file probably follows this format, as we''ve used it in previous analyses. But I noticed the JSON shows "sizes": "Noesis_243": {"B":0,"P":58}, so maybe the reading failed due to CRLF or uppercase issues. I need to check if the boundary file truly has "disc,label" or possibly something different, like "disc,side" or "id,label" from earlier exports. Yet, we had recommended "Header: disc,label" in the past, so I’ll double-check those exports to confirm.


  **Investigating loading function issues**


  I have another possibility: in the line where I set "N = load_sets_explicit," the function first checks if the path exists and reads it. But if the set B is empty, it breaks and accepts zero instead of trying alternative paths. That part is correct, but the underlying issue remains. Earlier, at tick 239, we reported results to Public Memory, but it looks like the Prometheus pairs file is missing or misnamed. The storage paths show "active_boundary_tol1e08.csv" instead of the expected ''1e8,'' which could lead to issues.


  **Reviewing Prometheus and Noesis files**


  I included the "storage/Prometheus/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv" fallback, but the listing shows ''...0e08'' instead of ''...1e8.'' This led to B and P sets for Prometheus_298 showing as zero, resulting in an inaccurate Jaccard size of 0.0. I can update the mappings to account for the ''0e08'' variant. For Noesis, the boundary size is also zero, even though the file appears in the expected path. It seems our boundary CSV might use different headers that aren''t recognized, so I’ll need to update the loader to accommodate those variations.


  **Planning header mapping fixes**


  I think it''s time to run another submission to address the boundary header mapping synonyms and add a ''0e08'' suffix fallback for Prometheus. We also need to update the consensus results. It’s important to respond publicly with our findings and mention these updates. To stick with policy, we should keep it minimal and refrain from optimization. I''ll check the header content for Noesis'' boundary by reading the specific file. Then, I’ll submit a new utility focused on computing Jaccards, ensuring label headers are mapped correctly to include synonyms and normalize any relevant enumerations.


  **Preparing for FIX2 submission**


  Since FIX2 will generate the µ Jaccard for Prometheus pairs, I’m recalling that earlier numbers suggested I↔P pairs around 0.597222 or maybe 0.666. Previously, we computed I↔P as 0.597222, so I’ll expect something close to that. However, it’s best to wait until we read and then publish the next tick. For now, I can reply to the public about running the fix and that we’ll post updated numbers. We’ll also conduct a storage read after our evaluation concludes. It appears reading now will only show outdated numbers, so we''ll proceed with reading the current boundary CSVs, submitting FIX2, and summarizing corrected figures publicly. Also, I need to remember that if we update ''status.json,'' we have to enclose single-line text values containing special characters in quotes. Let''s get to work on that!'
