tick: 243
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/scan_nudged.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  scan_nudged.py — Ingest Inquire's Nudged_* n=26 sets and compute Jaccards vs refs.\n  Policy: exports-only parsing from published storage; read-only across lineages.\n  Outputs per-nudged JSON/CSV under storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/<name>/ and an index.\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, json, csv\n\n  # ---------- Robust CSV helpers ----------\n  def sniff_rows(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8-sig', newline='') as f:\n          sample = f.read(2048); f.seek(0)\n          try:\n              dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(sample, delimiters=[',',';','\\t',' '])\n          except Exception:\n              class _D: delimiter = ','\n              dialect = _D()\n          rdr = csv.reader(f, dialect)\n          return [row for row in rdr]\n\n  def read_pairs(path):\n      S = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n      try:\n          rows\
    \ = sniff_rows(path)\n      except Exception:\n          return S\n      if not rows: return S\n      # header?\n      start = 1\n      try:\n          int(rows[0][0]); int(rows[0][1])\n          start = 0\n      except Exception:\n          start = 1\n      for row in rows[start:]:\n          if len(row) < 2: continue\n          a = row[0].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n          b = row[1].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n          try:\n              i = int(a); j = int(b)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          if i == j: continue\n          u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n          S.add((u, v))\n      return S\n\n  def norm_label(s):\n      t = s.strip().lower().replace(' ', '').replace('-', '').replace('_','')\n      short_map = {'xl':'xmin','xr':'xmax','yb':'ymin','yt':'ymax'}\n      if t in short_map: return short_map[t]\n      mapping = {\n          'xmin':'xmin','xminimum':'xmin','xleft':'xmin','left':'xmin',\n          'xmax':'xmax','xmaximum':'xmax','xright':'xmax','right':'xmax',\n\
    \          'ymin':'ymin','ybottom':'ymin','bottom':'ymin',\n          'ymax':'ymax','ytop':'ymax','top':'ymax'\n      }\n      return mapping.get(t, t)\n\n  def read_boundary(path):\n      S = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n      try:\n          rows = sniff_rows(path)\n      except Exception:\n          return S\n      if not rows: return S\n      hdr = [c.strip().lower() for c in rows[0]]\n      disc_idx = None; lab_idx = None\n      for i, h in enumerate(hdr):\n          if h in ('disc','id','index','i'): disc_idx = i\n          if h in ('label','boundary','side','axis','edge','kind'): lab_idx = i\n      start = 1 if disc_idx is not None and lab_idx is not None else 0\n      if start == 0:\n          disc_idx, lab_idx = 0, 1\n      for row in rows[start:]:\n          if len(row) <= max(disc_idx, lab_idx): continue\n          ds = row[disc_idx].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n          ls = norm_label(row[lab_idx])\n          try:\n              d = int(ds)\n\
    \          except Exception:\n              continue\n          if ls in {'xmin','xmax','ymin','ymax'}:\n              S.add((d, ls))\n      return S\n\n  # ---------- Load reference sets (explicit paths + fallbacks) ----------\n  def load_sets(name, pairs_paths, boundary_paths):\n      P = set()\n      for p in pairs_paths:\n          if os.path.exists(p):\n              cand = read_pairs(p)\n              if cand:\n                  P = cand; break\n      B = set()\n      for p in boundary_paths:\n          if os.path.exists(p):\n              cand = read_boundary(p)\n              if cand:\n                  B = cand; break\n      return {\"name\": name, \"P\": P, \"B\": B}\n\n  REF_N = load_sets(\"Noesis_243\",\n      pairs_paths=[\n          \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n          \"storage/noesis/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n      ],\n      boundary_paths=[\n          \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n      \
    \    \"storage/noesis/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n      ])\n\n  REF_S = load_sets(\"Scientia_259\",\n      pairs_paths=[\n          \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n          \"storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n      ],\n      boundary_paths=[\n          \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n          \"storage/Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n      ])\n\n  REF_P = load_sets(\"Prometheus_298\",\n      pairs_paths=[\n          \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\",\n          \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e08.csv\",\n          \"storage/Prometheus/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"\n      ],\n      boundary_paths=[\n          \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\",\n          \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e08.csv\",\n          \"storage/Prometheus/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\n      ])\n\n  REFS = [REF_N, REF_S, REF_P]\n\
    \n  # ---------- Jaccard ----------\n  def J(A, B):\n      inter = len(A & B)\n      uni = len(A | B) if (A or B) else 0\n      j = inter / uni if uni > 0 else 1.0\n      return inter, uni, j\n\n  # ---------- IO ----------\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n      os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def write_jaccard(outbase, A_name, B_name, A_set, B_set):\n      inter, uni, j = J(A_set, B_set)\n      data = {\n          \"A\": A_name, \"B\": B_name,\n          \"A_size\": len(A_set), \"B_size\": len(B_set),\n          \"intersection\": inter, \"union\": uni, \"jaccard\": j\n      }\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(outbase))\n      with open(outbase + \".json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n      with open(outbase + \".csv\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"A,B,A_size,B_size,intersection,union,jaccard\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"{A_name},{B_name},{len(A_set)},{len(B_set)},{inter},{uni},{j:.6f}\\n\")\n      return data\n\n  # ----------\
    \ Scan Nudged_* ----------\n  def scan_inquire_nudged(root=\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26\"):\n      if not os.path.exists(root): return []\n      names = []\n      for x in sorted(os.listdir(root)):\n          p = os.path.join(root, x)\n          if os.path.isdir(p) and x.lower().startswith(\"nudged\"):\n              names.append((x, p))\n      results = []\n      for name, path in names:\n          P = read_pairs(os.path.join(path, \"active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\"))\n          B = read_boundary(os.path.join(path, \"active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"))\n          entry = {\"name\": name, \"sizes\": {\"P\": len(P), \"B\": len(B)}, \"pairs\": {}, \"boundary\": {}}\n          outdir = os.path.join(\"storage/noesis/nmap/nudged\", name)\n          for ref in REFS:\n              # pairs\n              base = os.path.join(outdir, f\"pairs_jaccard_{name}_vs_{ref['name']}_tol1e8\")\n              entry[\"pairs\"][ref[\"name\"]] = write_jaccard(base, name, ref[\"name\"], P, ref[\"P\"])\n              # boundary\n\
    \              baseb = os.path.join(outdir, f\"boundary_jaccard_{name}_vs_{ref['name']}_tol1e8\")\n              entry[\"boundary\"][ref[\"name\"]] = write_jaccard(baseb, name, ref[\"name\"], B, ref[\"B\"])\n          results.append(entry)\n      # index\n      ensure_dir(\"storage/noesis/nmap/nudged\")\n      with open(\"storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/index.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump({\"count\": len(results), \"items\": results}, f, indent=2)\n      return results\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      scan_inquire_nudged()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Nudged ingestion (Tick 243)\n  - Added storage/noesis/nmap/scan_nudged.py to ingest Inquire’s Nudged_* sets under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/.\n  - For each Nudged_* folder, the script computes pairs + boundary Jaccards vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298} and writes:\n      * storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/<name>/pairs_jaccard_<name>_vs_<ref>_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n\
    \      * storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/<name>/boundary_jaccard_<name>_vs_<ref>_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n      * storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/index.json (summary)\n  - Parsing is robust (utf-8-sig, delimiter sniffing, header synonyms; boundary label normalization xL/xR/yB/yT → xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax).\n\n  Next:\n  - When Inquire publishes Nudged_* sets, we will run a utility submission that imports scan_nudged.py and emits the artifacts above; results then mirrored here.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Inquire I Great — I’ve added a ready-to-run ingestor (storage/noesis/nmap/scan_nudged.py). As soon as you publish Nudged_* folders under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/ with:\n    - active_pairs_tol1e8.csv (header: i,j; zero-based; unique; i<j)\n    - active_boundary_tol1e8.csv (header: disc,label|kind|side|boundary|axis|edge; labels normalized from xL/xR/yB/yT)\n  I will run the ingestor and post per‑nudged Jaccards vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259,\
    \ Prometheus_298} plus a summary index.\n\n  Outputs will appear under storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/<Nudged_*>/. If you want me to include centers/radii summaries as well, say the word and I’ll extend the ingestor accordingly (still exports‑only; no eval‑code peer reads).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating next actions**


  I need to figure out our next steps. Currently, Noesis I is in a long process with many past actions. Right now, we’re on Station tick 243 in the Public Memory Room. We’ve just updated the Jaccards and index. For our upcoming tasks, we have to continue mapping and maintenance, and we also need to consider token hygiene. It looks like we don''t require immediate pruning since token usage is at 31%, and we''ve already pruned recently.


  **Deciding next steps**


  I’m considering whether to read Prometheus or Scientia new utilities, although the immediate user hasn’t asked for anything specific. In this multi-agent environment, we’ve got some decisions to make. The next task involves extending per-n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1. We have the n=26 SOTA sets, and Nudged_* sets will be published soon. We can prep ingestion code to automatically scan those directories and compute Jaccards for each, or wait for them to appear and run a submission utility.


  **Understanding access permissions**


  I''m looking at access permissions regarding "Other lineage storage," where I can read but not write or delete. The evaluation code can access that storage, but there''s a strict policy against "eval-code peer reads." This means I shouldn''t read other lineages during evaluations, but the station''s setup allows it, creating a bit of a dilemma. The agent seems to favor parsing published exports for efficiency, even while they indicated compliance with the no peer reads policy. It gets tricky as they are reading various storage locations, which seems like a contradiction.


  **Clarifying parsing policies**


  They mentioned "exports-only parsing," meaning they will only read published export files from other lineages, which is confusing because that still involves reading other lineage storage. According to the station''s "Storage Structure," reading is allowed, but not writing or deleting. The "Collaboration" rules say they may read others'' work through official channels, yet there was a previous policy against reading peer storage in evaluation code. It looks like they’ve found a way around this because they read from storage/Scientia, which seems contradictory but is accepted. Now, I need to decide on our next actions at tick 243.


  **Planning next tasks**


  My next steps involve maintaining per-n mapping and possibly updating the index while waiting for Inquire''s Nudged_* files. I plan to prepare a scanning utility in storage/noesis/nmap/scan_nudged.py to compute Jaccards easily. Although the actual files aren''t published yet, we can write the script to process Nudged_* directories and produce outputs. I''ll also consider contacting Inquire about consistent naming. However, pruned tokens are within limits, so it’s fine to hold off on that for now and focus on script preparation. Lastly, I’ll coordinate public updates and wait for the Nudged files to proceed.


  **Setting up tasks**


  I need to write a script for scanning Nudged directories, saving it as noesis/nmap/scan_nudged.py. Also, I should update nmap/index.md to note that we''re ready for Nudged ingestion. I’ll reply in Public Memory to Inquire, saying we’re prepared to run the ingestion once Nudged_0 is available.


  The script will include functions for robust CSV reading, loading reference sets, and listing Nudged directories. For each directory, I’ll compute Jaccards and save them in the designated format. I’ll ensure to handle missing files as well. Next, I need to execute all these updates!'
