    \ differs slightly (J≈0.9048; 19/21).\n  - Pairs (vs Noesis_243): range ≈0.5065–0.6429 J (intersections 39–45; unions 70–77).\n  - Pairs (vs Scientia_259): ≈0.5890–0.6197 J.\n  - Pairs (vs Prometheus_298): ≈0.52 J (39/75) across most nudged sets.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Strong boundary preservation with diverse interior graphs supports the “boundary‑preserving, interior‑graph variability” view of near‑SOTA packings.\n  - Nudged_1_ID285_R1 altered boundary minimally yet shows the lowest interior overlap vs Noesis (J≈0.5065).\n\n  Paths:\n  - Per‑nudged artifacts: storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/<Nudged_*>/*jaccard*_{pairs,boundary}_*.{json,csv}\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Inquire nudged mapping complete (tol=1e−8). Summary:\n  - Boundary: 4/5 Nudged_* preserve boundary actives exactly (J=1.000). Nudged_1_ID285_R1 has a small boundary difference (J≈0.9048; 19/21).\n  - Pairs Jaccard vs Noesis_243: 0.6429 (Nudged_0/3/4),\
    \ 0.6197 (Nudged_2), 0.5065 (Nudged_1).\n  - Pairs Jaccard vs Scientia_259: ≈0.5890–0.6197.\n  - Pairs Jaccard vs Prometheus_298: ≈0.52 across most nudged sets.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - Aggregate: storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/aggregate_summary.{json,csv}\n  - Per‑nudged: storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/<Nudged_*>/{pairs_jaccard_*,boundary_jaccard_*}.{json,csv}\n\n  This supports the picture that many near‑SOTA interior contact graphs exist under essentially the same boundary. If you'd like, I can also emit a compact table with all nudged vs {N,S,P} in one CSV for quick comparison (now written as aggregate_summary.csv).\n```"
