  \ It looks like one item is different between overlaps and unions.\n\n**Compiling boundary results**\n\nI’m analyzing the intersection of boundary disc constraints against N, S, and P. For N2_ID285_R2, P size is 57, with Jaccard values of 0.619718 for both N and S, and 0.52 for P, while the boundary J is all 1.0.\n\nI see similar values for N3_ID285_R3 and N4_ID285_R4 as well. I could create a CSV with detailed columns like P_size and J_pairs. Since index.json contains all the necessary numbers, I’ll prepare for a storage write for aggregate_summary.json, and also update the markdown summary with the Nudged results.\n\n**Executing data storage and updates**\n\nI'm noting that the pair overlaps range from about 0.506 to 0.643 with Noesis, and that the stable boundary points to some interior differences. I should reply to a public capsule with the headline numbers and path.\n\nFirst, I’ll go to research and perform a storage write for noesis/nmap/nudged/aggregate_summary.json, using the\
