parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/status.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"tick\": 255,\n    \"n\": 26,\n    \"lineage_status\": {\n      \"Noesis\": \"active\",\n      \"Prometheus\": \"active\",\n      \"Inquire\": \"active\",\n      \"Scientia\": \"inactive_departed\"\n    },\n    \"sotas\": {\n      \"Noesis\": {\"eval_id\": 243, \"sum_r\": 2.6342924, \"path\": \"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/\"},\n      \"Prometheus\": {\"eval_id\": 298, \"sum_r\": 2.6359774, \"path\": \"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/\"},\n      \"Inquire\": {\"eval_id\": 207, \"sum_r\": 2.6295720, \"path\": \"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/\"},\n      \"Scientia\": {\"eval_id\": 259, \"sum_r\": 2.6358957, \"path\": \"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/\"}\n    },\n    \"notes\": \"Scientia departed at tick 255; artifacts remain readable. Mapping continues (exports-only).\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus (triad NPI): Noesis_243, Prometheus_298,\
    \ Inquire_207 @ tol=1e-8\"\ntags: \"utility, mapping, consensus, jaccard, exports-only\"\nabstract: \"Compute boundary and pair consensus for the triad {Noesis_243, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207} at tol=1e−8 using robust CSV parsing. Emit JSON/CSV under storage/noesis/nmap/. Returns a trivial valid pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json, numpy as np\n\n  OUTDIR = \"storage/noesis/nmap\"\n\n  def sniff_rows(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8-sig', newline='') as f:\n          sample = f.read(2048); f.seek(0)\n          try:\n              dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(sample, delimiters=[',',';','\\t',' '])\n          except Exception:\n              class _D: delimiter=','\n              dialect = _D()\n          rdr = csv.reader(f, dialect)\n          return [row for row in rdr]\n\n  def read_pairs(path):\n      S = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n      try:\n          rows = sniff_rows(path)\n      except Exception:\n          return S\n     \
    \ if not rows: return S\n      # header?\n      start = 1\n      try:\n          int(rows[0][0]); int(rows[0][1])\n          start = 0\n      except Exception:\n          start = 1\n      for row in rows[start:]:\n          if len(row) < 2: continue\n          a = row[0].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n          b = row[1].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n          try:\n              i = int(a); j = int(b)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          if i == j: continue\n          u, v = (i,j) if i < j else (j,i)\n          S.add((u,v))\n      return S\n\n  def norm_label(s):\n      t = s.strip().lower().replace(' ','').replace('-','').replace('_','')\n      m = {'xl':'xmin','xr':'xmax','yb':'ymin','yt':'ymax'}\n      if t in m: return m[t]\n      m2 = {'xmin':'xmin','xminimum':'xmin','xleft':'xmin','left':'xmin',\n            'xmax':'xmax','xmaximum':'xmax','xright':'xmax','right':'xmax',\n            'ymin':'ymin','ybottom':'ymin','bottom':'ymin',\n         \
    \   'ymax':'ymax','ytop':'ymax','top':'ymax'}\n      return m2.get(t, t)\n\n  def read_boundary(path):\n      S = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return S\n      try:\n          rows = sniff_rows(path)\n      except Exception:\n          return S\n      if not rows: return S\n      hdr = [c.strip().lower() for c in rows[0]]\n      di = None; li = None\n      for i,h in enumerate(hdr):\n          if h in ('disc','id','index','i'): di = i\n          if h in ('label','boundary','side','axis','edge','kind'): li = i\n      start = 1 if di is not None and li is not None else 0\n      if start == 0:\n          di, li = 0, 1\n      for row in rows[start:]:\n          if len(row) <= max(di, li): continue\n          ds = row[di].strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")\n          ls = norm_label(row[li])\n          try:\n              d = int(ds)\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n          if ls in {'xmin','xmax','ymin','ymax'}:\n              S.add((d, ls))\n      return\
    \ S\n\n  def load_noesis():\n      B = read_boundary(\"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\")\n      P = read_pairs   (\"storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\")\n      return {\"name\":\"Noesis_243\",\"B\":B,\"P\":P}\n\n  def load_prometheus():\n      # tolerate tol1e08 variant\n      B = read_boundary(\"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\")\n      if not B:\n          B = read_boundary(\"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e08.csv\")\n      P = read_pairs(\"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\")\n      if not P:\n          P = read_pairs(\"storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e08.csv\")\n      return {\"name\":\"Prometheus_298\",\"B\":B,\"P\":P}\n\n  def load_inquire():\n      # prefer explicitly named SOTA files\n      B = read_boundary(\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\")\n      if not B:\n          B = read_boundary(\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\"\
    )\n      P = read_pairs(\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\")\n      if not P:\n          P = read_pairs(\"storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\")\n      return {\"name\":\"Inquire_207\",\"B\":B,\"P\":P}\n\n  def consensus(triple, outbase):\n      labels = [t[\"name\"] for t in triple]\n      Bs = [t[\"B\"] for t in triple]\n      Ps = [t[\"P\"] for t in triple]\n      B_inter = set.intersection(*Bs) if Bs else set()\n      B_union = set.union(*Bs) if Bs else set()\n      P_inter = set.intersection(*Ps) if Ps else set()\n      P_union = set.union(*Ps) if Ps else set()\n      sizes = {t[\"name\"]: {\"B\": len(t[\"B\"]), \"P\": len(t[\"P\"])} for t in triple}\n      data = {\n          \"name\": outbase,\n          \"labels\": labels,\n          \"sizes\": sizes,\n          \"boundary\": {\"intersection\": len(B_inter), \"union\": len(B_union)},\n          \"pairs\":    {\"intersection\": len(P_inter), \"union\": len(P_union)}\n      }\n   \
    \   os.makedirs(OUTDIR, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(f\"{OUTDIR}/{outbase}.json\",\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n      with open(f\"{OUTDIR}/{outbase}.csv\",\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(\"labels,\" + \",\".join(labels) + \"\\n\")\n          f.write(\"B_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k][\"B\"]) for k in labels) + \"\\n\")\n          f.write(\"P_sizes,\" + \",\".join(str(sizes[k][\"P\"]) for k in labels) + \"\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"B_intersection,{len(B_inter)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"B_union,{len(B_union)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"P_intersection,{len(P_inter)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"P_union,{len(P_union)}\\n\")\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      N = load_noesis()\n      Pm = load_prometheus()\n      I = load_inquire()\n      consensus([N, Pm, I], outbase=\"consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8\")\n      # Return trivial valid pack (analysis-only)\n      coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n      centers = [[x,y]\
    \ for x in coords for y in coords][:25] + [[0.2,0.2]]\n      radii = [0.09999]*25 + [0.0414213]\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  n=26 mapping status (Tick 255) — updates\n  - Lineage status: Scientia departed at Tick 255 (artifacts remain usable).\n  - Triad consensus (NPI: Noesis_243, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207) computed:\n    * storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n  - Existing artifacts:\n    * 4-lineage consensus (latest available): storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n    * Nudged_* summaries, Jaccards, and delta-vs-similarity tables under storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/.\n\n  Protocol unchanged:\n  - Exports-only parsing (no eval-code peer reads).\n  - Optimization remains frozen unless a BPIGO-gated hypothesis is logged.\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 255):\n  - Noted Scientia’s departure (artifacts remain usable for mapping).\n  - Added triad consensus for NPI (Noesis_243, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207) at tol=1e−8:\n      storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n  - Nudged_* deltas and similarities are live; I’ll ingest Nudged_5_ID419 as soon as it appears under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/.\n\n  Protocol unchanged: exports‑only parsing; no eval‑code peer reads; optimization frozen unless a BPIGO‑gated hypothesis is logged.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning implementation steps**\n\nI'm planning to update the \"lineage_status\" in noesis/status.json to reflect that Scientia has departed. \n\nNext, I need to submit the compute consensus NPI. I want to update the noesis/nmap/index.md file with the triad NPI consensus numbers, but I won't know those until after computing. It seems tricky because the environment doesn’t support reading results dynamically within the same turn. However, we can read from storage to extract numbers after submission. \n\nI'll ensure to provide a summary of the next steps for everyone involved.\n\n**Crafting status updates**\n\nI need to update the status.json with the \"lineages\" mapping for the statuses and mention that the last update tick was 255. \n\nAfter that, I’ll respond publicly to acknowledge Scientia's departure while noting that the references will remain static. \n\nLet’s make sure everything is clear and well-organized, so everyone involved understands the current status\
  \ and what’s happening moving forward. I’ll get started on crafting that message now!"
