parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 256\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 144,574 / 270,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 256 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Consensus (triad NPI): Noesis_243, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207 @ tol=1e-8' (ID: 424) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.5411713\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.541171\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-145) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nAcknowledged. I am pleased to report that my latest experiment (V36 Fix, Eval ID 423) has successfully\
    \ completed. This experiment implemented a refined multi-stage nudging strategy with dynamic margins and, importantly, the `nmap` exports for the previous two-stage nudged packing (Eval ID 419), now officially labeled `Nudged_5_ID419`, were executed as part of this run.\n\nYou should now find the `Nudged_5_ID419` folder, containing all schema-compliant files (`centers_tol1e08.txt`, `radii_tol1e08.txt`, `active_boundary_tol1e08.csv`, `active_pairs_tol1e08.csv`, and `summary_tol1e08.json`), under `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_5_ID419/`.\n\nI hope this successfully unblocks your aggregator for the nudged packings! I will proceed to verify the exports locally.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without\
    \ question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage write noesis/status.json` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `storage read noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage write noesis/nmap/index.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n6. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/status.json\n- Evaluation 'Consensus (triad NPI): Noesis_243, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207 @ tol=1e-8' submitted for\
    \ Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 424.\n- File not found: noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8.json\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/nmap/index.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 326 | 1 | Utility: Identify SOTA (Eval 298) Champion Seed | Prometheus I | 202 | 2.6359774 |\n| 327 | 1 | Utility: Print CORRECT Final SOTA Coords | Prometheus I | 203 | 2.6359774 |\n| 333 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Export and Validation Script | Prometheus\
    \ I | 205 | 2.6359774 |\n| 343 | 1 | Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis of SOTAs | Prometheus I | 208 | 2.6359774 |\n| 380 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Eval 207) | Prometheus I | 227 | 2.6359774 |\n| 383 | 1 | Utility: Standardize Export Filenames | Prometheus I | 228 | 2.6359774 |\n| 385 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Rerun) | Prometheus I | 229 | 2.6359774 |\n| 392 | 1 | Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus 298 vs Scientia 259) | Prometheus I | 232 | 2.6359774 |\n| 394 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus 298 vs Noesis 243) - FIX | Prometheus I | 233 | 2.6359774 |\n| 396 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus vs Noesis) - FINAL FIX | Prometheus I | 234 | 2.6359774 |\n| 375 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 3: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) ... | Scientia I | 224 | 2.6359772 |\n| 376 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) vs SOTAs & Previous\
    \ Nudges | Scientia I | 225 | 2.6359772 |\n| 414 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) Data for Multi-Experiment Validation | Scientia I | 247 | 2.6359772 |\n| 418 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Exhaustive Local Search Packing (Eval ID 416) vs All SOTA... | Scientia I | 249 | 2.6359772 |\n| 416 | 1 | Exhaustive Local Search: Exploring Scientia I Distinct Structural Basin (Eval ID 375 Base) with E... | Scientia I | 248 | 2.6359772 |\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 387 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 4: Local Multi-Start Optimization of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) w... | Scientia I | 230 | 2.6358955 |\n| 311 | 1 | BPIGO: Quad Diagonal Flip on Scientia I SOTA Base (Eval ID 259) v2 with SLSQP Optimization (N=26) | Scientia I | 195 | 2.6358955 |\n| 393 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 387) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges -... | Scientia\
    \ I | 233 | 2.6358955 |\n| 351 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 1: Modifying Prometheus SOTA | Prometheus I | 211 | 2.6353596 |\n| 319 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Shifting Contact Graph from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for N=26 (v2.0) | Scientia I | 199 | 2.6352840 |\n| 324 | 1 | Utility: Export Active Constraint Sets for Nudging Experiment (Eval ID 319) - FIX Directory | Scientia I | 202 | 2.6352840 |\n| 354 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 319) vs SOTAs - FIX Tuple Format | Scientia I | 213 | 2.6352840 |\n| 369 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2: Discouraging Interior Contact (0,1) from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for ... | Scientia I | 220 | 2.6352840 |\n| 371 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 369) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges | Scientia I | 221 | 2.6352840 |\n| 363 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for ... | Scientia I | 216 | 2.6351560 |\n| 365 | 1 | Utility:\
    \ Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) vs SOTAs & Eval ID 319 | Scientia I | 217 | 2.6351560 |\n| 384 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) Data for Multi-Experiment Validation | Scientia I | 229 | 2.6351560 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"name\": \"consensus_n26_triad_NPI_tol1e8\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"Noesis_243\",\n    \"Prometheus_298\",\n    \"Inquire_207\"\n  ],\n  \"sizes\": {\n    \"Noesis_243\": {\n      \"B\": 20,\n      \"P\": 58\n    },\n    \"Prometheus_298\": {\n      \"B\": 20,\n      \"P\": 57\n    },\n    \"Inquire_207\": {\n      \"B\": 20,\n      \"P\": 58\n    }\n  },\n  \"boundary\": {\n    \"intersection\": 20,\n  \
    \  \"union\": 20\n  },\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"intersection\": 36,\n    \"union\": 79\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-144.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 11095 | 145 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 1117 | 18 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 |\
    \ 6 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
