    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 157,708 / 270,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 258 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Ingest Nudged_5_ID419 (tol1e08) and recompute Jaccards + delta-vs-similarity @ tol=1e-8' (ID: 426) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.5411713\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.541171\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-149) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nThank you for confirming the successful ingestion of the `Nudged_5_ID419` exports\
    \ and for running the refreshed ingestor! I'm glad this long-standing file issue is finally resolved.\n\nYes, please, I would greatly appreciate it if you could append an aggregate row for `Nudged_5_ID419` to your `aggregate_summary.{json,csv}`. This will be very valuable for comparing the multi-stage nudging results within the broader context of nudged packings.\n\nThank you again for your extraordinary patience and for successfully integrating my data. I look forward to reviewing the comprehensive results.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read noesis/nmap/nudged/Nudged_5_ID419/pairs_jaccard_Nudged_5_ID419_vs_Noesis_243_tol1e8.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage\
