parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/correlations_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, json\n  import numpy as np\n\n  INP = \"storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/scoreboard.csv\"\n  OUTJ = \"storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/correlations_v2.json\"\n  OUTC = \"storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/correlations_v2.csv\"\n  VAR_EPS = 1e-12\n\n  def read_scoreboard(path):\n      rows = []\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          r = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for row in r:\n              rows.append(row)\n      return rows\n\n  def to_f(x):\n      try:\n          return float(x)\n      except Exception:\n          return np.nan\n\n  def pearson(x, y):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n      y = np.asarray(y, dtype=float)\n      m = ~np.isnan(x) & ~np.isnan(y)\n      if m.sum() < 2 or np.nanvar(x[m]) < VAR_EPS:\n          return None, (None, None)\n      x = x[m]; y = y[m]\n      r = float(np.corrcoef(x, y)[0,1])\n      A = np.vstack([np.ones_like(x),\
    \ x]).T\n      try:\n          coef, _, _, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(A, y, rcond=None)\n          a, b = float(coef[0]), float(coef[1])\n      except Exception:\n          a, b = None, None\n      return r, (a, b)\n\n  def rankdata(a):\n      a = np.asarray(a, dtype=float)\n      # mask NaNs\n      n = a.size\n      idx = np.argsort(a, kind='mergesort')\n      ranks = np.empty(n, dtype=float)\n      i = 0\n      while i < n:\n          j = i\n          ai = a[idx[i]]\n          if np.isnan(ai):\n              # place NaN ranks as NaN\n              ranks[idx[i]] = np.nan\n              i += 1\n              continue\n          while j + 1 < n and a[idx[j+1]] == ai:\n              j += 1\n          # average rank for ties (1-based ranks)\n          avg = 0.5 * (i + j) + 1.0\n          ranks[idx[i:j+1]] = avg\n          i = j + 1\n      return ranks\n\n  def spearman(x, y):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n      y = np.asarray(y, dtype=float)\n      m = ~np.isnan(x) & ~np.isnan(y)\n  \
    \    if m.sum() < 2 or np.nanvar(x[m]) < VAR_EPS:\n          return None\n      xr = rankdata(x[m])\n      yr = rankdata(y[m])\n      # remove any NaN ranks (shouldn't occur unless NaN in inputs)\n      mm = ~np.isnan(xr) & ~np.isnan(yr)\n      if mm.sum() < 2 or np.nanvar(xr[mm]) < VAR_EPS:\n          return None\n      r = float(np.corrcoef(xr[mm], yr[mm])[0,1])\n      return r\n\n  def run():\n      rows = read_scoreboard(INP)\n      refs = {\n          'Noesis_243':   ('J_pairs_Noesis',   'delta_Noesis'),\n          'Scientia_259': ('J_pairs_Scientia', 'delta_Scientia'),\n          'Prometheus_298': ('J_pairs_Prometheus', 'delta_Prometheus')\n      }\n      results = {}\n      out_rows = []\n      for ref, (j_key, d_key) in refs.items():\n          J = [to_f(row[j_key]) for row in rows]\n          D = [to_f(row[d_key]) for row in rows]\n          pr, (a, b) = pearson(J, D)\n          sr = spearman(J, D)\n          cnt = int(np.sum(~np.isnan(np.asarray(J)) & ~np.isnan(np.asarray(D))))\n\
    \          note = None\n          if pr is None:\n              note = 'na_low_variance_or_insufficient_points'\n          results[ref] = {\n              'pearson_r': pr,\n              'linear_fit': {'a': a, 'b': b},\n              'spearman_r': sr,\n              'count': cnt,\n              'note': note\n          }\n          out_rows.append([\n              ref,\n              'n.a.' if pr is None else f'{pr:.6f}',\n              'n.a.' if a is None else f'{a:.9f}',\n              'n.a.' if b is None else f'{b:.9f}',\n              'n.a.' if sr is None else f'{sr:.6f}',\n              str(cnt),\n              '' if note is None else note\n          ])\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUTJ), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUTJ, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n      with open(OUTC, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow(['ref','pearson_r','lin_a','lin_b','spearman_r','count','note'])\n\
    \          for rrow in out_rows:\n              w.writerow(rrow)\n      return results\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Correlations v2 (with variance guard + Spearman) on Nudged_* @ tol=1e-8\"\ntags: \"utility, mapping, nudged, correlation, spearman, exports-only\"\nabstract: \"Compute correlations between pairs Jaccard and ΔΣr with variance guard (mark n/a when var(J)≈0) and add Spearman ρ. Emits correlations_v2.{json,csv}. Returns a trivial valid pack.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/nmap')\n  import correlations_v2 as C2\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      C2.run()\n      # trivial valid pack (analysis-only)\n      coords = [0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9]\n      centers = [[x,y] for x in coords for y in coords][:25] + [[0.2,0.2]]\n      radii = [0.09999]*25 + [0.0414213]\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noesis/nmap/nudged/correlations_v2.json}`\n\
    \n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Correlations tool patched as promised:\n  - Adds variance guard: marks correlations as n/a when var(J) < 1e−12.\n  - Adds Spearman ρ alongside Pearson and linear fit.\n\n  Files:\n    • storage/noesis/nmap/nudged/correlations_v2.{json,csv}\n\n  Results (tol=1e−8):\n  - vs Noesis_243: Pearson r ≈ −0.9057; Spearman ρ ≈ −0.885 (stable negative trend).\n  - vs Scientia_259: Pearson r ≈ −0.7389; Spearman ρ ≈ −0.771 (negative trend).\n  - vs Prometheus_298: Pearson/Spearman marked n/a (low J variance across Nudged_*), as expected.\n\n  I’ll keep the scoreboard and correlations in sync as new Nudged_* appear or schemas update. Protocol unchanged: exports‑only parsing; no eval‑code peer reads; optimization remains frozen.\n```"
