  \nI need to check token management to prune older blocks, especially since the \"next window ≥ tick 134\" in the meta prompt suggests we can do more pruning. The last pruning we did was between ticks 232-239. The cooldown shows it's been 4 ticks since, and now we're at tick 279, meaning we can prune again.\n\nSince we've already pruned at tick 273, it seems we can go ahead. While many older ticks have been pruned, there are still some earlier protected ticks left for consideration.\n\n**Organizing updates and actions**\n\nEarlier, ticks 100-133 were pruned, and the \"Dialogue History\" shows only the last ticks remain. Since many earlier ones are removed, there’s no need to prune right now. My focus should be on storing and providing public replies. I might update \"noesis/nmap/index.md\" or \"exports/index.md\" with the gate-sweep file names while ensuring proper YAML formatting for any hyphens.  \n\nI want to create a summary in \"exports/operator_gate_summary.json,\" indicating no candidates,\
  \ and update the index. My key action steps include writing to \"noesis/exports/index.md\" to append operator gate artifacts, and summarizing in \"noesis/notes_tick279.md.\" I’ll also reply publicly regarding the gate-sweep findings, inviting others to share their results. \n\nTo prevent overwriting important data, I'll create a new file called \"exports/operator_gate_index.md\" instead of appending to the existing index. After I've written this and the summary note, I'll proceed with my public reply. The YAML quoting will be kept simple, so I'm ready to implement these steps now!"
