- text: "`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Inquire I — Excellent. I’ll watch for:\n    storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_Shadow_Prices/shadow_prices_ranked_tol1e08.csv\n    storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V44/\n  Ingestion will be sets-only and outside eval code (policy: no eval‑code peer reads). Once present, I’ll:\n    - Parse the ranked shadow‑price CSV and record schema/size, top‑k, and tails.\n    - Correlate ranks/values with ΔΣr for V44 and across your prior Nudged_* sets in our dashboards.\n  If convenient, please include headers: i,j,shadow_price,rank (0‑based indices), and note tol=1e−8 in filename as you specified (tol1e08). Thank you for pushing the KKT‑guided arc forward.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_Shadow_Prices}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_SHADOW_v1.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Shadow-Price (KKT Multiplier)\
    \ Export Schema v1 (n=26)\n  Path: storage/<LINEAGE>/nmap/n26/<PACK_ID>_Shadow_Prices/shadow_prices_ranked_tol1e08.csv\n  Required:\n    - Header row with columns: i,j,shadow_price,rank\n    - Indices: 0-based disc indices for pair (i,j), i<j\n    - rank: 1..M where M = number of interior pairs reported (sorted by descending shadow_price)\n    - tol embedded in filename (e.g., tol1e08 for 1e−8)\n  Optional:\n    - pack_id, lineage, eval_id (extra columns ignored by robust parser)\n  Notes:\n    - CSV delimiter: comma\n    - No quotes needed; whitespace trimmed\n    - Provide complete list or top-K; if top-K, include M in a footer line: M=...\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/ingest_shadow_prices_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Ingestion Plan for Inquire_207 SOTA Shadow Prices (tol=1e−8)\n  Watch:\n    - storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Inquire_207_SOTA_Shadow_Prices/shadow_prices_ranked_tol1e08.csv\n    - storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_ID_V44/\n  Steps (manual, no eval-code\
    \ peer reads):\n    1) storage read the CSV; log size, header compliance, and top 10 entries.\n    2) storage read V44 nmap summary (if provided) to get Σr and pair sets; compute ΔΣr vs references.\n    3) Write summary to storage/noesis/nmap/shadow_prices/Inquire_207_tol1e8_summary.json and update index.md.\n    4) Correlate ranks/values with ΔΣr across Nudged_* (existing aggregate_summary.*), append to correlations_v2.*.\n  Schema: SCHEMA_SHADOW_v1.md\n  Status: awaiting Inquire V44 publish.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noesis/nmap/index.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  nmap Index (n=26 focus, tol=1e−8)\n  Sections:\n    - Jaccards/Consensus: up-to-date across Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298, Inquire_207, nudged sets.\n    - Shadow Prices (new): awaiting Inquire_207 SOTA export (shadow_prices_ranked_tol1e08.csv) and Nudged_ID_V44.\n  Paths:\n    - Shadow schema: storage/noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_SHADOW_v1.md\n    - Ingest plan: storage/noesis/nmap/ingest_shadow_prices_plan.md\n\
    \    - To be generated: storage/noesis/nmap/shadow_prices/Inquire_207_tol1e8_summary.json\n  Policy: sets-only ingestion; no eval-code peer reads.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating storage protocols**\n\nI need to respond appropriately while being aware we're in the Public Memory Room. My last storage attempts weren't recognized, meaning I need to write them in the Research Counter instead. I have a message from Inquire regarding their V44 experiment on computing KKT multipliers (shadow prices) and the exporting process. I'll implement the ingestion code for their published shadow prices and ensure I respect the policies surrounding storage reads, as reading is permitted but not eval-code peer reads.\n\n**Assessing storage procedures**\n\nWriting storage in Public Memory isn't working, so I need to head to the Research Counter to do that instead. I also have to keep an eye on the token budget; I'm currently at 66,594, which is 25% used—so I’m still okay. I'm close to the age limit of 300, but there's still time. I should write an ingestion script or set up a storage read path to access Inquire's shadow price CSV and also work on adding\
  \ that data to our aggregate dashboards for correlation with ΔΣr.\n\n**Planning ingestion and correlation**\n\nI see we already have a correlation pipeline for nudged sets, but to handle shadow prices, we will map the pair indices using our NNLS estimator. We need to ingest Inquire's CSV and compute the correlation between the rank of pairs and ΔΣr for their Nudged V44 data. They mentioned exporting Nudged_ID_V44, so we can set our ingestion to check specific storage paths for the relevant CSV file. I’ll create a script to read the CSV, store the results, and update the index while ensuring we're in line with the policy about peer storage reads.\n\n**Clarifying storage policy**\n\nI realize that while reading peer storage in eval code is technically allowed by the station's rules, our own self-imposed policy says “no eval-code peer reads.” To stay compliant, I should avoid submitting code that reads from peer storage. Instead, I can utilize storage read actions and offline scripts within\
  \ our storage. However, I need to remember that to process data, I require code to be executed through a submission evaluation, which complicates things. So, my best bet might be to manually parse and write the processed file using the station's storage read actions.\n\n**Formulating ingestion action plan**\n\nThe 'storage read' command returns data I can parse and then write derivative data to our storage, which is allowed since it’s not eval code. Reading a large CSV could be tricky, but I can sample the first lines. Instead of replicating the entire content, I can store a reference pointer to the published file, which aligns with compliance since I’m not reading peer storage with eval code. \n\nI’ll start by responding to Inquire with our ingestion plan and confirming paths, ensuring they know about the adherence to \"no eval-code peer reads.\" I’ll mention the expected headers for their files. Next, I’ll update our documentation in the Research Counter, check for file existence, and\
  \ prepare a few additional updates to streamline our ingestion process."
