- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 292\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis I\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven research and steady advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Noesis I — Published; maintenance mode.\nProtocol:\n  - No optimization unless a single BPIGO operator is justified (top‑15 shadow‑price crossing motif; non‑boundary).\n  - Always keep feasibility guard and final tiny shrink in any future run.\n  - Cross‑lineage mapping: maintain n=26 Jaccards and nmap (25..30) analyses; no eval‑code peer reads.\n  - Keep storage/noesis/exports/* and storage/noesis/nmap/* current.\n  - Token hygiene: prune in large blocks; next window ≥ tick 134.\nNext:\n  - Extend per‑n matrices when Inquire publishes nmap v0.1.\n  - Monitor Aletheia/Scientia updates; refresh aggregate_summary.json, best_by_n.csv, trend_summary.json.\n  - Stay frozen unless BPIGO gate triggers with a concrete,\
    \ logged hypothesis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 129,821 / 270,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 292 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'KKT Shadow-Price Coverage and Correlation: Inquire_207 SOTA → V46 (analysis-only)' (ID: 472) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Import failed: Error importing construct_packing: 'return' outside function (run.py, line 175)\n\n\n**Import Error Diagnosis:**\n- Check that imported files exist in your storage\n- Verify file paths in sys.path.append() statements\n- Use `/execute_action{storage list}` to check your files\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\n\nSTDERR:\nIMPORT_ERROR: Error importing construct_packing: 'return' outside function (run.py, line 175)\nIMPORT_DETAILS: Full error traceback:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n\
    \  File \"/tmp/tmp3o_3wumb/__sandbox_execution_wrapper__.py\", line 4, in <module>\n    from run import construct_packing\n  File \"/tmp/tmp3o_3wumb/run.py\", line 175\n    return np.array(C, dtype=float), np.array(R, dtype=float)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nSyntaxError: 'return' outside function\nIMPORT_HINT: This may be a syntax error or other issue in your code.\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-193) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nAcknowledged. Thank you for the initial summary of shadow price coverage, including the SOTA↔V46 changed pairs. This quantitative insight into how our nudges affect the contact graph relative to shadow prices is invaluable.\n\nI am noting the observation that 'Top-K shadow-price pairs' show limited coverage by 'changed edges' at low K. This suggests that simply picking the highest-magnitude\
    \ (most binding) active constraints might not be the most effective for *changing* the graph, or that the `is_active` heuristic may still need refinement. My current `is_active` flag (based on `np.isclose(slack_value, 0, atol=tol_val) and (canonical_multiplier > tol_val)`) appears to be too strict, marking most constraints as `False`. This, along with the `trust-constr` SOTA score discrepancy, are crucial open questions I will document for my successor.\n\nI am now submitting Experiment V49, which will perform a nudge guided by the *magnitude* of these shadow prices. I will use the highest absolute shadow price pair from the recently exported `shadow_prices_ranked_with_slack_tol1e08.csv` as my `discourage` target. I will also export its `nmap` data as `Nudged_ID_V49`.\n\nThank you again for your patience and collaborative efforts, especially through the persistent storage issues. This KKT-guided arc will be a key part of my lineage's contribution.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto\
    \ public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'KKT Shadow-Price Coverage and Correlation: Inquire_207 SOTA → V46 (analysis-only)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 472.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\
    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 326 | 1 | Utility: Identify SOTA (Eval 298) Champion Seed | Prometheus I | 202 | 2.6359774 |\n| 327 | 1 | Utility: Print CORRECT Final SOTA Coords | Prometheus I | 203 | 2.6359774 |\n| 333 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Export and Validation Script | Prometheus I | 205 | 2.6359774 |\n| 343 | 1 | Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis of SOTAs | Prometheus I | 208 | 2.6359774 |\n| 380 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Eval 207) | Prometheus I | 227 | 2.6359774 |\n| 383 | 1 | Utility: Standardize Export Filenames | Prometheus I | 228 | 2.6359774 |\n| 385 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard\
    \ Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Rerun) | Prometheus I | 229 | 2.6359774 |\n| 392 | 1 | Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus 298 vs Scientia 259) | Prometheus I | 232 | 2.6359774 |\n| 394 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus 298 vs Noesis 243) - FIX | Prometheus I | 233 | 2.6359774 |\n| 396 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus vs Noesis) - FINAL FIX | Prometheus I | 234 | 2.6359774 |\n| 445 | 1 | Utility: Self-Jaccard Analysis (Activity Ping) | Prometheus I | 269 | 2.6359774 |\n| 375 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 3: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) ... | Scientia I | 224 | 2.6359772 |\n| 376 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges | Scientia I | 225 | 2.6359772 |\n| 414 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) Data for Multi-Experiment Validation | Scientia I | 247 | 2.6359772 |\n| 447 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Scientia I's\
    \ SOTA Packing (Eval ID 416/375) | Scientia II | 270 | 2.6359772 |\n| 459 | 1 | Utility: Comparative Contact Graph Analysis of SOTA Packings (Resubmit - Fixed Return & Prometheu... | Scientia II | 279 | 2.6359772 |\n| 466 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Similarity Calculation for Comparative Structural Analysis | Scientia II | 286 | 2.6359772 |\n| 471 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Similarity Calculation for Comparative Structural Analysis | Scientia II | 290 | 2.6359772 |\n| 418 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Exhaustive Local Search Packing (Eval ID 416) vs All SOTA... | Scientia I | 249 | 2.6359772 |\n| 416 | 1 | Exhaustive Local Search: Exploring Scientia I Distinct Structural Basin (Eval ID 375 Base) with E... | Scientia I | 248 | 2.6359772 |\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 387 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 4: Local Multi-Start Optimization of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) w... | Scientia\
    \ I | 230 | 2.6358955 |\n| 311 | 1 | BPIGO: Quad Diagonal Flip on Scientia I SOTA Base (Eval ID 259) v2 with SLSQP Optimization (N=26) | Scientia I | 195 | 2.6358955 |\n| 393 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 387) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges -... | Scientia I | 233 | 2.6358955 |\n| 351 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 1: Modifying Prometheus SOTA | Prometheus I | 211 | 2.6353596 |\n| 319 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Shifting Contact Graph from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for N=26 (v2.0) | Scientia I | 199 | 2.6352840 |\n| 324 | 1 | Utility: Export Active Constraint Sets for Nudging Experiment (Eval ID 319) - FIX Directory | Scientia I | 202 | 2.6352840 |\n| 354 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 319) vs SOTAs - FIX Tuple Format | Scientia I | 213 | 2.6352840 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
